window.FWN_YOU_PROMISED_TO_BE_AN_IDLE_SON_IN_LAW_HOW_COULD_YOU_BECOME_A_LAND_IMMORTAL_CHAPTERS=(window.FWN_YOU_PROMISED_TO_BE_AN_IDLE_SON_IN_LAW_HOW_COULD_YOU_BECOME_A_LAND_IMMORTAL_CHAPTERS||[]).concat([{"number":201,"title":"Chapter 201 - 183: Simple, Just Be All About the Money","paragraphs":["Night fell.","As dark clouds gathered, the rain naturally began to fall again.","Although it was only a light drizzle compared to the downpours of the past two days, it was a refreshing change from the oppressive heat of the day.","At least the rain carried a cool breeze, preventing one from feeling stuffy and irritable.","Chen Yi, however, felt none of this.","With his mastery of Martial Arts, having reached the Sixth Grade Realm, he was practically immune to heat and cold.","Gloomy rain, scorching heat, and biting snow had little effect on him.","Still, compared to rain and snow, he much preferred sunny days.","To be precise, he loved the sunny days of spring.","The sunlight was gentle then, a soft breeze would blow, and green waves would ripple. Even the fish in the lakes, large and small, seemed more active than in other seasons.","Unfortunately, it was now the summer’s plum rain season.","The frequent rain, the heat, and the numerous matters weighing on him made it difficult to find a moment of peace and leisure.","’This is no good. No good at all.’","Chen Yi stood by the window, watching the rain fall on Spring Lotus Garden. After a few silent sighs, he shook his head and opened his wardrobe.","After rummaging through it for a moment...","Chen Yi found a robe similar to the one Black Tooth had worn the other day. He changed out of his long gown and, looking into a copper mirror, arranged his hair into a shoulder-length style more suited to the Jianghu.","Tonight, he was going to impersonate Black Tooth to meet Liu Wen and \"discuss important matters.\"","There was no room for even the slightest carelessness.","As he prepared, Chen Yi’s mind raced, mulling over the discoveries of the past two days and re-evaluating the plot to \"burn the summer grain of the Three Towns.\"","He considered the Xiao Family’s likely response.","He thought about how the Hidden Guard was fanning the flames and what arrangements they would have in place when the time came to act.","He also factored in the Jing State Liu Family’s involvement, among other things.","As these fragmented threads of information appeared in his mind, they were clearer than ever before.","Chen Yi knew this was because his Chess Dao had reached Great Success, making him much more adept at strategy and planning.","Furthermore, he now had more clues regarding Black Tooth, the Evil Demon, the Hidden Guard, and the Liu Family members.","It wasn’t difficult to sort out the various factions, and finding a way to break their scheme was also within reach.","As Chen Yi thought about this, he couldn’t help but grumble to himself about how he should have improved his Chess Dao sooner.","’Compared to the Martial Dao, Calligraphy Dao, and Medical Dao, the Chess Dao might seem flashy but impractical, yet it’s incredibly useful.’","’Fortunately, it’s not too late for me to realize this now.’","Once he was dressed...","Chen Yi put on a bamboo hat, applied a simple disguise, and used the cover of the rainy night to circle around the back of the mountain, heading straight for the residence on Chuansi Street.","He had previously instructed Zhang Dabao to wait for him there and had also informed Liu Lang.","In any case, he couldn’t go to the West Market for the time being.","He had to avoid running into Fang Hongxiu of the Imprisonment Department, or the people under Chen Yunfan and Cui Qingwu.","’I almost forgot.’","’The Old Marquis has probably sent people to Hundred Herbs Hall to investigate \"Chen Yu\" by now.’","In fact, earlier that day, the Old Marquis had spoken to him about the Xiao Family Medicine Hall.","He had hinted, both directly and indirectly, that Chen Yi should help Xiao Wan’er more in his free time.","Chen Yi had naturally agreed without hesitation.","He knew in his heart that the Old Marquis’s test was, on one hand, a trial, and on the other, a sign that he was already being treated as a member of the Xiao Family.","As long as he showed no ambition to become an official or join the army, and simply stayed dutifully at the Medicine Hall or the academy, the Old Marquis likely wouldn’t be too demanding of him.","Of course, this was all contingent on his \"Chen Yu\" identity not being exposed.","If the Old Marquis found out he was the owner of Hundred Herbs Hall, complications would inevitably arise.","’So, it’s best to be careful.’","After walking for less than fifteen minutes, with a few stops along the way...","Chen Yi arrived at the courtyard house.","Liu Lang hadn’t arrived yet, so he had Zhang Dabao apply his disguise first.","In addition to the mask for his \"Chen Yu\" persona, this time he also added the half-mask for \"Liu Wu.\"","After carefully checking for any flaws in the copper mirror, Chen Yi took a black iron mask and put it on.","Immediately, the aura around him changed.","Under the dim yellow candlelight, his figure was cast in light and shadow, emanating wisps of a cold, indifferent air.","Seventy percent sinister coldness, twenty percent cunning, ten percent caution—this was his impression of Black Tooth.","Like a venomous snake hiding in the shadows, ready to strike and devour its prey at any moment.","Beside him, Zhang Dabao unexpectedly met his gaze, and a chill shot up from his tailbone straight to the back of his head.","\"My lord, you... this time, you’re...\"","Chen Yi’s eyes twitched slightly as he spoke in a low, raspy voice, \"How is it? Do I look like an Evil Demon who has roamed the Jianghu for years?\"","Unexpectedly, Zhang Dabao paused, then hesitantly shook his head. \"You do, and you don’t.\"","\"Oh? Explain.\"","\"You have the coldness and the viciousness, but you’re missing a murderous indifference.\"","Hearing this, Chen Yi nodded in understanding. \"You’re right.\"","The moment he finished speaking, his aura shifted again, and his eyes gained a hint of killing intent that showed a complete disregard for life.","\"HISS!\"","Zhang Dabao took one look and quickly turned away, not daring to look again.","’Good heavens, the lord’s talent for disguise is truly on another level.’","’With just a few simple words from me, he’s like a completely different person. There are almost no flaws.’","’Forget a greenhorn like me; even those who’ve roamed the Jianghu for years probably couldn’t see through the lord’s disguise.’","Before Zhang Dabao could compose himself and offer some compliments...","The sound of footsteps came from outside, and Liu Lang hurriedly pushed the door open.","His eyes swept the room, and just as he was about to speak, his expression suddenly changed. \"Black Tooth?!\" he blurted out.","Not only that, but his hand also went to the hilt of his blade, ready to fight to the death if things went south.","Seeing this, Chen Yi nodded in satisfaction and said with a smile, \"Relax, it’s me.\"","\"Boss?\"","Liu Lang looked at him, then at Zhang Dabao beside him, before finally letting out a long breath.","\"At first glance, I really thought Black Tooth had discovered what we’ve been doing behind his back.\"","\"If it were really Black Tooth, you’d probably be collecting my and Dabao’s corpses right now.\"","\"Heh heh... The boss has fortune on his side. Nothing could happen to you.\"","’That flattery wasn’t nearly as smooth as Wang Ji’s.’","Chen Yi couldn’t be bothered with it. He waved his hand, signaling for him to sit down. \"Tell me what happened last night.\"","Liu Lang’s spirits lifted, and he immediately began to recount with great animation his meeting with Liu Wen.","There was Liu Zhaoxue’s nighttime meeting with the Five Poison Sect.","There was Liu Wen relaying a message to Liu Zhaoxue, stating his intention to visit the Old Marquis at the Xiao Family estate today.","Finally, he gave a detailed and meticulous account of his confrontation and conversation with Liu Wen.","After listening, Chen Yi didn’t speak immediately.","Instead, he tapped his fingers on the armrest of his chair, recalling the various behaviors he had observed from the siblings, Liu Wen and Liu Zhaoxue, at the Xiao Family estate that day.","’It seems the Liu Family is not a monolith after all.’","’You could see hints of that from Liu Jing.’","’Although Liu Jing is also a direct descendant of the Liu Family’s main branch, when he was sent to Shu State, he wasn’t even allowed to hang up the sign for Xinglin Hall.’","’Add to that the Liu Family’s suspicion of Liu Hong, the Chief Steward of the third branch... ’","It wasn’t hard for Chen Yi to deduce that the internal competition within the Jing State Liu Family didn’t just exist between the first, second, and third branches, but also extended down to Liu Wen’s generation.","\"That’s a bit of good news, neither big nor small.\"","Liu Lang smiled and nodded. \"I was thinking the same thing.\"","\"You have to understand, those people from the Five Poison Sect have always been ruthless. Because of their Cultivation Technique, they’re not just cruel to outsiders; they’re cruel to themselves too.\"","\"I remember before Granny Shan moved to wipe out the Five Poison Sect, they were quite powerful and committed several heinous acts.\"","Chen Yi raised an eyebrow. \"Granny Shan? The Five Poison Sect was annihilated by someone from the Mountain Race?\"","Liu Lang grunted in affirmation, hugging his long blade as he spoke. \"I don’t know many of the details.\"","\"I only heard that while the Five Poison Sect was active in Shu State, they somehow offended Granny Shan, provoking her to personally lead people to their doorstep.\"","\"They say that battle lasted for two full days and nights. In the end, Granny Shan proved to be the superior strategist. Using her Witchcraft and Gu Skill combined with the Mountain Race’s three great poisons, she completely uprooted the Five Poison Sect.\"","Liu Lang glanced at him and explained, \"Don’t be fooled by the fact that the Mountain Race is rarely active in Shu State these days.\"","\"Granny Shan’s reputation in the Jianghu is not the least bit small.\"","\"Especially her unfathomable Witchcraft and Gu Poison Skill. Even Martial Arts Powerhouses of the Upper Three Grades would meet a bitter end if they encountered it.\"","Chen Yi thought for a moment. \"Since the Five Poison Sect was wiped out by Granny Shan, why have they reappeared in the Jianghu?\"","Liu Lang paused and spread his hands. \"I don’t know either. I’d guess they’re some fish that slipped through the net.\"","\"But I have to admire their courage. Daring to show up in Shu State... they must not be afraid of Granny Shan coming after them again.\"","Chen Yi nodded in understanding but didn’t dwell on the matter of the Five Poison Sect.","\"Let’s go.\"","\"Let’s not delay and risk complications. The sooner we meet with Liu Wen, the sooner we can come back and rest.\"","Liu Lang got up and followed, saying with a smile, \"Boss, I’m putting my life in your hands tonight.\"","\"It wouldn’t be so bad if Liu Wen saw through the disguise, but if Black Tooth finds out, he’ll probably hunt us to the ends of the earth.\"","He paused, then asked with some concern, \"Boss, you won’t blow your cover, will you?\"","Chen Yi’s aura shifted slightly. He glanced at him from the corner of his eye and said in his raspy voice:","\"It’s simple. I just have to be greedy as hell.\"","Liu Lang couldn’t help but burst out laughing. \"Now that I think about it, Black Tooth really does love money more than his own life.\"","After leaving the house...","The two of them fell silent, stopping and starting as they made their way to the outside of Liu Wen’s residence.","Chen Yi didn’t sneak in immediately. Instead, he circled the entire residence, from front to back.","Only after memorizing the surrounding environment did he signal for Liu Lang to lead the way.","\"This way...\"","Just as Liu Lang was about to lead him in through the back door on the east side, Chen Yi suddenly raised a hand to stop him.","\"Someone’s coming!\""]},{"number":202,"title":"Chapter 202 - 184: Whom the Gods Would Destroy, They First Make Mad","paragraphs":["CREAK.","CLICK. CLACK.","Two old, weathered wooden doors slowly creaked open, and a guard in a short blue tunic cautiously poked his head out, scanning the surroundings.","A moment later, seeing nothing amiss outside the back door, he waved to someone behind him.","\"Come on out. No one’s here.\"","Then, two guards emerged from the residence, each carrying a burlap sack on his back. They glanced left and right.","Seeing that the coast was clear, the tense looks on their faces finally eased a little.","\"Old Liu, don’t wander off. Just guard the door from the inside. Remember to open it for us when we get back.\"","\"Hurry up and stop wasting time.\"","\"Let’s use the cover of this cloudy, rainy weather to get rid of these two wretched maids.\"","\"Alright.\"","The two guards nodded, said no more, and headed directly for the north city gate.","After they were gone, the guard surnamed Liu shut the wooden door, muttering curses under his breath.","\"That makes five of them now.\"","\"Hmph, why isn’t that old bastard Xiao Yuan dead yet...\"","Though his voice was low, it was heard clearly by Chen Yi and Liu Lang, who were hidden in the shadows outside the door.","Liu Lang wore a strange expression. He glanced at Chen Yi’s calm face out of the corner of his eye and said hesitantly,","\"The Liu Family’s second young master must have been rebuffed at the Marquis’s Mansion today. He’s probably still fuming.\"","Chen Yi glanced at him and nodded. \"A good thing.\"","\"Huh?\"","\"Stop ’huh’-ing. Lead the way.\"","Chen Yi didn’t elaborate. After giving the order, his gaze followed the two guards disappearing into the distance.","Faintly, he could still smell the thick, fading scent of blood.","’The fifth one today...’","’Heh, it seems Liu Wen was thoroughly infuriated by the old master.’","’Which is also good.’","’Those whom heaven would destroy, it first drives mad.’","’This Liu Wen is destined to die in Shu State!’","Although Liu Lang didn’t understand why he called it a \"good thing,\" he knew that Chen Yi was displeased.","In fact, Liu Lang also despised young masters from noble families like Liu Wen, who treated human life as if it were grass.","Even though he was a member of the Bright Moon Building, he didn’t take part in just any job, nor did he kill just anyone.","For instance, when he had gone with the Illusory Sound Sect to plunder the Xiao Family’s medicinal supplies.","He hadn’t even intended to draw his blade against the Jianghu escorts, disdaining to bully the weak.","Otherwise, Shen Huatang of the Celestial Sect would never have left alive.","But Liu Wen was a different story. He got angry at the Xiao Family during the day and took it out on his own servants at night. How was such behavior any different from the Evil Demonic Dao of the Jianghu?","「A few moments later.」","The two arrived at the eastern rear residence, one walking in front of the other.","Liu Lang composed himself, confirmed that no one was around, and pointed to a wooden building not far away.","Chen Yi nodded in understanding and pricked up his ears to listen.","\"...That old fool! He’s at death’s door, yet he dares to scold me?\"","\"My visit was a show of respect, but you?\"","\"I showed you respect, and you’re just shameless!\"","\"And that Xiao Wan’er, daring to refuse my generous offer!\"","\"Given the Xiao Family’s current situation, how dare you? Huh?!\"","The faintly heard voice caused a trace of killing intent to gradually surface in Chen Yi’s eyes as he looked at the wooden building.","He then waved his hand, signaling for Liu Lang to knock on the door.","KNOCK. KNOCK KNOCK.","The crisp sound silenced the shouting inside the wooden building.","Liu Wen asked coldly, \"Who is it?\"","Liu Lang lowered his voice and replied, \"Liu Er.\"","\"Has your master arrived?\"","Chen Yi stepped forward slowly, strands of killing intent piercing through the antique wooden door with his every step, pressing in on those inside.","\"I hope Young Master Liu will forgive my late-night visit.\"","Before he finished speaking, the wooden door creaked open inward, as if to welcome him.","Chen Yi strode inside without hesitation.","Liu Lang followed, glanced around, and gently closed the door.","Standing to one side of the main hall, long sword in hand, Liu Wen stared at Chen Yi with his narrow eyes, a smile appearing on his effeminate face.","\"Black Tooth?\"","Chen Yi glanced at him, took off his bamboo hat and placed it on the table, then nodded calmly. \"The very same.\"","He then looked at the long sword in Liu Wen’s hand and gestured toward it. \"Is this Young Master Liu’s way of saying I’m not welcome?\"","Liu Wen paused, then sheathed his long sword and said with a smile and a cupped-fist salute, \"The name Black Tooth is as famous as a clap of thunder. You are most welcome.\"","A man’s reputation is like a tree’s shadow.","Even though he was a direct descendant of the Jing State Liu Family and had plenty of ways to deal with Black Tooth and the Bright Moon Building.","But right here, right now, his cultivation was far inferior to Black Tooth’s.","Naturally, he wouldn’t put himself in danger.","Of course, more importantly, Liu Wen was somewhat curious about what business this Bright Moon Building elder had for him.","Seeing this, Chen Yi nodded. \"I have long admired Young Master Liu as well. Seeing you today, you are truly a dragon among men.\"","Listening to their exchange of compliments, Liu Lang secretly grimaced.","He didn’t know whether Liu Wen truly welcomed \"Black Tooth.\"","But he knew for a fact that his boss had no favorable impression of Liu Wen.","’Hard to believe the boss could say something like \"a dragon among men\" to his face.’","With these thoughts in mind, Liu Lang pretended he hadn’t heard anything and turned to stand guard at the door, facing outward.","After a few more pleasantries, Chen Yi and Liu Wen took their seats one after another.","\"So, Elder Black Tooth, what business do you have with me? If it’s about Liu Jing’s death, I’m not interested.\"","Hearing Liu Wen’s blunt words, Chen Yi understood that he was indicating he knew the real reason for Liu Jing’s death.","At the same time, it was a subtle reminder and a threat—he wasn’t as easily fooled as Liu Jing.","Chen Yi paused for a moment. \"I have a business deal I’d like to invite Young Master Liu to participate in.\"","Liu Wen thought, ’Just as I expected,’ a hint of disappointment showing on his face.","Still, he understood how the Bright Moon Building operated, so he asked, \"What kind of deal?\"","\"The Xiao Family.\"","\"If it’s a trivial matter like dealing with the Xiao Family Medicine Hall, I’m not interested.\"","\"Such a minor deal would be beneath notice and naturally wouldn’t be worthy of your attention, Young Master.\"","Liu Wen raised an eyebrow, his interest piqued. \"Let’s hear it.\"","But to his surprise, Chen Yi just shook his head and said, \"My apologies, Young Master Liu, but the Bright Moon Building has strict rules.\"","\"If you wish to participate, you must show your sincerity.\"","Liu Wen froze, looking at him with a strange expression. \"Are you saying I have to pay silver first just to find out the details of this deal?\"","\"Precisely. However, I can guarantee that after you hear it, you won’t care about a little bit of silver coins.\"","\"...And what if I’m not interested in getting involved?\"","\"The silver coins will not be returned.\"","\"...\"","Liu Lang almost burst out laughing.","The Black Tooth he knew was certainly greedy, but he’d never demanded money upfront without revealing anything at all.","’How is this any different from extortion?’","But on second thought, he more or less understood his boss’s plan.","’After all, this is about something as huge as burning the summer grain of the Dingyuan Army’s three garrisons. If he just came out and said it, Liu Wen would inevitably become suspicious.’","’This seemingly \"mysterious\" demand for silver coins could later be justified as simple \"caution.\"’","Sure enough, after meeting Chen Yi’s gaze for a moment, Liu Wen took a stack of silver notes from his robes and placed it on the table, saying with a smile,","\"I hope your Bright Moon Building won’t disappoint me.\"","\"We won’t.\"","As he spoke, Chen Yi picked up the stack of silver notes, thumbed through a few, but then placed them back on the table. \"Not enough.\"","Liu Wen stared at him, stunned. \"Two thousand silver... is not enough?\"","Chen Yi shook his head, unmoved. \"Indeed, it is not enough.\"","\"Let me be blunt. The deal involves six hundred thousand silver coins. If you wish to know the details, Young Master, it will cost at least ten thousand silver coins.\"","Liu Wen stared at him blankly for a good while, then suddenly burst out laughing.","\"Six hundred thousand... A huge deal indeed!\"","With that, Liu Wen stood up and returned to the side room.","After he left, Liu Lang forgot about watching the outside and turned his head toward Chen Yi, his lips moving as he silently mouthed a question:","\"Didn’t you say three hundred thousand?\"","Chen Yi shot him a glare, signaling for him to shut his mouth and turn back around.","Liu Lang turned back resentfully. This time, he truly couldn’t figure out what his boss was planning.","’He can’t possibly be trying to get Liu Wen to fork over another thirty thousand gold, can he?’","HISS...","’Damn, the boss is really something else.’","’To casually talk about a deal worth three hundred thousand silver.’","「Before long.」","Liu Wen returned with the full amount in silver notes and placed them on the table. A sinister, effeminate smile touched his lips as he said,","\"If you dare to deceive me, you know the consequences.\"","Chen Yi noncommittally put away the stack of silver notes, mentally chalking it up as repayment for the money previously given to Black Tooth.","Then, without further delay, he leaned close to Liu Wen’s ear and whispered a few words.","Liu Wen’s eyes shot wide open. He snapped his head to the side to look at him. \"Truly?\"","Chen Yi sat up straight and nodded slightly. \"If Young Master Liu is interested, you’re in on this deal.\"","The smile on Liu Wen’s face gradually turned strange.","It was a mixture of shock, ruthlessness, and madness, among other things.","This time, he was genuinely stunned by the deal Black Tooth had described.","’How dare these people?’","’They’re actually going to burn the summer grain of the Three Towns? Aren’t they afraid of being hunted to the ends of the earth by the Xiao Family?’","Because of this, however, Liu Wen finally understood why Black Tooth had demanded ten thousand silver coins from him.","A deal of this magnitude would bring about a fatal disaster if it were even spoken of, let alone carried out.","Thinking of this, Liu Wen tried hard to suppress the complex thoughts in his mind.","\"A deal like this is indeed beyond my expectations.\"","\"I just don’t understand why you came to me, Elder Black Tooth.\"","Chen Yi had long anticipated his reaction and said in a calm tone,","\"This matter is of great importance. With the help of the Liu Family, our chances of success will naturally be greater.\"","At this, Chen Yi paused, looked him directly in the eye, and continued, \"Furthermore, this matter will benefit you.\"","\"Once it is done, whether you wish to marry the Xiao Family’s eldest young lady or have other plans, your efforts will be doubly effective.\"","Liu Wen said in surprise, \"You know I want to marry Xiao Wan’er?\"","\"If the Bright Moon Building didn’t have its sources, how would I dare come and trouble you, Young Master?\"","Liu Wen nodded, understanding in his heart that \"Black Tooth\" was right.","He knew very well what would become of the Xiao Family after this deal was done.","The summer grain of the Three Towns burned, the Dingyuan Army short on silver and food, the Xiao Family driven to desperation, and accountability from the Imperial Court...","Under all this pressure, the Liu Family would have an opportunity to exploit.","At that time, whether he chose to loot a burning house or offer charcoal in a snowstorm, the goal of his trip could be accomplished.","\"But even if I don’t participate, you and the Bright Moon Building will still go through with this deal, won’t you?\"","Chen Yi chuckled. \"Young Master Liu, you ask a question you already know the answer to.\"","\"If I’m not mistaken, by tomorrow, news of your humiliation at the Xiao Family residence will have spread throughout Shu State City.\"","\"Add to that the fact your second uncle was rejected when he went to the Xiao Family to propose marriage... what do you think people in Shu State will say about you? What rumors will spread about the Jing State Liu Family?\"","Liu Wen’s face fell, and he glared at him coldly. \"That’s no reason for me to participate!\"","\"Don’t you want to personally send the Xiao Family to their graves?\"","\"As far as I know, the likelihood of the Jing State Liu Family’s Patriarch position falling to your elder brother... is much greater!\""]},{"number":203,"title":"Chapter 203 - 185: The Dagger is Revealed","paragraphs":["The dagger was revealed.","Chen Yi knew before he arrived that to get Liu Wen to join this deal midway through, he would have to give him several powerful reasons.","The Liu Family’s schemes and plots against the Xiao Family were one.","Elder Master Xiao’s humiliation of Liu Wen was another.","But these weren’t enough to make Liu Wen join in after weighing the pros and cons.","After much thought, he realized the only thing that could truly tempt Liu Wen was the position of Patriarch of the Jing State Liu Family.","Only by making Liu Wen believe that succeeding in this venture would elevate his prestige and status within the Liu Family would he be willing to take such a risk.","As these thoughts ran through his mind, Chen Yi said in a level tone:","\"The other Financier is only interested in revenge against the Xiao Family. There isn’t much personal gain for him, and he has no wish to reveal his identity.\"","\"If you were to join, he would be more than happy to remain in the shadows and let you take full credit for everything.\"","Seeing Liu Wen was tempted, Chen Yi lowered his voice slightly. \"If you don’t wish to participate, that’s fine too. Just pretend I was never here tonight.\"","\"But if you try to claim a piece of this monumental achievement afterward, the price will be far more than a mere six hundred thousand silver coins.\"","\"It is up to you to weigh your options, Young Master Liu.\"","With that, Chen Yi rose to his feet, ready to depart.","Seeing this, a ruthless, decisive smile spread across Liu Wen’s face. He raised a hand to stop him.","\"This deal... I will take part!\"","’Success.’","Chen Yi relaxed internally, but his eyes, hidden beneath the black iron mask, remained impassive. He nodded.","\"I believe that when you become the Patriarch of the Liu Family, Young Master Liu, you will be grateful for the decision you’ve made today.\"","\"Heh, haha... I was thinking the exact same thing!\"","Following that, Chen Yi struck while the iron was hot, settling with Liu Wen the amount of silver coins required to join the venture.","The amount was exactly three hundred thousand silver coins.","Although it pained him to part with the money, Liu Wen readily agreed when he recalled that Xinglin Hall had prepared a million silver coins for his trip to Shu State.","\"I will have my men prepare the silver coins tomorrow. I trust Elder Black Tooth will arrive on time to collect them.\"","\"Of course. The arrangements for the deal are already underway.\"","\"With your silver coins, I can recruit more experts from the Jianghu. We’ll see results within ten days.\"","\"Excellent...\"","After they discussed more details about burning the summer grain in the Three Towns, Liu Wen became completely convinced of the deal’s viability.","He never imagined Black Tooth and his men would be so daring.","Nor did he expect Bright Moon Building to have such extensive reach.","They even had an informant within the Dingyuan Army.","With the added support of people like Elder Demon Fang and Elder Demon Jia, the deal’s chances of success were over sixty percent.","For him, it was merely a matter of spending a bit more silver.","About the time it takes for an incense stick to burn, Chen Yi and Liu Lang left the wooden building one after another, vanishing silently into the rainy night.","As Liu Wen watched them depart, a smile slowly blossomed across his effeminate face.","He imagined the chaos that would engulf the Xiao Family, the shock that would ripple through his own Liu Family, and the praise they would shower upon him. He laughed maniacally in his heart.","Even the anger from Elder Master Xiao’s earlier humiliation had largely dissipated.","\"Once this succeeds... once this succeeds, haha...\"","\"The Liu Family will be mine!\"","\"And the Xiao Family will be mine too!\"","Chen Yi didn’t need to guess to know exactly what Liu Wen was thinking.","An ambitious man like Liu Wen could never refuse such a monumental temptation.","Compared to personally throwing the Xiao Family into chaos and winning the praise of the Liu Family’s elders, those three hundred thousand silver coins were nothing.","Liu Lang, who was beside him, was not nearly as calm.","Even though he already knew how formidable his boss was, he couldn’t help but feel a deep sense of awe at this moment.","First, he had impersonated one of Liu Wen’s subordinates to visit Bright Moon Building, casually dispelling Black Tooth’s suspicions and successfully getting in on the deal.","Then, he had impersonated Black Tooth to invite Liu Wen to join.","They seemed like two simple steps, but in reality, the slightest misstep in any detail would have brought the entire plan crashing down.","Liu Lang, at least, knew that if he were in Chen Yi’s shoes, he could never have pulled it off.","It required brains and nerve, neither of which could be lacking.","Furthermore, it required a vast amount of information and a deep understanding of people like Liu Wen and Black Tooth.","Add to that the ability to react under pressure...","In a word—Liu Lang was impressed.","After taking a winding route back to the residence on Chuansi Street, Liu Lang could no longer hold back.","\"Boss, you’ve truly opened my eyes today.\"","\"No matter how worldly and experienced that Liu Wen thinks he is, you had him running in circles.\"","\"And Black Tooth, haha... I can just imagine his reaction when he finds out. It’s bound to be priceless.\"","Chen Yi ignored him and sat directly down in the Grandmaster’s Chair, his mind finally able to relax.","Seeing this, Liu Lang set aside his admiration, sat down beside him, and asked with a smile, \"Boss, what are your orders?\"","This time, he was truly impressed.","He wasn’t asking because of the thirty tasks he had promised Chen Yi before, but because he genuinely wanted to help him.","Chen Yi glanced at him, rubbing the bridge of his nose as he pondered. \"Did you say just now that the person from the Five Poison Sect would be visiting Liu Zhaoxue again tonight?\"","Liu Lang nodded. \"That’s what he said last night.\"","\"Then go and do some eavesdropping. See what the Five Poison Sect and Liu Zhaoxue are planning.\"","\"Right.\"","As Liu Lang stood up, Chen Yi added a reminder, \"Be careful. You should change your attire. Don’t let Liu Wen notice anything is amiss.\"","\"Don’t worry, Boss...\"","After he left, Chen Yi let out a long sigh of relief.","He had appeared calm and composed throughout the entire affair, but in truth, he had been under immense pressure, constantly worried that something unexpected might happen.","Fortunately, his preparations had been thorough enough to convince Liu Wen to agree.","But looking back on it now, Chen Yi felt a pang of gratitude for his good fortune.","First, he was thankful for Elder Master Xiao’s public humiliation of Liu Wen during the day.","Second, he was thankful for the information Liu Lang had overheard the previous night.","If he hadn’t learned from Liu Lang about Liu Zhaoxue’s cooperation with the Five Poison Sect, Chen Yi wouldn’t have been so sure about the fierce competition for the Patriarch title among Liu Wen’s generation.","A short while later, after Zhang Dabao had helped him remove his disguise, Chen Yi gave a few instructions and headed back to the Xiao Family estate.","By now, it was late into the night.","The rain had grown heavier.","The pitter-patter of raindrops echoed all over Chuansi Street, where not a single soul could be seen.","Even the members of the City Guard Army and the Imprisonment Department on night patrol were nowhere to be seen.","Though Chen Yi was mentally drained, he was in a pleasant mood.","After tonight, his scheme was mostly complete. All that remained was to wait for it to bear fruit.","’By my calculations, Tiger Girl should have met with Xiao Jinghong by now.’","’I wonder what Xiao Jinghong will do after reading that letter. I just hope she can remain composed despite her anger.’","’If she recklessly returns to Shu State and confronts Black Tooth and his men directly, she’ll just ruin everything.’","’At least let me get my hands on that three hundred thousand silver coins before she makes a move.’","Musing on this, Chen Yi tilted his bamboo hat up slightly to look at the overcast night sky, a faint smile touching his lips.","’After all, there’s still Xiao Dongchen to deal with...’","Just then, the sound of a few gong strikes echoed through Chuansi Street.","Midnight—","[Daily Intel - Profound-rank Top Grade: At 10:45 PM, a Hidden Guard will receive a secret letter at the tailor shop in the West Market. A small Opportunity may be gained.]","’A secret letter?’","’A letter arriving at this hour...’","’It must be the reply to the letter that Lady Tiger and the others sent.’","Chen Yi raised an eyebrow slightly, made a mental note of the matter, and returned to Spring Lotus Garden without delay.","After changing his clothes, he rested for a moment before sitting cross-legged on his bed to begin his Cultivation of the Four Symbols Skill.","At last, his mind could relax completely.","’Now, we’ll see if Madame can keep her composure.’"]},{"number":204,"title":"Chapter 204 - 186: Oops, Something Dropped","paragraphs":["While Chen Yi was immersed in his Cultivation.","Liu Lang, having changed his attire, once again slipped into the Liu Family’s residence on Kangning Street and headed straight for the western courtyard.","—Where Liu Zhaoxue was staying.","This time, Liu Lang was even more cautious than before.","This was not only due to Chen Yi’s warning and Liu Wen’s presence, but also because he was wary of the Five Poison Sect.","Although the Five Poison Sect had not been seen in the Jianghu for a long time, rumors held that their methods were utterly ruthless.","Their sinister Poison Skills and Poisons, in particular, were still infamous throughout the Jianghu.","Once he sensed that the residence was silent, Liu Lang confirmed there were no guards nearby and no movement from the wooden building. Only then did he silently approach the side of the structure.","After concealing himself in a corner, he pressed his ear to the wall, listening intently to the sounds within.","The very first sentence he heard from inside made his eyes fly open.","’This Liu Zhaoxue’s ambition... is staggering!’","He heard Liu Zhaoxue’s voice coming from within, her tone tinged with ice.","\"...As long as there is the slightest chance, I will not give up on the position of Liu Family Patriarch.\"","Then, he heard the person from the Five Poison Sect laugh and say, \"It’s a good thing you’re ambitious, Miss Zhaoxue.\"","\"If you weren’t, why would my Five Poison Sect have traveled thousands of miles to get here? Especially to Shu State, a place of painful memories for us.\"","\"I almost forgot. Your Five Poison Sect was nearly wiped out by the Mountain Race. Aren’t you afraid that Granny Shan will discover you operating here?\"","The member of the Five Poison Sect sneered. \"Why should we be?\"","\"The Mountain Race has sided with the Xiao Family. They can barely protect themselves as it is.\"","\"Even if my Five Poison Sect does nothing, others will surely move against them.\"","Liu Zhaoxue asked, sounding somewhat surprised, \"You know about the Xiao Family’s situation?\"","The member of the Five Poison Sect replied, \"How could we not?\"","\"With the Old Marquis gravely ill and the Young Master still a child, the Dingyuan Army is propped up by Xiao Jinghong alone. Plenty of people are plotting against the Xiao Family.\"","\"Your Jing State Liu Family is no different. Sending Liu Wen to marry Xiao Wan’er—isn’t that just a ploy to take over what’s theirs?\"","Liu Zhaoxue grunted in agreement. \"That’s true.\"","\"The Xiao Family is besieged on all fronts. Even the Imperial Court is making things difficult for them here. It’s inevitable that other Noble Families will try to take advantage.\"","She paused, then continued, \"But we’re getting sidetracked.\"","\"Yan Fusha, let’s talk about how your Five Poison Sect plans to help me achieve my goal.\"","\"Of course...\"","’Yan Fusha?’","Liu Lang racked his brain for a moment. Certain he’d never heard that name in the Jianghu, he calmed himself and continued to eavesdrop.","He then heard the one called Yan Fusha from the Five Poison Sect speak in fragmented sentences, their voice intentionally lowered.","\"To achieve your goal, Liu Wen must die. And your eldest brother...\"","\"If we handle it correctly, framing the Xiao Family for Liu Wen’s death won’t be difficult.\"","\"Absolutely not! My second brother is not Liu Jing. If he dies in Shu State, the family will investigate this to the bitter end!\"","\"You can rest assured, Miss Zhaoxue. I have my own plans for this...\"","Liu Lang arched an eyebrow, thinking to himself, ’This woman is vicious.’","He knew Chen Yi also wanted Liu Wen dead, but Chen Yi and Liu Wen were on opposing sides. Their animosity was to be expected.","But for Liu Zhaoxue to plot the murder of her own brother just for the position of Patriarch... that was truly ruthless.","’No wonder the boss dangled the position of Liu Family Patriarch to bait Liu Wen.’","’Looks like they both have the same idea.’","After muttering a few more thoughts to himself, Liu Lang quietly slipped away.","He had accomplished his goal for the trip.","There was no need to listen to the finer details of the murder plot Yan Fusha and Liu Zhaoxue were hatching.","As he left the rear courtyard, he was about to head back to the house on Chuansi Street to see if the boss had left, but he overheard a conversation nearby.","\"...Liu Wu? The Second Young Master’s man? I’ve never heard of him.\"","\"Think again. He’s handsome, with a slender build, and he’s highly skilled in the Medical Dao.\"","\"Never heard of him. Maybe he’s the disciple of some Saint Hand from Xinglin Hall. It would be normal for us not to have any contact with someone like that.\"","’Liu Wu?’","A thought struck Liu Lang. He silently moved to conceal himself behind the two speakers.","Seeing they were both Guards wearing the blue attire of the Liu Family, he arched an eyebrow.","’The boss was right. Black Tooth came to the Liu Family to ask about him.’","After a moment of thought, a plan formed in Liu Lang’s mind, and a flicker of amusement crossed his eyes.","’I can’t let the boss’s cover be blown, no matter what.’","...","「Just after three in the morning.」","Amidst the gloomy, rainy weather, the sky remained dark.","With the rain obscuring the view, most early risers had to rely on candlelight to see their surroundings.","It was somewhat better inside the various state and county seats, where lanterns that burned year-round lit the streets and alleys.","But nearly a thousand li from Shu State Prefecture City, in the dense forest where Xiao Jinghong and the Mountain Race had established the \"Wu Mountain Mutual Market,\" visibility was significantly lower.","Fortunately, torches had been lit around the foundations of the various shops.","At least the interior of the Mutual Market had some light.","Early in the morning, men dressed in short tunics and trousers, wearing bamboo hats, emerged from the wooden cabins in small groups. At the foreman’s call, they lined up to receive their breakfast.","Despite the rainy weather, the Mutual Market was a project of great importance, and both the Xiao Family and the Mountain Race had exacting standards.","—Two streets of shops, one street of warehouses, and five hundred residences had to be built within three months.","The schedule was extremely tight.","Thus, after breakfast, these dark-skinned men all set to work.","Before long, the entire site selected for the Wu Mountain Mutual Market was filled with a cacophony of sounds. The scene could only be described as bustling with feverish activity.","And while the laborers toiled, Xiao Jinghong was not idle.","She was dressed as impeccably as ever, though her attire was simple and practical: just a single long, blue robe.","Aside from the half-armor mask on her face, she wore no other adornments.","She looked just like a wandering knight from the Jianghu.","Compared to her, Su Zhenyue, in her long skirt, looked far more feminine."]},{"number":205,"title":"Chapter 205 - 186: Oops, Something Dropped (Part 2)","paragraphs":["The two of them finished their breakfast.","Xiao Jinghong glanced at the sky outside the window and mused, \"The envoys from the Mountain Race are coming today. I need you to accompany them in my place to inspect the construction progress of the Mutual Market.\"","Su Zhenyue nodded in acknowledgment, then placed the booklet she was holding in front of her.","\"General, these are letters that just arrived from the Garrison Commanders of the Three Towns. They all mention the status of the New Army’s training.\"","Xiao Jinghong opened one and glanced at it, then ordered, \"Send a unified reply. Tell them to be prepared. I will inspect the New Army of the Three Towns again after the Mid-Autumn Festival.\"","She paused, then asked, \"Has there been any reply from the Commandant’s Office?\"","Su Zhenyue said, \"No news yet.\"","Xiao Jinghong gave a slight nod, a sharp glint flashing in her eyes as she gazed at the rain-streaked window.","\"It’s right for the Three Towns to pay their grain tax, but a ten percent tax is excessive.\"","\"If the Commandant’s Office does nothing again this time, then they can’t blame me for paying them a visit.\"","Su Zhenyue paused, looking at her expression before saying hesitantly, \"The Old Marquis sent a message before, stating that he would handle this matter.\"","Xiao Jinghong shot her a glance and said flatly, \"Those are two separate matters.\"","\"It’s true the Governor’s Office is pressuring the Three Towns because of the conflict between the Xiao and Liu Families. But that doesn’t mean the Commandant’s Office gets to stay out of it.\"","\"Before, when the summer harvest hadn’t arrived and grain was scarce, the Commandant’s Office couldn’t secure an allocation from the Imperial Court. I don’t blame them for that.\"","\"After all, that was the will of the Holy Emperor and the Nine Ministers.\"","\"But now the storehouses of the Three Towns are full. Forcing them to spit out what’s already in their mouths is not something the Commandant’s Office can talk its way out of.\"","Hearing this, Su Zhenyue understood her decision and didn’t try to persuade her further.","She then took out three other booklets. Just as she was about to speak, a series of JINGLES grew louder as they approached from a distance.","The next moment, the door to their wooden cabin was pushed open.","A figure stood in the doorway. It was Pei Guanli, who had braved the wind and rain all the way from Shu State Prefecture City.","She looked at the two women inside, her round face full of smiles, and hopped into the cabin on her fair, bare feet.","\"Sister Jinghong, Sister Zhenyue! It’s been so long. Did you miss me?\"","Xiao Jinghong looked her over, asking with some surprise, \"Why are you back?\"","\"I came back to see... Ah Ma and the others.\"","Pei Guanli, managing not to forget Chen Yi’s instructions, sat down. Her eyes darted around before she said:","\"It’s almost the Mid-Autumn Festival, so I brought lots and lots... lots of things for Ah Ma and the other people in the clan.\"","Seeing how earnest she seemed, Xiao Jinghong didn’t think much of it and nodded. \"In that case, I’ll have someone escort you back to the Mountain Race later.\"","Pei Guanli waved her hands. \"No, no...\"","\"Sister Wan’er already prepared a carriage for me. I’ll just have them go back with me.\"","Then, pretending to have just remembered something, she reached into her top and began to rummage around.","\"Oh, right! Sister Wan’er asked me to bring a letter for you, Sister Jinghong.\"","\"And one from brother-in-law.\"","Xiao Jinghong saw her shameless act, and the corners of her mouth twitched slightly.","\"You kept the letters in your clothes?\"","Pei Guanli let out a sound of affirmation. As she pulled all the letters out, she replied:","\"Well, it’s been raining this whole time, hasn’t it? I was worried the letters would get wet.\"","The truth was, she was only worried about the letter Chen Yi had entrusted her with getting wet, so she had simply decided to carry all of them on her person.","And to make sure Xiao Jinghong would see that specific letter first, Pei Guanli had intentionally placed it on top of the pile.","After pulling them out, she didn’t just toss them on the table in front of Xiao Jinghong. Instead, she pretended to lose her grip, letting that one piece of paper fall to the floor.","\"Oops, what fell?\"","Pei Guanli bent down to pick it up, a hint of a smile flashing in her bright eyes. Then she feigned surprise and said:","\"Huh? This letter... it doesn’t look like it’s from brother-in-law and the others.\"","Xiao Jinghong and Su Zhenyue exchanged a glance. It was obvious from her over-the-top act that something fishy was going on.","Immediately, Xiao Jinghong held out her hand. \"Give it to me.\"","Pei Guanli, of course, first handed over the two letters in her hand. Then she unfolded the separate piece of paper and said:","\"Let me see first. Maybe it’s a poem brother-in-law wrote especially for me.\"","Before she could make out the familiar characters, the letter was in Xiao Jinghong’s hand.","Pei Guanli immediately pouted and whined, \"Sister Jinghong, how could you?\"","But while she said that, her eyes were fixed on Xiao Jinghong without blinking, and she thought to herself:","’She’s frowning. Hehe.’","’Shocked... why isn’t she shocked?’","’She’s looking over, she’s looking over! Sister Jinghong is about to ask me something.’","’Go on, ask away. Brother-in-law already told me what to do. There’s no way I’ll mess this up.’","But as well as the Tiger Girl had planned, Xiao Jinghong’s first words nearly made her jump out of her seat.","\"Confess. Did you write this letter?\"","\"Pei Guanli, military matters are no joke. If you don’t explain yourself clearly, I’ll have you disciplined today!\"","\"Huh?\"","Pei Guanli was so startled she almost leaped to her feet.","Fortunately, she had rehearsed this dozens of times on the way here, so she managed to appear somewhat calm in the face of the crisis.","She then looked at Xiao Jinghong with a feigned expression of confusion. \"What do you mean, *I* wrote it?\"","\"Sister Jinghong, I’m already here in person. Why would I need to write a letter?\"","\"Honestly! I was just being nice and delivering a letter for you on my way, and you want to have me disciplined...\"","\"You just wait. I’m going to go tattle to Ah Ma later. Hmph.\"","Xiao Jinghong stared at her for a long time, her brow slightly furrowed. \"You really didn’t write it?\" she asked.","\"I don’t even know what’s written on it...\"","A smile spread across Pei Guanli’s face as she leaned in closer. \"Let me see what’s written on it. What’s got you so tense?\"","\"It’s not really a poem from brother-in-law to me, is it? Is it even better than the poems he writes for you?\"","Xiao Jinghong placed a hand on her head to stop her, thought for a moment, then passed the letter to Su Zhenyue beside her. \"Take a look.\""]},{"number":206,"title":"Chapter 206 - 186: Oops, Something Dropped","paragraphs":["Su Zhenyue took it and glanced at it. Her eyes widened, and she shot to her feet, exclaiming in anger,","\"The nerve of these people!\"","As soon as she spoke, Su Zhenyue turned to the protesting Pei Guanli and asked with a grave expression,","\"Miss Pei, are you certain you didn’t write this letter?\"","\"I already told you I didn’t.\"","\"Then how did it end up on you?\"","\"I, I don’t know...\"","No matter how Xiao Jinghong and Su Zhenyue interrogated her, Pei Guanli held fast to Chen Yi’s instructions and adamantly denied ever having seen the letter.","After a long moment.","Xiao Jinghong let her go, took the letter again, and read it over carefully twice more before she finally spoke.","\"I’ll believe you for now.\"","\"But if I find out later that you wrote this, I won’t spare you, even if Granny Shan herself is protecting you!\"","Pei Guanli pouted and mumbled an \"oh,\" grumbling to herself.","’How strange.’","’This isn’t going how I imagined.’","’Sister Jinghong wasn’t alarmed by the letter, and she didn’t rush out the door. She actually interrogated me first...’","’Jerk.’","At this point, however, Xiao Jinghong and Su Zhenyue clearly had no time for her.","After a moment of silence.","Su Zhenyue couldn’t help but speak up. \"General, when the Sword Madman left, he said he wanted to repay you for sparing his life. Could it be...\"","Xiao Jinghong, of course, hadn’t forgotten. She gave a slight nod. \"It’s better to believe it than to dismiss it.\"","\"What are your plans, General? Should I send word to the Three Towns now?\"","\"That won’t be necessary.\"","\"You...\"","Before Su Zhenyue could say more, Xiao Jinghong had already stood up and announced, \"I’ll go myself.\"","\"The letter doesn’t specify who is hiding among the troops in the Three Towns, which means we can’t rule out the three garrison commanders as suspects. I must confirm this myself before I can make the necessary arrangements.\"","\"While I’m gone, you’ll take my place here. Remember to maintain my identity; don’t let anyone realize I’ve left.\"","At this point, she was suspicious of everyone in the Three Towns.","She didn’t even plan to send word to the Xiao Mansion, for fear of tipping off her quarry.","Su Zhenyue knew the matter was urgent, so she naturally didn’t try to talk her out of it.","However, when she saw Pei Guanli pouting to the side, she couldn’t help but ask, \"What about her?\"","Xiao Jinghong fastened a long sword to her waist as she gave her instructions.","\"Her brother is coming today. Once he’s finished inspecting the progress at the Mutual Market, have her go back to the Mountain Race with him.\"","Pei Guanli shook her head instinctively. \"I don’t want to. I want to go to Shu State to find my brother-in-law.\"","\"Hm? Didn’t you just say you wanted to go back to the Mountain Race for the Mid-Autumn Festival?\"","Hearing this, Xiao Jinghong frowned at her. Her suspicions flared up again as she asked in a stern voice,","\"I’ll ask you one last time: do you know what is in that letter?\"","Feeling the terrifying force of her presence, Pei Guanli flinched and said with her head down,","\"I... I meant I’d go find my brother-in-law *after* the Mid-Autumn Festival.\"","Xiao Jinghong no longer believed her.","After staring at her for another moment, Xiao Jinghong snorted. \"When I get back, I’ll make you tell the truth!\"","Before her voice had even faded, she tucked the letter from the table into her sleeve. Her body blurred into a pale shadow that shot out of the wooden cabin and vanished.","Once she sensed that all was quiet,","Pei Guanli finally dared to lift her head. Her eyes darted around for a moment before meeting Su Zhenyue’s gaze.","Feeling a bit of relief, she couldn’t help but put on a pitiful expression and ask,","\"Sister Zhenyue, what in the world did that letter say? Why did it make you and Sister Jinghong so tense?\"","Su Zhenyue gave her a long, hard look. Without a word, she stood up, found a set of Xiao Jinghong’s clothes, and changed into them.","Seeing this, Pei Guanli pouted but didn’t dare say anything more.","But a troubled expression couldn’t help but cross her face.","’What should I do, brother-in-law? I think I blew my cover.’","’Sister Jinghong isn’t really going to interrogate me, is she?’","’Nooo, I’m scared of pain...’","Fortunately, Pei Guanli was resourceful enough to come up with a plan—of sorts.","’If worst comes to worst, I’ll just go beg Ah Ma to help me.’","’Hmph, hmph. With how clever Ah Ma is, she’ll surely know how to help me avoid Sister Jinghong’s interrogation.’","It was a good thing Granny Shan didn’t know her own granddaughter considered her \"cunning,\" otherwise...","...the Mountain Race’s clan rules would probably teach the Tiger Girl the true meaning of pain.","...","「Shu State. Dingyuan Marquis’s Mansion. Spring Lotus Garden.」","Of course, Chen Yi had no idea that Xiao Jinghong had seen through the Tiger Girl’s odd behavior.","After waking up bright and early, he took Xiao Wuge and Xiaodie to Jiaxing Garden for breakfast.","However, it was not a peaceful breakfast.","It wasn’t because of any \"lecturing\" from Xiao Wan’er. Rather, in the time it took them to eat, four separate calling cards had already been delivered.","That didn’t even include the verbal messages from the people of the Second and Third Households.","It left Chen Yi feeling awkward, neither able to stay nor leave. All in all, he felt bad about letting Xiao Wan’er take the heat for him.","Xiao Wan’er, on the other hand, acted as if everything was normal.","She accepted the calling cards as a matter of course.","Whether it was visitors from the Second or Third Households, or from other side branches of the family, she met with them all herself.","Even with Chen Yi sitting right beside her, Xiao Wan’er never had him give a definite answer or even asked for his opinion.","After breakfast, as Juan’er, Cui’er, Xiaodie, and the others cleared the table, Xiao Wan’er finally smiled and said,","\"Most of the people visiting now are close to the Mansion, so it wouldn’t be right to refuse them outright. I might as well let them come for a visit, and we can ask how they’ve been.\"","Chen Yi saw that she spoke of it lightly, but he was well aware that he was the reason for all this trouble.","After a moment’s thought, he promised again, \"I’ll resolve this matter as soon as possible.\"","The visitors now were people close to the Xiao Family, but it was inevitable that less-friendly faces would appear later.","He couldn’t keep letting Xiao Wan’er put on a false smile to entertain those people.","Xiao Wan’er accepted his promise, nodding with a smile before changing the subject.","\"It’s been a few days since that Boss Chen submitted his proposal. I’ve thought about it carefully, and I believe we should have him come so I can convey Grandfather’s intentions to him.\"","\"If you have some free time today, perhaps you could make a trip to Hundred Herbs Hall for me and ask if Boss Chen is still in Shu State.\"","Chen Yi’s interest was piqued. He asked, \"You’re not going to wait for word from the Old Master?\"","\"I don’t think Boss Chen will be a problem.\"","\"Even if he does turn out to be a problem, we’re only beginning the preparations now. It won’t affect our subsequent arrangements.\"","\"In that case, I’ll make a trip to Hundred Herbs Hall later.\"","’After all, Boss Chen most certainly wasn’t in Shu State.’"]},{"number":207,"title":"Chapter 207 - 187: You Are a Genius","paragraphs":["Xiao Wan’er’s words reminded Chen Yi.","Now that the old master had agreed to the \"Hundred Herbs Hall Expansion Charter,\" he really did need to start preparing.","After all, if he wanted to expand the Hundred Herbs Hall across all the prefectures and counties of Shu State, he needed to get a handle on many things beforehand: store locations, local customs, Noble Families, and other regional powers.","Even with the Xiao Family’s backing, the grunt work still had to be done by the people from Hundred Herbs Hall.","So, he would have to ship out either Wang Ji or Yan Sea.","Xiao Wan’er, oblivious to his thoughts, finished her instructions and began preparations to receive the day’s guests.","Of course, she was only responsible for outlining what needed to be done; Shen Huatang, along with Cui’er and Juan’er, would handle the actual tasks.","In a way, she and Chen Yi were quite in sync. Both were the type to be ’hands-off managers’.","However, there was someone in Jiaxing Garden with even more free time than Chen Yi and Xiao Wan’er: Shen Huatang’s senior martial sister, Xie Tingyun.","Ever since arriving at the Xiao Family estate, the renowned \"Fairy Tingyun\" of the Jianghu had completely transformed into \"Tingyun the Foodie.\"","Besides her duties of standing night watch and protecting Xiao Wan’er, she spent most of her time each day looking for things to eat.","To say nothing of other delicacies, she alone drank more than half of the various tea beverages delivered from the Xiao Family Medicine Hall.","She was especially fond of the sweet and sour Mushroom Tea and was never without it—two bottles in the morning, two in the afternoon, and another two at night.","Aside from eating and drinking, she was never seen practicing her Martial Arts Cultivation.","At least, Chen Yi had never seen her do so, nor had he heard any related sounds or talk.","More often than not, what he heard was Shen Huatang \"disciplining\" Xie Tingyun.","Things like, \"Senior Sister, if you keep this up, you’re going back to the Sect,\" or \"Senior Sister, if you don’t stop, I’m telling Master.\"","Xie Tingyun let these words go in one ear and out the other. She would always agree but never change, continuing to do as she pleased.","’It was a real mystery how she’d managed to cultivate to the Fourth Grade Realm.’","Chen Yi, of course, didn’t press the issue, simply laughing it off.","None of it really mattered. As long as Xie Tingyun could protect Xiao Wan’er, everything else was a trivial detail.","It seemed, however, that Xie Tingyun also felt a little bad about her lazy behavior.","While Xiao Wan’er was busy giving instructions to Shen Huatang and the others, she took the initiative to approach him, speaking in a rather mysterious tone.","\"Young Master, um, there’s something I’d like to ask your advice about.\"","Chen Yi raised an eyebrow, giving her a surprised look. \"Go on,\" he said.","\"Straight to the point, I like it,\" Xie Tingyun said, then lowered her voice to ask,","\"Young Master, do you think... do you think that Hundred Herbs Hall could open a branch at the foot of Tian Mountain?\"","\"...That’s what you wanted to ask?\"","Chen Yi instantly tossed aside his earlier assumption that she was looking for something to do.","Xie Tingyun blinked and grunted in affirmation.","\"Tian Mountain is pretty far from Shu State, I know, and it’s not very populated... But, you’re a learned man. You know a lot. Is there a way?\"","Chen Yi was exasperated. \"This has nothing to do with me being a scholar. You said it yourself—there’s almost no one near Tian Mountain. If Hundred Herbs Hall opens a branch there, who are our customers going to be?\"","\"Me! And the rest of the Celestial Sect.\"","Perhaps sensing that wasn’t a very convincing number, Xie Tingyun added, \"And we get a lot of visitors from other places, too.\"","\"My apologies, Fairy Tingyun. I can’t think of a solution. You’ll have to ask someone more capable.\"","’Hundred Herbs Hall isn’t a charity, after all.’","Even if the goal was to expand all across the land, they still had to prioritize.","A place like the Western State, where Tian Mountain was located, was not only sparsely populated but also had poor transportation. He’d have to be a fool to send Wang Ji to open a Hundred Herbs Hall there.","With the same amount of effort, he could open several more branches in Jiao State or Jiangnan Prefecture and make a fortune.","But Xie Tingyun wasn’t ready to give up.","\"Young Master, please, could you ask Shopkeeper Wang for me? Or that Boss Chen Yu? I’m being completely serious—I want to invite Hundred Herbs Hall to open a branch at Tian Mountain.\"","\"Besides, I... *we* won’t let Hundred Herbs Hall make the trip for nothing. There are plenty of benefits.\"","Chen Yi gave her a wry smile. \"Oh? Let’s hear them. What kind of benefits?\"","’He hadn’t expected Xie Tingyun to be this fond of the tea beverages.’","’So fond she’d be this persistent.’","’He certainly didn’t mind hearing what terms this devoted tea enthusiast was prepared to offer.’","Xie Tingyun paused. She shot a furtive glance at Shen Huatang, and seeing that her junior sister wasn’t paying attention, she leaned in closer and whispered:","\"The Celestial Sect can act as guards for Hundred Herbs Hall.\"","\"I remember the last time I visited, Shopkeeper Wang hired a few Wandering Martial Artists. Compared to them, the disciples of our Celestial Sect are much stronger.\"","At her words, Chen Yi froze for a second. After a moment of thought, he looked at her with a peculiar expression.","’He had to admit, that was an offer he couldn’t refuse.’","For one thing, just as Xie Tingyun said, the guards Wang Ji had hired couldn’t compare to the disciples of the Celestial Sect in either strength or reputation.","For another, as Hundred Herbs Hall expanded, all the new branches in the various prefectures and counties would need guards.","This was especially true for escorting shipments of the core medicinal ingredients for the tea recipes, which required powerful experts to ensure their safety.","If they could enlist the help of the Celestial Sect’s disciples, it would be a huge boon for Hundred Herbs Hall.","And the price was merely opening one branch that was guaranteed to lose money.","But even if the entire Celestial Sect drank to their hearts’ content, how much silver could they possibly lose in a year?","Chen Yi did a quick mental calculation and arrived at a staggering figure—an estimated annual loss of one thousand taels of silver.","If the Celestial Sect provided a rent-free building, that number would be cut in half.","’Hmm... how should I put this?’","’He had never seen such a profitable deal in his life.’","Seeing him stay silent, Xie Tingyun grew anxious. \"Young Master, what’s with that look? Dammit... I mean, are my terms not good?\""]},{"number":208,"title":"Chapter 208 - 187: You Are a Genius (Part 2)","paragraphs":["’No, quite the opposite.’","’This deal is too good.’","’You’re a business genius, Fairy Tingyun.’","Thinking this, Chen Yi smiled and nodded. \"I’ll ask for you shortly. I imagine... Boss Chen and Shopkeeper Wang won’t refuse.\"","Xie Tingyun’s expression relaxed. She smiled and cupped her fists. \"Thank you, Second Son-in-law. In that case, I won’t disturb you any longer.\"","Watching her walk away with a light spring in her step, Chen Yi felt a private amusement, but also an unavoidable twinge of guilt.","’Ahem, it’s not like I wanted this to happen.’","’But the senior disciple of the Celestial Sect just had to deliver herself right to my doorstep...’","After saying a few words to Xiao Wan’er, Chen Yi took Xiao Wuge and Xiaodie back to the Spring Lotus Garden first.","After a short rest, he opened an oil-paper umbrella and headed to the West Market’s Hundred Herbs Hall alone.","The rain wasn’t heavy, but it wasn’t light either.","The sound of falling rain filled the Xiao Mansion, naturally mixed with the whispers of servants and Personal Guard Armored Warriors.","It was all mostly trivial matters: someone from the Second Branch had argued with someone from some courtyard, or some master or madam from the Third Branch had bickered last night, and so on.","Some of the servants who saw him pass by steered the conversation toward him, saying things like, \"The Second Son-in-law is really something now,\" or \"Most of the recent visitors to the mansion have been for the Second Son-in-law.\"","Regardless of their tone or wording, at least Chen Yi’s reputation in the mansion was much better than before.","He made his way to the front courtyard.","He scanned the area and saw Liu Si’er and Ge the Third were both present, so he couldn’t help but go over to chat and joke with them for a bit.","\"Greetings, Second Son-in-law.\"","Chen Yi sized them up and asked with a smile, \"Brother Si, have your injuries healed?\"","Liu Si’er replied, \"Thanks to the First Miss, after taking the medicine prescribed by the Medicine Hall’s Physician, I was mostly recovered in less than ten days.\"","\"I recall the person who injured you hasn’t been caught yet?\"","\"...I’ll head to the Imprisonment Department later to ask again.\"","Ge the Third, who was standing beside them, chimed in with a snort, \"That scoundrel is far too bold. Once he’s caught, we have to throw him into the Punishment Hall for a proper ’serving’.\"","Chen Yi smiled. \"It’s been so long without any news. I reckon the Imprisonment Department hasn’t found any clues either.\"","\"But since he injured one of our mansion’s own, he’ll be caught eventually.\"","He showed no awareness of being the \"culprit\" himself, speaking of his own actions without the slightest hesitation.","Liu Si’er nodded. \"The Second Son-in-law is right. He won’t get away.\"","After a pause, he asked, \"Are you leaving the mansion, Second Son-in-law? Do you need me to prepare a carriage?\"","Chen Yi waved his hand. \"I’m just heading to the Hundred Herbs Hall... mm. I’ve been cooped up in the mansion for a few days, so it’s a good chance to get out and stretch my legs.\"","Hearing this, Ge the Third asked in a low voice, \"I heard the Marquis has decided to deepen the cooperation between the Medicine Hall and the Hundred Herbs Hall?\"","Chen Yi glanced at him and said impassively, \"The First Miss has always been in charge of the Medicine Hall’s business. I’m not too clear on the details.\"","’If I remember correctly, not many people know about this.’","’Previously, both Xiao Wan’er and the Old Master had warned not to let this news spread. So how did Ge the Third find out?’","Ge the Third seemed to realize he had let something slip. He gave a sheepish laugh and said no more.","Chen Yi, for his part, didn’t press the matter, merely making a mental note of it.","’If news is getting out, it means there are still Hidden Guards planted around Xiao Wan’er, the Old Master, or the Hundred Herbs Hall.’","’It was enough to make him wary.’","After a bit more small talk, Chen Yi took his leave and headed straight for the West Market.","Watching him walk away, Liu Si’er asked in a low voice, \"Third, how did you know the mansion was going to deepen its cooperation with the Hundred Herbs Hall?\"","Ge the Third couldn’t possibly reveal his source, so he answered vaguely, \"I just heard some people talking.\"","\"Is that so?\"","\"But it makes sense. The Medicine Hall has earned a lot of silver coins selling those tea drinks through the Hundred Herbs Hall. It’s only natural the Marquis would want to work with them more.\"","\"I guess so...\"","Chen Yi paid no mind to the \"small talk\" between Ge the Third and Liu Si’er.","’Two Hidden Guards hiding among the Xiao Family’s Personal Guard haven’t exposed their identities to each other. They couldn’t reveal any truly secret information anyway.’","’What he was concerned about was when Ge the Third, the \"Hawk,\" would make a move on the Three Towns’ summer grain.’","’Or rather, when Lady Tiger Lou Yuxue and Gray Wolf Xiao Dongchen would order him to act.’","’But on second thought, Chen Yi wasn’t too worried.’","’He had already made contact with Black Tooth using his \"Liu Wu\" identity.’","’Before they made their move, that band of Evil Demons would surely notify him.’","’As long as it’s not tonight, the rest of the time... it shouldn’t be a problem.’","...","Chen Yi spent the entire morning at the Hundred Herbs Hall.","He was mainly there to discuss future expansion plans with Wang Ji.","After some deliberation, they decided to have Yan Sea take a team to tour the various counties of Shu State to understand the local situation and take notes.","For one, Yan Sea’s name wasn’t well-known, unlike Wang Ji, who attracted attention as the Shopkeeper of the Hundred Herbs Hall.","For another, with Wang Ji remaining in the Prefecture City, he could provide cover for Chen Yi, preventing the Xiao Family from being unable to find \"Chen Yu\" and affecting future business for the Hundred Herbs Hall.","Once the official business was concluded, Chen Yi gave another small order.","\"Buy the few storefronts and residences surrounding the tailor shop in the West Market. Tell everyone they’re warehouses for the Hundred Herbs Hall.\"","Wang Ji didn’t ask any questions and nodded in agreement.","Chen Yi had no plans to make a move on the tailor shop for the time being.","’Based on his observations, that tailor shop should be a stronghold for the Hidden Guard in Shu State Prefecture City.’","’Something like a \"liaison station.\"’","’This wasn’t hard to deduce from the fact that Lady Tiger Lou Yuxue and Hawk Ge the Third had met there earlier.’","’Combined with the intelligence for tonight, keeping that tailor shop around would be useful in the future.’","After arranging everything, Chen Yi had lunch at a nearby restaurant and then went to his house on Chuansi Street.","After Zhang Dabao disguised him, he instructed Zhang Dabao to summon Liu Lang.","While waiting, he didn’t stay idle. He practiced several sets of Techniques right there in the house.","His Martial Arts Fist, Step, and spear techniques had all reached the Great Success Realm, but he had only cultivated his Mountain Shattering Fist and Hundred Flowers Palm to Mastery Level Perfection."]},{"number":209,"title":"Chapter 209 - 187: You Are a Genius","paragraphs":["His two Body and Footwork Techniques and the Dragon-Falling Spear Technique still had room for improvement.","Especially the Dragon-Falling Spear.","Every time he practiced it, it would stir the Heaven and Earth Spiritual Qi and layer his Dao Intent, creating quite a commotion.","Because Xie Tingyun and Shen Huatang were around, he hadn’t practiced this Spear Technique in a long time.","Of course, to avoid any unnecessary trouble, Chen Yi didn’t use the Five-section Spear at this moment either.","He only practiced the Meteor Butterfly Step and the Wandering Dragon and Phoenix Step Technique in the main hall, just to have something to do.","「About an hour later.」","Liu Lang hurried over, and the moment he saw him, he said with a wide smile:","\"Boss, you’re truly clairvoyant.\"","Chen Yi raised an eyebrow slightly and asked, \"Are the Five Poison Sect and Liu Zhaoxue plotting something big?\"","\"More than that.\"","\"When I went over last night, on top of overhearing Yan Fusha—the one from the Five Poison Sect—discussing the plot to murder Liu Wen with Liu Zhaoxue, I also ran into someone from Black Tooth.\"","\"Oh? Tell me the details.\"","After Liu Lang finished speaking, Chen Yi was amused as well.","\"I’ll credit you for this.\"","It turned out that last night, after Liu Lang ran into the person from Black Tooth sent to confirm Chen Yi’s identity, he had disguised himself as a Liu Family Guard and told the man a few things about \"Liu Wu.\"","He said that Liu Wu had studied under the Medical Saint Hand of Xinglin Hall and had once cured the illness of a very important person.","He also claimed that Liu Wu had astounding talent in the Martial Arts, achieving Minor Success in the Fist Dao before he was even twenty.","All in all, he sent the man back with that information.","Basically, as long as Black Tooth and Lou Yuxue don’t go to the Jing State Liu Family, his \"Liu Wu\" identity is unlikely to be exposed.","Liu Lang patted the long blade at his waist and said, \"Can’t let the boss give me a fine blade for nothing.\"","Chen Yi smiled, but his mind was on Liu Zhaoxue and the Five Poison Sect.","He had originally thought that the competition for the Patriarch position among the direct descendants of this generation’s Liu Family would have rules against taking lives.","Now it seemed both Liu Wen and Liu Zhaoxue were more ruthless than he had anticipated.","\"Plotting to murder her own brother... Liu Zhaoxue is the more vicious one.\"","Hearing his words, Liu Lang nodded in agreement. \"She’s ruthless, alright.\"","\"Having the Five Poison Sect kill Liu Wen and frame the Xiao Family, all while she hides in the shadows... you have to admit it’s a venomous plan.\"","At this point, he glanced at Chen Yi’s expression and couldn’t help but ask:","\"Boss, what are you planning to do?\"","\"Nothing.\"","\"Huh?\"","\"What ’huh’? It’s perfect to let the dogs fight it out. Saves us from getting our hands dirty.\"","Chen Yi shot him a glance and said coolly, \"Besides, I’m not a bloodthirsty person.\"","Originally, he had only planned to set a trap for Liu Wen, giving the Xiao Family a reason to make a move.","But how things developed after that...","In other words, whether Liu Wen lived or died would depend on the outcome of the struggle between the Old Patriarch and the Liu Family.","But now...","After trapping Liu Wen, he didn’t mind giving this Liu Zhaoxue a little push.","As long as the blame for Liu Wen’s death didn’t fall on the Xiao Family, this affair would surely stir up internal strife within the Liu Family.","After a moment of thought.","Chen Yi instructed, \"Tonight, after you’ve visited the Liu Family’s estate, go to the Spring Rain Building and ask about Black Tooth’s progress.\"","Liu Lang nodded in acknowledgment, a slight smile appearing on his face. \"Boss, if you don’t mind me saying something I probably shouldn’t...\"","\"If word of what you’re doing gets out, the Bright Moon Building will definitely not let you off the hook.\"","Chen Yi glanced at him. \"They won’t let *us* off the hook.\"","\"...That promise I made to do thirty things for you... it was indeed a bit shortsighted.\"","Outsiders might not know the true nature of the Bright Moon Building, but Liu Lang, who had operated within its circles, was naturally aware of some of its secrets.","Besides Black Tooth, the Bright Moon Building also had twelve Elders, each responsible for one of Great Wei’s Nine States and Three Prefectures, and their strength had all reached the Upper Three Grades Realm.","Furthermore, above them were four Protectors and the enigmatic Master of the Building.","This alone surpassed the strength of over ninety percent of the sects and holy lands in Great Wei.","Add to that the various Jianghu People who held Bright Moon Building Identity Tokens, and their power was far beyond what an ordinary person could provoke.","If the Bright Moon Building truly discovered what the two of them were up to, they would face endless trouble in the future, even with the Xiao Family’s protection.","Liu Lang knew all this, but he was in too deep to back out now; he could only see it through to the end.","Of course, setting all that aside, he did find what they were doing to be impressively daring.","If word of this got out in the future, it would only make his title, the \"Sword Madman,\" ring even louder.","At the very least, he could say he dared to tweak the Bright Moon Building’s whiskers.","Just as Liu Lang was getting up to leave, Chen Yi added a reminder:","\"If you get any leads from Black Tooth, remember to have Wang Ji inform me. He knows where to find me.\"","\"Alright.\"","After he left, Chen Yi didn’t linger. He removed his disguise and headed straight for the Xiao Family estate.","As the time for Black Tooth and the Lady Tiger’s scheme drew closer, he felt a growing sense of urgency.","’I still need to think this through carefully.’","’Considering the time, Xiao Jinghong should have seen that letter by now.’","’There’s no movement in Shu State City yet... That’s a good thing.’"]},{"number":210,"title":"Chapter 210 - 188: You Can’t Handle It","paragraphs":["Night fell, bringing a slight chill.","The heavy rain showed no signs of stopping.","It poured down relentlessly.","But in the sweltering summers of Shu State, such rain was rather welcome—certainly better than the scorching sun.","Especially when the night wind blew.","Tiny raindrops mixed with the wind, carrying a gentle, moist coolness.","And in the Spring Lotus Garden, the wind also carried the fragrance of purple bamboo, flowers, and other plants.","It was like a perfume gifted by nature, its fresh, sweet scent clinging to the air and one’s clothes.","At this moment, the hour of You was not yet half over.","Chen Yi had already changed into a set of simple black clothes and trousers. They were not the silk brocades he usually wore, but rather a coarse linen whose rough fibers he could feel under his touch.","These were the Night Clothes he had specially asked Wang Ji to prepare.","He had ten sets in total, hidden in a compartment under his bed for his excursions.","The preparations were necessary.","His previous few outings had inevitably left traces on his clothes.","Some clothes, though perfectly dry before, had been soaked by rain; others were torn during fights, and some were stained with the smell of blood.","Even if Xiaodie didn’t ask, she would inevitably notice something was amiss after a while.","Especially the torn clothing Chen Yi had discarded, which had made Xiaodie think a thief had broken into the garden.","If he hadn’t managed to fob her off with an excuse, there might have been Armored Guards patrolling outside the Spring Lotus Garden.","\"If this rain keeps up until the Mid-Autumn Festival... that would be bad.\"","Fully dressed, Chen Yi watched the falling rain outside his window and couldn’t help but feel \"concerned\" for Black Tooth and his men.","If the rain continued, it would be much harder for them to burn the summer grain.","What might have originally required only a few jars of fire oil would now likely need ten or twenty.","Otherwise, with the torrential downpour and the rescue efforts of the soldiers from the Three Towns, it was doubtful all the grain could be burned.","Of course, this was just him idly speculating.","If all went according to plan, Xiao Jinghong would have already set up defenses. If those men dared to make a move, they would have no chance of survival.","With these thoughts, Chen Yi sat by the window, waiting for Xiaodie and Xiao Wuge to fall sound asleep.","It was still early.","He could still hear Xiaodie moving about downstairs, sounding as if she were tidying up a room.","Xiao Wuge, on the other hand, was already in bed, tossing and turning endlessly while muttering a few things under his breath.","\"Etiquette is so tedious. When will Big Sis get rid of the tutor?\"","\"Brother-in-law won’t help me either. This is misery... I want to learn chess, or even practice calligraphy. I don’t want to study etiquette.\"","Perhaps because he wasn’t worried about being overheard, he grumbled on for a while before his voice gradually faded.","Fortunately, they were both simple souls with few worries, so insomnia was not an issue.","Hearing Xiao Wuge’s words, a small smile appeared on Chen Yi’s face.","He couldn’t help but recall seeing Xiao Wuge in Jiaxing Garden after returning from the West Market, bidding farewell to his etiquette tutor.","That was truly the epitome of teacher-student etiquette.","Not only were his movements meticulously precise, but his expression also had to be just right—respectful, dignified, and magnanimous, not one quality lacking.","After all, he had to embody the presence and refinement of a Marquis’s heir.","Forget Xiao Wuge—even Chen Yi, who was well-versed in etiquette, found it all a hassle to watch.","But there was nothing to be done. In the rear courtyard, Xiao Wan’er’s word was law.","When it came to her decisions, especially regarding Xiao Wuge’s upbringing and education, not even the Old Master could easily intervene.","It was the ultimate expression of \"an eldest sister is like a mother.\"","Chen Yi, for his part, would certainly not say something like, \"A passable understanding of etiquette is good enough.\"","He just pretended not to see Xiao Wuge’s pleading gaze and instead turned to say a few words to Xie Tingyun.","He told her that Shopkeeper Wang Ji was very interested in her proposal.","However, he would have to check with the boss, \"Chen Yu,\" before making a final decision.","Xie Tingyun’s face lit up with joy, and she didn’t forget to thank him.","Taking the opportunity, Chen Yi asked a couple more questions.","Such as, \"Which disciples can the Celestial Sect send?\" and \"How many silver coins would be needed each month?\"","He was almost amused to death by Xie Tingyun’s response: \"We get paid for this?\"","If the other disciples of the Celestial Sect heard her say that, they would probably resent their Senior Sister to death.","It turned out that all she had ever wanted was a \"Hundred Herbs Hall,\" and she hadn’t considered anything else.","After Chen Yi gave a simple explanation, he got a clear picture of the Celestial Sect’s situation.","Besides Xie Tingyun and Shen Huatang, the two Sect Leader’s Disciples, there were over ten other members in the Middle Three Grades Realm.","Adding the disciples of her martial uncles and aunts, the number of people who could come down the mountain to serve as guards for the Hundred Herbs Hall should exceed one hundred.","That would be more than enough to handle the initial expansion of the Hundred Herbs Hall.","He waited for about a quarter of an hour.","Once he heard the steady, even breathing of Xiao Wuge and Xiaodie, Chen Yi quietly slipped out of the Spring Lotus Garden.","Tonight’s matter was of great importance and allowed for no mistakes.","Thus, he moved with extreme caution, taking half an hour before finally arriving at the residence on Chuansi Street.","Zhang Dabao, who had long been waiting in the main hall, stepped forward to help him with his disguise and change of clothes without waiting for a command.","They worked in silence, yet with perfect coordination.","In just twenty breaths, Chen Yi’s face was transformed.","Another twenty breaths later, he had changed into a long black robe and donned a black iron mask. His entire presence and aura changed completely.","By candlelight, Chen Yi glanced at his reflection in the copper mirror. After confirming everything was in order, he asked:","\"What’s the status on Yan Sea’s preparations?\"","Zhang Dabao replied while packing up his tools, \"This afternoon, Steward Yan finalized the travel route.\"","\"I hear he plans to first go to Guangyuan County, the northernmost point, then head northeast to Central Sichuan, and then south to An Guang to inspect the counties and towns along the border between Shu State and Jing State.\"","\"Guangyuan County...\"","Chen Yi nodded slightly. He saw no issue with the way Yan Sea had planned the route."]},{"number":211,"title":"Chapter 211 - 188: You Can’t Handle It","paragraphs":["Guangyuan County to the north was at the border of Jing State, You State, and Shu State. It was a bustling hub for merchants, home to many Noble Families and people from all walks of life.","Add the Shu State Capital Commandery Office to the mix, and the relationships there were incredibly complex.","’Going to Guangyuan County first isn’t a bad choice.’","\"Who will be in the traveling party?\"","\"I don’t know their specific names, only that there’s an accountant, Doctor Sun, plus two Guards and Steward Yan. A party of five in total.\"","’They were quite thorough...’","’An accountant is meticulous and can record local details. A Physician can gauge the Medical Skill of Physicians from other Medicine Halls. The purpose of the Guards and Yan Hai goes without saying.’","Apparently, Wang Ji and Yan Hai had spent a good deal of time discussing the matter this afternoon.","After a short wait, Liu Lang arrived, braving the rain. He shook off his Raincoat and, seeing that Chen Yi was ready, said with a smile:","\"Boss, shall we head over now?\"","Chen Yi grunted in affirmation, told Zhang Dabao to get some rest, and then led Liu Lang toward Kangning Street.","It was not yet late into the night. The streets were still busy with pedestrians and carriages, and with the City Guard Army patrolling the alleys, the two of them were forced to move more slowly.","After a few twists and turns, Chen Yi and Liu Lang finally slipped into the courtyard of Liu Wen’s residence.","The moment they entered, they saw that the courtyard was brightly lit, with several men guarding both the inside and outside of a wooden building.","Liu Lang scanned the area and raised an eyebrow. \"Sir, there’s a Fifth Grade Realm Martial Artist here, but his Dao Realm is too low. He hasn’t reached Minor Success.\"","Chen Yi’s expression remained unchanged. After sizing up the situation, a theory formed in his mind.","’Either something has gone wrong, or Liu Wen wants to test us.’","\"This... Should we retreat?\"","Chen Yi shook his head slightly. After a moment’s thought, he took a porcelain bottle from his robes and handed it to him.","\"Immortal Drunk. Give everyone a little taste.\"","Liu Lang nodded in understanding. He took the bottle, silently approached the Guards, and took them down one by one.","He didn’t even spare the Fifth Grade Realm Martial Artist hidden inside the wooden building.","It took no more than ten breaths of time.","Once he was sure that everyone except Liu Wen had been silenced, Chen Yi began to walk unhurriedly toward the wooden building.","He had some idea of what Liu Wen intended with this arrangement.","After all, three hundred thousand silver coins was no small sum. It was only normal to be cautious.","Not only that, but having these Guards stationed inside and outside the wooden building was also a way to test his and Liu Lang’s abilities.","If even these men with their ordinary Cultivation and Techniques could detect their arrival, Liu Wen certainly wouldn’t believe they were from the Bright Moon Building.","Musing on this, Chen Yi stepped forward and knocked on the door.","However, the knock was merely a courtesy. After rapping on the wood, he pushed the door open and walked in, not lingering in the spacious hall but heading straight for the second floor.","Before he even reached the top of the stairs, his voice rang out, \"Young Master Liu, is it me, Black Tooth, you don’t trust, or is it the Bright Moon Building?\"","The semi-enclosed staircase made his deep, raspy voice echo with a certain hollowness.","But when the words reached Liu Wen’s ears, he showed no sign of anger. Instead, he rose with a smile to greet him:","\"Brother Hei, please forgive me. I meant no offense. I was simply worried I wouldn’t be able to attend to you properly on my own, so I had my men stay by my side.\"","Chen Yi, of course, didn’t believe a word of it.","As he rounded the top of the staircase, his emotionless eyes fell upon Liu Wen, and he said coolly:","\"I’ll let it slide this time. If there’s a next time, don’t blame me for being severe, Young Master Liu.\"","\"Of course, of course...\"","Liu Wen agreed readily while gesturing for him to come inside and take a seat.","Chen Yi didn’t move. \"I’ve only come for the silver coins tonight. I can’t stay long.\"","The smile on Liu Wen’s effeminate face froze. He sized Chen Yi up, his tone taking on an unavoidable note of displeasure.","\"Elder Black Tooth, keeping me at arm’s length like this is no way to treat your Financier.\"","Chen Yi looked him straight in the eye and said calmly, \"I have to gather a few old devils tonight to make arrangements. Time waits for no man. I hope Young Master Liu understands.\"","Liu Wen was taken aback for a moment, then his expression shifted to one of delight. \"You’re making your move this quickly?\" he asked.","\"The longer we delay, the greater the risk. I’m sure Young Master Liu can understand that.\"","\"I understand, haha, of course I understand. But Elder Black Tooth, could you perhaps tell me a little about your plan?\"","Chen Yi stared at him for a moment, then shook his head. \"To avoid any leaks, I can only tell you that our purpose this time is simply to draw the Xiao Family’s attention.\"","Liu Wen’s expression wavered slightly. \"To create an opportunity for the ones making the real move?\"","He understood that a major operation like this involved many people and couldn’t afford the slightest mistake.","Seeing that Chen Yi was unwilling to say more, he thought for a moment and didn’t press the issue. He turned, retrieved a thick stack of silver notes from a drawer under the table, and came back.","\"The reputations of Elder Black Tooth and the Bright Moon Building are well-known, so of course I trust you. These are all bearer silver notes from the Great Wei Bank. You can withdraw the funds yourself, Elder Black Tooth.\"","Chen Yi took the notes and glanced at them. Confirming there were no issues, he nodded and said, \"Young Master Liu, just wait here for a few days. Once the deed is done, someone will come find you.\"","Liu Wen faltered. \"You’re not coming yourself?\"","\"You must be joking, Young Master Liu. Whether this succeeds or fails, it will bring the Xiao Family and the Dingyuan Army hunting for us. It won’t be convenient for me to remain in Shu State for a while.\"","\"After everything has settled down, I will find an opportunity to catch up with you, Young Master Liu.\"","\"Excellent. When that time comes, I will surely roll out the red carpet and give you a proper welcome.\"","Chen Yi gave a slight nod, bowed, and then turned to descend the stairs.","Once he was out of the wooden building, Liu Lang floated down, opened an Oil Paper Umbrella over him, and they left together.","Liu Wen walked to the window and watched their figures disappear into the rainy night, a faint, sly smile gracing his effeminate features.","’Black Tooth of the Bright Moon Building... His reputation doesn’t do him justice. He truly is a man capable of great things.’","’Once this is done, even if it doesn’t topple the Xiao Family, it’s guaranteed to throw them into disarray.’"]},{"number":212,"title":"Chapter 212 - 188: You Can’t Handle It","paragraphs":["And once this matter had been allowed to brew for a while, it would be time for him to land the decisive blow.","’Big Brother, even though Father and a few of the family elders think highly of you, you’re lacking in both opportunity and ability. This Liu Family... you can’t handle it!’","Excitement flashed in Liu Wen’s eyes. He couldn’t help but look toward the Xiao Family estate as a vicious smile crept across his face.","’And the Xiao Family, Xiao Wan’er... as long as I get Xiao Wan’er, I can use her to get my hands on the Dingyuan Army.’","’When that time comes, haha, haha... who in all of Jing and Shu State would dare defy me?’","As if hearing Liu Wen’s laughter from a world away, Chen Yi weighed the stack of three hundred silver notes—each worth a thousand taels—in his hand and scoffed.","’That Liu Wen must be having sweet dreams right about now.’","’Well, I’ll let him be happy for a little while longer.’","Liu Lang, beside him, wasn’t thinking so deeply. His eyes were glued to the stack of silver notes, and his Adam’s apple bobbed as he swallowed hard.","Although he claimed not to care about money, having no major expenses besides his romantic dalliances, he couldn’t help but be tempted when he saw so many silver notes laid out before him.","\"Boss, these silver notes...\"","Chen Yi glanced at him, pulled out two notes, and handed them over. \"Spend it wisely.\"","Fortunately, he had previously received ten thousand taels in silver notes from Liu Wen, so giving two thousand to Liu Lang now wouldn’t affect his plans.","Liu Lang accepted them with a smile and tucked them into his robes. \"Thank you, Boss.\"","But after thanking him, seeing Chen Yi put the rest of the silver notes away, he couldn’t help but ask another question:","\"Is this silver for expanding Hundred Herbs Hall?\"","He was aware of the discussion between Wang Ji and Yan Sea earlier that day, and he couldn’t help but calculate how many Hundred Herbs Hall branches could be opened with three hundred thousand taels of silver.","But Chen Yi didn’t nod. Instead, he shook his head and said, \"I have other, more important uses for it.\"","Expanding Hundred Herbs Hall certainly required a large sum of silver coins.","But there were plenty of ways to raise silver coins for business dealings. At worst, he could find a way through the Xiao Family and the other Noble Families in various regions that had already agreed to cooperate.","’But these three hundred thousand taels in silver notes are crucial to the success of my current plan. I can’t touch them.’","...","Not long after, Chen Yi sent Liu Lang to Spring Rain Building to find Black Tooth, while he himself headed straight for the tailor shop in the West Market.","The two went their separate ways on Kangning Street, one heading south and the other west.","Soon, Chen Yi arrived outside the West Market. He carefully avoided Fang Hongxiu and a few other Imprisonment Officers who still hadn’t given up, and made his way to the residence behind the tailor shop.","The task he had given Wang Ji that day was progressing—not slowly, but not quickly either.","Neither of the two storefronts for the meager tailor shop had been secured, but someone in the residence behind it couldn’t resist the high price and had handed the deed over to Wang Ji that very day.","That was the residence where Chen Yi now was.","It was just past nine in the evening.","Although the rain had lessened, the sky was still thick with dark clouds. The surrounding gloom provided him with some cover.","About half an hour passed. Chen Yi heard a knock on the door of the tailor shop and rose, moving without a sound.","Based on his earlier observations, the Cultivation of these few Hidden Guards was not particularly high.","Even among the Silver Banner Officers like Ge the Third and Lou Yuchun, only Lou Yuxue had a Cultivation that reached the Middle Three Grades Realm.","It was nearly impossible for them to detect his presence.","Chen Yi carefully approached the tailor shop and pressed his ear against the outer wall.","Faintly, he heard Lou Yuxue’s voice from inside. \"A letter from the Pavilion Master?\"","Then he heard Ge the Third say excitedly, \"Quick, see what the letter says!\"","\"See for yourself.\"","After a rustling sound, the tailor shop fell silent for a long time.","Just as Chen Yi was growing puzzled, Ge the Third finally spoke. His voice was somewhat hoarse, as if his spirit had been shaken by seeing something he couldn’t accept.","\"The Pavilion Master... he... he wants us to finish that business, and then find a way to implicate Gray Wolf? Why? Why would he do that?\"","Lou Yuxue replied in a grave tone, \"Do you even need to ask?\"","\"Clearly, the Pavilion Master is displeased with Gray Wolf for using his position for personal gain. He’s even willing to eliminate the second branch of the Xiao Family.\"","\"However, I think this is a good thing for us.\"","\"Take this time, for instance. Gray Wolf acted recklessly for his own benefit, and it affects all of us.\"","\"Think about it. After this is done, you’ll lose more than half of the Iron Banner Officers you’ve planted in the Dingyuan Army.\"","\"It’s the same for me.\"","\"Black Tooth will have to flee Shu State, a new Elder will come from Bright Moon Building to take over, and even I will have to lie low for a time.\"","Hearing this, Ge the Third sighed. \"I just didn’t expect the Pavilion Master to be so decisive.\"","\"Gray Wolf’s identity is special. He’s not just the standard-bearer for the second branch of the Xiao Family, he’s also the Assistant Governor of the Governor’s Office. He could still be useful in the future...\"","\"Enough nonsense. It’s an order from the Pavilion Master. Do you dare disobey?\"","\"Of course I wouldn’t dare...\"","Hearing this, Chen Yi’s aura remained concealed, but a ripple of surprise went through him.","He also hadn’t expected the Hidden Guard to be so resolute in abandoning Xiao Dongchen. It seemed they even intended to eliminate him along with the second branch.","But on second thought, Chen Yi felt that while the Hidden Guard’s actions were unexpected, they were also perfectly logical.","Just as Lou Yuxue had said when persuading Ge the Third, Xiao Dongchen and the second branch were too selfish, which would interfere with the Hidden Guard’s plans.","’In that case, the Hidden Guard’s objective now aligns with mine.’","’I wonder who that Pavilion Master is. To be able to issue such a calm order from thousands of miles away.’","’That level of intelligence and decisiveness alone is beyond that of an ordinary person.’","After a moment of silence, he heard Lou Yuxue huff, \"Hurry up and look at the letter from the Golden Banner Officer. I have to get back to Spring Rain Building soon.\"","Ge the Third grunted in agreement and asked, \"When do we make our move?\"","\"Tonight, Black Tooth is going to get the silver from that Financier. Once I confirm that the three hundred thousand taels in silver coins are in our coffers, I’ll start arranging the next steps.\"","\"I estimate it will be in the next two days.\"","\"It’s the same for your side. Wait for the weather to clear up in a couple of days, and I’ll notify you when to act.\"","After hearing Lou Yuxue’s words, Ge the Third said no more and began to read the second secret letter, enunciating each word carefully:","\"Obtain one piece of the Fledgling’s calligraphy. Determine if his Calligraphy Dao has reached Perfection.\"","Lou Yuxue couldn’t help but ask, \"Calligraphy Dao Perfection? Are you sure it wasn’t deciphered incorrectly?\"","\"See for yourself...\"","Listening to their conversation, a strange look flashed in Chen Yi’s eyes.","’Calligraphy Dao Perfection?’","’How could the Hidden Guard know that my Calligraphy Dao broke through to the Perfection Realm?’","So far, he had only ever written for the Old Master and Sun Fu using his Perfect Calligraphy Dao.","Only three people knew about it.","He had even instructed Xiao Wuge not to reveal this matter.","Chen Yi recalled what he had heard Ge the Third say that morning and couldn’t help but wonder:","’Could there be a Hidden Guard concealed by the Old Master’s side?’","After thinking for a moment, Chen Yi couldn’t come up with any clues, but he was certain the person who leaked the secret of his Perfect Calligraphy Dao was connected to either the Old Master or Sun Fu.","However, after hearing about the secret letter from the Golden Banner Officer, he remembered something else.","—The piece of calligraphy he had lost earlier must have been taken by the Hidden Guard.","’How strange. Why do they care about my Calligraphy Dao?’","A moment later, Lou Yuxue and Ge the Third left the tailor shop one after the other.","[Witnessed the Hidden Guard receiving a secret letter. Reward: Zither Score \"Guangyuan Tune,\" Opportunity +18.]","[Evaluation: Presence achieved, sound heard, scene unseen...]","Chen Yi skimmed past the lines of golden text and, after a moment’s thought, chose not to return to the Xiao Family. Instead, he quietly followed Lou Yuxue.","’Black Tooth is going to get silver from another Financier tonight. I might as well follow along and have a look.’","’I can meet up with Liu Lang on the way and ask about the situation.’","When Lou Yuxue walked into a secluded alley, Chen Yi was about to follow but suddenly froze, hiding in a corner to the side.","From the alley up ahead, a hoarse, deep voice called out:","\"Lou Yuxue, where have you been?\""]},{"number":213,"title":"Chapter 213 - 189: I Know Your Depth, You Know My...","paragraphs":["As luck would have it.","The newcomer was none other than Black Tooth.","His current attire was quite similar to Chen Yi’s—a black robe with a black iron mask worn under the hood.","The only difference was that Chen Yi had an additional black cloak and a bamboo hat on his head.","However, both of them froze when they heard Black Tooth’s words.","But while Lou Yuxue was merely stunned, Chen Yi immediately held his breath and carefully concealed himself.","If Black Tooth hadn’t arrived without concealing his presence and with his eyes fixed only on Lou Yuxue, Chen Yi probably would have been cornered as well.","In contrast, after her moment of shock, a coquettish smile instantly bloomed on Lou Yuxue’s face. Her eyes drifted over to him as she said with a charming laugh:","\"My, I was wondering who was out scaring people so late at night. It turns out to be Elder Black Tooth~\"","\"Weren’t you going to collect the reward for that business deal? What are you doing here at this hour? Did you get the silver coins?\"","Black Tooth remained unmoved. His icy, emotionless eyes stared at her as he asked, enunciating each word:","\"Where. Did. You. Go?\"","Lou Yuxue’s expression didn’t change. She smiled and replied, \"Elder, you ask even though you know. I was worried there was an issue with Liu Wu’s identity, so I personally went to see Liu Wen to confirm.\"","\"And what was the result?\"","\"There were no problems, of course~ That Liu Wu really is one of Young Master Liu’s men. I made the trip for nothing~\"","Black Tooth studied her for a moment, then gave a slight nod. \"Is that so... I misjudged you. I thought you were going to leak information about the deal.\"","Hearing this, Lou Yuxue feigned annoyance. \"Elder, you worry too much. I belong to the Bright Moon Building, just like you. How could I be so reckless?\"","\"But you still haven’t said, is that sum of silver in your hands yet?\"","\"Naturally.\"","\"That’s wonderful. Then I must congratulate you, Elder, on another great achievement. I’m sure the leader will reward you handsomely upon hearing the news~\"","Black Tooth gave a noncommittal response. Just as he was about to take a step, his gaze suddenly shot toward the alley entrance behind him. His eyes turned icy as he asked:","\"Who’s there?\"","Hearing his words, Chen Yi’s heart skipped a beat. ’I’ve been discovered?’","Before he could think further, he suddenly felt an ice-cold killing intent wash over him.","It was coming from Black Tooth!","Seeing this, Chen Yi was certain that Black Tooth had found him.","His mind raced, and he stopped concealing his presence and aura.","But his first move wasn’t to show himself. Instead, he took off the mask on his face and stuffed it into his cloak.","Only after doing this did he speak up with a laugh. \"Elder Black Tooth, you truly live up to your reputation as a Martial Arts Powerhouse of the Upper Three Grades. I was so careful, yet you still found me. I’m impressed.\"","As he spoke, he walked to the mouth of the alley and rounded the corner to look at the two people inside.","Seeing him, Black Tooth was slightly surprised. \"Liu Wu?\"","Lou Yuxue was just as astonished. \"What are you doing here?\"","Chen Yi glanced at her, his smile slowly turning cold. His tone became sinister as he said:","\"Why am I here? Don’t you know, Miss Yuxue? I, of course, followed you all the way here.\"","A flicker of shock and suspicion crossed Lou Yuxue’s eyes. \"Followed me?\"","Chen Yi snorted. \"You didn’t think I was unaware of you going to the Liu Family to test me, did you?\"","\"Once last night, and again tonight. Heh, do you not trust me, or do you not trust my Young Master?\"","As he spoke, his eyes were locked on Lou Yuxue’s, a hint of mockery in his gaze.","’Hidden Guard Lady Tiger, heh, go on and deny it if you dare.’","When Lou Yuxue saw the look in his eyes, her heart filled with even more alarm and uncertainty.","She knew perfectly well that her claim about going to the Liu Family to test Liu Wu was utter nonsense, said only to allay Black Tooth’s suspicions.","Therefore, she was certain that what this Liu Wu before her was saying must also be false.","’Then...’","’If Liu Wu didn’t follow me here from Kangning Street, then where did he spot me?’","’Was it outside the West Market?’","’Or at the tailor shop in the West Market?’","’Was it before or after I entered the shop?’","The thought of these terrible possibilities, of her identity as a Hidden Guard potentially being exposed, made Lou Yuxue’s scalp tingle with dread.","However, with Black Tooth right there, even though she knew Chen Yi was lying, she had no choice but to play along for now.","Otherwise, if Black Tooth noticed something was amiss, neither of them would escape unscathed.","\"Please understand, Liu Wu. I was just trying to be absolutely certain.\"","Hearing this, Chen Yi laughed inwardly. He looked at the outwardly composed Lou Yuxue and said mockingly:","\"If that weren’t the case, why would I have tolerated it time and again?\"","\"Black Tooth, you’ve gone a bit too far this time.\"","At this, Black Tooth looked at him, then at Lou Yuxue by his side, and slowly shook his head.","\"The matter is of great importance. I hope Brother Liu Wu can forgive this minor indiscretion.\"","Hearing this, Chen Yi’s expression relaxed accordingly. He pursed his lips and said:","\"Since you’ve put it that way... I, Liu Wu, am not an unreasonable person, especially when it concerns my Young Master’s grand plan.\"","\"But if there’s a next time, don’t blame me for getting rough with her!\"","\"As it should be.\"","Black Tooth nodded in agreement. His earlobes twitched slightly, and he continued:","\"This is no place to talk. Why don’t we go to the Spring Rain Building to discuss things?\"","Chen Yi nodded. \"Perfect. My Young Master had a matter for me to discuss with you anyway.\"","He had been planning to go to the Spring Rain Building all along.","Although there had been a complication, he had no intention of changing his plan.","The three of them then made their way toward the Spring Rain Building.","Along the way, Lou Yuxue was clearly preoccupied, her gaze falling on Chen Yi several times, yet she didn’t dare say a single word.","Chen Yi, of course, noticed this, but he wasn’t worried.","’What was that saying again?’","’I know how deep you’re in, and you know... I’m a \"ghost.\"’","Right now, he and Lou Yuxue were in the same boat.","They both knew the other was lying, but they were both wary of Black Tooth.","’So...’","Chen Yi didn’t believe Lou Yuxue would dare to expose the truth.","Before long, the three arrived at the Spring Rain Building and headed straight for the private room on the top floor.","However, Black Tooth didn’t stay. He left ahead of them, leaving Lou Yuxue alone to attend to Chen Yi."]},{"number":214,"title":"Chapter 214 - 189: I Know Your Depth, You Know My...","paragraphs":["He was obviously going to hide the silver notes, or perhaps gold ones.","Both Chen Yi and Lou Yuxue were well aware of this.","However, they felt very differently about it.","Chen Yi was completely relaxed, leaning back in his chair, perfectly at ease.","Although Lou Yuxue wanted to confirm where Black Tooth was stashing the silver, what had just happened made her focus shift to Chen Yi.","\"Brother Liu, what message did your young master send with you?\"","Although Lou Yuxue asked the question with her usual charming tone, her face was a sheet of ice, and her eyes, fixed on Chen Yi, held a glint of killing intent.","At the same time, she dipped her finger in some water and wrote a few words on the table.","[Who are you, really?]","Chen Yi glanced at the words, a smile spreading across his face as he said:","\"Why do you ask, Miss Yuxue? Such lovely handwriting.\"","\"You?!\"","Furious, Lou Yuxue gritted her teeth and wiped the water from the table. Suppressing her rage, she asked, \"Lovely handwriting? Are you referring to your young master’s, Brother Liu?\"","At the same time, she wrote another line.","[If you don’t talk, we die together!]","Chen Yi read the words, then nodded with a smile. \"My young master was afraid I’d forget, so he wrote me a note before I came.\"","Then he, too, wrote two words on the table:","[West Market.]","Lou Yuxue’s expression flickered. While continuing to make small talk with Chen Yi, they began to communicate by writing on the table.","[Who are you?]","[Guess?]","[There’s no way you’re from the Liu Family!]","[And why not?]","[What’s your purpose here?]","[To burn the summer grain of the Three Towns, of course.]","[You...]","They went back and forth like this for ages, but Lou Yuxue couldn’t get a single straight answer out of him.","Her breathing grew ragged with anger, her chest heaving dramatically with each breath.","She suspected Chen Yi was from the Xiao Family.","But all signs indicated that the Xiao Family was still unaware of the Bright Moon Building’s plot.","The old patriarch even had the leisure to concern himself with matters between the Hundred Herbs Hall and the Xiao Family Medicine Hall.","It was the same story over at the Mutual Market; Xiao Jinghong had been there the whole time and hadn’t made a move.","’But if Liu Wu isn’t from the Xiao Family, then which faction sent him?’","’The Liu Family?’","’The Liu Family was a definite possibility.’","’But how did he appear in the West Market, and why was he following me?’","Right now, what Lou Yuxue wanted to confirm most was whether her identity as a Hidden Guard had been exposed. But the man before her was completely unyielding, making her seethe with frustration.","Finally, left with no other option, she wrote: [What will it take to make you tell the truth?]","Chen Yi raised an eyebrow slightly and wrote a few words: [Now that’s more like it.]","[But I have a very big appetite. I wonder if Miss Yuxue can satisfy it?]","Lou Yuxue gritted her teeth and wrote four words: [Let me hear it!]","[I want half of the silver from this deal. Is Miss Yuxue willing?]","[Dream on!]","[Then I have nothing to tell you.]","Lou Yuxue was fuming, but seeing the mocking smile in his eyes, she forced down her anger and wrote:","[Aren’t you afraid I’ll tell Black Tooth you’re not from the Liu Family?]","Chen Yi smiled, shook his head, and casually wrote two words:","[I am.]","[Impossible! If you were really from the Liu Family, why would you be after the silver?]","[Guess?]","Seeing Lou Yuxue’s eyes turning red with fury, Chen Yi, though secretly amused, knew that pushing her further would only make things worse.","After a moment of thought, Chen Yi wrote:","[Right now, who I am isn’t the most important thing. What’s important is ensuring this deal goes smoothly.]","[If Miss Yuxue is truly that curious, then do as I say: bring me one hundred fifty thousand silver.]","Lou Yuxue stared straight at him, weighing the pros and cons in her mind.","’Right now, I’m not sure of his identity, and I’m not sure if he knows I’m a Hidden Guard, but I can be sure of one thing—’","’—the Xiao Family is in the dark, and this man isn’t one of theirs.’","This judgment put Lou Yuxue somewhat at ease.","’At least the mission to burn the summer grain of the Three Towns can still proceed. Otherwise, I would never let Hawk take such a risk.’","’Even my own grand scheme, for which I’m hiding in the Bright Moon Building, would be affected.’","[If I find out you’re secretly sabotaging this, you will pay the price!]","Chen Yi watched her nervously wipe the words away as soon as she’d written them, a mischievous smile playing on his lips.","\"Miss Yuxue, for an establishment as grand as the Bright Moon Building, surely you wouldn’t be too stingy to refill a cup of tea?\"","When Lou Yuxue saw his smile, she had the sudden urge to scratch it right off his face.","But given the circumstances, she could only force a smile and say in a syrupy-sweet tone, \"My apologies, Brother Liu. Allow me to pour you some right away~\"","But as she held the teapot, she gave her wrist a flick, aiming the spout right at Chen Yi as she poured.","Although Chen Yi reacted quickly, some of the tea still splashed onto his clothes and legs.","He looked at Lou Yuxue, who was smugly pleased with her little trick, and said with a sigh that was half-amusement, half-exasperation:","\"Miss Yuxue, you’re so...\"","Before he could even call her \"petty,\" Lou Yuxue had already set down the teapot and moved closer. She began patting at his clothes, her voice full of apology:","\"Please forgive me, Brother Liu. I didn’t do it on purpose.\"","However, the force she used was clearly more than a mere \"pat.\"","Seeing this, Chen Yi let out a soft snort, releasing and then retracting his Fist Intent in a flash.","While Lou Yuxue was momentarily stunned by the mountain-like pressure of the Fist Intent, Chen Yi used one hand to twist her arm behind her back and pin her against the table.","\"Pardon my rudeness, Miss Yuxue.\"","Pinned by him, especially in such an undignified position, a flush of shame and anger crept onto Lou Yuxue’s face.","But her tone was still as charming as ever as she said:","\"Brother Liu, what are you doing~? Aren’t you going to let me go?\"","\"You...\"","But before Chen Yi could finish, a section of the wall slid open. Liu Lang appeared in the doorway.","When he got a clear look at the scene inside, a flicker of astonishment crossed Liu Lang’s eyes.","\"What are you two...?\"","He glanced at Chen Yi, then at Lou Yuxue pinned beneath him, and let out a sly chuckle."]},{"number":215,"title":"Chapter 215 - 189: I Know Your Depth, You Know My...","paragraphs":["\"A man and a woman alone in a room, doing... well, what one would expect. It’s perfectly normal, perfectly normal! Haha.\"","As he spoke, Liu Lang didn’t forget to close the door. \"You two continue. Just pretend I was never here.\"","Seeing the wall slide shut, Lou Yuxue, her face flushed red, hissed, \"Aren’t you going to let go of me?\"","Chen Yi did as she said and let go, taking a few steps back. A smirk played on his lips as he said,","\"Miss Yuxue, I told you we shouldn’t come here. You just had to be in such a rush. See? Now we’re the butt of the joke.\"","\"You...\"","Lou Yuxue nearly ground her teeth to dust at his shameless words.","But she knew Chen Yi was only saying this to deceive Black Tooth and Liu Lang. With a sigh of resignation, she closed her eyes and straightened her clothes. Then, in a soft, coquettish voice, she said,","\"It’s all your fault for being so handsome, dear Brother Liu. You made my poor heart flutter~\"","But just as the words left her mouth, Lou Yuxue had already opened the adjacent door. Looking at Liu Lang outside, she said with a smile,","\"Oh, come in, come in. Business comes first.\"","\"You’re done already?\"","\"...\"","Seeing Lou Yuxue give him a charming eye-roll, Liu Lang walked into the private room with a smile.","\"Don’t blame me for the bad timing. It was all that bastard Black Tooth. He’s the one who sent me.\"","Chen Yi shot him a glare, signaling him to shut up. Then, adopting Liu Wu’s impatient tone, he spoke.","\"Where’s Black Tooth?\"","\"If he doesn’t show up soon, I’m leaving.\"","Just then, Black Tooth appeared from behind another wall. \"I was delayed by some matters.\"","After a quick scan of the room, he gestured for them to sit, leaving no room for argument.","\"What message does Young Master Liu have for me?\"","Chen Yi glanced at him, his chin held high. \"My Young Master wants to know when that deal of ours will be settled. He’s waiting to pay another visit to the Xiao Family.\"","Black Tooth grunted in acknowledgment. \"I heard Young Master Liu ran into a wall with the Old Marquis?\"","Chen Yi snorted. \"If you know, why ask?\"","\"If that old fool knew what was good for him, my Young Master wouldn’t have had to send us here in the first place.\"","\"He also said that if your Bright Moon Building spent half as much energy on the deal as you do trying to verify my identity, this would all have been settled by now.\"","Hearing this, Black Tooth paused, then said:","\"Please, Brother Liu, go back and report that we will make our move soon.\"","\"A specific time?\"","Black Tooth said nothing, merely glancing at Lou Yuxue.","Lou Yuxue took the cue. \"When the weather clears, I will make the arrangements.\"","Chen Yi looked from her to Black Tooth, raising an eyebrow.","\"So, Miss Yuxue is the one calling the shots on this deal? Isn’t Elder Black Tooth the one in charge of the Bright Moon Building in Shu State?\"","Lou Yuxue felt another flare of anger. ’This man is infuriating! Every word he says is a trap, yet he never gives anything away himself. It’s maddening.’","\"You’re joking, dear Brother Liu~ I simply follow Elder Black Tooth’s lead. How could I dare to act on my own?\"","Chen Yi smiled and nodded. \"I’d imagine so. I only trust Elder Black Tooth.\"","\"In that case, I’ll go back and report.\"","Black Tooth grunted. \"We will contact you later.\"","Seeing this, Chen Yi didn’t linger. After signaling to Liu Lang, he got up and left the Spring Rain Building.","「Once all was quiet again.」","Black Tooth sat in silence for a moment before looking at Lou Yuxue. \"You were acting a bit differently today. Why?\"","A chill ran down Lou Yuxue’s spine, but she didn’t dare let her eyes waver. She looked directly at Black Tooth and said with a coquettish smile,","\"Please don’t be alarmed, Elder.\"","\"You know my origins... from the demimonde. Even as one of the Cultured Courtesans, it’s inevitable that people look down on me in this world. A woman has to find a safe harbor.\"","Black Tooth asked, unmoved, \"Liu Wu?\"","\"Yes. His status is high enough, and his skills in both Martial Arts and the Medical Dao are impressive. If I were to be with him, I would have someone to protect me from the storms of life.\"","\"Of course, I’m also doing this for the sake of our Bright Moon Building. After all, he’s a Medical Saint Hand. He’ll be of great use to us later on.\"","Seeing how earnest she sounded, Black Tooth simply gave her a long, hard look.","\"I don’t care what you have planned, but that deal cannot be affected in the slightest. If it is, your death is certain!\"","\"Of course...\"","As Black Tooth walked away, Lou Yuxue’s expression remained neutral, but inwardly, she was still seething with rage.","’Liu Wu!","You just wait!’"]},{"number":216,"title":"Chapter 216 - 190: No, No, Impossible","paragraphs":["It wasn’t hard for Chen Yi to guess what kind of mood Lou Yuxue was in.","He figured she probably wanted to kill him right about now.","But he wasn’t worried at all.","For one, his identity was well-concealed.","The only two people in on the secret were Wang Ji and Zhang Dabao. Even Liu Lang only knew of the existence of \"Chen Yu.\"","For Lou Yuxue to confirm that he was \"Liu Wu,\" she would have to overcome two obstacles.","It wasn’t impossibly difficult, but before Lou Yuxue could get past the \"Liu Lang\" barrier, Chen Yi would have time to take countermeasures.","The second reason was much simpler—Lou Yuxue wouldn’t dare to make a move against him.","At least, not for now.","Between the incident with the \"burning of the Three Towns’ summer grain,\" the three hundred thousand taels of silver, and the involvement of Bright Moon Building and the Hidden Guard, Lou Yuxue had to be somewhat wary.","It wouldn’t be an exaggeration to describe her as full of apprehension.","In short, Chen Yi had indeed put himself on the chessboard.","But he was a game piece hidden deep within the board.","He wouldn’t let anyone discover his existence anytime soon.","The rest of the journey was silent.","After taking a winding route, Chen Yi and Liu Lang returned to the residence on Chuansi Street.","After the incident where Black Tooth had killed Elder Demon Fang, their return trip was much smoother; they didn’t detect anyone following them.","They entered the main hall.","Liu Lang took off his bamboo hat, plopped down onto a chair, and couldn’t help but ask:","\"Boss, why were you at the Spring Rain Building tonight, too? When Black Tooth told me you were here, I almost blurted out something I shouldn’t have.\"","\"I had no idea that you and Miss Lou...\"","Chen Yi shot him a glare, cutting him off.","\"Never mind me. Tell me what happened after you got to the Spring Rain Building.\"","Liu Lang gave a knowing smile and said casually, \"When I arrived, Black Tooth and his men weren’t around, so I sat in the main hall for a bit.\"","\"The Spring Rain Building truly lives up to its name as the top Qin Building in Shu State. I hadn’t been in a few days, and they already had a new batch of girls, every one of them a real beauty.\"","\"And their tea drinks! I only knew that Hundred Herbs Hall sent them by the cartload to Yanhua Lane, but I never imagined they’d sell so well. Nearly everyone had a bottle in hand.\"","\"I even...\"","Seeing the displeased look on Chen Yi’s face, Liu Lang stopped, coughed, and changed the subject. \"Later, I ran into Black Tooth. When I heard from him that you’d arrived, I went to look for you.\"","\"You didn’t find anything else?\"","\"Nothing.\"","Chen Yi thought for a moment, then asked for more detail. \"Where did you run into Black Tooth? The main hall? The first floor, second, third, or fourth?\"","Liu Lang’s mouth fell open. He replied awkwardly, \"The third floor.\"","\"...How much silver did you spend?\"","\"Th-thirty or forty taels. I don’t quite remember.\"","Chen Yi said irritably, \"Try to be more frugal. Otherwise, you can just live off the monthly wage Hundred Herbs Hall gives you from now on.\"","Liu Lang let out a couple of sheepish chuckles but didn’t say anything.","’He knew himself best. His conduct lived up to the ’Lang’ in his name—with money in his pocket and time on his hands, how could he not go up to the third floor and enjoy himself?’","’Even if the Spring Rain Building’s courtesans sold their art and not their bodies, just feasting his eyes was satisfying enough.’","Chen Yi saw from his expression that the words had gone in one ear and out the other, so he didn’t press the matter.","’He silently back-calculated the time of Black Tooth and Liu Lang’s meeting.’","’He concluded that Black Tooth had probably stashed the silver coins somewhere on the third floor of the Spring Rain Building.’","’Either that, or he’d handed them over to someone else from Bright Moon Building for safekeeping.’","Chen Yi mentally filed away this deduction as his mind began to race.","With Liu Wen’s three hundred thousand in silver notes secured, all the pieces of his puzzle were now in place.","Now, there were only two things left for him to do.","After a moment of thought, Chen Yi tapped the armrest of his chair. He looked at Liu Lang, his expression serious. \"Tomorrow, go to the Governor’s Office and give Xiao Dongchen a message.\"","\"Xiao Dongchen? What message?\"","\"Tell him my young master wants to meet him tomorrow at the hour of the Dog, in the alley beside Jishi Medicine Hall in the East Market.\"","\"Young Master?\"","\"Liu Wen.\"","Liu Lang jolted, his hand instinctively going to the long blade at his waist. He asked:","\"Boss, are you planning to meet him as Liu Wen this time?\"","Chen Yi shook his head. \"I’m only borrowing Liu Wen’s name. I’ll still be going as Liu Wu.\"","Liu Lang scratched his head. \"What are you planning this time? Are you trying to get silver from Xiao Dongchen? But he’s from the Xiao family! Aren’t you afraid they’ll find out?\"","The barrage of questions made Chen Yi frown slightly. \"Enough. You’ll find out tomorrow night.\"","\"Remember, the usual rules apply. Deliver the message, say nothing more, and it’s best if he doesn’t see your face.\"","Liu Lang stared at him blankly for a moment before finally nodding.","But he clearly couldn’t fathom Chen Yi’s intentions.","’Still, based on what he’d learned about Chen Yi recently, he knew this inscrutable boss of his was an expert at setting traps and swindling people.’","’First, there was Black Tooth, who he’d tricked into thinking he was from the Jing State Liu Family to get him to participate in that business deal.’","’Then there was Liu Wen, who fell for his Black Tooth disguise and was cheated out of three hundred thousand taels in silver notes.’","’Xiao Dongchen... he probably wouldn’t be an exception.’","Chen Yi, for his part, paid no mind to Liu Lang’s thoughts.","After confirming there were no other issues, he dismissed Liu Lang.","Once Zhang Dabao had helped him remove his disguise, Chen Yi gave a few instructions and headed back to the Xiao Family estate.","It wasn’t until he was back in his room in the wooden building that Chen Yi finally let out a long sigh of relief.","\"One thing after another... what a hassle...\"","He might complain, but Chen Yi was well aware of the Xiao Family’s current predicament.","—They seemed like the uncrowned kings of Shu State, but in reality, they were surrounded by enemies.","These enemies came not only from the Imperial Court, but also from the great Noble Families and Government Office officials in both Shu and Jing States.","Even figures from the Evil Demonic Dao, like Black Tooth, were trying to trip up the Xiao Family.","They didn’t even have to confront the Xiao Family directly. They just needed to exploit the conflict between the Xiao and Liu Families, fishing in troubled waters to muddy the situation and severing the Xiao Family’s network of informants. That alone was enough to plunge the Xiao Family into a quagmire.","Under such circumstances, even if the Old Master was cautious and had contingencies in place, he would still struggle to distinguish friend from foe before the situation became clear."]},{"number":217,"title":"Chapter 217 - 190: No, No, Impossible","paragraphs":["If Chen Yi hadn’t intervened, the Old Master would have been left with only two paths.","Either suppress everyone, regardless of friend or foe.","Or strike one side with lightning speed to deter anyone else with ulterior motives.","The first option would cause too much of a stir. It would not only require mobilizing the Dingyuan Army but would also be self-destructive, essentially sacrificing the network of connections the Xiao Family had built over two hundred years.","The second option would cost less, but it would bring its own considerable set of problems.","Chen Yi’s role was to secretly relieve some of the pressure on the Old Master and the Xiao Family, preventing them from being left completely in the dark.","After all, he couldn’t just stand by and do nothing.","’I’ll definitely make Xiao Jinghong pay me back for this later.’","With this thought, Chen Yi subconsciously glanced toward Jiaxing Garden, mumbled a few words, and sat cross-legged on his bed to cultivate the Four Symbols Skill.","Five days had passed since he broke through to the Sixth Grade Realm.","With the empowerment of the Four Directions Divine Position’s Spiritual Essence, his Cultivation progress was no slower than before.","In fact, it had even increased.","Previously, in the Seventh Grade Realm, it had taken him five days to advance a minor stage. Now, in the Sixth Grade Realm, it still took him five days to break through a minor stage of his Cultivation.","Even now, as True Essence circulated through his body, the mercury-like substance was further compressed by the Four Directions Divine Position.","Not only did this expel the impurities from his body, but it also doubled his True Essence.","As his Cultivation advanced to the Middle Sixth Grade, the figures of the Cyan Dragon, White Tiger, Vermilion Bird, and Black Tortoise atop the Four Divine Positions within the Sea of Qi in his Forehead Acupoint grew more solid.","Their whiskers, feathers, and scales looked utterly real, covering the surfaces of their bodies.","Upon careful inspection, one could see they possessed an increasingly divine air. Even the effects of the Spiritual Essence flowing from them had improved slightly.","The most noticeable result was with the Four Symbols Skill—his Cultivation speed was faster.","He could now complete a major circulatory cycle in just one hour, which was twice as fast as before.","As Chen Yi vaguely perceived these changes, he became even more immersed in cultivating the Four Symbols Skill.","Wisps of a faint glow circled the space between his brows, flickering in and out of sight as they drew the Heaven and Earth’s Spiritual Mechanism into his body.","Gradually strengthening his Cultivation.","...","But while Chen Yi cultivated in peace, some were destined for a sleepless night.","First and foremost among them was Lady Tiger Lou Yuxue.","She tossed and turned, unable to stomach the humiliation.","’To think that I, a distinguished Hidden Guard Silver Banner Officer who commands several Iron Banner Officers and successfully infiltrated Bright Moon Building in Shu State... my ability and temperament are beyond question.’","’Yet tonight, some damn bastard had completely gotten the better of me.’","’He not only overpowered me at every turn but also threatened me, forcing me to back down.’","’That would have been one thing.’","In the past, to complete orders from her superiors, Lou Yuxue had feigned civility with difficult people before.","But at least she had known their identities and backgrounds.","It was nothing like now, where she didn’t even know the background or residence of this \"Liu Wu.\"","’This is too passive!’","Thinking of how that \"Liu Wu\" had taken liberties with her and overpowered her, Lou Yuxue gritted her teeth and slammed her fist on the bed.","She then sat up and looked out the window at the moonlight breaking through the scattering clouds, an icy expression on her face.","\"After I deal with Black Tooth and Xiao Dongchen, I will make you pay!\"","「Kangning Street.」","Liu Wen was too excited to sleep.","He had spent a huge sum of real money today—300,000 taels—and he couldn’t help but feel a thrill of excitement.","As he lay on his bed, visions of him trampling the Xiao Family and taking control of the Liu Family filled his mind, making it difficult for him to contain his excitement.","\"Just you wait, you old bastard. You’ll pay the price for provoking me!\"","Meanwhile, in the West Mansion, just a wall away.","Liu Zhaoxue was not idle, either.","She was quietly discussing their next steps with a black-robed Yan Fusha.","\"Making Second Brother die suddenly in such a short period of time is impossible. It will certainly draw suspicion from Father and the others, even if their true target is the Xiao Family.\"","\"Rest assured, Miss Zhaoxue. I have already planned for everything.\"","Yan Fusha took a porcelain vial from his robes and said with a low chuckle, \"This is the Five Poison Powder I prepared for you. You only need to have your Second Brother ingest it for seven consecutive days. He will surely die without a trace.\"","Liu Zhaoxue glanced at the porcelain vial but did not take it. She shook her head again.","\"You don’t understand what I mean.\"","\"Even if there are no clues surrounding Second Brother’s death, even if all evidence points to the Xiao Family, I will still be a suspect.\"","Yan Fusha’s expression flickered. \"Your father is that suspicious?\"","Liu Zhaoxue nodded. \"My father doesn’t believe in coincidences. His greatest talent is making his own schemes look like accidents.\"","\"It’s just like when he arranged for my aunt to marry into the Imperial Palace. He seized an opportunity when the Holy Emperor was away from the palace to orchestrate a ’chance encounter’ between them. That’s how she was able to rise to the rank of Noble Consort so quickly after entering the Imperial City.\"","Yan Fusha rubbed his chin. For a moment, he too felt this was becoming a headache.","\"If that’s the case, then we can’t just frame the Xiao Family. We need someone from the Xiao Family to actually kill Liu Wen.\"","Liu Zhaoxue agreed. \"Only then can I remain in Shu State and have a chance to take charge of Xinglin Hall.\"","\"Fine!\"","\"I will return and begin the preparations at once. Await my good news!\"","As Yan Fusha turned to leave, Liu Zhaoxue stopped him. A flicker of hesitation crossed her beautiful face as she asked:","\"Can you tell me first? What is the Five Poison Sect’s true purpose for coming to Shu State?\"","Yan Fusha glanced back at her and gave a sinister smile. \"The grand ambitions of my Five Poison Sect have nothing to do with your Liu Family.\"","\"Unfortunately for you, however, we need to borrow your Xinglin Hall.\"","\"Hm?\"","\"Rest assured, Miss Zhaoxue. We are only borrowing it, and it will not be a difficult matter for Xinglin Hall.\""]},{"number":218,"title":"Chapter 218 - 190: No, No, Impossible","paragraphs":["\"...I hope so.\"","...","「The next day.」","The rain had finally stopped, and the sky had cleared.","Chen Yi washed up and changed his clothes early. He didn’t just throw something on, either; he chose a formal brocade robe.","This prompted Xiaodie to ask him repeatedly about his plans for the day.","Chen Yi didn’t hide it from her. He smiled and said, \"I’m going to Guiyun Academy at noon.\"","\"Young Master, you aren’t scheduled to start teaching the Calligraphy Dao for another two days. Why...?\"","Before she could finish, Xiaodie seemed to realize something. She stared at him without blinking.","\"I know.\"","\"Young Master, you’re going to deal with all those people who’ve been coming to visit you, aren’t you?\"","Chen Yi reached out and tapped her on the forehead. \"Aren’t you a clever one.\"","\"It’s not that I’m clever. I just know the Young Master wouldn’t stand by and let the Eldest Miss suffer.\"","\"Hm?\"","\"Young Master, don’t look at me like that. It’s true, you wouldn’t.\"","Chen Yi raised an eyebrow slightly, then smiled and nodded. \"Well, I’m the one who caused this trouble. I have to be the one to solve it.\"","\"Alright, let’s have breakfast first.\"","Xiaodie let out a little \"oh.\" As she watched him walk ahead, she couldn’t help but stick her tongue out playfully.","Of course, there was a reason she’d said that—it was because of the \"love poem\" the Young Master had written for the Eldest Miss.","Even after all this time, Xiaodie still remembered the poem’s content.","The *Wan God’s Ode* and its line about her being \"rare in this world,\" and so on.","’I almost let it slip. Xiaodie, oh, Xiaodie, you can’t let the Young Master find out you broke the rules and secretly read those poems.’","As she thought this, Xiaodie patted her rather ample chest and followed Chen Yi downstairs.","But as she walked, she couldn’t help but think of something else that puzzled her.","’Did the Young Master hide that poem?’","’Why haven’t I seen it since then?’","But after thinking for a moment, scenes straight out of an opera playbook began to form in her little head—","’The Young Master... gave the poem he wrote with his own hands to his beloved, the Eldest Miss...’","’No, no, no, that’s impossible!’","Xiaodie shook her head, but she wasn’t paying attention to her surroundings and bumped right into Chen Yi’s back.","Chen Yi glanced back, looking puzzled. \"You’re acting strange today. What’s on your mind?\"","A blush instantly crept onto Xiaodie’s face. She waved her hands frantically. \"N-nothing.\"","\"Please forgive me, Young Master. I just zoned out, hehe.\"","Chen Yi sized her up but naturally couldn’t guess what she was thinking. He just assumed she was daydreaming about some romance and teased,","\"Xiaodie is a grown woman now. I think I’ll have to talk to Eldest Sister about finding you a husband.\"","At his words, the color drained from Xiaodie’s face. Her rosy cheeks turned deathly pale. She anxiously blocked Chen Yi’s path. \"Young Master, Young Master, are... are you trying to send me away?\"","\"Please don’t send me away, please, I...\"","Seeing tears of panic welling in her eyes, Chen Yi knew he’d taken the joke too far and had to fix it.","After a good deal of explaining, he finally managed to coax Xiaodie from tears to laughter.","\"Young Master, how... how could you joke about something like that?\"","\"You’ve cried, you’ve laughed. Now let’s hurry up and eat.\"","The two of them were just about to sit down for breakfast with Xiao Wuge when they heard footsteps outside the door.","Then, Xiao Wan’er, draped in a pure white cloak, came walking in gracefully.","Perhaps because she had been recovering well lately, she held her cloak with one hand and entered the room with a little skip as she crossed the threshold.","The sight took Chen Yi by surprise. \"Eldest Sister, you seem to be... in a good mood today?\"","A rare, bright smile appeared on Xiao Wan’er’s face, along with a hint of self-satisfaction.","This made Chen Yi all the more curious.","Xiao Wan’er explained, \"Last night, Cui’er, Juan’er, and I put together an expansion charter for the Xiao Family Medicine Hall.\"","\"I came over today specifically to have my brother-in-law here review it.\"","\"...The Xiao Family Medicine Hall... Expansion... Charter?\"","Chen Yi looked at the delighted Xiao Wan’er. Suppressing the strange feeling in his heart, he took the booklet from her hands and began to flip through it.","After reading just a few pages, he understood completely.","Just as he’d thought. The Eldest Sister’s business talent was limited to collecting payments and handing out monthly allowances.","This *Xiao Family Medicine Hall Expansion Charter* wasn’t exactly identical to the *Baicao Hall Expansion Charter*, but it was pretty close.","’Change a few words, and you could swap one for the other...’","Xiao Wan’er, oblivious to his thoughts, asked eagerly, \"What do you think?\"","Chen Yi couldn’t bear to crush her spirits. He put down the booklet and said after a moment’s thought, \"It’s acceptable.\"","\"However, there is some room for improvement...\""]},{"number":219,"title":"Chapter 219 - 191: Your Brother-in-law is the Best","paragraphs":["Chen Yi thought he had offered his suggestions as tactfully as possible, but seeing the smile slowly fade from Xiao Wan’er’s face, he couldn’t help but feel a pang of pity.","As he finished, he motioned for Xiaodie to pour some tea, then cleared his throat and said:","\"This proposal of yours actually has its merits. It’s just that the Xiao Family’s current Medicine Halls have a very demanding business model. Compared to Hundred Herbs Hall, we simply aren’t in a position to expand.\"","And it was true.","To expand a traditional Medicine Hall, you don’t just need competent Physicians and apprentices to run the storefronts; you also need a steady supply of various medicinal herbs.","It was nothing like the simple model of Hundred Herbs Hall, which focused primarily on medicinal teas and formulas for common ailments.","Training Physicians alone doesn’t happen overnight, to say nothing of spending a fortune on silver coins to stock herbs with no guarantee of when they’d be sold.","To put it bluntly, basing her proposal on the existing Xiao Family Medicine Hall was fundamentally flawed.","At least, the Xiao Family in its current state couldn’t support such a resource-intensive model.","After he finished, Xiao Wan’er thought for a moment and said, \"You’re right, Brother-in-law. I was getting ahead of myself.\"","\"That’s not entirely true...\"","Before Chen Yi could reassure her, Xiao Wan’er pursed her lips. \"You don’t have to comfort me. I truly didn’t think it through.\"","\"Thinking about it now, the only truly competent Physicians in our five Medicine Halls are the ones sent over from Hundred Herbs Hall.\"","Xiao Wan’er paused, then asked, \"So, based on what you just said, if I want to expand the Medicine Halls, I need a sufficient number of Physicians with superb Medical Skills?\"","Seeing that she wasn’t ready to give up, Chen Yi had a good idea of what she was thinking.","’He figured that Xiao Wan’er’s desire to expand the Medicine Halls wasn’t about earning silver coins. Just as always, she hoped to help more people escape the suffering of illness and disease.’","With this in mind, Chen Yi’s expression turned serious. \"If you’re truly set on this, Sister Wan’er, why not focus on the first step?\"","A flicker of emotion crossed Xiao Wan’er’s face, and her eyes instantly lit up, reflecting his image in their bright depths.","\"Please, speak plainly, Brother-in-law.\"","The truth was not far from what Chen Yi had guessed.","Having been frail and sickly since childhood, Xiao Wan’er understood all too well the suffering caused by illness. Thus, she hoped to do whatever she could to help those in pain from sickness and injury.","It was a wish born of the same spirit that longed to provide shelter for all the world’s suffering souls.","Chen Yi nodded and said thoughtfully, \"Expanding the Medicine Halls would consume too much manpower and silver coins, and it would be difficult to see any progress in the short term.\"","\"Why not simplify things? Instead of building more Medicine Halls, shift your goal to training more Physicians.\"","Hearing this, Xiao Wan’er began to understand. With a look that was both inquisitive and pleading, she said, \"Could you say that a little slower?\"","She then motioned for Shen Huatang to bring a brush and paper. \"I want to write this down.\"","Chen Yi was in no hurry. He waited until everything was ready before continuing.","\"It’s actually not so different from the academies we have now. However, those academies focus on teaching scholars, with the aim of helping them earn official ranks.\"","\"What you would be doing, Sister Wan’er, is creating an academy dedicated to teaching Medical Skills and the Medical Dao.\"","\"With the right methods, a rigorous curriculum, and Instructors who possess superb Medical Skills, students who are dedicated to the Medical Dao will be able to truly achieve something.\"","\"In several years, as more and more apprentices grow into fully-fledged Physicians, even without expanding the Medicine Halls, you’ll be able to benefit far more people.\"","Xiao Wan’er’s eyes grew even brighter. \"Yes, yes!\"","\"Brother-in-law, you’ve said exactly what was on my mind! As long as we can successfully establish an academy that teaches the Medical Dao, there will be more and more Physicians.\"","\"That way, even if they don’t work at the Xiao Family Medicine Hall, they can spread throughout Shu State, and even across the Great Wei’s Nine State and Three Prefectures, to treat the sick and save lives.\"","As she spoke, she used delicate, elegant strokes to record Chen Yi’s words verbatim.","After she finished writing, Xiao Wan’er asked, \"So, is there anything else I need to pay attention to?\"","Chen Yi thought for a moment. \"First, for the Medical Dao Academy to attract talented students, you’ll need a headmaster with superb Medical Skills—preferably a Medical Saint Hand.\"","\"Second, the medical curriculum will need to be specially compiled. The existing teachings of the Medical Dao are too disorganized and complex, which makes it difficult for students to master the material in a limited amount of time.\"","\"And finally...\"","He had never done anything like this himself, but by combining his understanding of the Medical Dao with things he’d heard about how medical academies were run, he was able to offer Xiao Wan’er a fairly complete and novel framework.","Chen Yi spoke for a full hour before he finally stopped.","\"This way, without spending too much on silver coins, you can benefit the people far and wide within five to ten years.\"","Xiao Wan’er put down her Wolf Hair Brush. Looking at the contents written on the few sheets of Yunsong Paper, her heart filled with joy.","In her excitement, she didn’t forget Chen Yi. \"Thank you. I know what to do now.\"","Chen Yi couldn’t help but admire her stunningly beautiful smile. \"I was just spitballing ideas. If this doesn’t work out in the future, you can’t blame me for running my mouth.\"","\"Of course... I won’t.\"","Noticing his stare, a blush crept up to her eyes. Yet, she didn’t speak in a chiding tone, instead using the excuse of tidying the papers to turn her head away.","’He gave me such helpful advice,’ she thought. ’I suppose I can let him look for a moment.’","But when she finished tidying up, she saw his gaze was still on her. Feeling a little flustered, Xiao Wan’er hastily stood up.","\"Huatang, Huatang! It’s getting late. Go see if Madam Tang, who is visiting today, has arrived yet.\"","Shen Huatang blinked in confusion. \"Miss, Madam Tang didn’t send a visiting card today. Miss Wan is the one coming around noon.\"","Xiao Wan’er’s face grew even redder. \"Right, I misremembered. It’s Sister Wan who is coming.\"","With that, she flusteredly bid Chen Yi farewell and hurried back to Jiaxing Garden with Shen Huatang and her other attendants.","Chen Yi smiled as he watched her retreating figure.","’But he knew that after today, Xiao Wan’er was going to be busier than ever.’","A Medical Dao Academy...","In the current Great Wei Dynasty, if not entirely unprecedented, it was at the very least forging a new path.","Therefore, to actually establish the Medical Dao Academy and bring it to fruition would be no easy task.","Selecting a site, building the academy, inviting renowned doctors, compiling medical texts, recruiting students, and managing its future operations—none of it could be handled carelessly.","If she wanted every detail handled with precision, Xiao Wan’er could not remain on the sidelines.","’This is for the best.’","’She has a long life ahead of her. Wasting her energy on collecting rent, managing silver coins, and distributing monthly allowances would be a bit too mundane.’","A smile touched Chen Yi’s lips as he pictured a future where Xiao Wan’er was bustling about, yet utterly content.","After a brief rest, he instructed Xiaodie to take Xiao Wuge to Jiaxing Garden, then headed to Guiyun Academy alone.","「When Xiao Wuge arrived at Jiaxing Garden.」","Xiao Wan’er was busy instructing Cui’er and the others to prepare for the day’s guests, all while looking over the sheet of Yunsong Paper that held Chen Yi’s advice.","\"Sister, are you really going to create that academy to teach people the Medical Dao?\"","\"Of course.\"","\"It might seem complicated, but as long as we do it and do it well, it will benefit our Xiao Family, too.\"","Xiao Wuge nodded, only half-understanding. But the thought that the idea came from Chen Yi was enough to convince him it was sound.","\"Brother-in-law is amazing.\"","Xiao Wan’er agreed. \"He does make a good point.\"","Xiao Wuge’s eyes darted about mischievously as he asked with a sly grin, \"How does it compare to the proposal *you* wrote, Sister?\"","Xiao Wan’er paused and turned to look at him, a smile gracing her pale but faintly flushed cheeks. \"You want to know?\"","\"Then after you finish your etiquette lessons for the day and read two volumes of pre-dynastic history, I’ll tell you.\"","\"Huh?\"","\"Make it three volumes.\"","Xiao Wuge didn’t dare ask any more questions and quickly had Xiaodie lead him to the study.","He was afraid that if he lingered any longer, his required reading would increase from three volumes to four.","As she watched him scurry off, Xiao Wan’er lifted her chin slightly. ’Hmph. Just because you know your brother-in-law is amazing doesn’t mean you can say I’m no good.’","But then she remembered how Chen Yi had picked apart the proposal she’d stayed up all night writing, and she couldn’t help but blush with a bit of embarrassment.","’He’s never done anything like this, so how does he know so much?’","Cui’er and Juan’er, standing nearby, had no idea what she was thinking, but seeing the blush on her face, they knew she was in a good mood.","\"Ever since the Young Miss started drinking Divine Doctor Ma’s medicinal soup, her complexion has been getting better and better.\"","Hearing this, Xiao Wan’er collected her thoughts and said with a smile, \"The Mid-Autumn Festival is approaching. Remind me to prepare a small gift for Doctor Ma.\"","\"And prepare one for the owner of Hundred Herbs Hall as well.\"","\"Yes, Miss.\"","Xiao Wan’er recalled what Chen Yi had told her yesterday—that the owner, \"Chen Yu,\" was not currently in Shu State—so after giving the order, she turned to her own affairs.","Since the owner of Hundred Herbs Hall was away, she would have to begin preparations on behalf of the Xiao Family Medicine Hall herself.","Things like funding, which personal connections to leverage, which county in Shu State to start with, and so on.","These were all tasks she felt were within her purview.","...","With the Mid-Autumn Festival less than ten days away.","The festive atmosphere could already be felt throughout Shu State Prefecture City.","The storefronts along the streets had been adorned with festive red lanterns, each one with a small string dangling beneath it, ready for lantern riddles.","In the windy, post-rain weather, they swayed like blossoming branches showing off their beauty.","Aside from these most obvious decorations.","The restaurants had rolled out seasonal mooncakes, rice cakes, and other pastries.","Some of the larger restaurants on Kangning Street had even posted notices announcing poetry gatherings to be held on the day of the festival.","Fengchun Building’s notice, for instance, listed which great scholars or literary figures might be in attendance, as well as the prize for the poet who took first place.","The prize wasn’t something as vulgar as silver coins, but rather items like masterpieces by renowned artists or the Four Treasures of the Study.","Chen Yi glanced at it as he passed by, noting the crowd of interested young scholars and ladies, but he paid no mind to the prizes.","Naturally, the Dingyuan Marquis’s Mansion was also making its own preparations for the Mid-Autumn Festival.","Similar to the Old Marquis’s birthday celebration, there would be ancestral worship, a family banquet, and tests and rewards for the younger generation from their elders.","It was just that none of this had anything to do with Chen Yi, the live-in son-in-law.","Unless the Old Marquis or Xiao Jinghong personally gave the word, he didn’t even have the right to sit at the banquet table.","Of course, he had no desire to appear on such an occasion anyway.","Not only was the eating and drinking restrictive, but he would also have to deal with the various scheming members of the Xiao family. It was draining, both mentally and physically.","It was far more peaceful and comfortable to stay in Spring Lotus Garden.","But that aside, Chen Yi quite enjoyed the lively atmosphere as the festival approached.","The streets bustled with passersby.","Whether they were street vendors, strolling scholars and beauties, visiting merchants, Jianghu People, or even those from Exotic Races like the people of Poshisu Country, everyone on Kangning Street wore a smile as bright as a flower.","Of course, some smiles were beautiful in spirit, some in appearance, and some were literally as beautiful as flowers.","Chen Yi walked and watched, a smile on his face, but deep down, he knew the truth.","It would be difficult for the Xiao Family to have a truly festive Mid-Autumn Festival this year.","Even if everything went smoothly, after the incident with the Evil Demons from Bright Moon Building like Black Tooth, and the intervention of the Dingyuan Army’s Hidden Guards, the Old Marquis, Xiao Jinghong, and the other masters of the Xiao Family were likely in no mood to celebrate.","And if one also factored in Xiao Dongchen...","Chen Yi grimaced. ’It’s hard to say about the others,’ he thought with a wry smile, ’but the members of the Second Branch will definitely not be in a good mood.’","Even if his own schemes failed.","Lady Tiger and the Hawk would not let that Gray Wolf go."]},{"number":220,"title":"Chapter 220 - 192: Post-rain Reflections","paragraphs":["Not long after.","Chen Yi arrived at Guiyun Academy and headed straight for the residential courtyard in the back.","It wasn’t his scheduled day to teach, so Mr. Yue Ming and the others were a little surprised to see him.","But their initial surprise quickly gave way to them rising to greet him.","Mr. Yue Ming smiled and welcomed him. \"Qingzhou, you’re here. Have a seat.\"","Chen Yi glanced around. Seeing that besides Mr. Yue Ming and Mr. Zhuo Ying, Ma Guan was also present, he relaxed and took a seat.","He had been an Instructor at Guiyun Academy for some time now and was familiar enough with Mr. Yue Ming and the others to be casual.","\"Dean, so you ended up expelling Heming from the study hall after all?\"","Mr. Yue Ming’s smile froze. He glanced at Ma Guan, who was standing respectfully to the side, and gave an awkward laugh.","\"We have indeed wronged Heming.\"","\"So, after discussing it with him, I’ve decided to have him assist you with your lessons.\"","’Isn’t that just a teaching assistant?’ Chen Yi raised an eyebrow.","He looked at Ma Guan, then at Mr. Yue Ming who was frantically giving him meaningful looks, and couldn’t help but say with a slight pout, \"You certainly know how to put people to work, Dean.\"","\"Let’s get this straight first. It’s fine for Heming to stay at the study hall in this capacity, but you can’t have him work for free. You have to at least pay him some silver coins.\"","Mr. Yue Ming nodded. \"Of course. We’ll give Heming one mace of silver per month, a little less than you.\"","Upon hearing this, Ma Guan looked at Chen Yi, stood up, and bowed. \"Heming thanks you for taking me in, sir.\"","Chen Yi waved his hand. \"’Taking you in’ isn’t the right way to put it. It sounds improper.\"","\"Your Calligraphy Dao is accomplished now. Even if you don’t stay at the study hall, you could earn a good amount of silver just by writing for people every day.\"","Ma Guan was taken aback. \"I... I hadn’t considered that.\"","Chen Yi said noncommittally, \"Well, you can start thinking about it now.\"","\"Now that you’ve learned a skill, put it to practical use. Don’t suffer needlessly.\"","\"If not for yourself, think of your family. You can’t just have coarse grain buns and plain water for all three meals a day.\"","Ma Guan nodded thoughtfully. \"I will remember your teachings, sir.\"","Seeing this, Chen Yi shook his head inwardly. He knew the young man was fixated on etiquette and rules, so he didn’t say any more.","He then explained the purpose of his visit to Mr. Yue Ming.","\"When the study hall originally set its rules, I guessed many people would come to visit the Xiao Family or the academy, but I didn’t expect there would be this many.\"","\"So I thought of a Method to stop those interested in the Calligraphy Dao from bothering us, or at the very least, reduce their numbers.\"","Hearing this, Mr. Yue Ming and Mr. Zhuo Ying gave wry smiles. \"The academy gets even more visitors than the Xiao Family.\"","\"It’s not just people from Shu State. Academy Masters from several nearby State Capitals have also brought their students. We really do need to figure something out.\"","\"Qingzhou, what do you have in mind? Please, tell us.\"","Chen Yi then explained his idea, which had two main parts.","The first was to add more rules to the study hall, mainly introducing rules for elimination and withdrawal.","For example, students like Ma Guan whose Calligraphy Dao was accomplished would be considered to have graduated.","For instance, students with poor attitudes or conduct, or those whose progress in the Calligraphy Dao was too slow, would be expelled from the study hall.","Most importantly, a dedicated space should be found within the study hall and built to serve as a place for viewing calligraphy copies.","\"Although displaying my own Calligraphy Dao might make me seem arrogant and shameless, it’s the most effective way to solve our current problem.\"","Chen Yi paused, looked at the thoughtful expressions on Mr. Yue Ming and Mr. Zhuo Ying’s faces, and said with a smile:","\"So, you two, I hope you’ll take out the calligraphy copies I left behind from my previous lessons and place them in that ’exhibition hall’.\"","Mr. Yue Ming and Mr. Zhuo Ying exchanged a glance and shook their heads in unison.","\"That won’t do, that won’t do.\"","\"Since it’s specifically for people from the Outer States who have come to admire your calligraphy, it naturally has to be done in a grander and more orderly fashion.\"","Mr. Zhuo Ying chimed in, \"The Dean is right.\"","\"Among the visitors are many Confucian scholars who intend to enroll in the academy to study. It would be inappropriate to display certain calligraphy copies related to the curriculum ahead of time.\"","The two of them were in perfect sync, only discussing the layout of the \"exhibition hall\" and asking Chen Yi to write new calligraphy copies. They completely avoided mentioning the rules for admission and withdrawal from the study hall.","Clearly, in their view, those two rules would indeed reduce some of their troubles.","Chen Yi naturally understood their intentions. After a moment’s thought, he didn’t refuse.","\"However, besides me writing some pieces to put in there, you two gentlemen, and Heming, will have to write a few as well.\"","At his suggestion, not only the two Academy Masters, Yue Ming and Zhuo Ying, but even the ever-honest Ma Guan’s breath hitched.","\"S-Sir... I... I can too?\"","\"Of course you can.\"","\"This is called showcasing the results of the academy’s teaching. The three of you are all renowned masters with accomplished Calligraphy Dao.\"","Hearing this, Mr. Yue Ming said humbly, \"I couldn’t, I couldn’t. Our Calligraphy Dao is far too inferior to Qingzhou’s.\"","Mr. Zhuo Ying, being a bit more thick-skinned, agreed to it directly.","\"If they aren’t willing, then forget it,\" Chen Yi said. \"My calligraphy alone should be sufficient.\"","Yue Ming was taken aback, then glared at Zhuo Ying and said, \"Hold on, hold on! What are you planning, you scoundrel? Who said I wasn’t willing?\"","\"I just haven’t decided what to write to put inside.\"","Ma Guan didn’t dare refuse either, afraid of missing such an opportunity to make a name for himself.","Seeing that the three had agreed, Chen Yi added, \"Let me be clear. I’m only responsible for writing the pieces and making the suggestion. I’ll have to trouble you all to handle the setup and everything else.\"","Yue Ming had no objections and agreed.","\"Later, Zhuo Ying and I will draft a set of regulations to prevent the visitors from other regions from disturbing the Xiao Family and the academy.\"","After a bit more small talk,","Chen Yi didn’t stay long.","Seeing that he was about to leave, Mr. Yue Ming thought for a moment and said, \"For the Mid-Autumn Festival, the academy will be holding a poetry gathering.\"","\"At that time, I was wondering if it would be convenient for you to attend, Qingzhou?\"","Chen Yi shook his head. \"It’s not convenient.\"","Without waiting for any further persuasion, Chen Yi signaled for Ma Guan to see him out.","’A poetry gathering is even more trouble than a Xiao Family banquet. There’s no way I’m going to get involved in that kind of bustling event, which is both tedious and full of competitiveness.’","Seeing this, Mr. Yue Ming gave a wry smile. \"That’s Qingzhou’s personality, all right.\"","Mr. Zhuo Ying watched Chen Yi and Ma Guan walk away and said, \"Qingzhou isn’t like an ordinary scholar. He has little desire for fame or fortune.\"","Mr. Yue Ming nodded. \"Indeed.\"","\"In all my years at the academy, I’ve seen many scholars who thought themselves extraordinary. There are gentlemen like Heming, who revere the Confucian Dao and study the ways of the ancient sages, and there are also those like Huai’gu, who became famous at a young age.\"","\"More or less, they all chase fame and fortune, hoping to use what they’ve learned in an official career.\"","\"But with Qingzhou, I see none of that.\"","\"He is clearly a man of immense talent, with both solid knowledge and practical methods. If he were to become an official at court, he would surely bring great fortune to a region.\"","Mr. Zhuo Ying retracted his gaze and said, \"Perhaps it’s related to his status.\"","\"A live-in son-in-law, and one of the Xiao Family at that. If he were to become a court official, he would inevitably arouse the Xiao Family’s suspicion.\"","\"You and I both know that the Xiao Family is already struggling to manage its own affairs. They probably don’t want any more trouble brewing in the rear household.\"","Mr. Yue Ming sighed at this and murmured that it was a pity.","\"I previously heard from Ju Yi that Qingzhou had great ambitions in his youth, and he looked up to his father, Chen Xuanji, as a role model.\"","\"To have ended up in this situation is truly a shame.\"","Mr. Zhuo Ying said thoughtfully, \"Actually, I’ve always had my doubts about Qingzhou marrying into the Xiao Family.\"","\"He’s from the Jiangnan Prefecture Chen Family and has been exceptionally intelligent since childhood. Why would he be sent all the way to Shu State?\"","\"Even if the Chen Family wanted to form a marriage alliance with the Xiao Family, they could have chosen a less outstanding junior.\"","Mr. Yue Ming was slightly taken aback. After a moment’s thought, he said, \"Jiangnan Prefecture is thousands of miles from Shu State. I’m afraid it would be very difficult for us to uncover the reasons behind it.\"","\"However, I can write a letter to Ju Yi later and ask.\"","\"That seems appropriate...\"","Chen Yi didn’t hear their conversation. If he had, he would have definitely called the two old men busybodies.","’Even if they figured out the reason for my marriage, so what?’","’Could I run to Jiangnan Prefecture to question the Chen Family? Or convince the Xiao Family to let me become a court official?’","’Obviously not.’","Chen Yi and Ma Guan walked out of the academy together.","Before parting, Chen Yi said with a smile:","\"Since you’ve already agreed to help the Dean with my lessons, I can’t very well let you be idle.\"","\"Please give me your instructions, sir. I will certainly do my utmost.\"","\"From now on, you will grade the students’ Calligraphy practice books first, and then bring them to me.\"","Ma Guan hesitated. \"Grading the practice books is no problem, but I’m worried the other students will be dissatisfied.\"","Chen Yi glanced at him sideways and smiled. \"Great art finds few admirers. It’s been that way since ancient times.\"","\"Since you study the ways of the ancient sages and gentlemen, you should understand this principle, no?\"","Hearing this, Ma Guan paused for a moment, then took a deep breath and said, \"I have been taught a lesson.\"","Chen Yi grunted in acknowledgment. \"Don’t worry so much. If anything happens, the Dean and I will take care of it.\"","\"That’s all I have to say. Go on and attend to your own business. I hope to see your name on the list for the next provincial examination.\"","Ma Guan bowed with a grateful expression. \"I... thank you, sir.\"","Chen Yi patted his shoulder and left the academy with a smile.","Ma Guan watched him leave, standing there for a long time. He bowed once more before returning to the academy.","’If I, Ma Heming, can’t make the list for the provincial examination, I will have failed my teacher’s guidance.’","’It’s time to work hard.’","...","After leaving the academy, Chen Yi didn’t wander around outside and went straight back to Spring Lotus Garden.","He spent the entire day in his study without going out.","He didn’t even bother to check on the piece of Yellow-level Lower Grade intelligence that had appeared last night regarding an incident in South City Yanhua Lane.","Taking advantage of the rare free time,","Chen Yi used his Great Success Calligraphy Dao to transcribe various essays by ancient sages in preparation for the academy’s exhibition hall, while simultaneously deducing the follow-up to the \"burning of the Three Towns’ summer grain\" incident.","’From the looks of things...’","’At the Bright Moon Building, Black Tooth still trusts Lou Yuxue enough to put her in charge of the whole business.’","’I estimate that Lou Yuxue, Ge the Third, and the others will make their move on the Three Towns’ summer grain within five days.’","’News should arrive from that side tomorrow, or the day after at the latest.’","’Then there’s Xiao Jinghong.’","’She should have received the news already.’","’And judging by the silence within the Xiao Family, it’s easy to deduce that Xiao Jinghong must have gone directly to the Three Towns.’","’Either to investigate the whereabouts of the Hidden Guard Iron Banner Officer or to make some arrangements in advance.’","’In any case, she couldn’t possibly remain indifferent.’","’Then there are my own plans, concerning both Xiao Dongchen and Liu Wen.’","He had assessed all these scattered pieces of information in his mind.","The only uncertain point was whether he should go along on the day of the Bright Moon Building’s operation.","As Chen Yi pondered these things, his eyes fell upon the dozen or so calligraphy pieces he had written on his desk, and his movements paused slightly.","The next moment, he picked up his brush, dipped it in ink, and began to write on a newly spread sheet of Yunsong Paper, his strokes like a Painting.","\"Post-rain Reflections.\"","\"Leaving Baidi at dawn under rainbow-colored clouds, a thousand miles to Jiangling, I return in a single day. The cries of apes on both banks have yet to fade away, my light boat has already passed ten thousand mountains...\""]},{"number":221,"title":"Chapter 221 - 193: If Brother-in-law Is Unwilling, I...","paragraphs":["\"...my skiff has already passed ten thousand mountains.","—Chen Qingzhou, 21st year of the Anhe era, the fifth day of the eighth month.\"","Even before he signed his name, as the words of the poem took form,","Chen Yi’s Perfection Realm of Calligraphy Dao had already manifested.","Just like with his previous work, Farewell to Duke Changming in Shu State, a scene began to materialize above the words.","At first, a magnificent city with towering, pale gray walls appeared, standing atop a lofty mountain peak.","It was surrounded by radiant, colorful light and shrouded in mist. It was as if the first light of dawn after a storm had broken through the overcast clouds, bathing the city named \"Bai Di\" in a splendid, multicolored glow.","Then, a man in a long, white robe appeared, riding a boat that cut through the waves of the river flowing at the mountain’s base.","The river surged, the sails billowed, and the boat carried the man swiftly forward.","As he passed between the mountains, the noisy and chaotic cries of monkeys echoed from both banks, yet they could not drown out the sound of the small boat slicing through the water.","Nor could they obscure the man’s singing.","But before anyone could make out what he was singing, the small boat had already passed through a thousand-mile stretch of mountains and was gliding across a placid river.","Faintly, within the Calligraphy Dao Realm, one could see the man’s appearance—he looked almost identical to Chen Yi.","After a long moment, Chen Yi returned to his senses. A small smile touched his lips as he looked at the Mental Realm floating above the Yunsong Paper.","His expression was one of indescribable ease and freedom.","\"It seems I have my answer.\"","\"I’ll go. That’s all there is to it.\"","As the hidden troublemaker behind the scenes, it would feel incomplete if he didn’t go see the results of the \"burning of the Three Towns’ summer grain.\"","’It would probably be a regret,’ he thought.","With that, Chen Yi rolled up the sheet of Yunsong Paper, and the Mental Realm dissipated.","After tying the rolled Yunsong Paper with a red string, he glanced at a stack of scrolls on the side of his desk.","He counted them.","\"A total of twenty-one calligraphy scrolls. This should be enough for the academy’s ’exhibition hall.’\"","Chen Yi muttered to himself. He looked at the only piece written with his Perfect Calligraphy Dao, Post-rain Reflections, hesitated for a moment, then placed it on top of the stack.","He hadn’t originally planned to reveal that he had reached the Perfection Realm of Calligraphy Dao.","But just now, his mind had been preoccupied with the matter of the \"burning of the Three Towns’ summer grain,\" and he had subconsciously written Post-rain Reflections.","’Since it happened by chance, it must be fate. I don’t need to deliberately hide the fact that my Calligraphy Dao has reached Perfection.’","\"So what if it’s exposed?\"","\"The Hidden Guard wanted to see my calligraphy anyway.\"","\"Instead of letting them investigate and pass information in secret, I might as well display it openly myself.\"","Having made his decision, Chen Yi felt a weight lift from his mind and body. He stood up and stretched.","Then, he called for Xiaodie.","As he cleaned up the ink, brushes, paper, and inkstone on his desk, he instructed, \"Tomorrow, go to Kangning Street and hire a mounting craftsman. Have him bring his tools and do the work here in the garden.\"","Xiaodie looked at the stack of Yunsong Paper scrolls and nodded. \"Young Master, I’ll go first thing in the morning.\"","Chen Yi grunted in acknowledgment. \"Remember to tell them the quantity and dimensions for the mounting, so they can come fully prepared. We don’t want any delays.\"","Having the craftsman come to them was, one, to prevent the scrolls from being lost, and two, to prevent anyone from seeing their contents ahead of time.","After all, he wouldn’t have much free time in the coming days, nor would he be in the mood to write more scrolls.","Once everything was tidied up, Chen Yi took Xiao Wuge and Xiaodie to Jiaxing Garden for dinner.","By this time, Xiao Wan’er had already seen off all the day’s visitors and hadn’t kept anyone to stay for the evening meal.","It was quite peaceful.","During the meal, Xiao Wan’er naturally took out the booklet where she had jotted down notes about the Medical Dao Academy that morning, wanting to discuss some of her ideas with Chen Yi.","It was easy to see that she had put a lot of thought into it.","Every question she asked pertained to the finer details of the Medical Dao Academy.","For instance, \"compiling medical texts,\" \"the types of Medical Skills to be taught,\" and \"which Medical Saint Hand to invite.\"","The first two weren’t difficult for Chen Yi. His Medical Dao had already reached Great Success, and he was a Saint Hand who possessed the most extensive and comprehensive Medical Skills within that realm.","Among those at the same realm, if he claimed to be second, no one could claim to be first.","His ability to diagnose and treat difficult and unusual illnesses, in particular, and his knowledge of obscure Medical Skills, were unmatched by any other Medical Saint Hand.","So,","Chen Yi gave a few simple pointers, just enough for Xiao Wan’er to get the general idea and ensure she didn’t stray in the wrong direction.","\"As for which Medical Saint Hand to invite... why don’t we ask Ma Liangcai and the others later?\"","Chen Yi didn’t trust bringing in outsiders.","It wasn’t that he thought their Medical Skills were lacking, but he was worried their intentions might not be pure. If they didn’t see eye to eye with Xiao Wan’er, it would inevitably cause problems.","\"Ma Liangcai?\"","Xiao Wan’er had a moment of realization. \"Oh, I’d forgotten. While Doctor Ma isn’t a Medical Saint Hand, his master should be.\"","\"The Mid-Autumn Festival is approaching. I’ve had Cui’er prepare a small gift for him. When we invite him over tomorrow, he can take it back with him.\"","Chen Yi nodded and said with a smile, \"That’s very thoughtful of you, Wan’er.\"","’What has Old Ma done to deserve such a ’small gift’?’","’Hmm, looks like I’ll have to give Old Ma some more responsibilities.’","’It would be best to help him reach Minor Success, or even Great Success, in the Medical Dao. That way, he could properly oversee the Xiao Family Medicine Hall.’","’Otherwise, he won’t be worthy of the Mid-Autumn gift Xiao Wan’er is giving him.’","After they had finished their meal, Xiao Wan’er waited until the others had busied themselves before looking at Chen Yi and asking hesitantly,","\"Do you... have anything to do tomorrow?\"","Chen Yi looked at her. He could see she was a little nervous; beneath her cloak, he could make out the distinct outline of her hands clasped and fidgeting in front of her. He couldn’t help but smile.","\"I shouldn’t have anything planned for tomorrow.\"","\"Do you have something for me, Wan’er?\"","Xiao Wan’er met his gaze, then looked away a little unnaturally and shook her head slightly.","\"Miss Liu from the Liu Family just sent an invitation. She wants to meet me at Fengchun Building tomorrow at noon.\"","\"I was thinking, if you’re free, you could... you could come with me.\"","The smile on Chen Yi’s face faded slightly. \"Which Liu Family?\" he asked."]},{"number":222,"title":"Chapter 222 - 193: If Brother-in-law Is Unwilling, I...","paragraphs":["\"Liu Zhaoxue of the Jing State Liu Family.\"","Chen Yi’s brow furrowed at the name.","’That ruthless woman who’s involved with the Five Poison Sect?’","\"Did she give a reason?\"","Suspecting nothing, Xiao Wan’er took out the invitation and handed it to him.","\"The invitation is brief. It just says she wants to meet and clear up some misunderstandings.\"","Chen Yi nodded, opening the invitation to take a look. It said more or less what Xiao Wan’er had told him.","But just seeing the name \"Liu Zhaoxue\" as the sender was enough to make him suspicious.","After a moment of thought, the smile vanished from Chen Yi’s face. A possibility occurred to him—Liu Zhaoxue wanted to use Xiao Wan’er to murder Liu Wen.","He didn’t know the exact details.","But he knew her objective, and her plot to have Liu Wen killed.","For her to approach Xiao Wan’er at this time, Chen Yi could think of no other possibility besides laying the groundwork for her plot against Liu Wen.","Of course, he hoped he was just being cynical. But when dealing with a woman like Liu Zhaoxue—so consumed by greed that she would cooperate with the Five Poison Sect—he had to prepare for the worst.","Just then, Xiao Wan’er saw his expression and assumed he didn’t want to go. A hint of disappointment clouded her features.","\"If you don’t want to go, I can just go by myself.\"","She hadn’t asked Chen Yi to accompany her for any improper reason, like some sort of clandestine meeting.","It was simply because the Jing State Liu Family had previously mentioned a marriage alliance, which left her feeling wary and uneasy.","She figured having Chen Yi with her would help put her at ease.","Her words snapped Chen Yi out of his thoughts, and he smiled again.","\"Since you’re the one asking, I’d drop everything to go with you.\"","\"Besides, I don’t really have anything to do tomorrow anyway.\"","\"I just spaced out for a moment. I was thinking about the Jing State Liu Family’s Xinglin Hall. I recall they have several Medical Saint Hands in residence, and it occurred to me that once the Medical Dao Academy is established, we could invite them to offer some guidance.\"","Xiao Wan’er glanced at him. Seeing that he seemed perfectly at ease, she chided him playfully,","\"We haven’t even laid a single brick for the academy. Why are you already thinking so far ahead?\"","Perhaps because she had just misunderstood him, her chiding tone sounded a little sheepish.","Still, she’d gotten what she wanted. With Chen Yi accompanying her to Fengchun Building, she felt a little more at ease.","Just then, Xiao Wuge, who had overheard them, ran over. \"Sis, take me with you!\"","Xiao Wan’er thought for a moment and was about to agree when Chen Yi said with a smile,","\"You have your etiquette lessons tomorrow; you can’t afford to miss them.\"","\"Besides, I just told Xiaodie to ask a mounting artisan to come over tomorrow. You can help me keep an eye on them, so they don’t damage the calligraphy scrolls.\"","Xiao Wuge blinked, feeling as if his brother-in-law had become a different person. ’Shouldn’t he be sticking up for me right now? Why is he shutting me down?’","Xiao Wan’er, on the other hand, saw nothing wrong with it. It didn’t really matter to her whether Xiao Wuge went or not.","Instead, she was more concerned about the calligraphy scrolls.","\"You have new poems?\"","Chen Yi shook his head with a smile and then explained that he had asked Guiyun Academy to prepare an \"exhibition hall.\"","\"...This way, we should be able to reduce the number of unsolicited visitors.\"","Xiao Wan’er nodded in delight. \"That’s a great idea.\"","\"I thought...\"","Chen Yi picked up where she left off, teasing, \"You thought I’d come up with some mischievous plan?\"","Called out, Xiao Wan’er blushed. \"You’ve done so many strange things in the past. I was just worried...\"","She paused, then quickly changed the subject. \"But putting the calligraphy in the academy is certainly a good idea.\"","\"For one, it will allow visitors from other states to see your work, and for another, it will enhance the academy’s reputation.\"","’Most importantly, it will raise Chen Yi’s prestige in the eyes of the scholars.’","Xiao Wan’er didn’t say this last point out loud, only feeling happy for Chen Yi in her heart.","She might have been happy, but Xiao Wuge was pouting.","’I want to go to Fengchun Building, too!’","But the two of them just kept talking and laughing, not giving him a single chance to get a word in.","’Brother-in-law, you’ve changed.’","...","「As night fell.」","The daylight had just faded.","Chen Yi spoke briefly with Xiaodie and Xiao Wuge, then made an excuse about being tired and retired early to his room.","The moment he closed the door, Chen Yi changed into a set of Night Clothes, donned a bamboo hat, and slipped out of the Xiao Family residence through a back window, heading straight for Chuansi Street.","It wasn’t yet seven o’clock.","There were many pedestrians on the road, and it took him quite a bit of effort to avoid being noticed.","Fortunately, it wasn’t far. Before long, Chen Yi arrived at the house and had Zhang Dabao apply his disguise.","He had just finished changing into a brocade long-robe when Liu Lang arrived.","Before Chen Yi could speak, Liu Lang said with a smile, \"Boss, it’s done.\"","Chen Yi grunted in acknowledgment, calmly put away the Copper Mirror, and motioned for him to drive the carriage away from the house.","Liu Lang was also in disguise, looking nothing like his usual self from Hundred Herbs Hall. A ghastly scar now marred his face.","\"Boss, aren’t you worried he won’t show up?\"","Chen Yi sat straight-backed inside the carriage, watching the surging crowd outside through a gap in the curtains. He replied calmly,","\"It doesn’t matter whether he comes or not.\"","If Xiao Dongchen comes, things will go more smoothly.","If he doesn’t come, it will just take a bit more effort, but the result will be the same.","Liu Lang pursed his lips, clearly not understanding. ’If it doesn’t matter whether he comes, then why are we making this trip at all?’","After a moment of silence, Chen Yi spoke up. \"Tell me more about the Five Poison Sect.\"","Liu Lang froze for a second, glancing over at him. \"Boss, why are you...\"","Chen Yi cut him off. \"Tell me about the Five Poison Sect’s Cultivation Techniques, their dangerous methods, their history... Just tell me anything you know.\"","’I just hope I’m being paranoid,’ he thought."]},{"number":223,"title":"Chapter 223 - 193: If Brother-in-Law Is Unwilling, I...","paragraphs":["Liu Zhaoxue might not actually want to harm Xiao Wan’er.","But regardless of Liu Zhaoxue’s intentions, he had to take precautions to prevent any mishaps.","Fortunately, Xiao Wan’er still had Xie Tingyun and Shen Huatang by her side.","Even if the Five Poison Sect were to make a move, they probably wouldn’t try to assassinate her in broad daylight.","Liu Lang, unaware of Chen Yi’s thoughts, paused for a moment before beginning his detailed account.","\"The Five Poison Sect excels in Poison Skill and raising venomous creatures. I’ve heard that some of their potent poisons can kill an Upper Three Grades Martial Artist within a few breaths.\"","\"Furthermore, their hidden weapons are extremely special, comparable to the hidden weapons of the previous dynasty’s Tang Sect. Combined with their potent poisons, they pose a significant threat...\"","Poison Skill, poison, and hidden weapons.","Chen Yi silently committed this to memory, his mind racing as he considered various countermeasures.","The Poison Skill wasn’t a major concern. He had his Martial Arts and his Great Success Medical Dao, so even if he were poisoned, he could find a way to deal with it.","Poisons were even easier to handle; he himself had researched some poison formulas.","As for the last item, the hidden weapons...","Chen Yi looked at the night outside the window, muttering that he should get a sturdy, iron-ribbed Oil Paper Umbrella for Xiao Wan’er.","Liu Lang, unaware of his thoughts, finished his long-winded explanation. Seeing that Chen Yi hadn’t spoken, he couldn’t help but ask:","\"Boss, do you have a plan for the Five Poison Sect as well?\"","Chen Yi gave a noncommittal reply, \"Tomorrow, find someone to deliver a message to Granny Shan. Just say that the Five Poison Sect has reemerged in the Jianghu, has come to Shu State, and is plotting a great revenge.\"","\"...Boss, I appreciate your high regard for me, but I have no standing to speak with Granny Shan, nor can I find anyone to deliver a message to her.\"","Liu Lang was a Desert North Swordman who had only just arrived in Shu State a few days ago. How could he possibly have contact with a figure like Granny Shan?","Chen Yi considered this. ’He has a point,’ he muttered.","It seemed he would have to find a way to reach Granny Shan through Pei Guanli. In any case, he had to make sure the Mountain Race knew about the Five Poison Sect’s presence in Shu State first.","A short while later, the carriage stopped in an alley outside the East Market, near Jishi Medicine Hall.","The sky had completely darkened.","Most of the medicine halls, taverns, and inns had closed their doors for the night.","Few people passed by.","This made the alley all the more secluded.","They waited for about an hour.","As the Hour of Xu drew to a close, and with no one in sight, Liu Lang couldn’t help but say, \"Boss, I’m afraid he isn’t coming.\"","Chen Yi said nothing more, replying with a single word: \"Wait.\"","After nearly two more hours of waiting, as midnight approached, the faint sound of footsteps finally emerged from the silent shadows.","Liu Lang’s ears twitched, and he glanced over.","Chen Yi had noticed as well, but he did not leave the carriage, simply calling out coolly:","\"Your caution is admirable, Lord Xiao.\"","From the shadows, the figure paused, revealing the faint outline of a set of simple Night Clothes.","But from his features, it was easy to see that he was from the Xiao Family’s second branch: Xiao Dongchen.","He studied the distant carriage and asked in a hoarse voice, \"You aren’t Liu Wen? Who are you?\"","Chen Yi replied coolly, \"I am merely a pawn for my young master, a nobody.\"","\"I have come only to ask a single question of Lord Xiao on my young master’s behalf.\"","\"What question?\"","\"Does Lord Xiao wish to be a pawn for the Xiao Family, or does he wish to become the Patriarch of the Xiao Family?\"","Xiao Dongchen’s eyes flickered. \"What of being a pawn? And what of being the Patriarch?\"","\"If the former, I will leave at once. Lord Xiao can simply act as though I was never here today.\"","\"If the latter...\"","Chen Yi paused, a hint of a smile in his voice. \"Then I shall, of course, present Lord Xiao with a generous gift.\"","Xiao Dongchen frowned slightly, his mind reeling with suspicion.","After a moment of silence, Xiao Dongchen asked, \"Is your young master not afraid that I will report this to the Old Marquis?\"","Chen Yi chuckled. \"My young master would not have sought you out if he weren’t confident. Wouldn’t you agree?\"","\"...Tell me about this generous gift.\"","\"Three hundred thousand taels of silver.\"","At this number, it wasn’t just Xiao Dongchen whose breath caught in his throat; even Liu Lang, sitting at the front of the carriage, was stunned by Chen Yi’s sheer audacity.","’So that’s why the boss scammed three hundred thousand taels of silver from Liu Wen! It was all to lay a trap for Xiao Dongchen?’"]},{"number":224,"title":"Chapter 224 - 194: It’s You, Scoundrel?","paragraphs":["Three hundred thousand taels of silver!","Three hundred thousand taels?!","Even Xiao Dongchen, who had tempered himself for over a decade in the Governor’s Office and believed he had mastered the art of composure, felt his mind reel at the figure.","But with such a massive sum of silver, it wasn’t just him; even the two Governors would likely find it hard to control themselves.","However, that wasn’t all.","While Xiao Dongchen was still stunned, Chen Yi unhurriedly took out a flint and struck a light.","Then, he pulled a thick stack of silver notes from his robes and held it outside the carriage.","In the faint light of the flint, he dangled it brazenly for Xiao Dongchen to see.","\"As long as Lord Xiao agrees to join forces with my young master, these silver notes are all yours.\"","As Chen Yi spoke in a slow, deliberate manner, he gently fanned the stack of silver notes.","One by one, he revealed the stamp of the Great Wei Bank in the upper-right corner and the characters denoting their one-thousand-tael denomination.","Under the light of the flint, the stamp glowed a deep, dark red.","The sight of the silver notes instantly made Xiao Dongchen’s eyes redden, and his breathing grew heavy and rapid.","As the Assistant Governor of the Governor’s Office, he was often responsible for collecting taxes from the merchants and commoners of Shu State. He had handled, if not an overwhelming amount, at least over a million taels in silver notes.","He could naturally tell whether the silver notes were real or fake.","It took only a single glance.","With just that one look, Xiao Dongchen muttered, \"They’re... actually real...\"","In that moment, a thousand thoughts raced through his mind.","There was the Jing State Liu Family’s plan, their reason for seeking an alliance with him, and, most of all, the greedy desire to make that stack of silver notes his own.","But one thing he could now confirm—the man in the carriage was undoubtedly from the Jing State Liu Family.","After a long while.","Xiao Dongchen managed to calm himself and asked in a low voice, \"What does your young master want to achieve by joining forces with me?\"","Chen Yi didn’t answer immediately.","Instead, he first put away the stack of silver notes and blew out the flint, plunging the area inside and outside the carriage back into darkness.","Only then did he chuckle softly and say, \"Lord Xiao should be well aware of my young master’s intentions.\"","\"From the very beginning, his only wish has been to marry Miss Wan’er.\"","\"If Lord Xiao can help my young master achieve his desire, not only will these silver notes be yours, but my young master will also help you become the Patriarch of the Xiao Family.\"","Xiao Dongchen frowned slightly and said with hesitation, \"This matter... forgive me, but I cannot agree.\"","\"Does Lord Xiao have reservations? Or is it that you are incapable?\"","\"Both.\"","\"Xiao Wan’er is the eldest daughter of the main branch and is highly regarded by the Old Marquis. Furthermore, she is gravely ill. If she is unwilling, the Old Marquis will certainly not agree to your young master’s proposal.\"","Xiao Dongchen knew that if he got involved in this, directly or indirectly, he would attract the Old Marquis’s attention.","It would inevitably affect all his subsequent plans and arrangements.","Chen Yi was naturally aware of this and was not surprised.","After a brief pause, he continued, \"I believe there must be a way, wouldn’t you agree?\"","Xiao Dongchen’s heart stirred, and he began to calculate his options carefully.","A moment later, he suddenly spoke, \"If the Xiao Family were to suffer a great calamity and be in urgent need of silver coins, there might be a chance.\"","What he had in mind was the chaos that would surely erupt within the Xiao Family after the summer grain stores in the Three Towns were burned.","At that time, whether the Xiao Family could find the culprit would be a secondary concern. The first priority would be to solve the grain and fodder issue for the Three Towns.","If the Liu Family could provide a sum of silver coins or grain, perhaps the Old Marquis, in order to stabilize the Dingyuan Army, would agree to the marriage.","Upon hearing this, a cold smile played on Chen Yi’s lips.","This was exactly what he had been waiting for Xiao Dongchen to say.","\"I knew Lord Xiao was a man of great talent. You certainly won’t disappoint my young master.\"","With that, Chen Yi stepped down from the carriage, beckoned to Xiao Dongchen, and said with a smile, \"Come, I must trouble Lord Xiao to step this way.\"","Seeing this, Xiao Dongchen felt a sense of relief. He took a deep breath and walked over.","Getting closer, he saw Chen Yi’s face clearly and found him to be a handsome young man. He couldn’t help but praise him:","\"I can tell at a glance that you are a young man of remarkable talent. With your assistance, your young master is truly like a tiger that has grown wings.\"","Chen Yi bowed slightly and smiled, \"Lord Xiao, you flatter me.\"","\"To avoid any complications from delay, I must ask you, my lord, to follow me to another location for a more detailed discussion.\"","\"Once we’ve finished our discussion, I can hurry back and give my young master the good news.\"","Xiao Dongchen sized him up, his gaze sweeping over Liu Lang, and then he stepped onto the carriage first.","After the curtain fell, Chen Yi glanced left and right, then sat down next to Liu Lang and gestured.","\"The residence in the East Market.\"","Liu Lang grimaced and nodded, then cracked the whip against the horse’s rump, driving the carriage toward the residence in the East Market.","As they traveled, he kept glancing at the composed Chen Yi, his heart a turmoil of mixed emotions.","He asked himself honestly.","’If I were Xiao Dongchen, faced with the temptation of three hundred thousand taels of silver, I’d probably agree too, even knowing that Chen Yi has ulterior motives.’","’Besides, Xiao Dongchen was already scheming to become the Patriarch of the Xiao Family.’","Because of this, however, Liu Lang also understood why Chen Yi was targeting Xiao Dongchen.","If it weren’t the wrong time, he really wanted to ask Chen Yi about his true identity and why he was so dedicated to helping the Xiao Family.","Chen Yi, however, paid no mind to Liu Lang’s thoughts.","During the journey, he would occasionally exchange a few words with Xiao Dongchen.","This served two purposes: one was to keep him settled and prevent him from overthinking or backing out.","The other was to use the opportunity to speak well of Liu Wen—mostly about how Liu Wen had been smitten with Xiao Wan’er at first sight.","’If you’re going to put on a show, you have to go all the way.’","Before long, the carriage bypassed the East Market and arrived at a residence near South City’s Yanhua Lane.","Chen Yi gestured for Liu Lang to light the lamps and prepare paper and a brush, while he invited Xiao Dongchen into the main hall.","Just as he was about to speak, several lines of text floated before his eyes.","[Daily Intelligence - Profound-rank Lower Grade: At the fifth quarter of the Zi hour, west of Shu State City, a Hidden Guard from the Dingyuan Marquis’s Mansion will be pursued by the Evil Demonic Dao. A small amount of Opportunity can be obtained.]"]},{"number":225,"title":"Chapter 225 - 194: It’s You, Shameless Scoundrel!?","paragraphs":["Chen Yi glanced over, a flicker of surprise in his eyes.","’A Xiao Family Hidden Guard is being hunted by the Evil Demonic Dao in the western part of the city?’","’A Hidden Guard...’","His first thought was of the man in black wielding a long spear whom he had encountered in the West Market.","’And now he’s being hunted by Evil Demons...’","’Is this related to Black Tooth from the Bright Moon Building?’","’Did he find out about the plot to burn the summer grain in the Three Towns?’","Chen Yi frowned inwardly. While calculating the hour, he said impassively:","\"Lord Xiao, time is of the essence. I hope you’ll get straight to the point.\"","Xiao Dongchen had no objection. He was also worried that a delay could lead to unforeseen problems, so he began reciting the speech he had prepared on his way over:","\"The Xiao Family is currently facing two critical issues.\"","\"First, the Dingyuan Army’s monthly pay and provisions.\"","\"Second, the Mutual Market being built in cooperation with the Mountain Race...\"","Chen Yi listened quietly, recording Xiao Dongchen’s words with a brush and paper.","Xiao Dongchen was puzzled by this but didn’t dwell on it. He simply assumed Chen Yi was afraid of misremembering the details and being unable to give a proper report to Liu Wen.","Even when he spoke of \"burning the Three Towns’ summer grain\" and saw Chen Yi’s eyes light up, he didn’t give it a second thought.","\"If everything goes smoothly, your Young Master can use the chaos within the Xiao Family as an opportunity to press the issue. I believe there’s a good chance the Old Marquis will agree to this marriage.\"","When Chen Yi finished listening and writing, he set down his brush, clapped his hands, and said with a smile,","\"Truly, Lord Xiao. With your level of cunning and skill, you could become the Patriarch of the Xiao Family one day even without my Young Master’s assistance.\"","Xiao Dongchen replied noncommittally, \"You flatter me, Young Master Liu. I was merely speaking of a possibility.\"","\"After all, ’burning the Three Towns’ summer grain’ is no easy feat. With my capabilities, however... it’s not entirely impossible.\"","He knew full well that joining forces with the Jing State Liu Family was tantamount to making a deal with a tiger.","But there were two sides to every coin.","If he wanted to succeed, he would have to take some risks.","Chen Yi raised an eyebrow. \"Lord Xiao, if you have something to say, please speak freely.\"","\"I have some eyes and ears in the Dingyuan Army. If your Young Master is interested in pursuing this, I can lend a hand. It’s just...\"","Xiao Dongchen said, feigning difficulty, \"The cost in silver coins will be somewhat higher.\"","Chen Yi paused, then asked with a faint smile, \"Three hundred thousand taels isn’t enough?\"","Xiao Dongchen replied, \"To be frank, Young Master Liu, those brutes in the Dingyuan Army haven’t seen silver in a long time. They have huge appetites.\"","\"Three hundred thousand taels of silver may seem like a lot, but it doesn’t amount to much when split among certain people in the Three Towns.\"","\"Besides, I also need some silver coins to grease the palms of my superiors and other key individuals.\"","Chen Yi said, \"Lord Xiao, just tell me how much silver you need.\"","\"Another three hundred thousand taels.\"","As his words fell, silence descended upon the hall.","Chen Yi and Xiao Dongchen met each other’s gaze for a moment. Then, Chen Yi smiled, nodded, and wrote this new demand on the paper.","At the end, he added a line: \"This plan requires a total of six hundred thousand taels in silver coins. A deposit of three hundred thousand taels is to be paid upfront. Upon completion, the Jing State Liu Family will pay Xiao Dongchen an additional three hundred thousand taels of silver.\"","After he finished writing,","Chen Yi set down his brush, picked up the paper, blew the ink dry, and handed it to Xiao Dongchen.","\"Lord Xiao, please review this.\"","Xiao Dongchen took the paper and read it, his previously relaxed expression instantly shifting.","He looked at Chen Yi, hesitating. \"You... what is the meaning of this?\"","Chen Yi gestured for him to finish reading, then said with a smile, \"Lord Xiao, you’re asking a question to which you already know the answer.\"","\"My Young Master is putting up hard cash; he requires some assurance. Consider this your pledge of loyalty. Sign and leave your thumbprint at the bottom, and you can take the silver notes with you tonight.\"","As he spoke, he took out three hundred thousand taels in silver notes from his breast pocket and placed them on the table.","In the flickering candlelight,","the stack of silver notes seemed to gleam, shimmering as if they were made of pure silver.","It wasn’t just Xiao Dongchen whose gaze was drawn to them; Liu Lang was also staring intently at the stack of silver notes.","The two could even smell the faint, grassy fragrance of the paper and the subtle scent of the cinnabar seal paste.","Chen Yi, however, paid the stack of silver notes no mind. His eyes were fixed solely on Xiao Dongchen.","It was as if he didn’t value those silver notes in the slightest.","After a long silence,","Xiao Dongchen finally pulled his gaze away. He mused, \"In that case, it would be impolite of me to refuse.\"","Chen Yi smiled and nodded. \"That’s the spirit.\"","He then handed the brush to Xiao Dongchen and pushed a pre-prepared box of Seal Paste across the table.","Once Xiao Dongchen had signed his name and pressed his thumbprint,","Chen Yi confirmed that everything was in order. He folded the paper, put it away, and pushed the silver notes across the table. \"Lord Xiao, please take them.\"","Although Xiao Dongchen’s expression was somber, the sight of the stacked silver notes before him forced a smile to his lips.","\"Please thank your Young Master on my behalf.\"","\"Once this is done, if it is convenient for your Young Master, I will be sure to pay him a personal visit.\"","Despite his fine words, Xiao Dongchen’s hand couldn’t help but press down on the silver notes.","Feeling the smooth texture of the paper, the smile on his face became a little more genuine.","With this silver, he could accomplish a great deal.","He could raise a private army or buy off some of the Xiao Family’s collateral branches.","If he could leverage the power of the Jing State Liu Family to connect with Governor Liu Hong, his path as an official would be wide open. It might not even be impossible for him to take Yang Ye’s position.","In short, he believed the risk was worth taking.","Chen Yi didn’t bother trying to guess Xiao Dongchen’s thoughts. Seeing that it was getting late, he rose to his feet and said:","\"Lord Xiao, I must go report to my Young Master. Will you be returning on your own, or shall we two escort you?\"","\"It is three hundred thousand taels in silver notes, after all. If you were to be robbed on the way, you might suspect my Young Master of burning the bridge after crossing it.\"","Xiao Dongchen secured the silver notes and waved his hand with a smile. \"No need to trouble yourselves. I have my own methods.\"","Chen Yi raised an eyebrow but said nothing more.","After seeing Xiao Dongchen out of the residence, he and Liu Lang boarded their carriage and headed north.","「Not long after.」","Outside the now-empty and secluded residence, Xiao Dongchen’s figure emerged from the shadows."]},{"number":226,"title":"Chapter 226 - 194: It’s You, Shameless Scoundrel!?","paragraphs":["He glanced at the residence, then toward the direction the carriage had departed, and subconsciously touched his chest.","Even now, it still felt somewhat unreal.","’It felt like the 300,000 silver came too easily.’","But after waiting a moment without seeing anyone suspicious appear, Xiao Dongchen finally let out a sigh of relief.","\"It seems it was real.\"","\"Still, the Jing State Liu Family is truly generous.\"","Just then, a cold voice spoke from nearby:","\"Gray Wolf, this is the second time I’ve helped you. Don’t forget what you promised me.\"","Xiao Dongchen paused for a moment. He quickly cupped his hands and smiled. \"Rest assured.\"","\"Since I have already given you my word, I will naturally not go back on it.\"","\"First thing tomorrow morning, after I arrive at the Governor’s Office, I will transfer that merit to Assistant Governor Chen.\"","\"That’s for the best. I’m leaving.\"","\"Thank you.\"","Once the footsteps had faded into the distance, Xiao Dongchen glanced around before heading back to the Xiao Family.","A few moments later.","Two shadows dressed in Night Clothes appeared where Xiao Dongchen had just been.","Two pairs of cold, bright eyes scanned the surroundings before finally settling on the residence.","One of them pondered for a moment before ordering, \"Tomorrow, have someone look into the background of this residence.\"","\"Also, those two from earlier were quite strong. Send someone to contact Liu Wen and see if anyone around him matches their description.\"","The other person understood and asked, stunned, \"Young Lady, are you worried there’s a problem with those two?\"","\"Yes. I couldn’t hear their conversation, but I know they made some kind of deal.\"","She paused, then added, \"I find it very strange that Xiao Dongchen would trust what those two said—and even their identities—after meeting them just once.\"","\"In any case, it’s best to be cautious.\"","\"Yes, Young Lady.\"","...","Meanwhile, Chen Yi had no desire to dwell on Xiao Dongchen any further.","’From the moment he got Xiao Dongchen’s signature and thumbprint, Xiao Dongchen and his entire second branch were as good as dead in his eyes.’","’And the 300,000 silver could be considered a grand gift from him to the old master and the Xiao Family.’","’Or perhaps, a betrothal gift from him, the Xiao Family’s live-in son-in-law.’","’As for whether Xiao Jinghong or anyone else would acknowledge it later, that wasn’t his concern for now.’","However, it was clear that Liu Lang, who had witnessed the entire exchange, struggled to understand his actions.","\"Boss, did you really give him that money?\"","\"That’s 300,000 silver!\"","Even though he knew Chen Yi was setting a trap for Xiao Dongchen, what if something went wrong and that 300,000 silver was lost? Wouldn’t that be a terrible waste?","Chen Yi didn’t answer. He glanced at the sky outside and knew that the Xiao Family’s Hidden Guard was already being pursued by the Evil Demonic Dao in the West Market.","He thought for a moment, then instructed, \"Once we’re back on Chuansi Street, you’re coming with me to the West Market.\"","\"...\"","Liu Lang was completely baffled by him. Knowing he wouldn’t get an answer, he couldn’t help but grumble to himself.","’His boss was just too mysterious.’","’Fortunately, he already considered himself one of Chen Yi’s people and had no intention of making an enemy of him, so at least he didn’t have to worry about his own safety.’","Doubts aside, he still carried out his duties meticulously.","After he parked the carriage on Chuansi Street.","Chen Yi and Liu Lang hurried toward the West Market.","But before they even reached the outskirts of the West Market, a flash of light appeared in his vision.","[Opportunity +2]","[Evaluation: To not arrive at the place, hear the sounds, or see the scene, yet fail to seize an Opportunity that falls from the heavens, is the mark of a truly lazy person.]","Chen Yi stopped in his tracks. ’It’s already over?’","Just then, he saw several figures hurry past the entrance to a distant alley.","He could faintly hear their voices drifting over:","\"Do you think this could be that bastard who embarrassed us before?\"","A woman’s voice replied, \"It’s not him.\"","\"That man was clearly younger and excelled at the Fist Dao, not the Spear Dao.\"","Another person sighed. \"I guess you’re right...\"","\"All right, forget about that bastard. I’ll catch him sooner or later.\"","\"For now, let’s get this man to the inner prison at the Government Office. Then find a Physician to treat him. We absolutely cannot let him die.\"","\"Hundred Households Fang, he’s badly wounded. I’m afraid...\"","\"Just do as I say!\"","\"Yes!\"","’Fang Hongxiu?’","’Someone from the Imprisonment Department?’","Chen Yi paused for a moment, then signaled for Liu Lang to cover his face as they began to stealthily follow the Imprisonment Officers.","Though Liu Lang was unsure of his boss’s plan, he had overheard the Imprisonment Officers’ conversation, and a flash of eagerness appeared in his eyes.","Since ancient times, Jianghu People have always held the \"hunting dogs\" of the Imperial Court in contempt.","This was especially true for a Government Office like the Imprisonment Department, which recruited heavily from the Jianghu.","They would trip them up whenever they got the chance, and kill a few if the opportunity arose. In short, the two sides couldn’t stand the sight of each other.","Liu Lang was no exception.","’I wonder if the boss is planning to cause some trouble for these Imprisonment Officers. If he is... that would suit me just fine.’","Soon, Chen Yi led Liu Lang closer to Fang Hongxiu’s group and immediately spotted the black-clothed man they were supporting.","Seeing the Long Spear held by one of the Imprisonment Officers, he confirmed his suspicion—the man in black had to be one of the Xiao Family’s Hidden Guards.","He didn’t know how the man had fallen into the hands of the Imprisonment Department, but now was clearly not the time to dwell on it.","With that thought, Chen Yi leaped forward, landing in front of Fang Hongxiu’s group in the blink of an eye.","Liu Lang followed close behind.","Fang Hongxiu’s expression changed. She signaled for the Imprisonment Officers behind her to halt, then stared at Chen Yi and Liu Lang and demanded in a low voice:","\"Who goes there?\"","With his back still to them, Chen Yi glanced over his shoulder and chuckled.","\"A moment ago, Hundred Households Fang was just muttering about me. Don’t you recognize me now?\"","As he spoke, he mimicked her voice in a high-pitched, mocking tone, \"All right, forget about that bastard. I’ll catch him sooner or later.\"","\"Haha! Hundred Households Fang, who is it you’re planning to catch?\"","Fang Hongxiu’s eyes narrowed, and she gritted her teeth. \"It’s you! You shameless scoundrel!\""]},{"number":227,"title":"Chapter 227 - 195: Who I Am Is Not Important","paragraphs":["Shameless scoundrel?","Liu Lang glanced at Chen Yi and chuckled. \"Boss, she’s calling you names.\"","Chen Yi had heard her, of course. His eyes fixed on Fang Hongxiu and her group as he chuckled softly.","\"As the saying goes: ’Strangers the first time, acquainted the second, and sharing a bed the third.’\"","\"Hundred Households Fang, this counts as our third meeting. Why don’t we just be open about this?\"","\"Let me take that man, and you can all pretend tonight never happened. How does that sound?\"","Fang Hongxiu glared at him, gritting her teeth. \"You lecher! Don’t even think about it!\"","However, she knew she and her subordinates were no match for the man before them. She quickly gave an order:","\"Old Liu, take him back to the Government Office! The rest of you, with me!\"","The words had barely left her mouth when Fang Hongxiu drew the long blade from her waist and charged.","The other three Imprisonment Officers followed close behind her.","Only one more experienced-looking Imprisonment Officer tried to circle around with the man in black.","Seeing this, Chen Yi shook his head, saying nothing more.","After signaling Liu Lang with a raise of his hand to go after the prisoner, he turned to face Fang Hongxiu and the other Imprisonment Officers alone.","His Cultivation had now reached the Middle Sixth Grade. His Punch, Step, and Spear Daos had all reached Great Success, and even his Saber Dao was at the Minor Success Realm. He was on a completely different level than Fang Hongxiu and her officers.","It only took a single exchange.","Using the Wandering Dragon and Phoenix Step Technique, Chen Yi wove through the four of them. With his hand as a blade, he struck each of them on the back of the neck.","Fang Hongxiu and the other three collapsed to the ground without so much as a grunt.","On the other side, Liu Lang had done the same, knocking out Old Liu and hoisting the Xiao Family’s Hidden Guard onto his shoulder.","\"What now?\"","Chen Yi glanced around. \"Let’s head back first,\" he said.","He then led Liu Lang straight back to their residence on Chuansi Street.","Liu Lang laid the man in black on a table. He glanced at the man’s face, noting he was just an ordinary-looking, middle-aged man, then turned his attention to his injuries.","\"This guy’s lucky to be alive.\"","\"Three puncture wounds that went straight through him. One in the chest, one in the lower back, and one on his thigh. Tsk, tsk.\"","Chen Yi had no time for his commentary. He called for Zhang Dabao to bring the Silver Needles, then motioned for him to open the man’s shirt.","After observing the man with his Qi Observation Skill, he deftly placed four needles.","As his True Essence flowed, he used the technique of Controlling Needle with Qi to quickly staunch the bleeding, repair the man’s meridians, and accelerate the healing of his wounds.","After about an hour,","Chen Yi finally removed the Silver Needles. \"Bandage his wounds,\" he instructed.","Zhang Dabao hurried forward with a towel and gauze.","Seeing this, Liu Lang asked curiously, \"Boss, do you know who this man is?\"","Chen Yi put away his Silver Needles and sat back down, resting. He sized up the middle-aged man as he said, \"A Hidden Guard of the Xiao Family.\"","Liu Lang was a little surprised.","Hidden Guards, to put it simply, were Death Warriors trained by the Xiao Family.","Their Cultivation might not be exceptionally high, but their identities were always kept absolutely secret.","An ordinary person would be lucky to have even heard of them, let alone know one.","’It seems the boss’s status within the Xiao Family is quite high.’","As he mulled this over, Liu Lang asked, \"If he’s one of the Xiao Family’s men, wouldn’t he be safer in the hands of the Imprisonment Department?\"","Chen Yi shook his head. \"If I’m not mistaken, the people hunting him belong to the Evil Demonic Dao.\"","\"Black Tooth?\"","\"If Black Tooth had been the one to strike, this man would already be dead.\"","\"That’s true.\"","After a moment of thought,","Chen Yi’s brow furrowed slightly as he gave his next order. \"In a little while, I want you to go to the Spring Rain Building and wait there.\"","Liu Lang blinked. \"The Spring Rain Building?\"","\"Weren’t you just telling me last night to spend less silver there? Why now...\"","Chen Yi shot him a glare, cutting him off. \"A Hidden Guard from the Xiao Family was being hunted by the Evil Demonic Dao. That means he must have uncovered some information.\"","\"If I were Black Tooth and Lou Yuxue, I’d make my move tomorrow... or the day after, at the latest.\"","\"So, I need you to keep an eye on things for me at the Spring Rain Building. The moment you hear anything, have Wang Ji notify me immediately.\"","Liu Lang understood and nodded in agreement.","Chen Yi was about to say more, but he saw the middle-aged man’s eyelids twitch. Realizing he had regained consciousness, he simply said:","\"If you get the chance, find out where they’re keeping that thirty thousand taels of gold.\"","\"Be careful. Don’t let them notice you.\"","\"Don’t worry.\"","After Liu Lang had left the residence, Chen Yi turned his gaze to the middle-aged man pretending to be unconscious.","After a moment’s thought, he pulled a bottle of Immortal Drunk from his robes. He slowly twisted the stopper open, a smile on his face as he spoke:","\"I don’t have any ill will toward the Xiao Family. On the contrary, we’re on the same side.\"","\"But to keep those people from doing something desperate, the Old Marquis can’t know about this just yet.\"","Realizing he’d been found out, the middle-aged man’s eyes snapped open and he stared at Chen Yi.","Chen Yi was expecting this. He clamped a hand over the man’s face, bringing the open bottle of Immortal Drunk with it.","The middle-aged man realized the danger, but under the influence of the Immortal Drunk, his already grievously injured body grew even weaker.","After struggling for a moment, he managed to force out the question, \"Who... who are you...\"","Chen Yi chuckled. \"Who I am isn’t important.\"","He paused, then offered no further explanation, only a comforting word. \"Just get some sleep.\"","\"By the time you wake up, this whole affair should be settled.\"","The middle-aged man vaguely heard his words before losing consciousness completely.","’This man, this man... How can he act this way? The burning of the Three Towns’ summer grain is at stake!’","Chen Yi, of course, was unaware of the man’s thoughts. But now that all his plans and arrangements were in place, it wouldn’t do to have the Old Marquis intervene prematurely.","He then summoned Zhang Dabao and gave him instructions. \"Tomorrow, find a place with no connection to the Hundred Herbs Hall and get him settled there.\"","Zhang Dabao bowed in acknowledgement, then stepped forward to remove the disguise from Chen Yi’s face.","Chen Yi let him work, his mind already turning over other matters. He continued giving orders, \"Tell Wang Ji to find several other residences in the city.\"","\"Also, find everyone involved with the residence in the East Market. Have Wang Ji give them some silver and arrange for them to leave Shu State for a while.\"","Zhang Dabao committed each order to memory. But, being a young man, he couldn’t quite hide his concerns. He hesitated before speaking:"]},{"number":228,"title":"Chapter 228 - 195: Who I Am Is Not Important","paragraphs":["\"Boss, I have a question, but I don’t know if I should ask.\"","\"Go ahead.\"","\"You’ve done so much for the Xiao Family. Why do you have to hide yourself?\"","Chen Yi smiled. \"Some things are hard to explain.\"","If not for his identity as a \"Fledgling\" of the Hidden Guard, he could certainly be more open about things.","Otherwise, if the Old Marquis, Xiao Jinghong, and the others found out what he’d done, it would inevitably arouse their suspicion.","Even if he had no intention of cooperating with the Hidden Guard, the Xiao Family would be wary of him.","It wasn’t a matter of trust.","It was simply human nature.","Chen Yi changed his clothes. He instructed Zhang Dabao to stay at the residence for the next couple of days and await his call. After that, he set off for the Xiao Family estate.","A confused look remained on Zhang Dabao’s face as he watched Chen Yi walk into the distance.","He thought it over from every angle, scratching his head as he walked toward the main hall and muttered to himself:","\"My master was right.\"","\"The Great Wei Dynasty is teeming with extraordinary individuals. The abilities of some of these immortal-like figures are far beyond what anyone could imagine.\"","\"If you ever meet someone like that, you either steer clear and never cross them, or you latch on for dear life. That’s how you guarantee a lifetime of wealth and glory.\"","After muttering for a bit, Zhang Dabao let out a foolish chuckle.","\"Looks like my luck is a damn sight better than my master’s.\"","A short while later, Chen Yi returned to Spring Lotus Garden. He shed his black, coarse-spun clothes, changed into a light robe, and lay down on the bed.","He was, of course, unaware of Zhang Dabao’s thoughts. He simply took out the document detailing the \"plan\"—the one Xiao Dongchen had signed and pressed his fingerprint on—and read it over twice.","As he read, Chen Yi let out a soft laugh.","’Now, we’ll see if my lady and I are on the same wavelength.’","As long as Xiao Jinghong was on her guard, he was certain Black Tooth and his men couldn’t possibly succeed.","His only worry was that Tiger Girl might not have delivered the letter.","If that was the case, he’d just have to accept it.","Fortunately, even if the summer grain of the Three Towns were to be burned, the Xiao Family had already gotten three hundred thousand taels of silver from Xiao Dongchen, enough to handle any subsequent trouble.","In fact, from the very beginning, Chen Yi had only wanted to get some silver coins from Black Tooth at the Bright Moon Building to lure Xiao Dongchen into a trap.","But before he could even put his plan into motion, people from the Jing State Liu Family arrived.","Worse, Liu Wen and his men had targeted Xiao Wan’er.","Left with no choice, Chen Yi had to put in more effort to devise his \"one stone, three birds\" strategy.","First, to frame Liu Wen and lead him into a trap.","Second, to frame Xiao Dongchen and make him take the bait.","And third, to leave the Xiao Family with a safety net, providing a remedy in case his plan fell through.","As Chen Yi mulled this over, he sat cross-legged on the bed and began to cultivate the Four Symbols Skill.","Then, strands of the Heaven and Earth’s Spiritual Mechanism surged into his body from all directions, transforming into rushing True Essence.","Steadily increasing his Cultivation.","In the unseen workings of fate, a thought flickered through Chen Yi’s mind. ’It’s time for this to end.’","...","「Cang Lang Town.」","It was a military town south of Shu State Prefecture City, near Mengshui Pass. It had been established to provide the fastest possible support to Mengshui Pass in its defense against the Barbarian Race.","It commanded thirty-two garrisons with a total of 160,000 men—more than the forces of the Profound Armor and Iron Wall towns combined.","It was of the highest strategic importance.","Thus, as the General of Cang Lang Town and its Border Defense Commander, Pang Xuan had been keenly aware of his immense responsibility from the moment he took command.","He rose every day at three in the morning and did not go to bed until eleven at night.","He drilled both new recruits and veteran soldiers, oversaw the military farms, supervised the construction of defensive fortifications, inspected the armories and warehouses, and patrolled every corner of the military town.","He never dared to be negligent.","Recently, however, with the Mid-Autumn Festival approaching and the summer grain safely in storage, the pressure within Cang Lang Town had eased considerably. Pang Xuan couldn’t help but let his guard down a little.","He slept in for an extra hour compared to his usual routine.","It wasn’t until nearly five in the morning that he finally rose to prepare for his inspection of the camp.","Pang Xuan, fully dressed, tidied his beard and hair in the copper mirror while calling out, \"Lu Lin, bring a basin of hot water.\"","Soon after, someone pushed the door open and entered. The person placed a porcelain basin on its stand, picked up a towel, dipped it in the water, wrung it out twice, and then handed it to him.","Pang Xuan took the towel and began to wipe his face, but his movements abruptly froze. \"You’re not Lu Lin?\"","Lu Lin was his Personal Guard, a notorious chatterbox who would never have been this silent.","When there was no response, Pang Xuan’s body tensed in cautious alert. He slowly lowered the towel, his eyes fixed on the reflection of the person behind him in the copper mirror.","He saw only a figure wearing a long robe, a long sword at their waist, and a bamboo hat.","\"Who are you?\"","\"Who do you think?\"","As the cool, detached voice sounded, Pang Xuan watched the visitor remove their bamboo hat, revealing a face covered by a half-armor mask. He spun around and said, astonished:","\"General Jinghong?\"","The visitor was indeed Xiao Jinghong, who had left the Wu Mountain Mutual Market two days ago.","Seeing that Pang Xuan had recognized her, Xiao Jinghong dropped the air of mystery. She walked directly to the desk, sat down, and placed her identity token on the tabletop.","Pang Xuan glanced at the token, confirming her identity. He immediately stepped forward, dropped to one knee, and saluted.","\"This humble general, Pang Xuan, pays his respects to General Jinghong!\"","\"Sit. Let’s talk.\"","\"Yes, General!\"","Pang Xuan sat down carefully across from her, his mind swirling with questions.","’Xiao Jinghong had clearly sent word that she would inspect the Three Towns *after* the Mid-Autumn Festival. So why was she here in Cang Lang Town now?’","’And in disguise, no less, looking as though she didn’t want anyone to know of her presence?’","’All signs pointed to only one conclusion: something major was about to happen!’","Having served as the General of Cang Lang Town for many years, Pang Xuan was at least that perceptive.","Xiao Jinghong could naturally sense his unease. After putting away her token, she said in a level voice,","\"I’ve come for one reason only.\"","As she spoke, she retrieved the note she had received from Pei Guanli, placed it on the table, and pushed it toward him.","\"I’ve received intelligence that someone plans to burn the summer grain of the Three Towns.\"","\"What? Burn the summer grain?\"","Pang Xuan’s expression hardened instantly. Without asking any more questions, he snatched the slip of paper and began to read.","When he finished, he suppressed the rage boiling in his heart and forced himself to review the layout of Cang Lang Town’s Summer Grain Storage Room in his mind.","’He now understood why Xiao Jinghong had come in secret—she clearly wanted to root out the villains hiding within each of the border towns.’","After a moment of silence, Pang Xuan couldn’t identify any vulnerabilities in Cang Lang Town’s grain storage, and he relaxed slightly.","\"General Jinghong, are you certain this intelligence is reliable?\"","\"After all, this ’Sword Madman’ is from the Jianghu. He probably doesn’t understand how heavily the Three Towns guard their grain.\"","\"Never mind some heretic from the Evil Demonic Dao; even for someone on the inside, burning that grain would be no easy task.\"","Xiao Jinghong was well aware of this. She proceeded to explain why she trusted the words of the \"Sword Madman,\" Liu Lang.","She concluded, \"Although my secret inspections of the Three Towns’ deployments these past two days have revealed nothing unusual, it’s better to be safe than sorry.\"","\"If the grain in any of the Three Towns is lost, neither you nor I can escape the blame.\"","After listening, Pang Xuan nodded. \"Your point is well taken, General. This humble general will strengthen our defenses immediately.\"","But to his surprise, Xiao Jinghong shook her head. \"Make it appear tight on the outside, but keep it lax on the inside.\"","Pang Xuan understood at once. His expression turned serious. \"This humble general will obey!\"","’He understood. Xiao Jinghong was planning to see just who was hiding within the army. She wanted to lure them out and catch them all in one fell swoop.’","After a moment of thought, he said, \"There are only a few days until the Mid-Autumn Festival. Perhaps the General could wait here?\"","Xiao Jinghong gave a slight nod. \"That was my intention.\"","Cang Lang Town had the most soldiers and the most grain. As long as nothing went wrong here, there would be room to maneuver even if chaos erupted in the other two towns.","However, before coming here, she had given her orders to Li Changqing and Ma Kui as well: any failure would be met with military justice!","After some brief conversation, Xiao Jinghong had Pang Xuan find her a residence close to the Summer Grain Storage Room.","After a brief rest, she sat cross-legged on the bed. With one ear, she listened for any sounds from the vicinity of the storage room, while with her hands, she took out a few letters from her robes and began to read.","She had been rushing between the Three Towns for days without a moment’s rest, and hadn’t yet found time to read the letters from Xiao Wan’er and Chen Yi.","Fortunately, none of the Three Towns’ generals had shown any signs of treason, which put her mind at ease somewhat.","Xiao Wan’er’s letter was much like her previous ones, mostly detailing happenings at the family estate.","The only thing of note was that Old Master Sun Fu had departed for Jinling, and that before he left, Chen Yi had written a poem for him.","’However, I didn’t get the full poem. I only remember a couple of lines: \"Don’t worry that you’ll have no soulmates on the road ahead; is there anyone under Heaven who does not know of you?\" I imagine Elder Sun was quite pleased.’","Xiao Jinghong silently recited the lines a few times, a flicker in her eyes.","Even without knowing the full poem, that couplet alone was enough to reveal its quality—it was undoubtedly a masterpiece.","Next, Xiao Jinghong opened Chen Yi’s letter, reading it carefully line by line.","’My Lady, please do not be upset by my hasty scrawl. Time was short, but I wanted to express my thoughts:","Thoughts of Summer","The blazing sun steams the clouds, the cicadas’ drone is wild.","Leaves of the wellside tree curl up, hidden in the afternoon shade.","I long to fashion a cool mat of ice to send with this silk-written word,","But fear that where you are, my lady, there is no such coolness to be had.’","After reading the letter, Xiao Jinghong carefully folded it away. A faint smile touched her lips. ’Compared to his previous ’Thoughts of a Summer Night’ poems, this one is indeed a bit hasty.’","Nevertheless, her mood had brightened considerably."]},{"number":229,"title":"Chapter 229 - 196: Flustered Xiao Wan’er","paragraphs":["The next day, the weather was clear and bright.","It was just past mao hour, and the rising sun already revealed the full might of the dog days of summer.","The brilliant sunlight bathed Shu State Prefecture City in a bright, clear light.","There were the bustling East and West Markets, the refined Kangning Street, the solemn and stately South Street Government Office Gate, and the graceful women of South City’s Yanhua Lane.","Perhaps because the Mid-Autumn Festival was approaching, everyone from common folk and merchants to government officials wore smiles on their faces.","Xiaodie was no exception.","She had woken up bright and early today. After tidying up a bit, she had the carriage driver take her to Kangning Street to hire a master from a mounting shop.","This mounting master was no stranger—it was the shop owner himself, along with two of his assistants.","The owner’s surname was Dai, with the given name Nian.","He was quite familiar with Chen Yi, who was a regular customer.","Xiaodie quietly led him to the study in Spring Lotus Garden.","Dai Nian looked around at the study’s furnishings, offered a few words of praise, and then asked, \"Miss Xiaodie, which calligraphy pieces are to be mounted?\"","Xiaodie pointed to the stack of Yunsong Paper on the desk. \"These.\"","\"That’s quite a few. How many scrolls?\"","\"There are... Let me count.\"","As she spoke, Xiaodie counted them one by one. \"One, two... Boss Dai, there are twenty-one scrolls in total.\"","Dai Nian noted the number, then began unrolling each scroll to measure its dimensions and prepare his tools.","With each one he measured, he made a note and commented on Mr. Qingzhou’s excellent calligraphy.","She didn’t need him to tell her whether it was good or not.","Xiaodie knew perfectly well.","But right now, her little face was tense, as if worried Dai Nian might try some funny business.","She clearly hadn’t forgotten the incident when a calligraphy piece had been lost at the mounting shop.","Fortunately, Dai Nian was oblivious to her thoughts; otherwise, he would surely be wailing and crying foul.","He recorded twenty scrolls in a row. Then it was time for the last one.","The moment Dai Nian took it, he sensed something different. He hefted it a couple of times and couldn’t help but mutter to himself, ’This one’s a considerable size.’","But when he unrolled the Yunsong Paper and saw the light and the Mental Realm materialize, his expression instantly went slack with shock.","\"This... this is...\"","Dai Nian’s eyes widened, and he nearly buried his face in the scroll, unable to finish his sentence.","Xiaodie also saw the Mental Realm on the poem, but she clearly didn’t understand its significance. She just thought the poem was good and the image was beautiful.","Especially at the end of the Mental Realm, when she saw the figure sailing a boat past ten thousand mountains, she couldn’t help but smile and say:","\"The Young Master is truly the Young Master. The poem is good, and the calligraphy is wonderful.\"","\"He even wrote himself into the poem.\"","Dai Nian, who hadn’t heard a word, asked with a tremble, \"M-Miss Xiaodie, was this... was this really written by your Young Master?\"","Xiaodie gave him a strange look. \"Of course my Young Master wrote it.\"","Then, she grew wary and asked, \"What are you planning? You’re not thinking of swapping it for a worse one again, are you?\"","Dai Nian’s hands trembled so hard he nearly dropped the scroll.","’Good heavens,’ he thought, ’this is a calligraphy piece at the Perfection Realm of Calligraphy Dao! I wouldn’t dare tamper with it even if you gave me ten times the nerve!’","’Even if I had the idea, I wouldn’t have the skill to pull it off.’","’Forget me—in the entire Great Wei Dynasty, there are probably only a handful of people who could create a forgery of this scroll convincing enough to pass for the original.’","As these thoughts raced through his mind, Dai Nian tremblingly rolled up the scroll and solemnly promised:","\"Rest assured, I swear on my life, I will absolutely, absolutely use the finest auxiliary materials and the best techniques to mount this scroll.\"","You have to understand, not his master, not his master’s master... no one in his lineage for eight generations back had ever mounted a calligraphy piece from the Perfection Realm of Calligraphy Dao.","To be able to mount a scroll of such a Realm in his lifetime—his life would not have been lived in vain.","Only then did Xiaodie nod in satisfaction. \"That’s good.\"","\"In any case, you can’t make any mistakes this time. If you damage it, I... I... the residence has Armored Warriors to give you a beating with a plank!\"","\"Rest assured, rest assured...\"","「The sun was high in the sky.」","As Xiaodie helped him get up, dress, and wash, Chen Yi heard the sounds from the study downstairs and casually asked:","\"How many have been mounted?\"","When she heard his question, Xiaodie puffed out her cheeks and said, \"He’s only just finished one.\"","\"Young Master, that man is so strange.\"","\"How so?\"","Xiaodie chattered on for a while before finally saying:","\"When I invited him over this morning, he clearly brought two apprentices with him, but when it was time to start, he was the only one working. Don’t you think that’s strange?\"","Chen Yi chuckled, guessing that the mounting shop’s owner must have seen the Calligraphy Dao Realm in \"Post-rain Reflections\" and didn’t want to entrust the work to others.","\"Slow is fine. As long as they’re all mounted before the Mid-Autumn Festival, it’s okay.\"","\"Young Master, I’ll be sure to keep an eye on him for you.\"","\"There’s no need to be so tense...\"","Amid their lighthearted banter, Chen Yi finished getting dressed.","Because he was accompanying Xiao Wan’er to Fengchun Building today, he had deliberately changed into a suit of brocade clothes.","A navy-blue, silk long-robe felt as light as air, worn over a pure white inner shirt, with a gold and jade-adorned belt at his waist and matching navy-blue boots.","He naturally exuded an air of nobility.","However, Chen Yi’s usual disposition was lazy and listless. Even if he put on airs, which was enough to carry the outfit, he still seemed somewhat frail and scholarly.","Xiaodie, however, looked him up and down and saw none of that.","She only felt that once the Young Master changed into these clothes, he was the most handsome man in the world.","As she sized him up, her face unconsciously grew a little hot, and she quickly said:","\"Young Master, please have a seat. I’ll go prepare something for you to eat.\"","Seeing her turn and leave as soon as she finished speaking, Chen Yi was slightly taken aback, but he didn’t think much of it.","However, after studying his reflection in the Copper Mirror for a few moments, he hesitated slightly, then took a deep breath. His expression immediately became calm and composed.","In the next moment, the listlessness about him vanished, replaced by a burgeoning noble aura. Even the sense of frailty and weakness mostly disappeared.","He looked just like a young nobleman from one of the great Noble Families.","Chen Yi glanced at his reflection a few more times, a smile playing on his lips. ’I guess you could call this a talent, too.’"]},{"number":230,"title":"Chapter 230 - 196: The Flustered Xiao Wan’er","paragraphs":["Of course it did.","It wasn’t just his current change in temperament. When he had previously disguised himself as men like Liu Wu and Black Tooth, his expressions, movements, and even the look in his eyes had been uncannily lifelike.","No one else could spot a single flaw.","He ate a couple of pastries.","Chen Yi went to the study to check on the mounting progress. The second piece of calligraphy had just been finished.","When Boss Dai saw him approaching, his previously mercenary attitude was gone. He bowed and spoke with great solemnity, as if this wasn’t merely a mounting job but a matter of life and death.","He was most likely thanking him for letting him handle that piece of calligraphy.","Chen Yi smiled, offered a few words of reassurance, and then told Xiaodie to stay and assist before leading Xiao Wuge toward Jiaxing Garden.","Xiao Wuge went reluctantly.","He clearly hadn’t forgotten that Xiao Wan’er and Chen Yi had refused his request yesterday.","\"Brother-in-law, can I come with you to Fengchun Building?\"","Chen Yi’s refusal was blunt. \"No.\"","Xiao Wuge was exasperated. \"Brother-in-law, you were always on my side before. Why won’t you help me this time?\"","’He just wanted to slack off; he didn’t want to go to his etiquette lesson!’","Chen Yi patted the boy’s head and said with a smile, \"It’s not that I won’t help you, but the circumstances are special.\"","\"What’s so special? Is there a problem with Sister Liu from Jing State? Her family is definitely bad news.\"","Seeing that Xiao Wuge had more or less guessed the truth, Chen Yi avoided a direct answer, simply offering a vague platitude to comfort him:","\"The Mid-Autumn Festival is in a few days. I’ll take you out to have some fun then.\"","\"You promise?\"","\"A gentleman never goes back on his word.\"","Perhaps she had overheard their conversation, because Xiao Wan’er, who was already waiting in Jiaxing Garden, smiled as soon as she saw them and asked:","\"What’s this about a gentleman’s word?\"","Before Chen Yi could reply, Xiao Wuge chimed in, wise beyond his years, \"That’s a secret between me and my brother-in-law. Right?\"","Chen Yi chuckled and nodded, spreading his hands toward Xiao Wan’er. \"The Young Master has spoken. I dare not disobey.\"","Hearing this, Xiao Wan’er looked at Xiao Wuge with mock reproach. \"So you’re all buddy-buddy with your brother-in-law now? Have you forgotten who used to take you out to play every Mid-Autumn Festival?\"","\"Big Sister, times have changed.\"","\"Oh? I was your sister last year, but I’m not today?\"","\"That’s not...\"","\"Hm?\"","\"Yes! No, I mean... Ow! Big Sister, you’ll pull it off! Brother-in-law, help, help, help...\"","Given their strong sibling bond, Chen Yi, the \"outsider,\" certainly wasn’t going to intervene.","Only after Xiao Wuge had been sent off to the study with his etiquette tutor did Xiao Wan’er signal for Chen Yi to leave with her.","Before long, a carriage departed from Jiaxing Garden. It left the Marquis’s Mansion and turned onto Kangning Street.","Chen Yi and Xiao Wan’er sat side-by-side inside the carriage. Up front, the fellow disciples Shen Huatang and Xie Tingyun were at the reins.","However.","Perhaps because she was alone in an enclosed space with a man, Xiao Wan’er had kept her head lowered ever since getting into the carriage.","Beneath her red cloak, her hands rested in her lap, her fingers twisting together without her realizing it.","She knew she ought to say something.","The silence in the carriage was becoming oppressive. It would make Chen Yi think something was wrong, and besides, it wasn’t like her to be so quiet.","But every time she thought of something to say, the words died on her lips.","Perhaps she worried she wasn’t prepared and her tone would sound forced.","Or perhaps she feared that any topic she chose would be too dull and only make the atmosphere more awkward.","And so, Xiao Wan’er’s head sank even lower, leaving only her bright eyes visible, staring at the tips of her shoes.","「A moment later.」","Xiao Wan’er puffed up her cheeks, then quietly tilted her head. She glanced at Chen Yi out of the corner of her eye and saw him looking out the window, which made her relax slightly.","’At least he didn’t notice my fidgeting.’","But her relief was tinged with a hint of resentment.","’Why won’t he say anything?’","Chen Yi, of course, had no idea what she was thinking. He had lifted the curtain and was studying the scene outside.","It wasn’t that he was intentionally avoiding conversation; as the carriage sped along, he had noticed something unusual about the streets.","For example, just after leaving the Marquis’s Mansion, they had passed more than twice the usual number of City Guard Army soldiers.","Just off Kangning Street, several Imprisonment Officers were scrutinizing pedestrians.","On top of that, various ranks of government officials were periodically stopping people for questioning.","As they passed, Chen Yi faintly overheard snippets of conversation.","\"...Last night, some men from the Imprisonment Department were taken down again. Lord Thousand Households is furious...\"","\"...Several Evil Demons spotted outside the West Market. We can’t let them escape...\"","\"...The Mid-Autumn Festival is almost here! Tighten security!\"","Chen Yi put the pieces together. He thoughtfully lowered the curtain.","He now had a rough idea of the current situation.","He turned his head, about to say something, but froze when his eyes met Xiao Wan’er’s playfully resentful gaze.","\"Big Sister, what’s with...\"","Startled at being caught, Xiao Wan’er jumped. Before he could finish his sentence, she turned her head away and cut him off in a flustered rush.","\"I, I... I was just looking at all the people on the street.\"","\"The Mid-Autumn Festival is almost here. Second Sister should be coming back, and Grandfather, and Wuge...\"","She herself barely knew what she was saying.","She was just trying to act casual.","Unfortunately, her attempt backfired. After just a few sentences, her face was beet-red with mortification, and she wished she could be anywhere but in that carriage—perhaps even under it.","Chen Yi had been watching her with an amused smirk, but when he saw how red her face had become, he knew he had to say something. If he didn’t, he was liable to embarrass her so badly her old ailment would relapse.","\"Never mind the Mid-Autumn Festival for now. I see you’ve prepared gifts for Miss Liu today, Big Sister. What are they?\"","His simple questions were enough to get Xiao Wan’er’s blank mind working again.","She paused, putting a stop to her earlier rambling, and replied softly, \"Some personal effects for a lady’s chambers, like a rouge box and so on.\"","The words were barely out of her mouth when Chen Yi said, \"Wow.\"","\"Big Sister, you truly are as wise as you are beautiful—so well-read, so proper, and so thoughtful. That level of consideration...\"","He was clearly running out of compliments and just forcing it."]},{"number":231,"title":"Chapter 231 - 196: Flustered Xiao Wan’er","paragraphs":["It was, however, remarkably effective.","The blush on Xiao Wan’er’s face faded visibly. She couldn’t help but protest, a mix of embarrassment and annoyance in her voice.","\"Brother-in-law, what are you talking about?\"","Chen Yi gestured ahead, saying mischievously, \"I imagine Miss Liu from the Liu Family won’t be quite as expressive as you are, Sister.\"","Xiao Wan’er understood his gesture and playfully swatted at him.","Still, she knew he was just clowning around to help her calm down.","And so, she did something quite out of character for her—she gave him a cute eye-roll.","\"Sister Zhaoxue seems to have excellent manners. That last time...\"","After a bit more small talk, Xiao Wan’er regained her usual poise, though a trace of bashfulness lingered in her heart.","It was likely because she had shown a side of herself to Chen Yi that was different from her usual self, stirring up the complicated feelings of a young woman.","Chen Yi, however, didn’t think too much of it. ’He just felt that this side of Xiao Wan’er was more real.’","’If she always acted like an ethereal fairy, untouched by the mortal world, how could she ever appreciate its lively chaos?’","Before long, the carriage stopped outside Fengchun Building.","Chen Yi followed Xiao Wan’er out of the carriage. As he scanned the surroundings, he spotted two other carriages parked to one side.","Both had ornate canopies and magnificent carriage bodies, with family crests hanging from their curtains.","When he recognized the crests, Chen Yi discreetly raised an eyebrow.","’Two carriages from the Liu Family...’","’Besides Liu Zhaoxue, has Liu Wen come as well?’","’Or could it be the pillar of the family’s second branch, Liu Yu?’","Chen Yi gazed at the bustling Fengchun Building, his expression impassive, but inwardly he grew vigilant.","’I should have checked the almanac before leaving today. I’m afraid there’s something strange about this luncheon.’","Xiao Wan’er, however, paid these details no mind.","She wasn’t one for deep-seated scheming, so after a quick glance, she simply stood shoulder-to-shoulder with Chen Yi to wait for Shen Huatang and Xie Tingyun.","Just then, a cheerful voice called out from nearby:","\"Sister Wan’er, please forgive me! I didn’t realize you had already arrived. My apologies for not being outside to greet you properly.\"","Chen Yi and Xiao Wan’er looked over to see Liu Zhaoxue stepping out of Fengchun Building, dressed in a long, yellow gown with a fresh-faced makeup style.","Clearly, she had been waiting for them.","Xiao Wan’er gave a slight curtsy and replied gently, \"I’ve only just arrived myself.\"","Liu Zhaoxue returned the curtsy, then came over and took her hand with practiced familiarity. \"It was I who invited you, Sister,\" she said with a smile. \"I couldn’t possibly be so improper.\"","Then, her gaze fell upon Chen Yi. Her smile unwavering, she said, \"And this must be the renowned Mr. Qingzhou, whose name echoes throughout Shu State?\"","\"I was not aware you would be joining us, Mr. Qingzhou. If I am discourteous in any way later, I hope you will not take offense.\"","Chen Yi nodded calmly. \"You’re too kind.\"","\"Oh, but I should be. I’ve heard that countless people both inside and outside Shu State have sought an audience with you recently, yet you are a very difficult man to meet.\"","\"How could I dare be neglectful when you have graced us with your presence today?\"","Liu Zhaoxue gestured with a smile. \"It’s crowded down here. Shall we head upstairs?\"","Xiao Wan’er glanced at Chen Yi, then nodded. \"Then we’ll impose on you.\"","\"Not at all, Sister! Here in Shu State...\"","Watching the two women enter Fengchun Building, Chen Yi glanced up toward the second floor before following along with Xie Tingyun and Shen Huatang.","Just as he’d expected, when they pushed open the door to the private room, they saw Liu Wen standing off to one side.","Xiao Wan’er froze mid-step, her smile stiffening on her face. She clearly hadn’t expected to see him here and was at a complete loss.","Liu Wen, however, approached them proactively. He gave a formal bow and said with a smile, \"We meet again, Miss Wan’er.\"","Liu Zhaoxue glanced at Xiao Wan’er’s uneasy expression and quickly explained,","\"My second brother happened to be hosting some friends at Fengchun Building today. He was just going to sit with us for a moment before leaving.\"","Hearing this, Xiao Wan’er hesitantly returned the courtesy. \"Young Master Liu.\"","Liu Wen immediately smiled and gestured for them to be seated, shooting an approving glance at Liu Zhaoxue.","However, when his eyes landed on Chen Yi behind them, his expression soured.","But he didn’t make a scene. He simply turned to follow Xiao Wan’er and Liu Zhaoxue to the table.","Chen Yi, of course, had noted the expressions of both him and Liu Zhaoxue. He took a step forward and sat down right next to Xiao Wan’er.","Liu Wen stopped in his tracks, his face turning ugly. \"You...\"","Liu Zhaoxue noticed the tension and interjected with a smile, \"Second Brother, please, sit down. Let’s talk.\"","Liu Wen shot her a glare, then with a flick of his sleeve, he sat down beside Chen Yi, directly across from Xiao Wan’er.","Once the four of them were seated, Shen Huatang and Xie Tingyun took up positions to stand guard outside the door.","Liu Wen’s voice could be heard from inside. \"Miss Wan’er, my previous behavior was rash. I hope you can find it in your heart to forgive me.\"","\"However, I must confess that ever since I saw you that day, I have been utterly captivated...\""]},{"number":232,"title":"Chapter 232 - 197: Soft and Boneless","paragraphs":["Love at first sight.","When Liu Wen uttered those four words, the private room fell silent.","A barely perceptible smile touched Liu Zhaoxue’s lips as her gaze shifted to Xiao Wan’er.","She watched as the eldest daughter of the Dingyuan Marquis’s Mansion, a figure renowned throughout Shu State, revealed an unsurprising expression of astonishment.","It was exactly as she had predicted.","But when Liu Zhaoxue’s gaze landed on Chen Yi, a flicker of confusion inexplicably crossed her mind.","’This Mr. Qingzhou... he seems far too calm.’","Xiao Wan’er glanced at Liu Wen, her astonishment turning to displeasure. Lowering her head slightly, she said softly,","\"Though I am a woman, I know one must be prudent in word and deed when away from home, so as to reflect one’s family teachings and personal refinement.\"","\"For you to speak so brazenly, Young Master Liu, is this a reflection of the Jing State Liu Family’s principles?\"","Just two sentences were enough to make Liu Wen, who had been staring at her with smug composure, scowl.","To accuse someone of having poor principles and lacking refinement was, in this era and for someone from a Noble Family, tantamount to a vicious curse.","\"You...\"","Before he could finish, Chen Yi started to laugh.","His laughter was tinged with ridicule and disdain.","He didn’t look at the sullen-faced Liu Wen, however. Instead, his gaze was fixed directly on Liu Zhaoxue.","\"Sister Wan’er has a point.\"","\"However, in my opinion, Young Master Liu is merely the second son of the main branch of the Jing State Liu Family. He can hardly represent the family as a whole.\"","\"Miss Zhaoxue, on the other hand, has been nothing but dignified and poised in every word and deed since arriving in Shu State. Now *that* is what one would expect from the fine heritage of the Jing State Liu Family.\"","Liu Zhaoxue’s expression faltered as he steered the conversation toward her.","Just as she was about to speak and defuse the tension, Liu Wen shot to his feet, pointed at Chen Yi, and barked,","\"And who the hell do you think you are?\"","\"You’re just a bastard cast off by the Chen Family of Jiangnan Prefecture! A dog who married into the Xiao Family and lives at their mercy!\"","\"How dare you lecture me?!\"","The words had barely left his mouth when Xiao Wan’er, her face flushed with anger, snapped, \"Young Master Liu, watch your tongue!\"","She had rarely gotten angry in her entire life.","Even when she did feel upset, she seldom argued with anyone.","Even when Chen Yi had fled their wedding, causing the Old Master to fall gravely ill, she had merely felt it was wrong. Afterward, she had even joined the Old Master in persuading Xiao Jinghong to be lenient.","But now.","Upon hearing Liu Wen’s disparaging words against Chen Yi, anger flared in Xiao Wan’er’s heart, and her usual gentle demeanor turned stern.","But Liu Wen ignored Xiao Wan’er, his cold glare still fixed on Chen Yi as he said,","\"Don’t think you can get all high and mighty just because you have good handwriting and have earned a little fame.\"","\"Mr. Qingzhou? Hah! What a joke!\"","At this, Chen Yi raised an eyebrow. His gaze, however, remained locked on Liu Zhaoxue as he said with pointed mockery,","\"A fool, oblivious to his own impending doom.\"","Liu Zhaoxue’s face paled. She stared at him, alarmed and suspicious, feeling as if his eyes could see right through her.","’What does he mean by that?’","’Who’s facing impending doom? Me?’","’Or Liu Wen...’","’But how could he possibly know the purpose of my invitation today?!’","Yet before the bewildered Liu Zhaoxue could collect her thoughts, and before the furious Liu Wen could speak, Chen Yi withdrew his gaze and gently patted the back of Xiao Wan’er’s tightly clenched hand.","\"Sister Wan’er, there’s no good to be had at this banquet. Let’s go home.\"","Xiao Wan’er, still simmering with anger, felt a warmth spread through her heart as his hand covered her own cold one.","She looked up at Chen Yi, and seeing his usual gentle smile, she nodded.","Chen Yi smiled, rose to his feet, and took her hand, leading her toward the door.","Seeing this, Liu Wen barked, \"Stop!\"","But clearly, neither Chen Yi nor Xiao Wan’er had any intention of getting entangled with him.","As he saw them about to leave, Liu Wen flew into a humiliated rage and threw a punch straight at them.","Hearing the commotion, a murderous glint flashed in Chen Yi’s eyes as he smoothly pulled Xiao Wan’er in by the waist.","Just as he was about to dodge, the door burst open, and Xie Tingyun appeared in a flash.","With a single palm strike, she slapped Liu Wen’s fist aside. \"What do you think you’re doing?!\"","Feeling the True Essence that erupted from her palm, Liu Wen used the force of the blow to retreat, staring at them with a mixture of shock and fury.","\"You!?\"","Xie Tingyun’s face was cold. \"Attacking the eldest daughter of the Xiao Mansion in public? I take it you don’t plan on leaving Shu State alive!\"","Seeing this, Liu Zhaoxue had no time for further thought. She quickly rose, pulled Liu Wen back, and forced a smile.","\"Sister Wan’er, please forgive him. My second brother just has a bad temper. He didn’t mean to offend you.\"","Liu Wen violently shook off her hand.","He was about to speak again, but his eyes met Xie Tingyun’s, then fell on Shen Huatang standing outside the door with her hand on her sword. He opened his mouth, but all that came out was a cold snort.","Only then did Xiao Wan’er, still held in Chen Yi’s arms, realize what had just happened behind her.","She hesitated, pulling back a little, and said softly, \"Let’s go.\"","Chen Yi grunted in agreement and led her out of the private room.","Xie Tingyun shot the silent Liu Wen a glare, muttered, \"Spineless coward,\" and followed after them with Shen Huatang.","Before they could even exit Fengchun Building.","They heard the sound of crashing and shattering from behind them.","Chen Yi looked at Xiao Wan’er beside him and said with a smile, \"You were quite formidable back there, Sister Wan’er.\"","Xiao Wan’er’s face flushed slightly as she lowered her head. \"W-Was I? I... I just didn’t like him being so brazen.\"","\"Mm, but how did it feel to curse someone out, Sister Wan’er?\"","\"Ah? Were those few words I said considered cursing?\"","\"Compared to me, you’ve still got a ways to go.\"","\"Cursing... it’s not right. But I couldn’t help it, especially after what he said about you...\"","\"Don’t worry. It takes a villain to punish a villain.\"","Behind them, Xie Tingyun saw Chen Yi and Xiao Wan’er holding hands. Her eyes darted about mischievously before she immediately leaned over to whisper in Shen Huatang’s ear.","After listening, Shen Huatang froze for a second, then also cast a strange look at the pair ahead of them."]},{"number":233,"title":"Chapter 233 - 197: Soft and Boneless","paragraphs":["\"They’re having an affair, aren’t they?\"","\"Senior Sister, don’t talk nonsense. It was probably just because of the special circumstances just now.\"","\"They definitely are.\"","\"Even if they are, you shouldn’t use the word ’affair’.\"","\"Adultery?\"","\"...Shut up.\"","It wasn’t until the Xiao Family’s carriage was far in the distance that Fengchun Building returned to a state of calm.","Everyone looked at each other, none of them knowing what had just happened.","Meanwhile, in the private room upstairs.","Liu Wen was still in a blind rage. After smashing everything in sight, he glared at Liu Zhaoxue with bloodshot eyes and demanded:","\"You’re pretty pleased with yourself, aren’t you?\"","\"That bastard just now was praising you! He said you’re the model of the Liu Family, that you have grace and know when to advance or retreat!\"","Liu Zhaoxue shook her head and hesitated. \"Second Brother, you...\"","Before she could finish, Liu Wen flicked his sleeve and stormed out.","\"I will explain everything that happened today to Second Uncle and the family later.\"","\"You should prepare to return to Jing State soon.\"","Liu Zhaoxue stared blankly as he left the room, her expression suddenly turning grim.","’Second Brother, you truly are... a fool!’","Just then, a pot-bellied, ordinary-looking middle-aged man walked in from outside.","He glanced at the wreckage on the floor, clucking his tongue. \"Second Young Master Liu lashes out in a fury, and the young miss of the Xiao Family leaves in anger.\"","\"Miss Zhaoxue, everything is going just as you predicted.\"","At this, the middle-aged man’s tone shifted, and he asked with a smile, \"So, are we proceeding with the plan tonight?\"","But to his surprise, Liu Zhaoxue shook her head, her face cold. \"We’re holding off for now.\"","The smile vanished from the man’s face. He asked seriously, \"Why is that?\"","\"Miss Zhaoxue, you should be aware that if we act now, everyone will assume it was Second Young Master Liu’s doing.\"","Liu Zhaoxue shook her head again. The image of Chen Yi’s calm yet piercing eyes surfaced in her mind, and a sense of apprehension arose within her.","\"Let’s wait. Acting tonight would be too obvious.\"","\"Very well. We’ll let the young miss of the Xiao Family live a few more days.\"","Liu Zhaoxue thought for a moment before saying, \"I need you to do something for me in the next couple of days.\"","The middle-aged man put on a fawning smile. \"Miss Zhaoxue, we’re in the same boat now. If you need something, just give the order. There’s no need to be so polite.\"","\"Help me investigate that live-in son-in-law of the Xiao Family.\"","\"Oh? The one named Chen Yi?\"","Liu Zhaoxue grunted in affirmation. \"Help me dig into his background.\"","The middle-aged man nodded nonchalantly. \"He’s just some frail scholar, that’s all.\"","\"If Miss Zhaoxue finds him displeasing, I can go kill him right now.\"","Liu Zhaoxue looked at him. \"I advise you to be cautious. I have a feeling he’s not as simple as he appears.\"","\"Is that so?\"","\"Well then, I’m rather curious to see why he’s earned such apprehension from Miss Zhaoxue, heheh...\"","...","The outcome was just as Chen Yi had expected.","There was indeed something fishy about today’s trip to the Fengchun Building.","Although he didn’t know the specifics of the banquet Liu Zhaoxue had arranged, he knew her target was Liu Wen.","’It could only be one of a few schemes.’","’She probably wanted to use today’s conflict between Liu Wen and Xiao Wan’er to frame the Xiao Family for Liu Wen’s subsequent death.’","’Or, if her schemes ran deeper, she might have targeted Xiao Wan’er directly to provoke the Xiao Family into dealing with Liu Wen.’","’A classic case of borrowing a knife to kill someone.’","’The result would be the same either way—Liu Wen would die in Shu State!’","But...","’Liu Zhaoxue probably never expected that Xiao Wan’er wouldn’t come to the appointment alone today.’","As Chen Yi considered all this, he made a decision. He couldn’t let her get her way.","Just then, he felt a slight movement in his hand and turned his head to look.","He saw Xiao Wan’er, her head buried in her cloak, pretending to be nonchalant as she discreetly tried to pull her hand from his grasp.","Chen Yi chuckled inwardly. He turned to look out the carriage window, pretending not to notice as he tightened his grip slightly.","Xiao Wan’er immediately froze.","She quietly raised her head, her slightly reddened eyes glancing at Chen Yi, who was still \"lost in thought.\" She let out a soft sigh of relief.","’He didn’t notice. Thank goodness.’","Xiao Wan’er thought to herself and wiggled her hand a little.","Seeing that she could pull it out a bit, she continued to inch her burning-hot palm away.","Then Chen Yi tightened his grip again.","Once again, Xiao Wan’er didn’t dare to move.","A moment later.","She tried again.","But this time, not only did Chen Yi add a bit more pressure, he also gave her hand a mischievous little squeeze.","’As soft as if it had no bones.’","Xiao Wan’er almost cried out. In an instant, she felt as if her entire body was on fire.","Even so, she didn’t dare lift her head, terrified of meeting Chen Yi’s eyes.","’If that happened, she didn’t know if she would die of embarrassment and wish for the ground to swallow her whole.’","’Hopeless.’","After that, Xiao Wan’er gave up trying to move, simply letting him hold her hand.","Her heart was pounding relentlessly.","Her mind a chaotic mess, she felt for the first time in her life that time was passing so slowly.","Fengchun Building was only two streets away from the Dingyuan Marquis’s Mansion.","It was so close, yet the journey felt so long.","It wasn’t until the carriage entered the Dingyuan Marquis’s Mansion and Shen Huatang knocked twice on the carriage wall to announce their arrival that Xiao Wan’er dared to lift her head from her cloak.","But when she met Chen Yi’s teasing, smiling face, she instinctively shrank back again.","’Cute.’","The word popped into Chen Yi’s mind, and he chuckled inwardly.","Without realizing it, he had seen several of Xiao Wan’er’s rare expressions today.","’But we’re home now.’","Chen Yi let go of her hand and said with a smile, \"Eldest Sister, we’ve arrived at the mansion.\"","Xiao Wan’er quickly pulled her hand back. \"I-I know.\"","After taking a long moment to compose herself, she finally nodded and stepped out of the carriage first.","But her face was still bright red, and she seemed to be in a daze.","Xie Tingyun saw this and couldn’t help but wink at Shen Huatang again.","’See? I told you there was something going on between them.’","’Stop talking nonsense.’","Chen Yi, of course, was unaware of the thoughts of the two high disciples of the Celestial Sect outside the carriage.","He stepped out of the carriage.","Just as he was about to speak, he saw Wang Ji in the distance and, understanding, waved him over.","\"Eldest Sister, Shopkeeper Wang is here. It must be that Boss Chen Yu from Hundred Herbs Hall has sent a reply. I’m going to go see.\"","Xiao Wan’er’s eyes darted quickly between him and Wang Ji before she nodded and walked toward the rear courtyard without a word.","Shen Huatang followed close behind.","Xie Tingyun, meanwhile, led the carriage to the stables.","Watching the three of them leave, Chen Yi greeted a few acquaintances nearby before leaving the Xiao Family grounds with Wang Ji.","Xiao Wan’er, on the other hand, walked a long way. It wasn’t until she had passed through the central courtyard that the coolness of the air finally began to seep into her.","She couldn’t help but let out a long breath.","Seeing her like this, Shen Huatang hesitated for a moment before asking in a low voice, \"Eldest Miss, you and the Second Young Master-in-law...\"","A blush rose on Xiao Wan’er’s face again, and she hurriedly quickened her pace.","\"Huatang, quickly, come with me to sort through the mansion’s ledgers. The Mid-Autumn Festival is coming, and we need to prepare extra gifts for the various courtyards.\"","\"...\"","Shen Huatang watched her go, a flicker of astonishment crossing her usually cool and detached face.","’No way. Could Senior Sister have been right?’","’It can’t be, can it?’","’He’s the Second Miss’s...’","...","「A few moments later.」","Aboard the Hundred Herbs Hall carriage, Chen Yi discreetly spread a bit of his True Essence to confirm no one was paying attention before he asked calmly:","\"Did Guard Liu send you?\"","Wang Ji replied respectfully, \"Yes. Guard Liu said you gave him instructions in advance.\"","Chen Yi grunted. \"Change course and head to Chuansi Street.\"","After giving the order to the driver, Wang Ji continued, \"I’ve also taken care of the matters Dabao mentioned this morning.\"","\"The residence in the East Market was purchased through a familiar broker. He has already left the city to lay low for a while.\"","\"Before leaving, he helped purchase three residences, all near Chuandong Street.\"","Chen Yi nodded slightly. \"Make sure to clean up any loose ends.\"","Wang Ji’s heart stirred. He looked at Chen Yi and asked, \"My lord, is something major going to happen in the city soon?\"","Chen Yi glanced at him but didn’t elaborate, only instructing, \"It doesn’t concern you.\"","\"You just need to manage Hundred Herbs Hall well.\"","\"This lowly one spoke out of turn. My lord, please forgive me.\"","Soon, Chen Yi arrived at the residence on Chuansi Street.","After having Zhang Dabao apply a disguise, he summoned Liu Lang.","Before long, Liu Lang hurried over.","\"Boss, we’ve received word from the Spring Rain Building, just as you expected.\"","Chen Yi wasn’t surprised. \"Tell me the details.\"","\"Early this morning, Black Tooth came to find me. He told me to inform you that there’s a gathering at the Spring Rain Building tonight.\"","\"Anything else?\"","Liu Lang faltered. \"Anything else... No, that’s all he said.\"","Chen Yi glanced at him sideways and prompted, \"The third floor.\"","Realization dawned on Liu Lang, and he said with some embarrassment, \"I haven’t been able to locate the silver coins.\"","\"Did you notice anything unusual?\"","\"Unusual... yes, there was something.\"","\"There are several new guards on the third floor. They don’t look like they belong to the Spring Rain Building. In fact, they have the air of Evil Demons about them.\"","Chen Yi understood. He looked out the window at the high sun and said thoughtfully, \"I’ll go over tonight.\"","\"But I’ll probably be a bit late. Explain that to Black Tooth for me.\"","Liu Lang was taken aback. \"What are you going to do?\"","\"I’m going to invite a distinguished guest to accompany me to the Three Towns...\""]},{"number":234,"title":"Chapter 234 - 198: Liu Wu, Most Suspicious","paragraphs":["「Just past noon.」","The scorching sun beat down, and pedestrians along the road were drenched in sweat.","But Wang Ji, riding in his horse-drawn carriage and holding an ice-filled jar, was feeling refreshed and clear-headed. As he thought about the tasks Chen Yi had given him, he couldn’t help but have some reservations.","Since Chen Yi had entrusted him with running the Hundred Herbs Hall as its Shopkeeper, he had come to know the man quite well.","In his mind, Chen Yi was not only a greatly talented scholar but also skilled in the art of business and the Medical Dao.","This was evident from the ever-growing success of the Hundred Herbs Hall.","But there were other things Chen Yi did that Wang Ji simply couldn’t fathom.","Even though he had a hand in some of these affairs, they still felt shrouded in mystery.","For example, why sell the house in the East Market right after buying it, only to purchase several more?","And why was Guard Liu active only at night? What was he doing?","Then there was what Zhang Dabao had unintentionally let slip—that Chen Yi sometimes went out at night in disguise.","With all these things going on, Wang Ji couldn’t help but overthink.","It wasn’t that he was worried for his own safety. He was simply afraid that if he were kept on the sidelines for too long, Chen Yi would no longer see him as important.","Take today, for instance. He had deduced that Chen Yi and Guard Liu were planning something major.","And yet, he was still stuck doing minor tasks like buying property and delivering letters.","It was hard not to feel dejected.","’Looks like I’ll have to brief Yan Hai properly before he leaves for Shu State. Can’t have him botching this trip.’","A short while later, Wang Ji’s carriage arrived at the Xiao Family estate.","This time, he didn’t intend to enter for a visit. Instead, he handed a letter to the Third Steward, who was waiting at the entrance, and said with a respectful clasp of his hands,","\"I must ask you, Steward, to please deliver this letter to the Eldest Miss for me.\"","The Third Steward, Lu Tong, was younger than the first and second stewards of the mansion. He was about forty, in the prime of his life, and naturally quick-witted.","He took the letter, glanced at it, and said with some surprise, \"Oh? Is this from the Second Young Master-in-law?\"","Wang Ji smiled and nodded. \"My boss and Mr. Qingzhou hit it off immediately. They’ve made plans for an evening outing by Quchi tonight. To prevent anyone in the mansion from worrying, Mr. Qingzhou asked me to deliver this letter to the Eldest Miss.\"","The Third Steward put the letter away with a nod of understanding and clasped his hands in thanks. \"Thank you for taking the trouble to come all this way, Shopkeeper Wang.\"","Having been with the mansion for a long time, he was naturally aware of the partnership between the Xiao Family Medicine Hall and the Hundred Herbs Hall. He had also heard that the mansion was earning a handsome profit from it.","As such, he naturally held Wang Ji, the Shopkeeper of the Hundred Herbs Hall, in high regard.","\"You’re too kind, Steward Lu. Now that the letter is delivered, I won’t take up any more of your time. I’ll let you get back to your work.\"","Just as Lu Tong was about to reply with a few pleasantries, he heard a commotion behind him.","With no time for further words, he simply bid Wang Ji farewell before taking the letter and hastily shutting the mansion gates.","Wang Ji, for his part, didn’t try to pry.","It was only natural for a great house like the Xiao Family to have matters they preferred outsiders not to see.","In any case, he had delivered the letter.","Meanwhile, Lu Tong entered the front courtyard. He took one look, his brow furrowed, and asked in a low voice,","\"Hundred Households Wang, what is going on?\"","He saw Wang Lixing, who had been away from the mansion for some time, berating Ge the Third and Liu Si’er. When he heard Lu Tong’s question, he offered no detailed explanation, simply saying,","\"My apologies, Steward Lu. I was a bit loud just now.\"","\"As long as you’re aware. This is not far from the main gate. A commotion here will inevitably attract the attention of passersby and start idle talk.\"","\"You’re right to correct me.\"","Seeing that he had stopped, Lu Tong said no more and headed directly for the rear courtyard with the letter.","Wang Lixing pursed his lips, glaring coldly at Ge the Third and Liu Si’er.","\"You two are veterans in this mansion, so I’ll let it slide this time. If there’s a next time, you can go explain yourselves to the Second Master and receive your punishment!\"","Liu Si’er and Ge the Third nodded with sheepish smiles. \"We’ll head to the medicine halls in a bit to try and fix this. You have to put in a good word for us with the Second Master.\"","\"Hah. Scared now, are you?\"","\"Mistakes happen. We really didn’t expect such a lapse during our patrol. To think someone would steal herbs from the Medicine Hall in broad daylight.\"","\"Enough excuses. Get over there and find out what’s going on before word of this reaches the Eldest Miss.\"","\"Right, right, right...\"","Wang Lixing shot the two of them a final glare before turning and heading toward the central courtyard.","Once he was a good distance away,","Ge the Third and Liu Si’er exchanged a glance. Then, wearing woeful expressions, they placated the surrounding Armored Warriors before leaving the Marquis’s Mansion together.","It wasn’t until they were on South Street that Liu Si’er’s lips finally moved. \"I truly never imagined you were ’Hawk,’ sir.\"","\"If you hadn’t given me that signal earlier, I nearly would have reported you to Wang Lixing.\"","Ge the Third cracked a smile. The miserable look on his face was long gone, replaced by a shrewd glint in his eye.","\"Something unexpected came up. Otherwise, I wouldn’t have willingly exposed myself.\"","Liu Si’er didn’t ask what the unexpected event was. He remained silent, waiting for further orders.","Ge the Third glanced at him and nodded to himself, inwardly approving of the Iron Banner Officer’s discipline.","After they had walked a bit farther, he finally explained,","\"Recently, I and several other Silver Banner Officers have been planning a major operation.\"","\"It was supposed to be top secret, but last night, one of the Xiao Family’s Hidden Guards got an insider to talk.\"","\"Although that Hidden Guard was critically injured and the Old Marquis hasn’t received the intel yet, my associates and I must respond to this. We can’t let it jeopardize our main objective.\"","\"I can’t go into the specifics.\"","\"I’m telling you this so you can be prepared. It’s very likely I’ll have to pull out ahead of schedule.\"","As he spoke, Ge the Third carefully scanned their surroundings for anything out of the ordinary. Once he was certain no one was watching, he continued,","\"Whether our operation succeeds or fails, you have only one mission from here on out: maintain your cover and keep a close eye on the ’Fledgling’ for me.\"","Liu Si’er committed every word to memory.","’No wonder the Old Marquis was in such a rage today,’ Liu Si’er thought. ’He even ordered the Third Master to make inquiries with the Imprisonment Department. It must have been about that Hidden Guard.’"]},{"number":235,"title":"Chapter 235 - 198: Liu Wu, the Most Suspicious (Part 2)","paragraphs":["Ge the Third gave a slight nod. \"The Xiao Family’s Hidden Guard were once top scouts from the Dingyuan Army’s Scout Camp, and they received extensive training from Xiao Fengchun himself. They’re highly capable. You need to be careful and keep a low profile from now on.\"","\"I understand.\"","\"That’s all for now. Head on to the Medicine Hall. I’m leaving.\"","Liu Si’er grunted in acknowledgment. He watched Ge the Third disappear into the West Market, then turned and walked toward the Medicine Hall to the north.","Soon after they parted ways, Ge the Third arrived at a tailor shop in the West Market. After exchanging some pleasantries, he walked into an inner room.","There, a bewitchingly beautiful woman in a long purple dress was already waiting inside.","It was none other than the Hidden Guard’s Lady Tiger, Lou Yuxue.","The two sized each other up.","Ge the Third said with a smile, \"Lord Lady Tiger, my apologies. I’m late.\"","Lou Yuxue looked at him, her face devoid of expression. \"I knew you would need time to get away.\"","However, after speaking, she glanced at the sun outside and frowned. \"There isn’t much time left. You’d better inform them quickly.\"","Ge the Third paused for a moment, his expression turning serious. \"Are we certain we’re making our move tonight?\"","\"Any delay invites complications. If that Hidden Guard from last night makes it back to the Xiao Family, our entire plan is doomed to fail.\"","\"Fine. I’ll send word to them immediately.\"","Seeing Ge the Third immediately begin to write a coded message, Lou Yuxue still couldn’t relax.","She ran through the events of the last few days in her mind, a vague sense of unease prickling at her.","But she couldn’t quite pinpoint the source of this feeling.","As she mulled it over, the image of \"Liu Wu\" surfaced in her mind. ’Is he really the most suspicious one?’","Ge the Third heard her mutter and asked in a low voice, \"Who’s suspicious?\"","Lou Yuxue snapped back to the present. \"Liu Wu,\" she said, watching him consult a codebook as he wrote.","\"The one sent by the second young master of the Jing State Liu Family? Is there a problem with him?\"","\"It’s just a feeling I can’t quite describe...\"","Lou Yuxue went on to recount what had happened between her and \"Liu Wu\" that night, finishing with,","\"Even if the Xiao Family hasn’t been alerted and everything seems normal, I still have this nagging feeling that there’s a major problem with this ’Liu Wu’ character.\"","Ge the Third thought for a moment. \"Perhaps,\" he said. \"But as long as he has no ties to the Xiao Family, we can always find an opportunity to deal with him later.\"","\"For now, that other matter is our top priority.\"","Lou Yuxue frowned at his words. After a moment, she put the matter of Liu Wu out of her mind.","\"You’re right. After tonight, no matter how mysterious this Liu Wu is, I’ll have a way to drag him into the light.\"","Ge the Third nodded. \"I’ll have to leave Shu State for a while. You’ll need to be careful.\"","\"You’ve decided?\"","\"Yes. To avoid compromising the other hidden Banner Officers, I have to take full responsibility. That was the reason I disagreed with Gray Wolf’s scheme in the first place.\"","\"But with you and that sum of silver coins here, I believe the situation in Shu State will become much more favorable for our operations.\"","Lou Yuxue’s eyes flickered in thought. \"What do you need my help with?\"","Although the Silver Banner Officers within the Hidden Guard usually operated independently, each responsible for their own affairs, the situation in Shu State was unique. She, Hawk, Gray Wolf, and Simurgh Phoenix maintained contact with one another to operate more effectively.","Unless it was a matter of someone having their own selfish agenda, like Gray Wolf, she didn’t mind lending a hand.","Ge the Third finished writing the three secret letters. He began to retrieve carrier pigeons and tie the messages to their legs, speaking as he worked.","\"First, the matter concerning Gray Wolf can only be handled by you and Simurgh Phoenix.\"","\"Second, Fledgling’s situation is fairly stable, so there’s no need to push things along for now. Wait for further instructions after I’ve consulted with the Lord Golden Banner Officer.\"","\"Third, that sum of silver coins...\"","He paused, released the carrier pigeons, and watched them fly into the distance before turning back to Lou Yuxue.","\"You’ll have to make a trade-off. My men can’t withdraw empty-handed; they need silver coins to create new identities.\"","Lou Yuxue replied without hesitation, \"Once I get my hands on those silver coins, I won’t forget you. It’s just that, right now...\"","For some reason, the image of \"Liu Wu\" reappeared in her mind, and she recalled his words: \"I want fifty percent of the silver notes.\"","Seeing her fall silent, Ge the Third couldn’t help but ask, \"It’s just what?\"","Lou Yuxue shook her head. \"Nothing.\"","’As long as those silver coins end up safely in my hands, I refuse to believe ’Liu Wu’ has any way of prying them from my grasp.’","After a moment of silence, Ge the Third asked with a smile, \"Are you sure you don’t need me with you tonight?\"","Lou Yuxue paused, then stood up. \"Your Martial Arts are too weak. You’d only be a burden.\"","\"It’s better for you to get away safely than to put yourself in danger.\"","\"...You’re right, of course, but that doesn’t make it any less harsh to hear.\"","\"The truth hurts...\"","\"In any case, here’s to hoping everything goes smoothly.\"","...","「Nightfall.」","Perhaps it was due to the sweltering heat, or maybe because the Mid-Autumn Festival was approaching, but there were far fewer patrons than usual in Shu State City’s South City Yanhua Lane.","Even the famous Spring Rain Building had few patrons coming in or out.","Only a few idle libertines lingered in the main hall, admiring the forms of the dancing girls.","The Madam stood just inside the doorway, muttering to herself while craning her neck to peer outside, likely wondering where all the patrons had disappeared to.","Several Pimps stood by, cowering and not daring to speak for fear of saying the wrong thing and earning a reprimand.","Liu Lang observed all of this, finding it rather amusing.","He had been waiting in the Spring Rain Building ever since leaving Chuansi Street at noon.","Although he couldn’t guess the identity of the \"distinguished guest\" Chen Yi had mentioned, he knew clearly that Black Tooth and his men were about to make their move.","He was, at the very least, looking forward to the outcome—","would the mysterious, unfathomable Boss Chen prove to be one move ahead, or would the Bright Moon Building always be a step beyond?","However.","Anticipation was one thing.","Liu Lang also harbored some complaints against Chen Yi.","Even now, after having done so much under Chen Yi and having seen the ins and outs of certain events, there were still a few things he couldn’t grasp clearly."]},{"number":236,"title":"Chapter 236 - 198: Liu Wu, the Most Suspicious","paragraphs":["’So mysterious...’","’Boss, you’d better not let this plan fall through in the end.’","’If it does, I’ll definitely have a good laugh at your expense.’","Just as Liu Lang was grumbling to himself, a burly man in black clothes walked over and said in a low voice, \"It’s time.\"","Liu Lang glanced at him, dropped the tea he was holding, and stood up to follow him upstairs.","They made their way to a quiet room deep within the top floor.","The moment he walked in, Liu Lang let out an involuntary, loud whistle.","\"Brother Black Tooth, you’ve got quite the full house tonight.\"","Inside the spacious, quiet room, besides Black Tooth and Lou Yuxue, there were over fifty other black-clad men of varying heights.","Twice as many as last time.","Clearly, Black Tooth hadn’t been idle these past few days.","Liu Lang, completely unconcerned about exposing his identity, joked around before taking a seat and asking:","\"Looks like we’re making our move tonight?\"","Black Tooth shot him a glance, his tone as cold as ever as he asked:","\"You’re the only one here? Where’s Liu Wu?\"","Liu Lang spread his hands. \"I don’t know either.\"","\"But before I came, I reported to him that you were gathering everyone.\"","\"He just said he’d be a little late, mentioning that a distinguished guest also wanted to come along and have a look.\"","A flicker of light in Black Tooth’s eyes. \"A distinguished guest?\"","At that moment, Lou Yuxue, who was standing to the side, spoke up. \"Perhaps it’s that Young Master Liu. I heard he had a conflict with that young mistress at the Fengchun Building today.\"","Black Tooth thought for a moment, then nodded. \"That would be for the best.\"","Lou Yuxue glanced at him and said hesitantly, \"Time is short. Why don’t you start making arrangements first, Elder?\"","\"Very well.\"","However, an hour passed.","Black Tooth had finished assigning personnel to each of the Three Towns, but still, there was no sign of Liu Wu.","He frowned, staring at Liu Lang. \"Are you sure you passed the message to Brother Liu Wu?\"","Seeing the menacing glint in his eyes, Liu Lang grinned. \"You should know that I can’t control the comings and goings of a Medical Saint Hand.\"","The words had barely left his lips when Elder Demon Jia, not far away, let out a sinister chuckle.","\"Well, he is a Medical Saint Hand. It’s understandable if he’s a bit arrogant.\"","\"Besides, we all saw him take down Elder Demon Fang with poison the other day. With poison Skills like that, which rival even the Five Poison Sect of old, it’s only normal for him to have a strange temper.\"","Someone nearby shook their head. \"That may be so, but business doesn’t wait. We can’t let one person jeopardize the entire operation, can we?\"","\"Exactly. Cang Lang Town is far away. Even with Black Tooth leading the way, it’ll take six hours.\"","\"Heh heh, so arrogant...\"","Seeing the dissatisfaction among these Evil Demons, Lou Yuxue suggested, \"Elder, why don’t we assign Liu Wu to one of the other two towns?\"","\"You can take Elder Demon Jia and the others to the outskirts of Cang Lang Town first. We don’t want any unexpected problems from being late.\"","Black Tooth glanced at her and nodded slowly. \"Let’s do that, then.\"","Then, he stood up and gestured to several Evil Demons in the room. \"Those assigned to Cang Lang and Profound Armor Towns, head out first.\"","Lou Yuxue understood his intention and said with a charming laugh, \"How thoughtful of you, Elder. Sending that Liu Wu to the closest town, Iron Wall Town, is the most suitable arrangement~\"","Liu Lang also nodded. \"Makes sense.\"","Black Tooth ignored them both. After giving his orders, he led his men out of the Spring Rain Building.","Just before leaving, he instructed Lou Yuxue to wait for an hour at most.","Lou Yuxue readily agreed, then continued to wait in the quiet room with Liu Lang and the others.","But after another hour, with the hour of the Pig approaching, there was still no sign of Liu Wu.","Lou Yuxue immediately stood up and walked out. \"We’re not waiting any longer!\"","The unexpected situation deepened her suspicions about Liu Wu, and she had a faint, bad feeling.","But the arrow was already on the bowstring; she had no choice but to act. She couldn’t come up with any other countermeasures.","Seeing this, Liu Lang couldn’t say much either and could only follow the others out of the Spring Rain Building.","It wasn’t until they were outside the South City gate, where Lou Yuxue found the fast horses waiting for them, that she noticed something was amiss in their surroundings.","\"Who’s there?\"","A light laugh drifted from the distance. \"The distinguished guest has arrived. I’ve kept you all waiting.\"","\"Liu Wu?\""]},{"number":237,"title":"Chapter 237 - 199: Please Go to Your Deaths","paragraphs":["The one who had arrived was none other than Chen Yi.","But in Liu Lang’s eyes, he was Chen Yu, the mysterious boss of Hundred Herbs Hall.","And to Lou Yuxue, he was Liu Wu, the mysterious Medical Saint Hand from the Jing State Liu Family.","But now, as Lou Yuxue looked at \"Liu Wu,\" clad in a black cloak and a black iron mask, an inexplicable sense of familiarity washed over her.","The feeling grew even stronger when she saw his indifferent eyes.","Just then, a few members of the Evil Demonic Dao who also saw \"Liu Wu\" exclaimed in shock and doubt:","\"Black Tooth?!\"","\"Elder Black Tooth?\"","\"Black Tooth...\"","Hearing this, Lou Yuxue took another look and had a flash of realization. ’Isn’t \"Liu Wu’s\" current getup the very style of Black Tooth?’","’No, it’s not just his clothes.’","’The faint, icy aura about him, his emotionless eyes—they’re all identical to Black Tooth’s.’","’Why is he dressed like this?’","Lou Yuxue’s expression flickered as thoughts began to surface, and she started to piece together Liu Wu’s recent actions.","First, there was the time in the Spring Rain Building, when Liu Wu and Liu Lang had come to her, proposing to join the deal to burn the summer grain of the Three Towns.","Then, she had sent people to the Jing State Liu Family to check—twice—and both times the response confirmed that a man named Liu Wu was indeed at Liu Wen’s side, and that he was a Medical Saint Hand.","And then, the night before last, after her confrontation with Liu Wu, his identity had become highly questionable.","Until tonight, when Liu Wu appeared in the guise of \"Black Tooth\"...","As Lou Yuxue thought about all this, she felt she was on the verge of grasping something, but she was still missing the main thread that tied it all together.","’What on earth is Liu Wu’s purpose in doing all of this!’","Chen Yi, on the other hand, paid no mind to their shocked cries.","Or rather, he had hoped these Evil Demons would react this way.","However, noticing that Lou Yuxue seemed to have caught on, Chen Yi leaned in closer, his voice an almost inaudible whisper.","\"Three hundred thousand silver notes. A sixty-forty split, your favor. Otherwise... we’ll just be doing the Xiao Family a favor. Coincidentally, they’ll be able to use that money to cover their losses after tonight.\"","Lou Yuxue stared at him, asking through gritted teeth, \"What exactly are you trying to do?\"","Chen Yi chuckled. \"The same as you. I just want to see the fireworks tonight.\"","With that, he called out to a carriage on the road behind him, \"Wouldn’t you agree, Young Master Liu?\"","Lou Yuxue then heard a sinister voice from the carriage. \"Don’t waste any more time. Let’s get going.\"","Hearing this, Lou Yuxue’s eyes widened slightly.","’So Liu Wen really came in person?’","’But why would Liu Wu...’","’No, this man before me is definitely not from the Liu Family!’","’Otherwise, he wouldn’t have impersonated Black Tooth to lure Liu Wen here!’","’Could it be...’","’His target is the Jing State Liu Family?!’","However, before Lou Yuxue could ponder further, Chen Yi unleashed the pressure of his Great Success Fist Dao Realm, bearing down on her.","In an instant, Lou Yuxue felt as if a great mountain was crushing her. Her face flushed red as she struggled to resist the pressure.","\"You...\"","But she had only managed to utter a single word before Chen Yi’s mountain-like pressure intensified, forcing the rest of her words back down her throat.","Seeing this, Chen Yi gestured for Liu Lang to lead the other Evil Demons ahead, saying aloud:","\"Yuxue and I will bring up the rear. The rest of you, go on ahead.\"","\"Alright.\"","Liu Lang smiled and nodded, but inwardly, he offered a silent moment of mourning for Liu Wen while marveling at Boss Chen’s profound foresight.","At any rate, he knew that Boss Chen’s scheme for the Three Towns tonight would not fail.","He then motioned for the other Evil Demons to mount their horses and depart.","He didn’t forget to instruct the driver of Liu Wen’s carriage, either. \"We’re headed to Iron Wall Town. Remember, blades have no eyes. Just be careful and follow along behind.\"","Liu Wen snorted from within the carriage. \"I don’t need your reminders. Go.\"","Only after Liu Lang and his group had ridden for several miles did Chen Yi withdraw the pressure of his Great Success Fist Dao Realm. He smiled and said:","\"Let’s go. We should get moving as well.\"","As the pressure on her vanished, Lou Yuxue instinctively clutched her chest and took a deep breath, trying to ease the terror in her heart.","She stared daggers at the man before her, her voice strained. \"You... You’ve fooled everyone!\"","\"I never expected that on top of your Medical Dao, your Martial Arts would be this terrifying!\"","Although Martial Arts Realms are divided into entry-level, Minor Success, and Great Success, that doesn’t mean there aren’t differences in power within the same realm.","Take this man’s Fist Dao, for example; it was clearly at the absolute pinnacle of the Great Success Realm.","’To think he could contain his Martial Arts Realm to just the two of them, right in front of several Middle Third-Grade Martial Artists, without anyone else sensing it.’","’Such power not only required a profound enough Mental Realm but also demanded absolute control over the Heaven and Earth’s Spiritual Mechanism.’","’If even the slightest fluctuation had leaked out, it would have inevitably alerted the nearby Evil Demons and Liu Wen.’","Chen Yi smiled and gave a slight bow, making a \"please\" gesture to indicate she should follow Liu Lang and the others.","\"I know Miss Yuxue has many questions, but time is of the essence. Let’s talk on the way.\"","Lou Yuxue gritted her teeth and refused. \"Impossible!\"","’She was a dignified Hidden Guard Silver Banner Officer, yet this man had played her like a fiddle from start to finish. How could she not be furious?’","’And how could she willingly let him have his way?’","Chen Yi asked with a smile, \"Are you really not going to cooperate?\"","\"Absolutely not!\"","\"So you don’t want to know my true purpose? And you’re willing to give up on those three hundred thousand silver notes?\"","\"Hmph!\"","Lou Yuxue turned her head away, determined not to compromise.","She was, however, well aware of how terrifying this man’s Martial Arts were and knew she was no match for him.","She had even prepared herself for death.","Chen Yi let out an amused laugh. \"I didn’t expect you to choose ’death before dishonor.’ I have to admit, that’s a bit of a surprise.\"","There was a moment of silence.","When he saw she still had no intention of cooperating, Chen Yi thought for a moment before asking, \"Hawk... he’s probably already planning to withdraw from Shu State, isn’t he?\""]},{"number":238,"title":"Chapter 238 - 199: I Invite You All to Your Death","paragraphs":["Lou Yuxue’s eyes flew wide. She stared at him in disbelief. \"You, how do you know about Hawk... Was it... was it that night?!\"","The only thing she could think of was their encounter outside the West Market that night.","’So my guess was right—this man was outside the tailor shop in the West Market that night!’","Chen Yi gave a noncommittal nod. \"Actually, I know far more than you think.\"","\"What else do you know? My identity?\"","\"More than just that...\"","\"Never mind. If you want to know, follow me. If not, feel free to head straight back to the Spring Rain Building.\"","Chen Yi felt it was all rather dull. He gave her a look, then turned and mounted his horse.","\"But as long as you remain in Shu State, I’ll always be able to find you.\"","With that, he didn’t wait for Lou Yuxue to speak again. He cracked his whip against his horse’s rump and galloped down the main road, chasing after Liu Lang and the others.","Seeing him leave so decisively, Lou Yuxue’s expression flickered. She suddenly shouted, \"Wait up!\"","But Chen Yi didn’t even slow down. His voice, laced with a curse, drifted back. \"Wait, my ass. If you’re coming, then come.\"","\"You...\"","\"Me what?\"","\"Stop dawdling. And you call yourself a Hidden Guard Silver Banner Officer?\"","\"If I’d wanted to kill you, you wouldn’t have lived to see tonight!\"","Lou Yuxue seethed. Gritting her teeth, she leaped onto her horse and galloped straight after him.","However, when she finally spurred her horse and caught up with Chen Yi, every one of the several questions she asked was met with the same single-word answer: \"Guess.\"","No matter how composed Lou Yuxue normally was, he made her absolutely livid.","\"You said you were going to tell me!\"","Chen Yi chuckled. \"That was then, this is now. You’re the one who refused, aren’t you?\"","\"You...\"","\"Ten percent of the silver notes per question. Think carefully before you ask.\"","Beneath her mask, Lou Yuxue’s lips parted slightly as she stared at him, dumbfounded.","’What kind of question is worth thirty thousand silver coins?’","But seeing as they were getting closer and closer to Liu Lang and the others, Lou Yuxue took a deep breath and asked the one question she most wanted answered:","\"Who are you, really?\"","Chen Yi had clearly expected this. He pursed his lips. \"Ask another one. I don’t feel like answering that.\"","Lou Yuxue was instantly incensed. \"Are you messing with me?\"","If not for the sliver of reason she still possessed, and if not for the fact that she knew she couldn’t beat him, she really would have smashed her fist into his face.","’Just to see if his skin was really that thick.’","Seeing her persistence, Chen Yi said, \"Fine, listen up. I’m a member of the Xiao Family.\"","Lou Yuxue, of course, didn’t believe him. She huffed, \"If you were with the Xiao Family, how could you dare keep this from the Old Marquis?\"","\"And what makes you so sure the Old Marquis doesn’t know?\"","\"Hawk... Are you trying to trick me into giving you information?\"","When she still didn’t believe him, Chen Yi shook his head. \"Alright, fine. Actually, I’m with the Jing State Liu Family.\"","\"Impossible!\"","Lou Yuxue still refused to believe it. Pointing at the carriage up ahead, she said, her voice tight with exasperation, \"If you were one of Liu Wen’s men, why would he have come along?\"","\"Don’t tell me you plan on letting him go back alive.\"","Chen Yi glanced at her, a faint, unreadable smile on his lips. \"The main branch of the Liu Family has many legitimate heirs.\"","\"Is it not possible I work for Liu Zhaoxue?\"","\"Liu...\"","Lou Yuxue froze for a moment. She tilted her head to size him up, considering the possibility.","’Clearly, the answer was yes.’","’It’s just...’","\"Liu Zhaoxue would dare to have Liu Wen killed?\"","\"Why wouldn’t she? There is only one position of Patriarch in the Liu Family. Why can’t it be Zhaoxue?\"","\"But...\"","Before Lou Yuxue could press him further, Chen Yi raised a hand to cut her off. \"I’ve told you who I am. I don’t wish to elaborate on the reasons.\"","\"Whether you believe me or not is for you to decide.\"","Lou Yuxue gave him a long, hard look before asking her second question. \"What are you really trying to do?\"","Chen Yi looked at her in astonishment. \"You have to ask that? Are you just trying to give me free silver? I’m starting to doubt your intelligence.\"","\"Just tell me!\"","\"To kill Second Young Master Liu, of course.\"","\"...\"","Lou Yuxue stared at him blankly for a moment, then slapped her forehead in frustration.","’Even if this man’s identity was a lie, his intention to kill Liu Wen was absolutely real.’","’I really did ask a stupid question.’","Chen Yi ignored her. Seeing they were about to catch up to Liu Wen and the others, he said in a low voice,","\"Question time is over. Remember your promise. That silver—we split it sixty-forty, my favor.\"","With that, he spurred his horse forward, pulling up right alongside Liu Wen’s carriage and striking up a conversation with him.","Lou Yuxue watched his back, grinding her teeth in frustration.","’Even now, in her confrontation with this man, she was still on the losing end.’","’She was like a child, being toyed with in the palm of his hand, utterly unable to resist.’","’Now, all she could hope for was that the plan to \"burn the Three Towns’ summer grain\" would go off without a hitch.’","’After all, that was the outcome the Pavilion Master himself had approved.’","’If it failed, no matter where she and Hawk tried to hide, they would surely be punished.’","’Hawk...’","Thinking of Hawk, who’d been forced to flee Shu State, Lou Yuxue couldn’t help but feel a pang of gloom.","’It seemed unlikely that this plan of the Hidden Guards would reach a perfect conclusion.’","’At the very least, they wouldn’t be able to get all of the silver...’","As these thoughts ran through Lou Yuxue’s mind, her gaze toward the group ahead of them wavered uncertainly.","A moment later, she abruptly yanked her reins, turning her horse to ride back the way they had come.","’Liu Wu, scheme all you want, but I’ll never let you have that silver!’","Chen Yi naturally noticed her movement the instant it happened. He immediately smiled and said, \"Young Master Liu, please go on ahead. I have a small matter to attend to.\"","Liu Wen lifted the carriage curtain and glanced back. \"Is she running away?\"","Chen Yi nodded. \"There are always cowards who cling to life. It’s not surprising.\"","As he spoke, he calmly turned his horse around and rode after Lou Yuxue.","One chased, the other fled.","Lou Yuxue sensed him following and shouted coldly, \"The silver or Young Master Liu! You can only choose one!\"","Chen Yi, chasing her at a leisurely pace, just smiled. \"I’ll take both.\"","\"Then you can just try—huh?\""]},{"number":239,"title":"Chapter 239 - 199: Please, Go to Your Deaths","paragraphs":["Lou Yuxue was about to say something harsh when she suddenly felt her entire body go limp.","Not only could she not channel her True Essence, but all her physical strength was gone as well.","\"Why... is this happening?\"","Lou Yuxue struggled to stay upright for a moment before collapsing to one side, a bewildered look on her face. A faint understanding dawned in her mind: the bastard behind her was responsible.","’He... he even planned for this...’","Just then, Chen Yi spurred his horse forward and swept her into his arms. Without pausing, he grabbed the reins, wheeled the horse around, and gave chase to Liu Lang and the others.","Lou Yuxue leaned weakly against his chest and said feebly, \"You... you bastard... When did you drug me?\"","Chen Yi replied with a smile, \"Before I caught up with Young Master Liu. But you can’t really blame me.\"","\"If you hadn’t tried to run, you wouldn’t have fallen for it.\"","\"Hmph...\"","Lou Yuxue let out two weak huffs and turned her head away, clearly not wanting to acknowledge him.","’She had indeed lost miserably this time, but she would never let this go.’","’As long as she was alive, she would make this bastard pay!’","Chen Yi could more or less guess what she was thinking, but he didn’t mind chatting a bit more.","\"Can you tell me what the Hidden Guard is?\"","\"One question, ten percent... ten percent of the silver notes.\"","\"Fine.\"","\"...\"","Lou Yuxue gave him a charming eye-roll, clearly not believing he would actually pay up.","\"As a member of the Liu Family, how could you have never heard of the Hidden Guard?\"","Chen Yi told the truth. \"I really haven’t.\"","\"You must have at least heard of the White Tiger Guard, right?\"","’White Tiger Guard?’","Chen Yi thought for a moment but couldn’t recall anything.","\"I... probably have.\"","Lou Yuxue shot him a glare that held no menace and said with a hint of resignation:","\"The White Tiger Guard is one of the four guards under the Secretariat of our Great Wei Dynasty. We specialize in infiltrating enemy nations and neighboring states, with the duty of inciting defections and provoking disputes.\"","’So they’re just spies,’ Chen Yi realized.","’But their duties are a bit different from the Jinyi Guard I was picturing.’","\"Then what are you doing in Shu State?\"","Lou Yuxue leaned limply against him. \"That’s not a question for you to ask, nor is it something I would know.\"","Chen Yi privately pursed his lips. ’He knew that these Silver Banner Officers were only responsible for their own tasks. Even if they suspected their current mission deviated from the White Tiger Guard’s official duties, they wouldn’t dwell on it.’","’It wasn’t wise to press the matter further.’","’After all, the only reason he had spared Liu Si’er, Ge the Third, Lou Yuxue, and the others was to pry more secrets from them.’","’If he revealed too much, he would inevitably alert the higher-ups in the Hidden Guard.’","’If they were replaced, his losses would outweigh his gains.’","Just as Chen Yi was pondering this, Liu Wen’s voice came from up ahead:","\"Black Tooth, it’s midnight! Pick up the pace!\"","Chen Yi was about to reply when several lines of large, golden text suddenly floated before his eyes:","[Daily Intel · Celestial Level, Lower Grade: At a quarter past one in the morning, Black Tooth of Bright Moon Building will gather a group from the Evil Demonic Dao and, in collaboration with the Great Wei Dynasty’s White Tiger Guard, set fire to the summer grain of three border towns in Shu State. A significant Opportunity can be obtained.]","’Celestial Level!’","Chen Yi’s eyes fixed on those two words.","’Even without this rare \"Celestial Tier Opportunity\" tonight, he had planned to check on the Three Towns anyway. But he was naturally delighted that such an Opportunity had presented itself.’","After scanning the text and confirming there was nothing else of note, he rode up to Liu Wen’s carriage and said in a cold tone:","\"Young Master Liu, please be patient. Once we reach Iron Wall Town, your wish will naturally be granted.\"","Liu Wen snorted. \"It had better be.\"","\"I’ve spent so much silver and even come in person. If your Bright Moon Building can’t get this done, don’t blame me for turning ruthless.\"","Chen Yi laughed. \"In two hours, you can see for yourself when you arrive.\"","With that, he ignored Liu Wen and spurred his horse forward, shouting to Liu Lang and the others:","\"The Financier has given an order! Speed up! We need to reach Iron Wall Town within the hour!\"","Upon hearing this, Liu Lang was the first to chime in. \"You all heard what Black Tooth said, right? Pick up the pace!\"","\"I was getting impatient already! Faster, faster, faster! I’m itching to go on a killing spree!\"","\"Old Ghost Lin, don’t go berserk later. There’s an army of nearly eighty thousand there. If we get surrounded, we’re dead for sure.\"","\"Right, we can’t go deep into the Border Town. We just need to wait outside for our contact to pull out.\"","\"What’s there to be afraid of? With Elder Black Tooth here, you’re worried we can’t escape?\"","\"I remember Black Tooth was supposed to be heading to Cang Lang Town. Why’d he come back?\"","Liu Lang laughed heartily. \"He was scared he’d die in Cang Lang Town! What other reason could there be?\"","\"HAHAHA, so even Elder Black Tooth gets scared sometimes.\"","\"...\"","Listening to the conversation of the Evil Demonic Dao members up ahead, a smile touched Chen Yi’s lips. He then activated his Qi Observation Skill to carefully examine their auras.","’Middle Three Grades, Middle Three Grades, still Middle Three Grades... There was even one Evil Demon whose Cultivation had just reached the Sixth Grade Realm.’","’After a full sweep, the one with the highest Cultivation was surprisingly Liu Lang.’","Chen Yi understood. He turned his head and asked, \"Black Tooth went to Cang Lang Town?\"","But Lou Yuxue didn’t answer his question. Instead, she asked one of her own:","\"How much silver did you get from Liu Wen?\"","\"...You guess.\"","\"I want forty percent.\"","\"Heh. Miss Yuxue, have you ever heard the saying? ’A heart that is never content is like a snake trying to swallow an elephant.’\"","Lou Yuxue leaned against him, her head resting on his shoulder. Her breath was warm and fragrant as she said, \"Ten percent. Or you and I go our separate ways.\"","Chen Yi grabbed her by the neck and pulled her upright. He met her gaze for a moment and saw she wasn’t the least bit afraid, seemingly determined to follow through on her threat. He couldn’t help but smile and nod.","\"Ten percent it is. We’ll just deduct it from your share of the silver coins. That way, we’re still splitting it fifty-fifty.\"","Lou Yuxue’s eyes widened, and she stared at him, dumbfounded. \"That... that’s also three hundred thousand taels of silver?!\"","Chen Yi raised an eyebrow and pushed her back down against him, muttering, \"Should’ve told her a smaller number.\""]},{"number":240,"title":"Chapter 240 - 199: Please, Go to Your Deaths","paragraphs":["\"Liu Wu, you... you took so much silver, why did you have to rob us too?!\"","\"Simple. It’s faster to just take it.\"","\"You... you bastard! I’ll kill you!\"","Lou Yuxue was seething.","She and Hawk had worked themselves to the bone, scheming for so long. They had lost an Iron Banner Officer and risked discovery by Black Tooth’s people, all for a mere 150,000 silver.","But \"Liu Wu,\" all by himself, had taken less than ten days to not only steal their 150,000 silver, but also swindle another 300,000 from Liu Wen...","’How... how in the world did he manage it?’","Little did she know, Chen Yi was currently wondering, ’Should I leave that 150,000 silver for the Hidden Guard?’","He mulled it over.","Then he came to a decision.","’I should probably leave them a little something. Don’t want them getting so desperate they do something reckless.’","As Chen Yi considered this, he saw faint flickers of light appear at the far end of the official road.","The distance was so great that the lights were no bigger than fireflies, twinkling prettily like scattered stars.","Chen Yi froze. ’Wait... did the Hidden Guard succeed?’","’Xiao Jinghong, what are you doing?!’","...","「Cang Lang Town.」","Just after midnight, Xiao Jinghong sensed a strange disturbance near the Summer Grain Storage Room.","Sure enough, someone was about to burn the grain supplies for the soldiers of the Three Towns.","After confirming Liu Lang’s intelligence was accurate, Xiao Jinghong felt a swirl of complicated emotions.","She didn’t know whether to be pleased or furious.","She couldn’t understand who would employ such a vicious scheme to drive the Xiao Family to ruin.","’The Imperial Court?’","’One of the great Noble Families from Shu State?’","’Or was it a hostile foreign power?’","Xiao Jinghong found herself hoping it was the latter.","Whether it was Poshisu Country, the Barbarian Race, or the Western Continent Southern Invaders—any of them would have been a more palatable answer.","But things in this world rarely go as one wishes.","Mulling this over, Xiao Jinghong let out a soft sigh, rose, and stepped out of her wooden cabin.","In a single leap, she was on the roof, her eyes fixed on the distant Summer Grain Storage Room.","There, she saw a dozen or so soldiers in mismatched armor pouring flammable oil around the perimeter of the storage room.","Further off, General Pang Xuan of Cang Lang Town was leading a hundred Heavy Armored Soldiers, quietly encircling the building.","About fifteen minutes later.","The dozen or so soldiers finished pouring the oil.","Then, one of the soldiers pulled a bamboo tube from his tunic. With a quick push and pull, a shower of sparks shot skyward.","The next moment, a firework soared into the air from outside Cang Lang Town, a clear response.","Xiao Jinghong’s gaze snapped toward it, a flicker of murderous intent appearing in her eyes.","Without a moment’s hesitation, the might of her Martial Arts erupted from her.","The Heaven and Earth’s Spiritual Mechanism swirled like wind and fire, then plunged down around the grain storage like a sharp sword.","In the blink of an eye, she had suppressed the dozen or so soldiers, pinning them to the ground.","\"Th-this is...\"","\"There’s an Upper Three Grades master here...\"","\"We’re doomed...\"","As the soldiers reeled in terror, Xiao Jinghong shot into the air, flying off into the distance.","Seeing this, Pang Xuan dropped all pretense of stealth. He rushed to the front of the storage room, his face turning livid as he took in the sight of the flammable oil. He gritted his teeth and roared:","\"Capture them!\"","\"Be thorough! I want them alive!\"","\"I’d like to see just who has the gall to pull a stunt like this!\"","The situation behind her was resolved without a sound.","Xiao Jinghong’s attention was no longer on the storage room. Her eyes were fixed on the depths of the dense forest outside of town.","Her aura already enveloped a hundred-zhang radius of the area.","Just then, a similar power, one that churned the Heaven and Earth’s Spiritual Mechanism, rose from deep within the forest.","A sinister voice followed. \"Xiao Jinghong?\"","\"What are you doing here?\"","Xiao Jinghong hovered in mid-air, her hand resting on the hilt of her sword. Her voice was ice-cold as she replied:","\"I have been awaiting you all for some time—to invite you to your deaths!\""]},{"number":241,"title":"Chapter 241 - 200: A Wisp of Qing Feng in Hand Can Destroy the Nine States","paragraphs":["\"Heh heh... General Jinghong, what bold words.\"","\"You’re all alone. You have no grand army to back you up. How dare you invite us to our deaths?\"","\"Hee hee ha ha... Death is imminent, yet you remain oblivious.\"","\"Little girl, you’re a far cry from your father, Xiao Fengchun.\"","The moment Xiao Jinghong finished speaking, several strange, sharp voices echoed from deep within the forest.","They mocked her for overestimating her own strength.","It was likely the three Upper Three Grades Realm experts on their side that gave them such confidence.","\"Even if your father, Xiao Fengchun, were here, we would still cut him down—\"","\"Kill!\"","As Elder Demon Jia spoke, he plucked three strings, as if to bolster the morale of his fellow Evil Demons.","The music began.","Three wisps of wind stirred.","Like blades, they shot across fifty zhang in an instant, slicing straight for Xiao Jinghong.","Xiao Jinghong’s cold gaze, however, remained unchanged. With a flick of her slender hand...","SHIIING—","A sword hummed, and a flash of snowy light erupted.","She vanished into the night sky.","A chill shot through Black Tooth. With no time to warn the others, he instantly unleashed the Gang Qi in his body.","As his robes swelled, the Heaven and Earth’s Spiritual Mechanism converged in a two-zhang radius around him.","He had mounted his full defense the very instant he saw Xiao Jinghong disappear.","The next moment, Black Tooth saw the snowy light that had just streaked across the distant night sky materialize right in front of him.","It was as bright as day, bathing several Evil Demons in its glow.","The other Third Grade Realm Swordman finally reacted. Fear filled his eyes, and his long blade was already out of its sheath before he could even form a conscious thought.","Bathed in the snowy light, Elder Demon Jia from the Illusory Sound Sect let out a strange cry, his fingers plucking rapidly at his instrument.","The other Evil Demons with weaker cultivation, however, had no time to react.","Or rather, before they even could, they lost the chance to react at all.","The next moment, the light abruptly faded.","Only a faint, silvery-white trace remained, flickering in and out of existence.","It cast an unsteady, flickering light on Xiao Jinghong’s form, who now stood behind Black Tooth and the others.","One breath.","Two breaths.","Three...","Only then did Black Tooth let out a breath. The force of his exhale split the black iron mask on his face down the middle.","The two halves slid off and fell to the ground.","CLANG. CLANG.","A faint line of blood appeared on Black Tooth’s otherwise handsome face.","But he paid it no mind.","To be precise, he was gazing at the scene before him with a look of both terror and admiration—","Within a fifty-zhang radius, every thick tree and large rock had been silently sliced in two.","The air filled with the continuous RUMBLE of their collapse.","It drowned out the sound of more than ten Evil Demons, also cleaved in half, falling to the ground.","Both the quick-reacting Third Grade Swordman and Elder Demon Jia, who had managed a single attack, had died to that one sword strike from Xiao Jinghong.","They died in bewilderment and terror, without making so much as a ripple.","As the noise died down and dust filled the air, Black Tooth touched the bloody line on his face.","The crimson blood glowed, shifting from bright to dark red under the flickering, ethereal light.","Black Tooth glanced at the blood, sighed, and praised in admiration, \"A wisp of Qing Feng in hand can shatter the mountains and rivers of the Nine State.\"","\"That sword technique... was that the legendary ’Qing Feng,’ the ultimate art of the old Sword Master?\"","Without waiting for Xiao Jinghong to answer, Black Tooth nodded to himself. \"It must be.\"","\"Thirty years ago, the Elder Sword Master, already over a century old, went to the Wind and Rain Tower to duel Immortal Bai. They fought fiercely for three days and three nights, but he lost by a single move.\"","\"I heard his final strike was this very ’Qing Feng’.\"","\"They say one strike could sever a thousand-li wave of clouds. The sight must have been magnificent.\"","\"A pity... I was not fortunate enough to witness it.\"","Black Tooth sighed softly. He turned to face Xiao Jinghong, who stood ten zhang away, and sized her up before continuing.","\"Ten years ago, the Elder Sword Master accepted an invitation from the senior Sword Ghost to a duel on Kunlun Mountain. There were few spectators, but a few details still got out.\"","\"Sword Ghost didn’t last ten moves. The Elder Sword Master then forsook his sword and went into seclusion. And one other thing: the Sword Master’s ultimate art had found a successor.\"","Black Tooth paused, his expression turning serious. \"You must be the little girl who was at the Elder Sword Master Li Wudang’s side back then, aren’t you?\"","\"The whole world has been deceived. Who would have thought that the renowned General Jinghong was a disciple of the Sword Master? That she was the same little girl who defeated the head disciple of the Kunlun Sect at the age of ten?\"","\"Even I believed you were merely a master of both sword and spear, with a Fourth Grade Cultivation.\"","\"Heh heh, there’s no shame in this loss. Ha ha, no shame at all.\"","Black Tooth laughed heartily for a moment, then abruptly stopped. \"Kill me.\"","’He knew he was no match for Xiao Jinghong.’","’Even with his Great Success in Fist Dao, he couldn’t block a single strike from someone like Xiao Jinghong, who possessed the Sword Master’s ultimate art, had achieved Sword Dao Perfection, and had such a formidable cultivation.’","’Resistance and struggle would be useless.’","Xiao Jinghong regarded him calmly and said flatly, \"I will spare your life, but I want to know who hired your Bright Moon Building.\"","\"My apologies, General Jinghong, but it’s against the rules of the Bright Moon Building. I cannot say.\"","Black Tooth grimaced, a rare, bitter smile on his face.","’He could hardly remember the last time he’d felt so powerless.’","’But now, here it was again.’","Xiao Jinghong gave him one last look and said nothing more.","She simply thrust her sword forward.","Once again, a brilliant light flashed. Once again, the sword’s energy surged out fifty zhang, sending trees and rocks flying.","Black Tooth’s head flew into the air, a final breath still left in him.","As his head spun through the air, he laughed again. \"What a pity, General Jinghong! Burdened by the Xiao Family, you were forced to cultivate the Spear Dao as well. I’m afraid it will be nearly impossible for you to advance your Sword Dao any further now.\"","\"Ha ha ha... To think that even a goddess floating in the heavens can fall to the mortal world.\"","Amidst his laughter, Black Tooth’s head hit the ground and rolled a couple of times.","In his final moments, a single question remained in his mind—’Who betrayed the Bright Moon Building? Who told Xiao Jinghong to lay an ambush here?’","’You son of a bitch, I’ll be waiting for you in hell!’","Once the dust settled.","After confirming there was no one else suspicious, Xiao Jinghong flashed away, returning to the warehouse in Cang Lang Town."]},{"number":242,"title":"Chapter 242 - 200: A Wisp of Qing Feng in Hand, Can Destroy the Mountains and Rivers of the Nine States (Part 2)","paragraphs":["Seeing her return, Pang Xuan breathed a sigh of relief. He strode over and knelt on the ground.","\"Reporting, General! The traitors have all been apprehended!\"","Pausing for a moment, Pang Xuan’s face flushed with shame. \"I have been incompetent. I failed to detect the villains in town in time, causing you trouble, General. I await your punishment!\"","Seeing this, the surrounding soldiers also knelt down.","Only the dozen or so masked soldiers who had made a move earlier were bound and thrown to the side.","Xiao Jinghong swept her gaze over them and said coolly, \"Your merits and demerits cancel each other out. Rise.\"","Pang Xuan glanced up at her and offered a hesitant \"Thank you.\" After he stood, his face still bore a trace of shame.","The other soldiers rose as well.","Xiao Jinghong, of course, paid no mind to their feelings. Her gaze fell upon the dozen or so traitors who had come to burn the summer grain, and she commanded:","\"Interrogate them through the night. By tomorrow, I want to know who the mastermind is.\"","Pang Xuan quickly assented. \"I’ve already had my men search them for any poisons, lest they... Huh?\"","Before the words had left his mouth, he whirled around to look at the dozen-plus traitors.","The men, who were bound and gagged, were now bleeding from their eyes, ears, noses, and mouths, one after the other.","Pang Xuan’s face filled with astonishment. \"Quick!\" he shouted. \"Get a Physician to treat them!\"","\"It’s too late.\"","After observing them closely for a moment, Xiao Jinghong shook her head. \"It must be a Poison hidden beneath the skin, triggered by the vibrations of bone and muscle to corrode the internal organs.\"","\"But...\"","Before Pang Xuan could say more, Xiao Jinghong had already turned away.","\"I’m leaving this to you. I’m going to the Iron Wall and Profound Armor towns to check on their situations.\"","Seeing this, Pang Xuan had no choice but to bow. He then turned and commanded in a stern voice:","\"The Summer Grain Storage Room is vital ground! All of you will guard it with your lives! Any further lapses will be met with the full force of military law!\"","\"Yes, sir!\"","Xiao Jinghong heard the shouts behind her but simply focused on pushing her Gang Qi to its limits. Executing her Body Technique, she sped toward Iron Wall Town.","’She knew very well. Since assassins had come to burn the summer grain in Cang Lang Town, the other two towns would surely be no exception.’","’Fortunately, she had made arrangements beforehand. Li Changqing and Ma Kui should have been able to stop them.’","...","Yet even the best-laid plans can go awry.","Despite Xiao Jinghong’s orders, General Li Changqing of Iron Wall Military Town had remained skeptical.","His reaction was likely much the same as Pang Xuan’s when he first heard the news.","He looked down on the \"Sword Madman,\" Liu Lang, for being a man of the Jianghu, and so he was naturally disinclined to trust his words.","Furthermore, after two days passed with no incident following Xiao Jinghong’s orders, he had grown complacent.","By the time he realized his mistake, flames were already engulfing the area around the storage rooms.","Searing flames leaped into the sky, filling the air with black smoke laced with the fragrance of roasting wheat and rice.","A searing heat wave rolled out in all directions.","But all Li Changqing felt was a deathly chill. He stared at the inferno in disbelief, his face a ghastly, shifting shade of pale.","’It’s over.’","’I’m definitely going to be punished for this.’","Just then, the squads of Armored Warriors who had been guarding the vital storage rooms began to shout frantically:","\"Fire!\"","\"Someone, quick! Put out the fire!\"","\"Hurry—\"","In an instant, every soldier in the Iron Wall Military Town was on alert.","No one could remain calm, especially when they saw that the flames were coming from the vital storage rooms for the summer grain.","\"Which son of a bitch did this?\"","\"Damn them to hell! I finally get a few days with a full belly, and now someone’s burning our rations? Are they trying to starve us to death?\"","\"Enough talk! Put out the fire!\"","\"The fire hasn’t spread far! We still have time!\"","Led by the Vice General, several Deputy Generals began organizing men to fight the fire while berating the soldiers who were falling apart around them.","\"General Li, General Li...\"","The shouts finally brought Li Changqing back to his senses. Seeing the worried, anxious faces of the soldiers at his side, he pushed aside his thoughts and immediately gave the order:","\"I smell lamp oil, but it probably hasn’t soaked through yet! Try to break down the storage room walls and get the grain out!\"","After so many years leading troops, he knew a thing or two. A fire fueled by oil was nearly impossible to extinguish with conventional methods.","Rather than waste time trying, it was better to sacrifice the grain on the outer edges to save what was left inside.","His Personal Guard immediately acknowledged the order. After dousing themselves with buckets of water, they charged into the storage room with a group of Armored Warriors.","Other soldiers, relying on their high Cultivation, hacked and stabbed at the sturdy walls of the storage room with their blades and spears.","After about a quarter of an hour, Li Changqing saw men managing to pull several intact sacks out of the fire, and he felt a sliver of relief.","’At least my method is working.’","But when he thought of the consequences, he knew he couldn’t possibly escape punishment.","’The only thing to do now is to salvage as much as I can.’","As these thoughts raced through his mind, Li Changqing’s expression hardened. He bellowed:","\"Men! Follow me and capture the arsonists! We cannot let them escape, or we’ll all be implicated!\"","But with the current chaos, finding the traitors among the crowd was clearly impossible.","Li Changqing immediately ordered all soldiers not engaged in fighting the fire or saving the grain to deploy and pursue the culprits in all directions.","\"I want them found—dead or alive!\"","「Meanwhile.」","On a hillside ten li north of Iron Wall Town.","Liu Wen gazed at the distant glow of the fire, his effeminate face wreathed in a smile.","\"Excellent, just excellent... A fine fire. Burn it all to the ground, haha...\"","Chen Yi stood at his side, his expression hidden behind his black iron mask.","But his gaze toward Iron Wall Town held a hint of resignation.","’He still couldn’t understand. He had clearly arranged for Pei Guanli to warn Xiao Jinghong in advance, so how had they still succeeded at Iron Wall Town?’","But Lou Yuxue, still held in his arms, breathed a sigh of relief.","’The summer grain at Iron Wall Town was burned. Not only could she and the Hawk now report back successfully, avoiding punishment from the Pavilion Master, but she had also confirmed her suspicions in the process.’"]},{"number":243,"title":"Chapter 243 - 200: A Wisp of Qing Feng in Hand to Shatter the Nine States","paragraphs":["—This mysterious \"Liu Wu\" was indeed not from the Xiao Family.","As for whether \"Liu Wu\" was from the Jing State Liu Family, that was something she still needed to confirm.","All in all, it wasn’t the worst possible outcome.","Nearby, Liu Lang, who was also in on it, glanced at the fiery glow of Iron Wall Town. He couldn’t help but lean closer to Chen Yi and ask in a low voice,","\"Boss, weren’t you...\"","Chen Yi raised a hand, cutting him off. \"Weren’t I what? Get a move on and take our comrades to provide support.\"","Liu Lang froze for a moment. He glanced aside and noticed the looks from the other Evil Demons, then gave a subtle nod.","\"Let’s go. Follow me to meet them!\"","\"Heh heh, I like this kind of easy business. Elder Black Tooth, if another opportunity like this comes up, please be sure to save a spot for me.\"","\"After this job, we’ll have thousands of silver in hand. That’s more than our last ten jobs combined.\"","\"Easy money, haha...\"","Once Liu Lang and the others were a good distance away, Chen Yi confirmed no one else was watching. He then turned his head to Liu Wen and asked,","\"Young Master Liu, are you satisfied?\"","Liu Wen smiled and nodded. \"Satisfied. I am very satisfied!\"","\"I had some concerns at first, but after seeing this, I’m completely convinced.\"","\"The Bright Moon Building truly lives up to its reputation as one of the top powers in the Jianghu. Your reach is incredible. You actually managed to burn the summer grain of the Three Towns.\"","\"Elder Black Tooth, we must stay in close contact after today.\"","Even though Liu Wen was worldly and came from a prestigious family, he had rarely been involved in something as momentous as burning a Border Town’s grain supply.","He hadn’t just never experienced it; he’d only ever heard stories about it.","So, when he witnessed the grain stores of Iron Wall Town burning with his own eyes, the immense satisfaction and sense of accomplishment sent him into a state of euphoria.","For the first time in his life, he felt the exhilarating thought that ’the world is in my hands.’","Chen Yi could, of course, understand what Liu Wen was thinking.","It was similar to a greenhorn at a casino winning a million silver with a ten-silver bet.","They probably truly started to see themselves as a \"Son of Destiny\" or \"the Chosen One.\"","Little did they know, some feelings that seem so real are nothing but smoke and mirrors.","They shatter with a single poke.","Chen Yi smiled, his eyes flicking to the charioteer behind Liu Wen. He knew the man was also a Middle Third-Grade Martial Artist, so he didn’t hesitate any longer.","A small porcelain bottle then slid into his hand.","CRACK.","The crisp, pleasant sound naturally didn’t attract Liu Wen’s attention.","Only Lou Yuxue noticed his movement. She looked at Liu Wen with pity in her eyes.","’This Second Young Master Liu is pathetic. Being played like a fiddle without even knowing it. He deserves to die.’","’Ugh, why did I say \"too\"?’","Sure enough, before long, both the ecstatic Liu Wen and his charioteer noticed something was wrong with their bodies.","Before they could react, they collapsed one after the other.","\"What’s happening? I... why can’t I move?\"","\"Black Tooth? Black Tooth?\"","Liu Wen looked at the tall figure in front of him, then at the limp Lou Yuxue in his arms. No matter how foolish he was, he realized whose scheme he had fallen for.","He immediately demanded in fury, \"Black Tooth, what are you doing? How dare you move against me? Do you have a death wish?!\"","Before Chen Yi could reply, Lou Yuxue, unable to bear his stupidity, couldn’t help but say,","\"It’s obvious.\"","\"You’ve been tricked.\"","Chen Yi paused, then grabbed her by the neck and lifted her into the air. \"You talk too much.\"","Lou Yuxue snorted. \"I’ll talk if I want. Kill me if you have the guts.\"","Chen Yi shook his head. \"Killing you would be too much trouble.\"","\"I knew you wouldn’t dare. You...\"","But before Lou Yuxue could finish, Chen Yi had already chopped the side of her neck, forcing her into silence.","\"I was going to let you listen in for a bit, but since you’re so chatty, why don’t you take a nap first?\"","Chen Yi muttered this, carried her to the carriage, and only then turned back to Liu Wen’s side, saying with a smile,","\"My apologies, Young Master Liu. I’ll be borrowing the carriage.\"","Before he could speak, Chen Yi continued, \"But I imagine you won’t be needing this carriage anymore, so you shouldn’t mind.\"","Liu Wen’s face was ashen as he glared, his features twisted with rage, his eyes filled with a crazed killing intent.","\"What exactly are you trying to do?\"","\"I have no past grievances or recent grudges with you. Why are you harming me?\"","\"I even gave you three hundred thousand silver! Is this how you treat me!?\"","Chen Yi chuckled. \"Young Master Liu, you have a lot of questions. I’m not sure where to begin.\"","\"How about I tell you a story?\"","Without waiting for Liu Wen’s consent, Chen Yi began to remove the Five-section Spear from his arm and assemble it as he spoke.","\"Once, there was a poor scholar who, for certain reasons, was forced to come to Shu State. He was the type of person who was an outcast, unloved by all.\"","\"That was fine, though.\"","\"After all, he himself had no love for fame or fortune. He just wanted to live a quiet, peaceful, and carefree life.\"","\"Although his circumstances weren’t ideal, he was determined to keep a low profile and not attract attention, so his days were manageable.\"","Chen Yi paused. He finished assembling the Five-section Spear and looked at Liu Wen’s still hateful and furious eyes, then said with a smile,","\"But then one day, some ridiculous fellow appeared out of nowhere and insisted on taking him for a ’trip’.\"","\"That fellow was truly baffling. The scholar had done nothing at all, yet he was still targeted.\"","\"Then, that fellow even threatened to kill him and seize his wife and sister-in-law.\"","\"Left with no choice...\"","The smile in Chen Yi’s voice faded slightly as he thrust the Five-section Spear in his hand into the heart of the nearby charioteer.","Then he twisted it twice.","The still-furious Liu Wen froze at the sight, his eyes wide with disbelief as he stared at Chen Yi.","After three breaths, his expression had unknowingly changed.","From hatred and fury to pleading and desperation. He began to beg for his life.","\"Stop talking, please stop! Whatever you want, I’ll give it to you, I’ll give it all to you!\"","\"Silver? I’ll give you a hundred thousand! No, a million! I’m begging you, please don’t kill me...\"","Chen Yi pulled out the Long Spear, glanced at him, and let out a dry laugh.","\"You and he are truly brothers, connected by blood. You even have the same reaction right before death.\"","\"The only difference is that I had crushed his larynx back then, so he couldn’t speak and could only kneel on the ground and beg.\"","\"You, Second Young Master Liu, simply can’t move. There’s still a difference.\"","Hearing this, Liu Wen’s pleas died in his throat. He stared at Chen Yi in stunned terror, his voice strained as he said,","\"It... it was you... who killed Liu Jing?\""]},{"number":244,"title":"Chapter 244 - 201: All Men Must Die","paragraphs":["Since the Jing State Liu Family had sent Liu Wen to Shu State to manage Xinglin Hall, he was naturally no fool.","Though Chen Yi’s story was baffling at first, Liu Wen caught on the moment he heard \"brother\" and \"on his deathbed.\"","The man before him had killed Liu Jing.","Then came a second thought—’This person definitely isn’t Black Tooth!’","\"Who... who in the world are you?\"","Before Chen Yi could answer, Liu Wen started rambling, as if he had finally pinpointed what had felt so wrong earlier.","\"His wife, his sister-in-law...\"","\"A scholar, forced to come to Shu State...\"","As Liu Wen muttered these phrases over and over, a look of stunned disbelief spread across his face as he stared at Chen Yi.","\"You, you you... you’re...\"","Chen Yi smiled. \"Have you guessed?\"","\"But then, I never intended to hide it from you.\"","\"After all, a Financier as generous as Young Master Liu, willing to part with three hundred thousand silver at once, is a rare find. It wouldn’t feel right to let you die without knowing the truth.\"","\"Don’t you agree?\"","But Liu Wen seemed deaf to his words, still reeling in disbelief.","He was too stunned to even think of begging for his life again.","\"How could it be you?\"","\"But you’re just an outcast from the Chen Family! A despised live-in son-in-law! Nothing more than a scholar who got a little famous from his calligraphy...!\"","\"I’ve seen plenty of parasites like you. They all come to a bad end. But why... why is it you?\"","\"Why is it you, you bastard!?\"","Liu Wen now understood everything completely.","His sixth brother was dead, and the Xiao Family didn’t know who the killer was. To stop the Jing State Liu Family from causing more trouble, they had no choice but to find a scapegoat.","But this man before him, Chen Yi, had been hiding in the shadows all along, scheming and plotting.","Liu Wen couldn’t accept it.","He had been meticulously plotted against while completely unsuspecting, and a bellyful of rage and indignation welled up inside him.","If he didn’t let it out, he would go mad even if he managed to survive this.","Seeing this, Chen Yi just smiled and shook his head. \"Perhaps it’s because I’m luckier.\"","Then he took off his black iron mask, revealing a handsome face, and continued:","\"I was indeed lucky. I met a few people here that I care about, and it’s given me a bit of a sense of belonging.\"","Chen Yi paused, looking at the still-dazed Liu Wen, and said in a serious tone:","\"I don’t want what I’ve worked so hard to get to be taken away, and I especially don’t like my peaceful life being disrupted.\"","\"So, I’ll just have to work a little harder to make sure you, and everyone else who wants to drag this place into the mud, all die.\"","Liu Wen snapped back to his senses at those words. Staring at the unfamiliar face that seemed completely disconnected from the man he’d seen during the day, a crazed look appeared on his own.","\"Who do you think you are!?\"","\"You’re just a live-in son-in-law to the Xiao Family! You’re their dog!\"","\"After all you’ve done, do you think they’ll appreciate you? They won’t! In their eyes, you’re still just a dog used to keep Xiao Jinghong around!\"","Chen Yi gave a noncommittal nod. \"Perhaps.\"","His calm demeanor drove Liu Wen to the brink of madness. He roared, his face twisted in a snarl:","\"Don’t get cocky!\"","\"Even if you got lucky this time, my Liu Family will definitely make you—and the Xiao Family—pay the price!\"","\"And even if my Liu Family doesn’t succeed, there are the other Noble Families of Shu State, the great families of Jing State, Jiao State, and other places! They all want to see the Xiao Family fall, and they’re all waiting to carve up the Dingyuan Army!\"","\"Even your own Jiangnan Prefecture Chen Family, do you think they don’t have the same idea?\"","With that, Liu Wen began to laugh maniacally, as if he’d struck a nerve.","\"When that time comes, what will you do? What can you do? Will you destroy the Chen Family too?!\"","Chen Yi watched him in silence. After a moment of serious thought, he sighed and said again, \"Perhaps.\"","’I’ve never considered that question before.’","’I had assumed I’d have no more dealings with the Jiangnan Prefecture Chen Family.’","’Even with Chen Yunfan there, I only ever figured we’d just be able to sit down for a chat.’","’I never imagined I might end up on the opposite side of the Chen Family.’","’But if that day really came...’","’Heh. I’ve always been the type to side with my own, right or wrong.’","’What does the Jiangnan Prefecture Chen Family have to do with me?’","With that thought, Chen Yi steadied himself. He glanced toward Iron Wall Town and saw Liu Lang and his men about to return. \"Alright,\" he said.","\"The hour is late. It’s time to send you on your way.\"","The wild, crazed smile on Liu Wen’s face froze, replaced by the terror of impending death, mingled with faint traces of regret and anger.","Immediately after, Liu Wen began to plead in a panic, \"Mr. Qingzhou, please forgive me! Please let me go, spare my life.\"","\"I... I’m useful. I can help you.\"","\"Silver, men, or anything else. As long as you spare me, anything is fine.\"","\"I can even help you fend off the Liu Family! No, I’ll even help you destroy the Liu Family if you want! You’re only one person, and the Xiao Family won’t help you. I’ll help you...\"","Watching him, Chen Yi smiled and shook his head. \"No.\"","\"If you had only intended to kill me, or only offended me, I might have spared you, seeing as you still have some use.\"","\"But you had to go and provoke someone you never should have.\"","Chen Yi recalled Xiao Wan’er’s panic when she first heard of the Liu Family’s marriage proposal, and her shock when Liu Wen had accosted her that day. The memory soured his mood.","\"I’ll apologize, I’ll compensate, you...\"","This time, however, Chen Yi had run out of patience.","In one swift motion, he thrust his spear into Liu Wen’s chest and slowly began to twist the tip.","Liu Wen felt no pain, but he could feel the unnatural stirring inside his chest.","\"No, no, I beg you, I beg you to spare my life...\"","Hearing this, Chen Yi paused slightly, as if remembering something, and said with a smile:","\"I almost forgot. There’s one more thing I haven’t told you.\""]},{"number":245,"title":"Chapter 245 - 201: All Men Must Die","paragraphs":["\"Truth is, even if I hadn’t tricked you into coming here tonight, you wouldn’t have lived much longer.\"","\"Because your third sister has already joined forces with the Five Poison Sect to have you killed.\"","Liu Wen’s hateful expression gave way to a sliver of astonishment. \"She... she’d dare?\"","Chen Yi looked at him, not without a trace of pity, and said, \"The incident at Fengchun Building today was, no doubt, a trap she set for you.\"","\"Alright, I’ve said my piece.\"","\"Have a good journey.\"","As he spoke, Chen Yi unhesitatingly twisted the Long Spear, shredding Liu Wen’s heart.","Blood immediately trickled from the corner of Liu Wen’s mouth. With a strength from God-knows-where, he managed to lift a hand, glaring venomously at Chen Yi as he struggled to say:","\"I’ll... I’ll be waiting for you...\"","Chen Yi smiled, pulled out the Long Spear, wiped it clean on the man’s clothes, and said:","\"Here’s a saying for you.\"","\"All men must die. Some deaths are lighter than a feather, others heavier than Mount Tai.\"","\"The meaning isn’t hard to understand. So I advise you to reincarnate as soon as possible. You might even get to be an animal.\"","\"Even if you wait for me on the other side, I’ll do nothing but mock, ridicule, and scorn you. Why bother?\"","\"You... you...\"","Liu Wen’s eyes instantly filled with blood. He pointed a trembling finger at him, and then fell silent.","Chen Yi clicked his tongue. \"In the end, you still couldn’t die in peace. A waste of breath.\"","Muttering this, he casually closed Liu Wen’s eyes.","Seeing Liu Lang and the others approaching, Chen Yi thought for a moment, then hefted his Long Spear and went to meet them.","As expected, a few of the Hidden Guard’s Iron Banner Officers stationed in Iron Wall Town had managed to escape. The Evil Demons hadn’t met with any real resistance either.","But when they saw Chen Yi, their running footsteps faltered.","\"Who are you?\"","\"Why are you wearing Elder Black Tooth’s clothes?\"","\"Look over there! How did Young Master Liu die?\"","\"Be careful! Something’s wrong with this guy!\"","Chen Yi’s gaze swept over them, finally landing on Liu Lang. He gestured and said, \"Kill them all.\"","Liu Lang smiled and nodded. \"It’s about time.\"","When he saw Liu Wen lying on the ground, he had already guessed this would be the outcome, so he wasn’t surprised.","In contrast, the other Evil Demons were stunned, not understanding what was happening.","And the few soldiers from Iron Wall Town who had just escaped with their lives were even more clueless.","But they did know that Chen Yi and Liu Lang intended to kill them, and they reacted quickly.","\"Fucking ’Sword Madman,’ and you, pretty boy! You’re courting death!\"","\"You think the two of you can kill all of us?\"","\"What a joke!\"","However, at this point, whether it was a joke or not no longer mattered.","After giving the order, Chen Yi didn’t leave Liu Lang to handle it alone. He struck first.","He was seen gripping the butt of his Long Spear with both hands, his body held taut and straight.","As True Essence circulated within him, the Heaven and Earth’s Spiritual Mechanism instantly gathered at the tip of his spear.","Then, a glint of cold light flashed—Chen Yi shot forward with his spear.","Like an arrow loosed from a fully drawn longbow, he thrust straight toward the group of Evil Demonic Dao practitioners.","\"You’re courting death!\"","The Evil Demons drew their weapons one after another to meet his charge.","Some tried to block, others drew their blades to chop, but it was clear none of them had detected Chen Yi’s Great Success Spear Dao.","But as he closed in, they all felt as if a mountain had suddenly crashed down upon them.","Their bodies, which should have been swift and fierce, felt as if they had sunk into a quagmire.","Chen Yi, on the other hand, was completely unaffected.","The spear passed.","The spear’s light swept out in its wake.","The Evil Demonic Dao practitioners were like sheets of thin paper cut by a sharp edge—their bodies were severed, as were the weapons in their hands.","In a single move, Chen Yi had instantly killed five people.","Seeing this, Liu Lang’s eyes went wide. \"Gr-Gr-Gr-Great...\"","Chen Yi didn’t pause for a second, continuing his charge toward the others while cursing, \"Great what? Reinforcements will be here soon! Get a move on!\"","Liu Lang suppressed the shock in his heart. As he drew his Blade and charged the nearest Evil Demon, he shouted:","\"Boss, you really are a Martial Arts genius!\"","’Great Success in Fist Dao was one thing, but to think his Spear Dao was also at the Great Success Realm.’","’If I add his Medical Dao to the list...’","’Damn, just what kind of monster is Boss Chen?’","But thoughts were just thoughts, and Liu Lang was not slow to act.","He and Chen Yi blocked the Evil Demonic Dao practitioners’ escape route from the front and back.","In just three breaths’ time, they made short work of the rest, killing every last one.","Not even the few soldiers from Iron Wall Town who had just escaped managed to get away.","Once everything had quieted down, Chen Yi glanced at the rapidly approaching torchlight in the distance and, without pausing, turned to leave.","\"Get the carriage. We’re heading back to the city.\"","\"Right.\"","Liu Lang sheathed his long Blade and ran toward the carriage.","Chen Yi, meanwhile, returned to Liu Wen’s body. He took a letter from his robes and stuffed it into the dead man’s.","To make it look authentic, he deliberately smeared some of Liu Wen’s blood on the letter.","After doing all this, Chen Yi leaped onto the carriage.","\"Go!\"","Liu Lang was well aware of their situation. With two cracks of the whip, he urged the horses on, speeding toward Shu State.","Once the carriage had left the forest and was galloping along the main road,","Liu Lang relaxed slightly and couldn’t help but speak up:","\"Boss, could I ask a favor of you?\"","Chen Yi came down from the roof of the carriage and landed beside him. While putting away his Five-section Spear, he asked, \"So formal?\"","Liu Lang gave a sheepish grin. \"When you have some free time, would you be willing to spar with me?\"","Chen Yi raised an eyebrow slightly, turning his head to look at him with a half-smile. \"Trying to bully me because my Cultivation is lower than yours, are you?\"","\"You misunderstand, I just... I just get excited when I see a worthy opponent.\"","\"After all, achieving Great Success in both Punch and Spear Dao is a rarity in the Jianghu, hehe.\"","Liu Lang quickly added, \"If you’re worried, I’ll definitely suppress my Cultivation to match your Realm.\"","\"That won’t be necessary...\"","Although Chen Yi wasn’t particularly enthusiastic about sparring matches, he wasn’t strongly opposed to them either.","After all, he had often crossed hands with Pei Guanli in the past."]},{"number":246,"title":"Chapter 246 - 201: All Men Must Die","paragraphs":["He was, however, self-aware.","At his current Martial Arts Realm and cultivation, he could handle bullying those weaker than him. But against a veteran of the Jianghu like Liu Lang, his experience was sorely lacking.","Chen Yi thought for a moment. \"I’ll agree to the duel.\"","But before Liu Lang could express his joy, Chen Yi continued, \"But not now.\"","\"The burning of the summer grain in the Three Towns is just the beginning. There are still some loose ends to tie up.\"","\"It won’t be too late for us to duel after the dust has settled.\"","Liu Lang nodded and smiled. \"As you say.\"","With the matter settled, he finally relaxed.","\"Boss, do you think we’ll still have trouble after this?\"","Chen Yi grunted in acknowledgment. He secured his Five-section Spear and glanced at the trees lining the road.","\"There’ll be no shortage of trouble.\"","\"First, Bright Moon Building will be a significant problem.\"","\"We’ll be better off if Black Tooth is dead; the trouble would be delayed. If he’s still alive, he’ll definitely investigate the source of the leak.\"","\"Then there’s the burning of the summer grain at Iron Wall Town. Someone will have to pay the price for that.\"","\"The Xiao Family and the Dingyuan Army won’t stop investigating the matter until they get to the bottom of it.\"","\"But the ones who will bear the brunt of it should be the Jing State Liu Family and... the other Financier.\"","Come to think of it, Chen Yi still didn’t know the Financier’s identity.","’I’ll have to make a note of it for now.’","\"The third problem... is a major one for both of us, one that needs to be dealt with urgently.\"","Liu Lang, however, was unfazed. \"I’m not afraid of trouble.\"","\"I’m only afraid they won’t have any real strength. Cutting them down would be too dull.\"","Hearing this, Chen Yi glanced at him with a faint, wry smile. \"What about Xiao Jinghong?\"","Liu Lang froze. The thought of the terrifyingly powerful General Jinghong made him chuckle nervously.","\"Sh-she wouldn’t come looking for us, would she?\"","\"Because of that letter I sent her in your name, she’s bound to come looking for you.\"","\"Boss, can I tell her the truth?\"","Chen Yi shot him a glare. \"Of course not.\"","\"So, you’ll need to lie low for a while. I’ll have Zhang Dabao send you supplies regularly.\"","Liu Lang nodded helplessly. \"I suppose it’s the only way.\"","Faced with the extraordinarily talented General Jinghong and her heaven-defying cultivation, he had no confidence he could keep his mouth shut.","Chen Yi knew this as well, so he also planned to keep a low profile for the time being.","In fact, besides the problems he had just mentioned, there were a few other matters that could potentially involve him.","For instance, the Hidden Guard—people like Lady Tiger and Hawk—would certainly not let him off the hook.","Then there was the Jing State Liu Family.","Even with Liu Wen dead here tonight, confirming his involvement in burning the Three Towns’ summer grain, the Liu Family would likely find a way to shirk responsibility.","They would lose some influence at worst.","But regardless of the outcome, the Liu Family was bound to investigate Liu Wen’s death and the events of tonight.","When that happened, Chen Yi would have to find a way to erase all traces of his involvement.","’Or... I could divert the Liu Family’s attention.’","A moment of silence passed.","\"Boss, where are we headed next?\"","\"First, come with me to Spring Rain Building to pick something up.\"","\"The silver?\"","\"Yes. It would be a shame to let someone else get their hands on it...\"","...","「An hour later.」","The once-bright night sky had dimmed, and a thick bank of dark clouds was rolling in from all directions.","Lightning tore across the sky as the clouds churned.","Thunder boomed.","A torrential downpour followed.","At that moment, on a small hill outside Iron Wall Town.","Li Changqing stared grimly at the two rows of corpses arranged on the ground. He asked in a cold voice,","\"Is this all of them?\"","A deputy general in Vine Armor beside him bowed. \"The battle was already over when we arrived,\" he replied.","\"We found wheel tracks, but a search turned up no other suspicious individuals. However...\"","He hesitated, glancing at Li Changqing’s expression before continuing, \"However, all of the escaped traitors are here.\"","Li Changqing laughed in fury. \"So I’m supposed to thank someone for double-crossing their own partners?\"","At his words, the surrounding soldiers immediately dropped to their knees. \"We were incompetent! We await your punishment, my lord!\"","Li Changqing snorted. \"Punishment? The grain was burned. Do you think a simple punishment will be the end of this?\"","He knew, however, that the soldiers had little to do with it.","Instead, he would be the one to bear the full weight of responsibility.","His eyes swept over the scene.","Li Changqing’s gaze landed on Liu Wen. His brow furrowed as he walked straight toward the body.","The Personal Guard holding an umbrella over him hurried to keep up.","Li Changqing drew closer, examining the body carefully.","’This man... Fine robes, a jade belt, distinguished features... from a Noble Family?’","Typically, only young masters from the great Noble Families could afford such attire.","But since Li Changqing didn’t know the man’s identity, he couldn’t be certain.","He was about to order a thorough investigation when something on Liu Wen’s chest caught his eye.","To be precise, he saw the corner of a piece of paper sticking out from his robes.","Li Changqing quickly crouched down, pulled open the man’s lapel, and drew the paper from the blood-soaked fabric.","’A letter?’","Without hesitation, he opened it and began to read by the light of his Personal Guard’s torch.","He only needed a single glance.","Li Changqing, who had been wracked with worry, suddenly broke into a joyful expression.","\"Haha... Heaven always leaves a way out! Excellent, just excellent...\"","\"To think today’s disaster was the work of an inside man. No wonder... no wonder my guard was down.\"","’Xiao Dongchen, you treacherous bastard!’","’It’s only right that you take the fall for me!’","Li Changqing couldn’t help but be overjoyed.","Originally, with the summer grain at Iron Wall Town burned, he would have been unable to escape blame no matter what he did.","But now, things were different.","With this secret letter signed and marked by Xiao Dongchen, plus the corpse of a man from a Noble Family, he could at least break even, his merits canceling out his failures.","Thinking of this, Li Changqing quickly ordered his men to take all the bodies and return to Iron Wall Town.","Just then, a cold voice laced with anger echoed across the sky above Iron Wall Town:","\"Li Changqing, get over here!\"","\"I clearly notified you two days ago that someone was planning to burn the summer grain. How could you still have allowed this to happen?!\"","The smile on Li Changqing’s face instantly froze. ’Xiao Jinghong?’","’Crap, I forgot about that.’","’Now, breaking even is going to be difficult.’"]},{"number":247,"title":"Chapter 247 - 202: What’s to Fear? A Beating at Most.","paragraphs":["No wonder Xiao Jinghong was furious.","Two days ago, she had repeatedly warned Li Changqing to guard the warehouse carefully and prevent any miscreants from succeeding.","But upon her arrival, she was met with the disastrous scene around Iron Wall Town’s Summer Grain Storage Room.","Any joy she’d felt knowing that Cang Lang and Profound Armor Towns were safe instantly vanished.","Xiao Jinghong scanned her surroundings and asked, \"What is the situation now?\"","A soldier, his entire body blackened by smoke, hastily knelt.","\"Reporting to the General, of the nearly five hundred thousand stones of summer grain, we... we only managed to save two hundred thousand...\"","\"But thanks to the heavy rain, the fire is under control. There should still be quite a bit of grain left underneath.\"","Xiao Jinghong’s hand subconsciously went to the hilt of the sword at her waist.","’If Li Changqing were here right now, she might have run him through with her sword.’","’Three hundred thousand stones of grain... That was equivalent to nearly four months of rations for the soldiers of Iron Wall Town.’","’For a loss this great, having Li Changqing’s head for it would not be an overreaction.’","However, upon seeing the crucial warehouse reduced to ruins before her and the soot-streaked faces and bodies of the surrounding soldiers, Xiao Jinghong sighed softly and gave her orders:","\"Continue salvaging the summer grain. Save as much as you can.\"","\"Also, when General Li arrives, tell him I will be waiting for him at the General’s Mansion.\"","\"Yes, General.\"","In a flash, Xiao Jinghong was at the town’s General’s Mansion. She sat upright in the main hall, watching the downpour outside.","As her True Essence circulated, she calmed her heart and mind, and the events of the evening inevitably surfaced in her thoughts.","’If someone hadn’t warned her in advance, the losses would have been even greater.’","’Losing less than three hundred thousand stones of grain was a stroke of luck amidst this misfortune.’","’Moreover, the perpetrators were all eliminated, including those of the Evil Demonic Dao from the Bright Moon Building. The outcome wasn’t so terrible.’","’As long as she found the mastermind, she was certain the Xiao Family had the power to recoup these losses.’","But a flicker of anger still remained in Xiao Jinghong’s heart.","She wasn’t angry about the loss itself, but about Li Changqing’s arrogance and pigheadedness.","’If Li Changqing had been like General Ma Kui of Profound Armor Town and taken strict precautions, how could the fire possibly have started?’","「A short while later.」","Li Changqing hurried back with his men. After telling the Armored Warriors to wait at the entrance, he straightened his appearance and solemnly walked into the hall.","He knelt on one knee, clasping his hands in a salute.","\"Li Changqing, General of Iron Wall Town, pays his respects to the General.\"","Xiao Jinghong watched him calmly. Seeing no remorse for his impending punishment in his expression, she spoke:","\"Report what happened this time.\"","Li Changqing inwardly breathed a small sigh of relief. ’At least Xiao Jinghong didn’t just cut me down with her sword.’","Without hesitation, he said from his kneeling position, \"The loss of summer grain in Iron Wall Town is my fault. My momentary negligence allowed the miscreants to succeed.\"","\"However...\"","Li Changqing paused, took a letter from his robes, stood to place it before Xiao Jinghong, and then knelt back down. He continued:","\"However, I also made a discovery. I found this, which should help you, General, find the mastermind behind this incident.\"","Xiao Jinghong picked up the letter and began to read, her eyes immediately narrowing.","*[If you wish to become the Xiao Family Patriarch, you must cooperate with my Young Master... Show your sincerity... Burn the summer grain in the Three Towns...]*","*[An initial payment of three hundred thousand silver coins, with another three hundred thousand upon completion... Wishing you success—Xiao Dongchen!]*","Xiao Jinghong’s gaze fell to the end of the letter. At the sight of the blood-red handprint and the blood-stained signature, a chill ran through her.","’Xiao Dongchen... Tonight’s events were the work of a traitor within the Xiao Family?’","Li Changqing looked up at her and said hesitantly:","\"General, regarding the loss of the grain, I was indeed derelict in my duty. I await your punishment.\"","Xiao Jinghong snapped back to her senses and looked at him, her tone cold as she asked, \"Where did you find this letter?\"","Li Changqing paused, then clapped his hands and ordered to those outside, \"Bring them in.\"","Several Armored Warriors quickly carried the bodies of Liu Wen and the others, placing them in the hall.","Li Changqing pointed to the rain-soaked body of Liu Wen and said:","\"I found the letter on this man. He also had this Jade Pendant on him.\"","As he spoke, he also placed the Jade Pendant on the table.","Xiao Jinghong remained unmoved. Her gaze was fixed on Liu Wen and the others as she carefully examined the wounds on their bodies.","’Great Success in Spear Dao.’","’Great Success in Saber Dao...’","’This style feels somewhat familiar...’","’Liu Lang? Was it him?’","The image of that blade strike outside the Mutual Market surfaced in Xiao Jinghong’s mind, and her confusion only deepened.","Next, she picked up the Jade Pendant for a look, and her brow furrowed slightly beneath her mask.","’An identity Jade Token for someone from the Jing State Liu Family.’","As the thoughts flashed through her mind, Xiao Jinghong had already pieced together most of what happened that night.","’The burning of the summer grain in the Three Towns must have been the work of some Young Master from the Jing State Liu Family, in collusion with Xiao Dongchen.’","But this only raised more questions in her mind.","’Did Xiao Dongchen recruit the traitors in the Three Towns and the Evil Demons from Bright Moon Building?’","’Why was the Young Master Liu killed by Liu Lang and the others?’","’What other secrets lay hidden here?’","Xiao Jinghong had the faint feeling that something about tonight’s events was strange, as if another group with a different agenda was also involved.","Especially the death of the Young Master Liu here, and that letter, so deliberately signed and marked by Xiao Dongchen.","It was as if someone had orchestrated it all, serving up the culprits behind tonight’s events to her and the Xiao Family.","’But to what end?’","After a long moment of thought, Xiao Jinghong spoke, \"Keep this matter confidential for the time being. Anyone with knowledge of this who leaks the information will be punished according to military law.\"","\"Yes,\" Li Changqing replied, then asked hesitantly, \"Then, what should we do next...?\"","Xiao Jinghong stood up and looked at him. \"First, secure the remaining summer grain. We will discuss everything else after that.\"","\"As for your punishment... I will report this to the Marquis. He will be the one to decide.\"","\"I hope you remember tonight’s lesson and do not repeat this mistake.\"","Li Changqing’s expression soured. He would rather have been punished by Xiao Jinghong now than face the Old Marquis."]},{"number":248,"title":"Chapter 248 - 202: What’s to Fear? A Beating at Most (Part 2)","paragraphs":["Fortunately, he’d found some things tonight. The crime was serious, but not a capital offense.","Xiao Jinghong paid his thoughts no mind. After stowing the letter and the Jade Pendant, he took Liu Wen’s body and headed straight for the Shu State Prefecture City.","The events of tonight were too significant. They involved not only Xiao Dongchen of the Xiao Family’s second branch but also a young master from the Jing State Liu Family.","Furthermore, the summer grain in Iron Wall Town had been burned, and there were still people with unknown motives hiding in the shadows.","For both official and personal reasons, Xiao Jinghong had to meet with the Old Marquis to discuss and decide on the next steps.","\"We must get to the bottom of this!\"","...","「Yin Hour, Fourth Quarter.」","Chen Yi had just arrived at the Spring Rain Building with Liu Lang, carrying Lou Yuxue in his arms.","The round trip had taken no more than four shichen—eight hours—but so much had happened in that time that he couldn’t help but feel mentally drained.","Therefore, after returning to the quiet room, Chen Yi didn’t stand on ceremony. He had Liu Lang fetch a basin of cold water and splash it on Lou Yuxue.","\"COUGH, COUGH...\"","Lou Yuxue woke up instantly. She scanned her surroundings, her eyes locking onto Chen Yi as she said angrily:","\"You bastard, why did you knock me out?\"","Chen Yi sat calmly in his chair. Waving for Liu Lang to go stand guard outside, he replied:","\"You talk too much. It’s annoying.\"","Lou Yuxue: \"...\"","Liu Lang, who hadn’t yet left the quiet room, couldn’t help but laugh out loud.","\"Boss, you really don’t know how to be gentle with a lady.\"","Chen Yi shot him a glare. \"Get lost, and be quick about it.\"","\"Right away.\"","After Liu Lang left, Lou Yuxue suppressed her anger and asked, \"What was the final situation over there?\"","Chen Yi didn’t hide it from her. \"The summer grain in Iron Wall Town was burned, the Young Master Liu is dead, and those from the Evil Demonic Dao and a few soldiers didn’t make it out either.\"","Lou Yuxue’s eyes narrowed. \"You killed all of them, didn’t you?\"","Chen Yi nodded with a sigh. \"It wouldn’t be good for people to know that I’m the one who killed Second Young Master Liu.\"","\"Then aren’t you afraid I’ll leak it?\"","\"Of course I am. That’s why I gave you a share of the silver. Otherwise, all thirty thousand taels of gold would have been mine.\"","\"...Despicable! Shameless!\"","It was no wonder Lou Yuxue was grinding her teeth at Chen Yi.","This time, she and Ge the Third had invested a great deal, especially in those Iron Banner Officers hidden within the Dingyuan Army.","Even if it wasn’t all of them, it still laid waste to years of their hard work.","But after such a huge loss, they only ended up with a fifty-percent share in the end—about one hundred and fifty thousand taels of silver.","That was one thing.","But for this bastard to pin the blame for tonight’s events on the White Tiger Guard—how could she not be furious?","Chen Yi more or less guessed her thoughts and chuckled. \"I’d say we’re two of a kind.\"","\"Who’s ’we’ with you?\"","\"We went to Iron Wall Town together, we killed Liu Wen and the others together. How could that not be a ’we’?\"","\"You, you, you... I, I, I... I’ll fight you to the death!\"","Seeing Lou Yuxue charge at him in a rage, Chen Yi shook his head, and a Fist Intent as heavy as a mountain pressed down on her.","WHAP.","Caught off guard, Lou Yuxue fell flat on the ground.","But this only made her struggle more furiously. \"Let me go!\"","\"You’re the one who did all those things, yet you want me to take the fall for you! You, how can you be so shameless?!\"","Chen Yi grinned. \"Miss Yuxue, compared to the storms your White Tiger Guard has been stirring up in Shu State, what I’ve done is nothing.\"","\"Besides, after today, you can be considered an ally of my Jing State Liu Family’s Third Miss. That’s to your advantage.\"","Lou Yuxue struggled to lift her head, staring at him and asking through gritted teeth, \"But are you really a member of the Liu Family?\"","Chen Yi said without a hint of a blush, \"Guaranteed genuine.\"","Using the Jing State Liu Family to occupy the Hidden Guard’s attention was also one of his goals.","In short, he needed to get them to fight amongst themselves, to keep those two factions from having the free time to specifically target the Xiao Family.","Of course, Lou Yuxue couldn’t possibly believe him completely. She snorted, \"I don’t care who you are. As long as I’m alive, I will never let you go.\"","Chen Yi smiled and said, \"Miss Yuxue, it’s a bit too early to be saying that.\"","\"Who knows? Maybe in a while, I’ll turn over a new leaf and join the White Tiger Guard, becoming one of your ’own people’?\"","\"Even then, I wouldn’t let you off the hook!\"","Chen Yi pursed his lips. \"Suit yourself. I...\"","Just as he was about to say something more, several lines of dazzling, brilliant gold text suddenly appeared before his eyes:","[Witnessed Bright Moon Building’s Black Tooth gathering practitioners of the Evil Demonic Dao to collude with the Great Wei Dynasty’s White Tiger Guard in burning the summer grain of three Shu State Border Towns. Reward: Dragon-Falling Spear Technique’s grade elevated to Celestial Tier, Opportunity +433.]","[Evaluation: Arrived in person, heard the commotion, witnessed the event.]","[Collaborated with Xiao Jinghong to foil Black Tooth and the White Tiger Guard’s plot against the summer grain in the Cang Lang and Profound Armor towns, indirectly slaying Black Tooth and other Evil Demons.","Plotted against Liu Wen and slew him. Framed Xiao Dongchen, sabotaging all of the White Tiger Guard’s plots.","Performance—Commendable.]","Chen Yi read it carefully, a smile appearing on his face.","’Commendable, huh? That’s rare.’","But aside from the evaluation and rewards, he was even happier that Xiao Jinghong hadn’t disappointed him.","Not only was Black Tooth dead, but the summer grain in Profound Armor and Cang Lang towns hadn’t suffered any losses. The outcome wasn’t too terrible.","If one also factored in the three hundred thousand silver coins he had left for the Xiao Family, it was enough to cover the losses in Iron Wall Town with a considerable surplus.","\"Not bad, not bad...\"","Seeing him suddenly start laughing, Lou Yuxue asked, bewildered, \"What crooked scheme are you cooking up now, you bastard?\"","Chen Yi glanced at her, then retracted his True Fist Dao Intent and said, \"You should go get your silver.\"","Lou Yuxue felt the pressure on her body disappear. She shot to her feet, about to strike, when she heard Chen Yi continue:","\"Lord Lady Tiger, you wouldn’t want to end up with nothing, would you?\"","Lou Yuxue’s delicate fist stopped right before his face. Staring at his detestable expression, she gritted out, \"Just you wait!\"","Seeing her turn and leave, Chen Yi reminded her unhurriedly:","\"Lord Lady Tiger, one hundred and fifty thousand taels... oh, I almost forgot. That ten thousand taels I gave to Black Tooth earlier? I’ll be taking that back, too.\""]},{"number":249,"title":"Chapter 249 - 202: What Am I Afraid of? The Worst I’ll Get is a Beating","paragraphs":["\"The total is one hundred sixty thousand in silver. Make sure you don’t overpay.\"","\"...You just wait!\"","Chen Yi smiled and shook his head, assuming she was just telling him to wait there for the silver.","「Not long after.」","Lou Yuxue hurried over, holding an ebony box, her face still extremely displeased.","But after seeing Chen Yi, she still snorted coldly, opened the box, took out a stack of gold notes, and prepared to count out one hundred sixty thousand.","But before she could start counting, she suddenly caught a glimpse of a black shadow from the corner of her eye, followed by a sharp pain in her neck.","Lou Yuxue stared blankly at Chen Yi. \"You...\"","The next moment, the familiar feeling of dizziness washed over her again.","As she lost consciousness, a final thought surfaced in her mind.","’This bastard is burning the bridge after crossing it!’","Chen Yi, however, didn’t think much of it. After settling her down, he sat at the table and began to count the gold notes in the box.","The method was roughly as follows:","\"One for you, one for me, one for me, hey, one for me...\"","\"One for you, one for me, one for me, hey, one for me...\"","Finally, Chen Yi finished counting. He looked at the thin stack of gold and silver notes left for her, and the smile on his face grew wider.","\"Leaving you fifty thousand silver should be enough to cover your losses, right?\"","Then he looked at the thick stack of gold and silver notes in his own hand and couldn’t help but sigh. \"Making money is so hard.\"","’I’ve been busy for over half a month, and all I’ve earned is... less than three hundred thousand silver?’","The reason it was more was because the box contained not only the thirty thousand in gold notes from this transaction but also Bright Moon Building’s recent earnings.","Saying this, Chen Yi put away the silver and gold notes, got up, and called for Liu Lang to leave Spring Rain Building.","\"Boss, did you get the silver?\"","\"Mhm, it was a decent haul.\"","Liu Lang rubbed his hands together and chuckled. \"How much?\"","Chen Yi looked at the faint light appearing in the east and replied casually, \"Two hundred ninety thousand silver, I’d say.\"","\"Two hundred... huh? Miss Yuxue agreed to that?\"","\"Of course she didn’t agree.\"","\"Then how... uh, did you rob her?\"","Seeing Chen Yi nod, Liu Lang was secretly speechless. At the same time, he couldn’t help but feel a little sympathy for Lou Yuxue.","’She’s probably going to die from anger, right?’","Chen Yi didn’t care about any of that. After calculating the time, he instructed:","\"Just as I said, go into hiding first. Be careful and don’t let anyone notice you.\"","Liu Lang nodded and said with a smile, \"Don’t worry, Boss. When I want to hide, not even Bright Moon Building can find me.\"","\"That’s for the best. You...\"","Before Chen Yi could finish, he abruptly looked up at the sky.","Liu Lang, beside him, did the same.","In the distance, under the cover of dark clouds, an extremely fast figure streaked from far to near, heading straight for the north.","Faintly, they could still feel the sharp, domineering, and cutting Dao Intent emanating from her.","Chen Yi and Liu Lang both didn’t dare to make a single move.","Only after they could no longer feel that powerful aura did they look at each other, both feeling somewhat relieved.","Liu Lang gave a dry laugh. \"Boss, was... was that General Jinghong?\"","Chen Yi grunted in affirmation. \"It was her. But she’s returned to Shu State a little earlier than I expected.\"","\"That aura of hers is terrifying... Aren’t you afraid?\"","\"What’s there to be afraid of? The worst that could happen is a sound beating.\"","Even if Xiao Jinghong and the Xiao Family found out what he had done, they wouldn’t do much to him.","When it came down to it, this could only be considered a \"family dispute.\"","Of course, Chen Yi couldn’t possibly say this out loud. He just waved his hand, signaling Liu Lang to proceed with the plan.","He himself went silently to Quchi and boarded the Painted Boat that had been prepared long ago.","「About an hour later.」","After changing his clothes, washing up, and cleaning away all traces, Chen Yi finally relaxed completely.","Listening to the pitter-patter of the rain on the Painted Boat, the beautiful figure he had just seen appeared in his mind, and a slight smile touched his lips.","’Xiao Jinghong has returned with Liu Wen. She must have gotten that letter from Xiao Dongchen by now.’","’What happens next depends on how she and the Old Master deal with it.’","’I reckon even if the Old Master is sentimental about old ties, he’ll be able to act decisively against someone with such malicious intentions as Xiao Dongchen.’","’The only fear is that the Second Branch will interfere or plead for him. He might not die then.’","’But fortunately, the Hidden Guard will make a move.’","’As for the Jing State Liu Family... heh, their troubles are just getting started.’","With these thoughts, Chen Yi leisurely lay down on the bed.","As the Black Tortoise Concealment Technique circulated within him, it masked all traces of his Martial Arts aura.","While Xiao Jinghong was back, he didn’t dare reveal the slightest bit, lest he cause unnecessary trouble.","Of course, this definitely couldn’t be called fear.","It was purely out of his deep respect for his wife.","After all, he had to consider the dignity of Xiao Jinghong, the General of the Dingyuan Army. It wouldn’t do to claim all the credit.","The figure he had just seen and her sharp, domineering True Sword Intent appeared in Chen Yi’s mind, and he muttered to himself.","’Xiao Jinghong’s Upper Three Grades Cultivation, her True Sword Intent at the Perfection Realm... tsk, she’s really strong.’","’When will I ever be able to reassert my authority as a husband?’","Thinking this, Chen Yi let out a soft breath.","Sigh, what an exhausting night. Time for sleep.","Anything is possible in dreams.","...","But while Chen Yi slept soundly, some people in Shu State City were destined for a restless night.","「Inside Bright Moon Building.」","Lou Yuxue slowly regained consciousness. After realizing how deathly quiet it was, she sat down at the table.","Looking at the meager few dozen gold and silver notes on the table, her enchantingly beautiful face was completely expressionless.","It was the calmness that comes from reaching the pinnacle of rage.","\"Liu Wu, heh heh!\"","A whole three hundred forty thousand silver!","In the end, what she was left with was a mere fifty thousand.","If she excluded Bright Moon Building’s earnings, the silver coins she could provide to the Hidden Guard amounted to only thirty thousand.","This was a full ten times less than the figure she and Ge the Third had discussed during their planning.","As Lou Yuxue thought about this, a smile actually appeared on her face.","Enchanting, charming, gorgeous, exquisite.","Clearly, she was about to go mad with rage.","She could never have imagined that such a shameless bastard existed in this world.","Even among the many varied practitioners of the Evil Demonic Dao she had seen in Bright Moon Building, none had ever made her angrier than that \"Liu Wu.\"","\"A quick death is one thing, but he... what he did is worse than killing me. He’s rotten to the core!\"","\"Bastard!\"","\"I don’t care where you’re hiding, and I don’t care if you’re one of the Jing State Liu Family or not! I will find you, and I will repay today’s humiliation in full!!\""]},{"number":250,"title":"Chapter 250 - 203: What Are His Intentions?","paragraphs":["Inside the Dingyuan Marquis’s Mansion.","It was nearly dawn, and many people in the Xiao Mansion were already awake. The estate was far from quiet.","The chefs in the rear kitchen were busy cooking while apprentices washed vegetables and stoked the fires, the entire place bustling with activity.","In the various residences, Maids were helping their masters and mistresses wash up and dress.","Household Servants took advantage of the rain to clean the courtyard walls and pavilion corners.","The front courtyard was the busiest of all.","Several grooms had prepared carriages early in the morning, ready to take the masters who served in the Government Office to check in for duty.","The steward and gatekeepers recorded the purpose of any visitors who had been waiting at the entrance since dawn, accepted calling cards, and sent messengers to the residences in the back.","But in the Qingjing Residence, located in the central courtyard, the Old Marquis had dismissed all his attendants.","He not only forbade the servants who were to help him dress and wash from entering, but also specifically ordered several Armored Warriors to stand guard, allowing no one to come within ten zhang.","This led most of the Xiao family members walking through the central courtyard that morning to murmur amongst themselves, speculating that something major must have occurred in the mansion.","But they could only murmur and speculate.","They all knew that even if they went up to ask, they wouldn’t get any answers.","Those Armored Guards would never reveal the slightest detail.","In truth, Wang Lixing, Liu Si’er, and the others assigned to guard the Qingjing Residence were completely in the dark.","They had only received the order to stand guard a quarter of an hour ago.","Just then, an Armored Warrior in a corner spoke in a low voice, \"Brother Xing, something feels off today.\"","\"I’ve got a chill running down my spine.\"","Wang Lixing shot him a sideways glance and hissed, \"Stand your post properly.\"","\"Have you forgotten where we are?\"","The Armored Warrior sullenly closed his mouth. His head turned reflexively for a glance at the Qingjing Residence as he continued to mumble under his breath.","He still felt the atmosphere in the Marquis’s Mansion was bizarre today, but he couldn’t quite put his finger on why.","Liu Si’er, standing to the side, overheard their exchange and naturally had his own suspicions.","Before Ge the Third left yesterday, he had mentioned he was off to handle something big. He had specifically warned Liu Si’er to be discreet and cautious, and to not give anything away.","Those words, combined with the Old Marquis’s current strange behavior, made it impossible for him not to read into things.","’What exactly is Ge the Third planning?’","’What news did the Old Marquis receive?’","’And who is with the Old Marquis right now?’","’Is it one of the Xiao Family’s Hidden Guards? Or someone else?’","Liu Si’er had no answers. His entire body tensed, and his already stern, unsmiling face grew even more solemn.","Inside the residence behind him, the Old Marquis was far more grim.","The Old Marquis listened to Xiao Jinghong’s account, his gaze fixed on the young man lying on the floor.","His brow was deeply furrowed, his expression grave.","He, of course, recognized Liu Wen.","But he never imagined that Liu Wen would dare to scheme against the summer grain of the Three Towns.","Seeing his expression, Xiao Jinghong asked, \"Grandfather, have you met him before?\"","The Old Marquis grunted in affirmation, his gaze still fixed on Liu Wen.","\"He is the second son of the main branch of the Jing State Liu Family.\"","\"Just two days ago, he paid me a visit. He even brought up a marriage proposal, wanting to marry your eldest sister.\"","Xiao Jinghong’s brow furrowed slightly. \"You didn’t agree, Grandfather?\"","The Old Marquis nodded. His expression faltered for a moment before he looked at her. \"Do you suspect he bore a grudge because of it?\"","\"I cannot be certain, but based on the timing, it’s a possibility.\"","\"The timing? What else do you know?\"","Xiao Jinghong nodded. She retrieved a blood-stained envelope from her robes and placed it hesitantly before the Old Marquis.","Just as the Old Marquis reached for the letter, she couldn’t help but speak up.","\"Grandfather, why don’t I read it to you?\"","The Old Marquis froze. A suspicion bloomed in his mind, and he couldn’t help but ask with a small smile, \"And why is that?\"","\"Are you worried this old man won’t be able to bear the contents and will fall ill again?\"","\"I wouldn’t dare, it’s just...\"","Before Xiao Jinghong could finish, the Old Marquis had already opened the letter. \"Don’t worry,\" he said.","\"The burning of the summer grain at Iron Wall Town and the secret machinations of the Jing State Liu Family couldn’t make me ill. What harm could a single letter do?\"","\"I... I...\"","The Old Marquis saw the letter’s contents, and the words caught in his throat.","His eyes widened. The wrinkles on his old face twitched, and his very lips began to tremble.","He was clearly incandescent with rage.","Xiao Jinghong couldn’t bear to watch.","But she knew that in order to investigate and deal with Xiao Dongchen, the Old Marquis had to be informed.","As expected.","When the Old Marquis saw the signature, fingerprint, and date at the bottom, he slammed the letter onto the table.","SLAM!","\"That monster!\"","\"How could he dare commit such a treasonous act?\"","\"For the Patriarch position? For the Marquis Position? For that, he would plunge the entire Xiao Family into ruin?\"","\"Doesn’t he realize that such an act is no different from digging his own grave? The fool!\"","\"Utterly, unbelievably foolish!\"","The Old Marquis pounded the table as he cursed Xiao Dongchen, his face flushed and his eyes bloodshot with fury.","At last, he broke into a coughing fit, which finally silenced his tirade.","Seeing this, Xiao Jinghong rushed forward, using her True Essence to regulate the Qi Mechanism in his body.","\"Grandfather, please don’t be angry. Your health is what’s important.\"","\"Let me call a Physician for you...\"","Before she could finish, the Old Marquis waved a dismissive hand. He leaned back weakly in his chair, gasping for breath.","\"No need, no need... This old man... won’t die just yet.\"","Of course, Xiao Jinghong didn’t believe a word of it. She remained by his side, ready to protect his heart meridian at a moment’s notice.","A long silence fell.","The Old Marquis finally composed himself somewhat, but his face seemed to have aged even more.","It was as if he had grown several years older in the blink of an eye.","But the Old Marquis seemed oblivious, his eyes fixed on Liu Wen’s corpse, his hand subconsciously tightening its grip on the incriminating letter from Xiao Dongchen.","\"What do you make of this matter?\""]},{"number":251,"title":"Chapter 251 - 203: What Are His Intentions?","paragraphs":["Hearing this, Xiao Jinghong glanced at Elder Master Xiao. ’She could roughly guess what he was thinking.’","The Jing State Liu Family was one thing.","Liu Wen had died outside Iron Wall Town, and with a letter as evidence, his guilt was already established.","Even if the Liu Family was unaware, the Xiao Family had ways to make them pay the price.","And there was even less to say about the Bright Moon Building.","They were an Evil Demonic Dao sect in the Jianghu, long accustomed to vicious cruelty. All that was needed was an opportunity to wipe them out in one fell swoop.","Therefore, the only thing that could be giving the Elder Master a headache right now was Xiao Dongchen—or rather, the second branch of the family.","Thinking this, Xiao Jinghong decided not to beat around the bush and said directly:","\"Xiao Dongchen is to be struck from the family registry and handed over to the authorities.\"","\"The second branch will no longer preside over the Punishment Hall. It will be transferred to the third branch or revert to the main branch’s control.\"","Here, Xiao Jinghong paused, her tone growing a bit more serious. \"Furthermore, Second Grand-uncle should be sent away from the Marquis’s Mansion. If you agree, it would be best for him to leave Shu State entirely.\"","This time, she wasn’t just dealing with Xiao Dongchen; she had no intention of leaving the second branch any leeway.","If not for the Elder Master’s feelings, she would have even wanted to drive the entire second branch out of Shu State and treat them as nothing more than distant relatives of the Xiao Family.","This included Xiao Ziqi, who held a post in the Shu State Capital Commandery, and Xiao Qiuyun, who had been married off to Guangyue Prefecture.","After hearing her out, a trace of sorrow couldn’t help but surface in the Elder Master’s cloudy eyes.","’It was likely a mix of frustration at their failure to live up to expectations and the bitter feeling that his kindness had been utterly wasted.’","At the same time, he began to recall certain events from over the years.","There were the exhortations of several late elders: \"Brothers must be of one heart.\" \"As Duke Dingyuan, you must care for your family and your brothers, shouldering everything on your own.\"","There were the actions of the second branch over the years.","And there were the changes in the Punishment Hall after the second branch took control.","After a moment of silence, the Elder Master let out a weary sigh. \"The second branch... do as you’ve said.\"","Then he pointed at Liu Wen and asked, \"What about the Liu Family?\"","Xiao Jinghong’s expression turned cold. \"Confiscate their assets and exterminate their clan!\"","Although she knew such an outcome was unlikely, the Liu Family’s actions were tantamount to treason.","Hearing this, the Elder Master slowly shook his head. \"The Liu Family currently enjoys great imperial favor. It will be difficult.\"","\"However, this matter will, at the very least, force the Liu Family to give something up.\"","His tone grew colder as he huffed, \"I may just have to pay a personal visit to the Governor’s Office.\"","Xiao Jinghong naturally understood his intentions.","The Xiao Family was in the right on this matter. Even if they couldn’t destroy the Liu Family, they wouldn’t let them off easy.","The loss of summer grain in Iron Wall Town, the grain tax owed to the Governor’s Office, and so on—the Jing State Liu Family would have to bear the cost for all of it.","As Xiao Jinghong considered this, she said, \"I will follow your lead.\"","After a pause, she changed the subject. \"How should we deal with Li Changqing?\"","The Elder Master glanced at her and managed a smile.","\"You are in charge of the Dingyuan Army now. All related matters should be handled by you.\"","Xiao Jinghong nodded and said no more.","Seeing that the official business was concluded, Elder Master Xiao relaxed a little. Looking at Liu Wen’s corpse on the floor, he sighed.","\"Actually, there’s one more thing. Thinking about it now, it must be related to last night’s events. The Hidden Guard, Xiao Jing...\"","Before he could finish, Xiao Jinghong suddenly raised a hand, interrupting him. \"Someone’s coming.\"","The next moment, they both saw a middle-aged man in black clothes rushing toward them through the rain.","When the Elder Master saw his face, a hint of joy appeared, and he couldn’t help but rise to his feet. \"Xiao Jing?\"","But the middle-aged man seemed not to hear him. He hurried over and fell to his knees with a thud, his voice urgent. \"Marquis, the Bright Moon Building is planning to burn the summer grain in the Three Towns!\"","\"I beg you, Marquis, to notify the three Generals as soon as possible so they can take precautions!\"","\"...\"","Even after everything they had just been through, Xiao Jinghong and the Elder Master couldn’t help but smile at this dramatic interruption.","When the middle-aged man, Xiao Jing, saw the smiles on their faces, he grew even more frantic.","\"Marquis! General! This is a matter of great urgency! If we’re too late, everything will be lost!\"","Seeing this, the Elder Master could only wave his hand, signaling for him to calm down.","Xiao Jinghong then explained the situation again, finally dispelling Xiao Jing’s worries.","Realizing what had happened, Xiao Jing was relieved but also ashamed. He said:","\"This subordinate was incompetent and failed to inform you in time, Marquis. I await your punishment.\"","The Elder Master smiled reassuringly. \"It’s not your fault. You were severely injured that night, after all. You...\"","Before he finished speaking, the Elder Master sized him up and said with surprise,","\"Your injuries have healed?\"","Xiao Jing belatedly touched his chest and said uncertainly, \"I think so...\"","As if remembering something, he said in astonishment, \"Was it that person? He’s actually a Medical Saint Hand?\"","\"Who?\"","Xiao Jing then recounted what had happened that night.","\"...After I learned of the plot, I was pursued by a group from the Evil Demonic Dao and gravely wounded, eventually falling unconscious in the hands of the Imprisonment Department.\"","\"When I awoke, I vaguely heard people talking beside me, something about thirty thousand taels of gold notes and their location.\"","\"Oh, right. In the end, he also said a few words to me.\"","Elder Master Xiao and Xiao Jinghong exchanged a look. The Elder Master asked, \"What did he say?\"","Xiao Jing thought back for a moment, a strange expression appearing on his face.","He looked at the Elder Master and said hesitantly:","\"The man said he bore the Xiao Family no ill will; on the contrary, he was an ally.\"","\"But to prevent those people from growing desperate, he couldn’t let you, Marquis, know for the time being.\"","After saying these two sentences, Xiao Jing’s mind suddenly connected them to the current situation. He couldn’t help but swallow hard and stammer:","\"He... he also said that by the time I woke up, this whole affair would be over...\"","Connecting this to what he had just heard about the summer grain in the Three Towns, it was clear the man’s words had come true.","’But... but... how is that possible...’","It wasn’t just him.","At this moment, both Elder Master Xiao and Xiao Jinghong wore grave expressions, their thoughts likely mirroring Xiao Jing’s.","After a long while, the Elder Master began to laugh.","\"It seems now that we’re no different from the Liu Family or Xiao Dongchen. We’ve all been used as pawns by someone.\""]},{"number":252,"title":"Chapter 252 - 203: What Are His Intentions?","paragraphs":["\"Not only did that person find out about this in advance and meticulously plan everything, they also thwarted the entire affair and laid out all the masterminds and their evidence right before us.\"","\"And us? We didn’t figure a thing out and still somehow muddled our way to a perfect resolution.\"","\"All while paying the smallest price for the greatest reward!\"","As he finished, the old Marquis couldn’t help but slam his hand on the table and curse:","\"But what did he mean by that!?\"","\"What’s this about telling me beforehand would make those people desperate?\"","\"Am I that incompetent in his eyes? Huh?\"","It was no wonder the old Marquis was furious.","While that person’s actions had certainly been a great help to the Xiao Family.","But throughout the entire affair, the Xiao Family was not only the last to find out, but also the one that profited the most.","It was practically a windfall they’d just stumbled upon.","\"Does he think we’re too stupid? Or does he think he’s just that capable?\"","\"Damn it! In all my years of leading armies and fighting wars, this is the first time I’ve been looked down on like this!\"","Xiao Jinghong wanted to laugh, but she couldn’t bring herself to.","Looking back at the whole affair, aside from notifying the Three Towns General in advance to prepare his defenses, the only thing she could take credit for was killing Black Tooth and his men.","Everything else, whether it was Liu Wen, Xiao Dongchen, the Liu Family, or Bright Moon Building, had been delivered right to them by that person.","Just as the old Marquis said, their Xiao Family had done very little but reaped all the rewards.","Thinking of this, Xiao Jinghong looked at the stunned Xiao Jing and asked, \"Did that person have any distinguishing features? Or anything that would make them easy to identify?\"","\"He’s done us such a huge favor. If we don’t show our gratitude, it’ll make us look ill-mannered.\"","Hearing this, the old Marquis nodded and grunted, his expression dark. \"Jinghong is right. Our Xiao Family should indeed thank him.\"","\"So, Xiao Jing, think back carefully. See if you can identify that person so I can pay him a visit.\"","’I’d like to see for myself just what kind of superhuman this is, to hold me in such contempt.’","Xiao Jing paused, stunned for a moment. He recalled the events carefully, and then his eyes widened. \"I did notice something.\"","\"Marquis, do you remember a while ago when I obstructed the Imprisonment Department’s investigation into Liu Jing’s death?\"","\"Yes, I remember that.\"","\"The voice of the person who killed that old man that night was very similar to the one who saved me the other day.\"","\"Thinking about it carefully, they must be the same person.\"","The old Marquis just snorted at this. \"It’s indeed the same style. Helping from the shadows, leaving no name.\"","\"Good. Very good. Now I’m even more curious to find out who he is.\"","Xiao Jinghong knew, of course, that the old Marquis wasn’t truly angry, just vexed and embarrassed.","In fact, she was feeling something similar herself.","But beyond her vexation, she felt a profound sense of relief.","If it weren’t for that person’s help, the Xiao Family would probably be in complete chaos by now.","The outcome would have been far worse than this.","With that in mind, Xiao Jinghong said thoughtfully, \"It shouldn’t be too difficult to find him.\"","The old Marquis’s spirits lifted. \"Oh? Go on.\"","\"The ones who notified me before were ’Sword Madman’ Liu Lang and Granny Shan’s granddaughter, Pei Guanli. At least one of them must be in on it and should know that person’s identity.\"","\"Then let’s bring them in for questioning. We can’t just let him do all this for nothing.\"","Xiao Jinghong hummed in agreement, then added, \"But thinking about it now, that person is truly formidable.\"","\"Besides his scheming, he himself is a Medical Saint Hand, and he has two subordinates who have reached Great Success in Martial Arts.\"","\"Even when I traveled the world with my master, I rarely encountered such a figure.\"","In her view, the Spearman outside Iron Wall Town, just like Liu Lang, was one of that person’s helpers.","After all, for a Medical Saint Hand to also cultivate Martial Arts would be even more difficult than her own dual cultivation of the Sword Dao and Spear Dao.","Hearing this, the old Marquis’s expression softened a little. He nodded and said, \"If he weren’t so capable, he couldn’t have done so much without us discovering him.\"","He paused, then sighed. \"However, once we find him, it would be best to treat him with courtesy.\"","\"If we can win him over as an ally, it would benefit you, me, the Xiao Family, and the Dingyuan Army.\"","Xiao Jinghong nodded. \"I understand.\"","After they had shared all their information.","The old Marquis glanced at the sky outside, a cold look returning to his face as he gave his orders:","\"It’s getting late. Take down Xiao Dongchen first. Remember to find that three hundred thousand silver, so we can compensate for the loss of Iron Wall Town’s summer grain.\"","\"After we’ve dealt with our family’s affairs, I will personally deliver his ’dear nephew’ to Liu Hong.\"","\"In short, we must resolve everything before the Holy Emperor gets word of this!\"","\"I’ll go at once...\"","After Xiao Jinghong left, the old Marquis looked at Xiao Jing and mused,","\"Who do you think should be in charge of the Punishment Hall now?\"","Xiao Jing hesitated for a moment before bowing. \"Marquis, there is something I wish to say, but I’m not sure if it’s appropriate.\"","\"Speak freely.\"","\"Marquis, the Marquis’s Mansion is currently facing threats from within and without. We must enforce strict discipline to ensure the stability of the inner residence.\"","\"Therefore, I believe the Punishment Hall should be handed over to someone from the main branch.\"","The old Marquis understood. He stood up and said, \"Then let Xuanshuo take charge for the time being.\"","He was indeed sentimental about old ties, but he had no patience for fools.","Especially fools who would betray the Xiao Family for immediate gain.","...","Nearing noon, the torrential rain continued unabated.","Amidst the CRASHING and PITTER-PATTER of the rain, Chen Yi, dressed in a long green robe and holding an Oil Paper Umbrella, returned to the Xiao Family residence without any hurry.","The moment he entered the front courtyard and saw the expressions on the faces of the Armored Guards, he knew in his heart that the old Marquis and Xiao Jinghong had already made their move.","It wasn’t outside his expectations.","As Chen Yi considered this, he put on an oblivious expression and strolled leisurely across the front courtyard toward Spring Lotus Garden.","Along the way, seeing the situation outside Qingjing Residence, he even greeted Wang Lixing, Liu Si’er, and the others.","It’s just that Liu Si’er and the others weren’t in a good mood, and their responses were mostly perfunctory.","Chen Yi naturally didn’t mind, nor would he go over and ask what was wrong, lest he get himself tangled in some trouble.","However, when he reached the rear courtyard, his mood was no longer so relaxed.","From a distance, he saw a tall, slender figure standing outside Spring Lotus Garden.","The figure was dressed in red, a Long Sword hanging from her waist. Beneath a high ponytail was a silver mask.","Her eyes, like autumn ripples, were staring at him without blinking.","—Who else could it be but his wife, Xiao Jinghong?","Chen Yi secretly raised an eyebrow, muttering to himself, ’Xiao Jinghong should be busy. What’s she doing here?’","Despite his confusion, he didn’t stop walking. He smiled and quickened his pace to greet her.","\"Wife, when did you return?\"","Xiao Jinghong’s eyes twinkled slightly, which likely meant she was in a good mood.","\"This morning.\"","\"That’s unfortunate. I was invited to Quchi last night to discuss Medicine Hall business and returned late.\"","\"It doesn’t matter.\"","Chen Yi smiled and asked with a natural expression, \"Now that you’re back, you should be staying home through the Mid-Autumn Festival, right?\"","Xiao Jinghong paused, lowering her head slightly. \"I... still have a few things to do. But I’ll try my best to finish them before the Mid-Autumn Festival.\"","\"I see...\"","Chen Yi knew in his heart that there were still follow-up matters from last night, so he smiled and said:","\"In that case, don’t forget to let the old Marquis know. With Duke Zhang and Mr. Sun the Elder leaving one after another recently, he’ll probably want to use the Mid-Autumn Festival to liven things up.\"","\"And there’s Eldest Sister’s side...\"","Chen Yi chattered on about recent interesting events as he led Xiao Jinghong into Spring Lotus Garden.","Just as the two reached the wooden building and were about to part ways.","Xiao Jinghong suddenly asked,","\"Husband, I was wondering, did Pei Guanli act strangely at all in the days before she left?\"","Chen Yi’s heart skipped a beat.","’Don’t tell me Tiger Girl slipped up?’"]},{"number":253,"title":"Chapter 253 - 204: Anti-Xiao Alliance","paragraphs":["Whatever he thought, Chen Yi couldn’t let it show on his face, especially not in front of Xiao Jinghong.","Chen Yi feigned recollection. \"For a few days before she left, that girl was in secluded cultivation. There was nothing out of the ordinary.\"","\"Before that, though, she, Tingyun, and Huatang were wandering around inside and outside the Prefecture City, and they bought a lot of things for the clan.\"","He paused, a slight smile gracing his lips as he continued,","\"She can be a bit eccentric and willful, but her heart’s in the right place. She’s a good person, really. She even took a whole cart of things back with her before she left.\"","Chen Yi didn’t know how much Pei Guanli had let slip, so he had to do some damage control.","If he couldn’t dispel Xiao Jinghong’s suspicions, he at least hoped she’d go a little easier on Pei Guanli during questioning.","Xiao Jinghong listened, nodding thoughtfully. She didn’t press the matter, saying instead,","\"I just came back to grab a few things, then I have to leave. There are still some matters I need to attend to.\"","Chen Yi tilted his head to look into her eyes. \"You already said that, my lady.\"","Xiao Jinghong met his gaze, a hint of awkwardness on her face.","Fortunately, her mask hid her expression, so she wasn’t worried about Chen Yi noticing.","\"I have a few things I’d like to ask you to handle for me.\"","Chen Yi smiled. \"Please, speak freely. I may be an Instructor at Guiyun Academy and the Shopkeeper at Jishi Medicine Hall, but I still have some time to spare.\"","On the surface, his words sounded reasonable enough.","But between the lines, the message was clear.","He was already busy, so she shouldn’t ask for anything too troublesome.","Of course, Xiao Jinghong caught his meaning, and a faint smile touched her lips.","’My husband really hasn’t changed a bit.’","’So incredibly talented, yet still so lazy and carefree.’","No wonder the Old Master had specifically instructed her this morning to treat Chen Yi well, to give him more responsibilities when the time was right. He had even told her, \"Your husband has now reached Calligraphy Dao Perfection.\"","Even for someone as experienced and worldly as Xiao Jinghong, this news was rather surprising.","After all, the realms of the scholar’s Four Arts—Music, Chess, Calligraphy, and Painting—were comparable to those of Martial Arts, and their cultivation was no less difficult.","Chen Yi raising his Calligraphy Dao to the Perfection Realm was actually on par with her Sword Dao Perfection.","The only difference was that Chen Yi used his brush to express his will. If he wanted to harm someone, he would have to attack their mind and spirit.","By channeling emotions like sorrow, joy, anger, or fear through his Calligraphy Dao, he could inflict harm without a trace.","She, on the other hand, could kill with her sword, which was far more direct and decisive.","Of course, Xiao Jinghong knew it was unlikely that Chen Yi, unlike her, would ever think of using the Calligraphy Dao for slaughter.","He would most likely use it for composing odes, singing praises, or expressing his innermost feelings.","’A warrior’s stereotype of a scholar, most likely.’","\"Don’t worry. I only want you to rewrite these few poems for me, then have them mounted and hung in our room.\"","As she spoke, Xiao Jinghong took out the letters she had previously received from within her robes.","There was \"Thoughts of a Summer Night,\" \"Two Thoughts on a Summer Night,\" \"Thoughts of Summer,\" and the first one he ever wrote for her, \"Magpie Bridge Immortal.\"","\"...\"","Chen Yi glanced at the letters in her hand, then his gaze shifted to her face. He asked hesitantly,","\"You’ve been carrying these with you this whole time, my lady?\"","A flicker of uncertainty crossed Xiao Jinghong’s eyes. Unsure how to answer, she simply shoved all the letters into his hands.","\"Also, over the next few days, I need you to help me prepare some gifts. For the Old Master, Second Uncle, and Third Grand-uncle in the family, as well as people outside—the two Commanders from the Commandant’s Office, the Prefectural Magistrate’s Office, the Governor’s Office, and so on.\"","\"Prepare them in advance, so we don’t seem discourteous if my return is rushed.\"","Seeing her rush through her words, Chen Yi couldn’t help but smile. He nodded and said,","\"The eldest sister should have a specific list of names. I’ll go ask her in a bit.\"","But after saying that, he added teasingly, \"My lady, my memory isn’t half-bad, you know. I still remember all the poems. Why don’t you hold on to these letters?\"","Xiao Jinghong froze. Then, she snatched the letters back, stuffed them into her sleeve, and turned toward the inner wooden building, her face quietly flushing with embarrassed anger.","’How could I be so stupid? I can’t believe I forgot about that.’","’I could have just asked him to rewrite them from memory.’","’But no, now he knows I’ve been carrying these letters with me this whole time...’","So mortifying.","Watching her hurry back into the wooden building, Chen Yi had a good idea of what she was thinking and couldn’t help but let out a soft laugh.","’So, she does get shy after all.’","With that thought, Chen Yi glanced at the sky. Estimating that the downpour wouldn’t let up anytime soon, he headed straight for his study.","The incident with the burning of the Three Towns’ summer grain was over for now. What came next depended on how the Old Master and Xiao Jinghong decided to handle it.","They should be able to use this as an opportunity to secure some advantages for the Xiao Family. At the very least, it would serve as a warning to their enemies and alleviate some of the pressure they were facing, both internal and external.","Chen Yi had a rough idea of how things would play out, but he didn’t plan on getting involved.","At least, he wouldn’t be making any moves himself anytime soon.","When he arrived at the study, Chen Yi looked around. The twenty-one calligraphy sheets he had written earlier were all fully mounted. He opened them one by one for a quick inspection, and after confirming there were no issues, he placed them back in their box.","The calligraphy sheets were ready. He just had to wait for the exhibition hall at Guiyun Academy to be cleared out so they could be hung.","’Looks like I’ll have a few more days of peace and quiet.’","At this moment, Xiao Wuge, who had received the news, came running back with Xiaodie.","Chen Yi could hear him calling for his brother-in-law from a long way off.","Chen Yi put away the box and walked out to greet them.","Seeing him, Xiao Wuge immediately smiled and asked, \"Brother-in-law, when did you get back?\"","\"Just a little while ago.\"","\"So, have you heard what’s been happening at the manor?\"","Chen Yi saw the three words \"ask me about it\" practically written on his face and couldn’t help but laugh. \"No, I haven’t. What happened?\"","\"Something huge, Brother-in-law! Let me tell you...\""]},{"number":254,"title":"Chapter 254 - 204: Anti-Xiao Alliance","paragraphs":["Listening to Xiao Wuge’s loud and excited recounting of what had happened in the mansion that morning, Chen Yi nodded to himself.","This time, the Old Master and Xiao Jinghong hadn’t been as lenient as before, which made all his efforts worthwhile.","Early in the morning, Xiao Jinghong had intercepted Xiao Dongchen on his way to the Governor’s Office and brought him to the Punishment Hall for questioning.","Although Xiao Dongchen refused to confess no matter what, once Xiao Jinghong’s men found the three hundred thousand taels in silver notes at Four Directions Hall, he was imprisoned in the Punishment Hall without another word.","The Old Master hadn’t been idle, either. He had directly summoned several clan elders, the Chief Steward of each branch, and men like Xiao Wang and Xiao Shen.","He not only reclaimed control of the Punishment Hall from Xiao Wang, announcing on the spot that Xiao Xuanshuo would now be in charge, but he also ordered Xiao Wang and his entire second branch to leave Shu State.","At first, Xiao Wang was unwilling to yield, but he was left speechless when the Old Master produced Xiao Dongchen’s letter, followed by the newly discovered silver notes.","Now, everyone from the second branch was packing their belongings. Word was that they would soon be departing for Guangyue Prefecture to join Xiao Qiuyun.","\"Brother-in-law, why do you think Uncle Dongchen betrayed the family? Grandfather and our sisters have always treated the second branch well, haven’t they?\"","Xiao Wuge sounded both confused and angry.","It was what you might call a young man’s sense of justice.","Chen Yi pondered for a moment, then looked out at the falling rain and said with a smile,","\"Human greed is like a snake trying to swallow an elephant, I suppose.\"","\"There are too many temptations in this world—fame, fortune, power, status, beauty... Once you fall for them, they slowly erode your mind and spirit.\"","\"A good person can become sinister and cruel, a strong person can have their very essence drained, and even those with lofty ambitions and resolute minds can be led astray.\"","Chen Yi paused, catching a glimpse of Xiao Jinghong carrying a bundle from the corner of his eye. He continued, \"Strength comes from having no desires. I suppose that’s what the saying is about.\"","Xiao Wuge nodded. \"Then I want to be someone who has no desires, so I can be strong too.\"","Chen Yi couldn’t help but laugh. He looked down at him and said, \"You can’t do that.\"","\"Huh? Why not?\"","\"You’re the Young Master. Being too perfect will only bring you more trouble.\"","In the Xiao Family’s current circumstances, the more Xiao Wuge stood out, the more he would be feared and resented by others.","On the other hand, if he were to indulge in some harmless pursuits, like appreciating art and nature, it would serve to hide his true abilities.","Xiao Wuge didn’t fully grasp this reasoning. With a look of partial understanding, he asked, \"Then what are your desires, Brother-in-law?\"","Chen Yi paused, then said, deliberately yet casually, \"Me?\"","\"Probably just playing chess and going fishing every day. Of course, a wife, kids, and a warm home would make it even better.\"","He wasn’t just saying this for Xiao Jinghong’s benefit, who he knew was nearby.","These were his genuine thoughts.","But no sooner had he finished speaking than a set of footsteps sounded from outside, followed by Xiao Jinghong’s voice:","\"Husband, Wuge, I have something to take care of. I must be going.\"","\"Second Sister?\"","Before Chen Yi could say anything, Xiao Wuge let out a whoop and dashed outside. He grabbed Xiao Jinghong’s arm, grinning.","\"When did you get back, Second Sister? You didn’t even say a word! Can’t you stay? The Mid-Autumn Festival is almost here, and Eldest Sister was just asking about you the other day...\"","The barrage of questions was almost too much for the already flustered Xiao Jinghong to handle.","Especially when she saw Chen Yi walk out the door behind him, she averted her eyes and said,","\"I have something very important to handle. You stay with your brother-in-law for now. I’ll return as soon as I’m done, and I’ll try my best to be back before the Mid-Autumn Festival.\"","Xiao Jinghong was clearly flustered; her face even felt a little hot.","It was the same feeling she’d had when the Old Master had pushed her and Chen Yi to consummate their marriage, leaving her feeling completely at a loss.","However, just as Xiao Jinghong was about to depart, Wang Lixing came rushing over.","\"General, something’s happened!\"","Upon hearing this, not only did Xiao Jinghong fail to look grave, but she actually seemed to sigh in relief. \"What is it?\" she asked quickly.","Wang Lixing said anxiously, \"It’s Xiao Dongchen. He... he’s dead.\"","Xiao Jinghong’s eyes narrowed. The last traces of her bashfulness vanished, replaced by a stern tone. \"Didn’t I order you to take strict precautions?\"","Wang Lixing dropped to his knees. \"This subordinate has failed in his duties. Please punish me, General!\"","Xiao Jinghong gave him a frowning glance, then bid a quick farewell to Chen Yi and Xiao Wuge before departing hastily with Wang Lixing.","\"Brother-in-law, did you hear that? Uncle Dongchen...\"","\"It has nothing to do with you. If you’re that bored, I can have a word with Eldest Sister. I’m sure she could have a few tutors here for you by this afternoon.\"","Sidetracked by Chen Yi, Xiao Wuge immediately forgot his question and started protesting loudly.","Chen Yi was, of course, joking. He followed up by suggesting they go fishing and play chess that afternoon.","It was an unconventional use of the ’hit with a stick, then give a Sweet Date’ method.","Still, Xiao Dongchen’s sudden death inevitably made him suspicious.","The more he thought about it, the more he felt that the likelihood of Xiao Dongchen committing suicide was slim.","It was most likely the work of the Hidden Guards.","’Ge the Third, or was it Lou Yuxue?’","’Or perhaps another Hidden Guard concealed within the Xiao Mansion?’","As Chen Yi mulled this over, he took Xiao Wuge to the pond to fish, his mood generally relaxed.","Regardless of how Xiao Dongchen had died, the Hidden Guards, the Bright Moon Building, and the Liu Family would now face the Xiao Family’s counterattack.","Of course, he, the one pulling strings from the shadows, would be no exception.","Fortunately, he had already made preparations. As long as Liu Lang and Pei Guanli kept their mouths shut, he would be safe for the time being.","Chen Yi could also guess where Xiao Jinghong was headed after leaving the mansion.","She was most likely heading to the Mutual Market to stand guard and prevent any retaliation from their enemies. He could think of no other possibility.","After all, with the second branch no longer stirring up trouble, the Xiao Family was now a united front internally. The Old Master only had to focus his full attention on outside threats."]},{"number":255,"title":"Chapter 255 - 204: Anti-Xiao Alliance","paragraphs":["It wasn’t long before news arrived.","To be precise, the news was brought back by Xiaodie from outside the Spring Lotus Garden.","\"Master Chen, I heard that Master Dongchen committed suicide. He even wrote a confession.\"","\"It says he was possessed and goaded by the Liu Family’s second young master into making a terrible mistake. It also says he used a veteran of the Dingyuan Army, Ge the Third, to order the criminals in the Three Towns to burn the summer grain.\"","Xiaodie patted her chest, which was already filling out, and said with lingering fear, \"Ge the Third, of all people.\"","\"Master Chen, not long ago, Ge the Third was driving me and Miss Guanli around the Prefecture City. I never thought he’d be that kind of person!\"","Chen Yi sat by the pond, staring at his empty hook. \"You can know a person’s face, but not their heart,\" he replied listlessly.","It had been so long since he’d last fished, he’d forgotten he shouldn’t have done it with Xiao Wuge.","It was another day with no catch.","Xiao Wuge, however, felt differently. As he tossed a Golden Carp he’d just caught back into the water, he said, \"The bad guys are hidden so deep. They’re just terrible.\"","Xiaodie nodded at his words. \"The Young Master is right.\"","\"It’s such a shame, though. Ge the Third has disappeared. But the Second Miss has already sent people to track him down.\"","\"Also, also! The news about the summer grain being burned in Iron Wall Town has spread all over the city, but the stories are all over the place.\"","\"Some say it was an enemy invasion, people from the Barbarian Race or Poshisu Country. Others say it was mountain bandits from the border between Shu and Jing State.\"","\"The most outrageous one is a rumor that the Second Miss staged the whole thing, wanting to exchange the summer grain for silver to build the Mutual Market.\"","Hm?","Chen Yi raised an eyebrow slightly and turned his head to ask, \"Is that last rumor widespread?\"","Xiaodie nodded gravely. \"Quite a few. I heard from one of the boys in the front courtyard that it’s being spread in the taverns and marketplaces.\"","Chen Yi frowned to himself, a chill creeping into his heart.","It was actually quite normal for rumors to spread whenever something big happened, but most of them were just wild tales meant for bragging.","Things like, \"My neighbor is in Iron Wall Town. It was pouring rain last night when the enemy nation attacked!\" were all just to attract attention, to prove one’s own importance by bragging about knowing things others didn’t.","These kinds of rumors were rarely meant to be malicious slander.","This last rumor, on the other hand, was far too pointed and purposeful. It was even logically self-contained. Clearly, someone had deliberately started it.","’The only ones who could come up with such a scheme and act on it so quickly must have known about the arson in advance.’","’The Bright Moon Building, the Liu Family, the Hidden Guard, myself, and... that Financier pulling the strings from behind the scenes?’","Black Tooth of the Bright Moon Building had died at the hands of Xiao Jinghong. Lou Yuxue was busy erasing any trace of the Hidden Guard, and her other people were all worried about the Xiao Family finding them. They wouldn’t dare to surface for a short while.","The same went for the Hidden Guard. In just half a day, orchestrating Xiao Dongchen’s removal was the absolute limit of what they could accomplish.","Even if they wanted to release rumors to sabotage the Mutual Market, they wouldn’t do it now.","And then there was the Liu Family...","They were likely still completely confused. They probably didn’t even know that the Xiao Family had Liu Wen’s body.","Eliminate the other possibilities, and what’s left, however unlikely, is the only solution.","—The one who acted was the Financier hiding in the shadows!","After a moment of thought, Chen Yi let out a soft breath. ’Thank goodness,’ he thought.","He had pieced most of it together.","’The Financier must have prepared these rumors in advance.’","’Fortunately, the summer grain losses in the Three Towns weren’t severe. Otherwise, the Xiao Family would be in serious trouble.’","If the Bright Moon Building and the Hidden Guard had succeeded in burning the summer grain, the impact of that rumor would have been devastating.","At that point, the Xiao Family would have had to investigate the fire in the Three Towns and solve the Dingyuan Army’s grain shortage. They would also have had to face potential investigations and punishments from the Imperial Court and other government offices, all triggered by the rumors.","Most importantly, if the Xiao Family got bogged down in these troubles, it would inevitably impact the construction of the Mutual Market.","At that point, the Xiao Family—short on people, grain, and money—would be facing threats from all sides. The pressure from an Imperial Court investigation, spurred by the rumors, would be immense. Other than leading the Dingyuan Army in rebellion or becoming bandits, their only option would be to wait for death.","Even if the Old Patriarch and Xiao Jinghong responded perfectly, exhausting their connections to secure aid, they would still have paid a heavy price.","Vicious. Truly vicious!","This scheme to kill three birds with one stone was truly venomous!","Having pieced most of it together, Chen Yi couldn’t help but twist his lips into a smirk. \"I suppose I’ve underestimated the people of this world.\"","He had originally believed his own plans accounted for everyone, but he had never expected that low-key Financier to be so ruthless.","They bided their time, but when they finally struck, it was to drive the Xiao Family to their doom.","Far more vicious and clever than the likes of Xiao Dongchen and Liu Wen.","With this in mind, Chen Yi gave an order, his expression unreadable:","\"Xiaodie, go out and look around again. See if there’s any other news.\"","\"Oh, and focus on the reactions of the various government offices—the Governor’s Office, the Inspectorate Office, the Prefectural Magistrate’s Office, and so on.\"","\"Also, ask about the price of grain and medicinal herbs.\"","\"You got it.\"","Without a second thought, Xiaodie left the Spring Lotus Garden.","Xiao Wuge slowly caught on and asked, \"Brother-in-law, is there a problem with those rumors? It’s all just street gossip.\"","Chen Yi shook his head slightly. \"It’s nothing if only a few people believe it. But if enough people believe it, a rumor becomes reality.\"","\"Then... then will it affect our family?\"","\"A little, but not much.\"","\"That’s good...\"","About two hours later, Xiaodie returned.","But the gossipy expression from before was gone, replaced by a strange look.","\"Master Chen, it’s so strange.\"","Chen Yi put away his fishing rod and looked at her seriously. \"What’s strange?\"","\"It’s as if those rumors vanished into thin air. Now, everyone in the city is praising the Second Miss for her incredible valor, for eliminating an Elder from some ’Building,’ and for her cultivation reaching the Upper Three Grades.\"","\"They’re also saying she patrolled all Three Towns in a single night, thwarting the villains’ plot and saving the Dingyuan Army’s grain supply.\"","Chen Yi was stunned for a moment, then broke into a wry laugh. \"What else?\"","’They sure react quickly.’","’The Financier must have learned the truth of last night’s events and immediately rearranged their plans.’","\"And about the government offices... The Prefectural Yamen and the Governor’s Office haven’t done much. I heard they just sent people to ask the Master for confirmation.\"","\"But at the Inspectorate Office, someone had apparently already written up a memorial to the throne. If Lord Tang hadn’t discovered it in time, it would have been sent to the Capital Prefecture.\"","’Just as I thought,’ Chen Yi said to himself. ’One link after another. That Financier really did account for all the follow-up actions.’","’No doubt the prices of grain and medicinal herbs fluctuated today, too. Or perhaps some grain stores are reporting shortages.’","Just then, Xiaodie continued, \"What’s even stranger is that the second steward, who’s in charge of procurement for the estate, said that this morning, several of the larger grain stores in the city raised their prices. They’re claiming this summer’s harvest was poor and grain is scarce...\"","Chen Yi cut in, \"They all raised their prices?\"","Xiaodie nodded. \"Yes, all of them did.\"","’Well, it seems the Financier isn’t a single person, but a group.’","’No wonder they move so fast, their reach is so wide, and they get information so quickly...’","’But what is this supposed to be?’","’An Anti-Xiao Alliance?’","\"Oh, right, Master Chen! Before I came back, I saw the Second Miss leaving with some Armored Warriors. I heard they found some ’Building’.\"","’Bright Moon Building?’","’No, it’s the Spring Rain Building.’","Chen Yi realized what was happening. Their opponent was trying to use Xiao Jinghong’s hand to eliminate the Spring Rain Building, that den of vice, to keep the Xiao Family from investigating them.","Tsk, tsk, tsk. Lou Yuxue really was in a miserable spot.","’She’s probably going crazy with anger right now, huh?’"]},{"number":256,"title":"Chapter 256 - 205: The Xiao Family Must Have a Profound Expert","paragraphs":["The truth was quite the opposite.","Lou Yuxue had grown numb.","She felt no anger at all. Instead, after Chen Yi took the 290,000 taels of silver, she quickly regained her composure.","She analyzed the situation, weighed the pros and cons, and formulated a response.","Not only had Lou Yuxue evacuated the Spring Rain Building ahead of time, but she had also dispersed her subordinates and made proper arrangements for them.","This included the Hidden Guards and some personnel from the Bright Moon Building.","She had even completed one of the two tasks assigned to her by the White Tiger Guard Pavilion Master and the Golden Banner Officer—killing Xiao Dongchen.","Only as night fell did she finally relax a little and make her way to Kangning Street.","It was late afternoon, and the sky was dim.","Although colorful lanterns had been put up early on Kangning Street for the approaching Mid-Autumn Festival, their candlelight remained faint in the gloomy, rainy weather.","The area near the adjacent Quchi Pond was even darker.","Only the few pavilions built along the pond’s edge were illuminated by red lanterns.","From a distance, the scene was a hazy blur.","Usually, when night descended, these pavilions would be the liveliest spots, serving as rendezvous points for scholars and beauties.","Tonight, however, there were few people in sight.","It was as if everyone had found better places to be overnight.","Lou Yuxue gazed at the distant Quchi Pond. After confirming that no one was around, she silently entered one of the pavilions.","Lou Yuxue was no longer in her usual seductive dresses and qipaos, but had changed into coarse cloth garments. She had deliberately tied her hair into a bun and even smeared some tung oil on her face.","It was the typical attire of a peasant woman.","Even those familiar with her identity would likely fail to recognize her now.","After wiping clean a bench on one side of the pavilion, Lou Yuxue leaned back on it, her gaze fixed on the pond’s surface, which was being disturbed by the rain.","The ceaseless pitter-patter of the rain filled the air.","Paradoxically, the noise calmed her mind, allowing her to contemplate the future.","Everything that had happened in the past few days flashed before Lou Yuxue’s eyes like fleeting shadows:","First, Gray Wolf contacted Hawk. Due to the joint construction of the Mutual Market by Xiao Jinghong and the Mountain Race, he wanted to burn the summer grain in the Three Towns.","Hawk had no choice but to agree.","She, Lady Tiger, then got involved.","Her original plan was to use Black Tooth and the Bright Moon Building to support Hawk’s subordinates and minimize their losses.","By a twist of fate, Black Tooth received a job offer: a major Noble Family in Shu State was offering thirty thousand taels of gold for the same purpose—to deal with the summer grain in the Three Towns.","When she got wind of this, she thought it over and devised a plan to kill four birds with one stone.","The first was for Gray Wolf.","The second was for the silver.","The third was to support Hawk’s Iron Banner Officers.","And the fourth was to throw the Xiao Family into chaos, destabilize Shu State, and simultaneously delay the construction of the Mutual Market.","’So, when did the plan start to fall apart?’","Lou Yuxue’s thoughts naturally turned to \"Liu Wu.\"","’It wasn’t just because \"Liu Wu\" appeared so suddenly.’","’Or maybe not suddenly. \"Suspiciously\" would be a better word.’","’Because the \"Sword Madman\" Liu Lang had approached Black Tooth with the job of burning the Three Towns’ summer grain one step before \"Liu Wu\" did.’","’So Liu Wu never intended to act himself. Just like that Financier, he only wanted to reap the rewards without lifting a finger.’","’But after learning the Financier’s whereabouts, he began his own scheme, plotting against Liu Wen, against me... No.’","Lou Yuxue shook her head, her eyes cold and clear.","’My presence wasn’t part of his initial objective. He must have been after Black Tooth’s money, and I just happened to be the person closest to it.’","At this thought, two questions arose in her mind.","’Why did he plot against Xiao Dongchen?’","’Was he the one who notified Xiao Jinghong?’","When Lou Yuxue had dealt with Xiao Dongchen, she had learned the full story. She discovered that Liu Wu had not only impersonated Black Tooth to get close to Liu Wen, but had also pretended to be Liu Wen’s Attendant to approach Xiao Dongchen.","Furthermore, Liu Wu had used three hundred thousand taels of silver to gain Xiao Dongchen’s trust, tricking him into signing and fingerprinting a document.","’So, what he said last night wasn’t entirely a lie.’","’He did get Liu Wen’s silver, but it was to lure Xiao Dongchen into a trap. Afterward, he left the letter and Liu Wen’s body for Xiao Jinghong...’","Lou Yuxue paused, frowning as she muttered to herself, \"The silver also ended up with the Xiao Family.\"","The moment the words left her mouth, a flash of insight struck her.","Suddenly, everything clicked into place.","’So it was Liu Wu who alerted Xiao Jinghong, allowing her to prepare in advance.’","’He also deliberately left that silver for the Xiao Family.’","’Which means he’s... a member of the Xiao Family?!’","A look of shocked disbelief appeared on Lou Yuxue’s face.","’If he’s from the Xiao Family, why would he scheme against Xiao Dongchen? Unless... he knew Gray Wolf’s identity and intentions...’","’Then again, the ambitions of the Xiao Family’s second branch are common knowledge. Taking out Xiao Dongchen is also a possibility.’","’And the fact that the Old Marquis was kept in the dark was probably part of his scheme, too—to make us lower our guard, I’d wager.’","’Because his real killing blow was aimed outside Shu State City, at Xiao Jinghong herself...’","As she connected these dots, Lou Yuxue’s expression grew even more complex.","She suddenly remembered that \"Liu Wu\" had told her last night that he was from the Xiao Family.","It was just that her knowledge had been limited at the time. Only now did everything make sense.","This left her deeply frustrated.","What frustrated her even more was that—even after figuring out everything \"Liu Wu\" had done—she still didn’t know who he was.","A member of the Xiao Family’s Hidden Guard?","Someone from the Xiao Family Branches?","Both were possible.","The only impossibility was the Xiao Family’s main branch.","’Xiao Wan’er and Xiao Jinghong are both women, Xiao Wuge is too young, and Xiao Xuanshuo is crippled. None of these people from the main branch could be Liu Wu.’","’The only one left with ties to the main branch is Fledgling. Heh, he’s just a weak scholar, and he’s being watched by Hawk. There’s no way he could be Liu Wu.’","She mulled it over and over, concluding that \"Liu Wu\" must be a member of one of the Xiao Family Branches, or perhaps someone from another of Shu State’s Noble Families close to the Xiaos.","\"No matter who you are, I will find you and lock you away in the Inner Prison this time!\"","Just then, the sound of carriage wheels echoed from the distance."]},{"number":257,"title":"Chapter 257 - 205: The Xiao Family Must Have a Master","paragraphs":["A rumbling sound shattered the quiet of the rainy night, coming to a stop on nearby Kangning Street.","Lou Yuxue looked toward the sound.","Two graceful figures stepped down from the carriage, one after the other.","The one in the lead was strikingly beautiful, wearing a phoenix hairpin. Her brows and eyes were clear and elegant.","The other was dressed as a maid in a pale yellow cloth dress, carrying two long swords.","It was Cui Qingwu and her maid, Huan’er.","The two of them walked to the pavilion together.","Cui Qingwu lifted a hand, and Huan’er opened an Oil Paper Umbrella, silently standing guard outside the pavilion without a word.","Cui Qingwu sized up Lou Yuxue, a smile playing on her lips as she said,","\"You really lost badly this time, Lady Tiger.\"","Lou Yuxue rose to her feet and looked at her, saying flatly, \"I’m still standing here. How can you say I’ve lost?\"","\"Even if we were affected by this—with Hawk having fled and Gray Wolf dead—do you really think you can remain untouched?\"","The implication was clear: they were both Silver Banner Officers stationed in Shu State. If the Pavilion Master decided to punish someone, he would treat them equally.","Cui Qingwu kept smiling. \"I finished my business yesterday. Any impact on me is negligible.\"","\"You, on the other hand... not only did you fail to get many silver coins, but your Spring Rain Building was hit. If you hadn’t run so fast, Xiao Jinghong would have had you cornered by now.\"","\"My people didn’t suffer heavy losses.\"","\"And Hawk?\"","Upon hearing this, Lou Yuxue’s tone became stiff. \"His mission was already complete. He won’t be punished by our superiors, no matter how many men he lost.\"","Cui Qingwu asked noncommittally, \"So you only lost some silver coins this time? Two hundred and ninety thousand taels?\"","Lou Yuxue pressed her lips together. Though she was already numb from the blow, she still seethed with anger at the thought of that bastard, Liu Wu.","After a moment of silence, she said, \"I didn’t seek you out today to be mocked by you.\"","Cui Qingwu watched her with an unreadable smile. \"Let’s hear it. Why did you look for me?\"","\"Xiao Jinghong has completely swept the Evil Demonic Dao out of West City. It will be hard for them to re-establish themselves before a new Elder from the Bright Moon Building arrives. So, I need you to help me find a place to lay low.\"","\"Are you begging me?\"","\"Cui Qingwu, don’t push me...\"","Before Lou Yuxue could finish, Cui Qingwu’s tone shifted. \"I can help you with that.\"","\"But I have a condition.\"","Lou Yuxue suppressed her anger. \"Name it!\"","Cui Qingwu said with a smile, \"Before I leave Shu State, you have to do three things for me.\"","Lou Yuxue’s brow furrowed. \"What else are you planning?\"","\"You came to Shu State on your own this time. The Pavilion Master and the Golden Banner Officer are already displeased. If you stay any longer, aren’t you afraid the Pavilion Master will call you to account?\"","Cui Qingwu’s smile faded slightly. \"That’s my business, not yours.\"","\"Besides, even if they’re displeased, what can they really do to me?\"","Lou Yuxue paused at her words, giving her a long, hard look. \"I can agree to your condition, but it must not conflict with the mission.\"","\"Of course.\"","\"After all, who in the White Tiger Guard doesn’t know that the Lady Tiger is famously impartial and devoted solely to the Pavilion Master?\"","\"Hmph!\"","Lou Yuxue snorted coldly and turned her head to look toward the Quchi, ignoring the taunt.","\"Later, I will assess the situation with the Xiao and Liu Families and report what has happened here to our superior. Until he replies, neither of us can make another move.\"","\"Relax. I’m not as invested in the affairs of Shu State as you are.\"","\"Then why did you come to Shu State? To help Chen Yunfan?\"","Cui Qingwu gave her a radiant smile. \"Take a guess.\"","At her words, an image of that detestable man’s face flashed through Lou Yuxue’s mind. Her tone turned rigid.","\"Suit yourself. Just don’t forget what you promised me. And remember, somewhere in North City would be best.\"","\"Oh?\"","\"...The Xiao Family’s Hidden Guard have been watching South City and West City recently, and East City is too far from the Xiao Family.\"","After that brief explanation, Lou Yuxue turned and walked away.","Cui Qingwu watched her until she was in the distance, then let out a soft chuckle. She beckoned Huan’er over with the umbrella and returned to her carriage.","Huan’er glanced around before driving the carriage south toward Tingyu Pavilion.","\"Miss, that woman is so tactless.\"","\"She is a bit, but... never mind. Tomorrow, remember to acquire a storefront on Kangning Street.\"","\"A storefront?\"","’It wouldn’t do to let her have too much free time.’","Cui Qingwu watched the rain fall outside the carriage window, her mood quite pleasant.","Despite her earlier taunts, she actually held Lou Yuxue’s abilities in high regard. Otherwise, she never would have proposed that condition.","’But approval was one thing. That woman, Lou Yuxue, was far too rigid in her single-minded loyalty to the Pavilion Master.’","’She had to be cautious.’","「After the carriage left Kangning Street.」","A dark figure quietly emerged from the grass beside the Quchi.","The dim yellow glow of a lantern illuminated his form, revealing a tall, slender man with a long, thin face.","It was none other than Ning Yu, Chen Yunfan’s Guard.","’Miss Cui is connected to the Hidden Guard, too?’","’I have to report this to the Young Master immediately...’","...","「Late evening.」","「Tingyu Pavilion.」","Inside a room in the central courtyard, Chun Ying stood by the window, gazing toward the rear courtyard with a thoughtful expression on her delicate face.","Ning Yu stood respectfully by her side, waiting quietly.","A moment later, Chun Ying seemed to snap out of her thoughts. She smiled and said, \"Brother Yu, you should go rest. I’ll find the Young Master and tell him what happened.\"","Ning Yu bowed slightly. \"Thank you for your trouble, Miss Chun Ying.\"","Chun Ying nodded, and after bidding him farewell, she walked with light steps toward a room deeper in the complex.","She glanced at Chen Yunfan, who was fast asleep, hugging his quilt. After a moment’s thought, she turned and fetched a basin of warm water.","After soaking a towel in the water, she came to the bedside. She gently wiped Chen Yunfan’s eyes with the damp cloth and whispered,","\"Young Master, wake up...\"","Chen Yunfan stirred as if sensing her, turning over and mumbling groggily, \"What is it? Why are you disturbing me?\"","Chun Ying sighed helplessly. Pressing a hand on his shoulder, she said, \"Young Master, we have a lead on what happened during the day.\"","\"The burning of the Three Towns’ summer grain... it was orchestrated by the Hidden Guard. That group of Evil Demons from the Bright Moon Building were just providing cover.\""]},{"number":258,"title":"Chapter 258 - 205: The Xiao Family Must Have a Master","paragraphs":["\"Oh.\"","\"Also, there’s been some movement from the Liu Family. Liu Wen, whom you met some time ago, hasn’t been seen for a day.\"","\"Mm.\"","Seeing that Chen Yunfan was unmoved, Chun Ying hesitated. \"Then there’s Miss Cui. She just met with Lady Tiger, the White Tiger Guard Silver Banner Officer.\"","\"Cui Qingwu?\"","Chen Yunfan slowly sat up. Rubbing his eyes, he looked at her and asked, \"What did Cui Qingwu and Lady Tiger say to each other?\"","Seeing that he wasn’t angry, Chun Ying breathed a sigh of relief. \"According to Brother Ning, Lady Tiger wanted to ask Miss Cui for help in securing a place for herself.\"","\"She agreed?\"","\"It seems so. She also made one condition: Lady Tiger has to do three things for her.\"","Upon hearing this, Chen Yunfan lay back down. He didn’t go back to sleep, however. Leaning against the pillow, he asked lazily,","\"What else?\"","Chun Ying proceeded to recount everything Ning Yu had seen and heard. \"That’s the gist of it.\"","Chen Yunfan yawned. \"As a young lady of the Qinghe Cui Family, it’s normal for her to have connections with the White Tiger Guard.\"","\"As long as she wasn’t involved in the burning of the Three Towns’ summer grain, it’s fine.\"","After a brief pause, he looked at Chun Ying and asked, \"What about the Xiao Family?\"","\"There’s news from them as well.\"","\"Xiao Dongchen of the second branch has committed suicide. The Old Marquis has driven Xiao Wang and the others out of Shu State, and they intend to head for Guangyue Prefecture.\"","Chen Yunfan froze for a moment, surprised. \"Xiao Dongchen is dead?\"","\"Yes. The Xiao Family hasn’t suppressed the news, but there’s no word on why he killed himself.\"","\"How strange.\"","\"Just yesterday morning, that very same Xiao Dongchen transferred credit for one of his achievements to me. Why would someone who tried so hard to curry favor with me suddenly commit suicide?\"","Chun Ying thought for a moment. \"Could Xiao Dongchen have been involved with the attack on the Three Towns’ summer grain?\"","Chen Yunfan grinned. \"Then he got what he deserved.\"","\"I saw the rift between the Xiao Family’s second branch and the Old Marquis long ago. I just didn’t expect Xiao Dongchen to be so audacious.\"","\"No, I should say he was stupid.\"","\"The Xiao Family has stood strong in the Great Wei Dynasty for two hundred years. Even if things are difficult now, the Old Marquis is still alive.\"","\"For the second branch to act up like that... they were just asking to be put down.\"","Chun Ying nodded at his words and continued, \"Sir, there’s one more thing.\"","\"After slaughtering the criminal elements in the city’s west side today, Xiao Jinghong didn’t return to the Xiao Family. He left the Prefecture City directly.\"","Chen Yunfan mused, ’Xiao Jinghong must be returning to the Mutual Market.’\"","\"That was my guess as well.\"","\"The losses to the Three Towns’ summer grain weren’t substantial this time, so the Old Marquis remaining in the Prefecture City is enough to handle things. Besides, all those who made a move have already been eliminated...\"","Before she could finish, Chen Yunfan shook his head. \"That’s only part of it.\"","\"The second, and most important point...\"","\"With Xiao Jinghong away from the Prefecture City, it forces certain people to stay their hand.\"","It dawned on Chun Ying. \"You’re saying the Xiao Family is keeping Xiao Jinghong at the Mutual Market as an insurance policy, to prevent the entire family from being wiped out?\"","\"Exactly. If a major incident were to happen within the Xiao Family, Xiao Jinghong could mobilize the troops of the Three Towns. At that point... heh heh...\"","At this, Chen Yunfan looked out at the falling rain and remarked with admiration, \"I wonder who’s behind the scenes, masterminding the Xiao Family’s strategy.\"","\"Perhaps their ability to navigate this crisis is also thanks to this person.\"","Chun Ying’s eyes shifted. \"Sun Changming was staying with the Xiao Family for a while. Could it be him?\"","\"You’re a White-robed Minister. How could you not know which old foxes are in the Xiao Family?\"","\"You jest, Sir. I’m just a novice White-robed Minister.\"","\"Then go back and ask. The Xiao Family is facing threats from within and without, yet they keep turning disaster into fortune. There must be a master strategist involved.\"","Chun Ying nodded. \"I’ll write a letter back shortly.\"","But then Chen Yunfan shot her a sideways glance. \"I meant for you to go back personally. To leave Shu State.\"","\"...Sir, if you’re dissatisfied with me, you can just say so.\"","\"You call yourself a White-robed Minister when you can’t even see the real reason why Xiao Jinghong is staying away?\"","\"You didn’t actually think he’s out there just to avoid my Brother Yi, did you?\"","Chun Ying’s mouth fell open. \"I... I...\"","Seeing her flustered, Chen Yunfan burst out laughing. \"You fell for it, didn’t you?\"","\"You actually believed the nonsense I was spouting?\"","Chun Ying looked at him, frustrated, unsure which part of what he’d said was the \"nonsense.\"","’In her mind, Xiao Jinghong staying at the Mutual Market really did allow him and the Old Marquis to form a pincer, keeping everyone else in check.’","’Some military treatises even described it clearly, calling it a \"pincer advantage.\"’","\"Sir, do you know something I don’t?\"","Chen Yunfan’s laughter died. He muttered, \"How boring,\" and rolled over. \"Now hurry up and go. I need to rest.\"","\"You...\"","\"What, you want to warm my bed for me?\"","\"N-no, that’s not...\"","Chun Ying fled in a panic.","After the door clicked shut, Chen Yunfan opened his eyes. He stared at a corner of the bed, muttering to himself.","’The Xiao Family was getting hit from all sides, yet they still managed to foil the Hidden Guard’s plot and catch their breath.’","’Now all those people waiting for the Xiao Family to collapse are going to be disappointed.’","Thinking of this, Chen Yunfan clucked his tongue twice and closed his eyes again.","But a moment later, his eyes shot open. ’Dammit, this is bad.’","’If the Xiao Family’s situation keeps improving, then everything I warned Brother Yi about... won’t it all have been for nothing?’","’He’ll never let me live it down!’","Muttering to himself that this wouldn’t do, Chen Yunfan resolved to find a chance to salvage the situation.","’The Mid-Autumn Festival?’","’I’m all lonely and miserable here in Shu State. Brother Yi wouldn’t have the heart to leave me like this...’","...","「Meanwhile, in a residence adjacent to the Governor’s Office.」","Liu Yu paced back and forth in the main hall, his anxiety plain to see as he occasionally glanced up at the night sky outside.","In a Grandmaster’s Chair nearby, a middle-aged man in plain black clothes was sipping from a blue-and-white porcelain teacup.","SLURP, SLURP.","Perhaps irritated by the slurping, Liu Yu stopped pacing and frowned."]},{"number":259,"title":"Chapter 259 - 205: The Xiao Family Must Have a Master","paragraphs":["\"Lord Governor Liu Hong, are you truly not worried about your nephew Liu Wen’s safety?\"","The middle-aged man in black—Liu Hong, the Left Governor of the Shu State Governor’s Office—set down his teacup and said with a smile:","\"Second Brother, Wen’er is a grown man. It’s quite normal for him to stay out all night occasionally. What is there to worry about?\"","\"Under normal circumstances, I wouldn’t be worried, but look at the timing!\"","\"The Dingyuan Army’s three border towns were hit by a night raid, the summer grain at Iron Wall Town was burned, and at this critical juncture, Wen’er has disappeared. He...\"","Seeing Liu Yu pause, a serious expression appeared on Liu Hong’s square-jawed face as he asked:","\"Second Brother, are you worried this is related to Wen’er?\"","\"Or... do you know something?\"","Liu Yu glanced at him and fell silent for a moment before sighing. \"The day before yesterday, Wen’er took three hundred thousand taels in silver notes from the accounts.\"","Liu Hong’s brow furrowed slightly. \"Second Brother, why didn’t you tell me about something so significant sooner?\"","Liu Yu hesitated. \"I... I just assumed Wen’er took the silver coins to expand Xinglin Hall in Shu State, didn’t I?\"","\"But I’ve already asked Zhaoxue. Wen’er hasn’t been seen all day, and he never showed up at the storefronts we’d already picked out.\"","\"Third Brother, do you think Wen’er might... might have already fallen into the Xiao Family’s hands?\"","Liu Hong pondered for a moment, then said in a low voice, \"If that’s the case, then we can only wait for the Old Marquis to come knocking and demand answers.\"","\"This...\"","Before Liu Yu could speak, the sound of footsteps came from outside the door.","Then, Liu Zhaoxue hurried in. After bowing to the two men, she said, \"Second Uncle, Third Uncle, the Xiao Family just delivered a formal calling card.\"","Liu Yu and Liu Hong exchanged a look. ’Speak of the devil,’ they thought.","Liu Yu stepped forward to take the calling card. As he opened it, his expression changed drastically.","He quickly handed the card to Liu Hong, saying, \"The Old Marquis is coming in person early tomorrow morning. He’s specifically asked to see the two of us.\"","Liu Hong glanced at it, placed the card on the table, and said nothing more.","Seeing this, Liu Yu couldn’t help but say anxiously, \"It’s come to this. If you have something to say, just say it.\"","Liu Zhaoxue looked at the expressions on both their faces and realized something must have happened. A serious look crossed her face as well.","’Could this be related to Second Brother?’","Liu Hong ignored their gazes. Tapping on the armrest, he kept his head down and said:","\"At this point, worrying is useless. We need to think about how to handle this.\"","Compared to Liu Yu and Liu Zhaoxue, he had been operating in Shu State for many years and had a deep understanding of both the Xiao Family and the Old Marquis.","He knew full well that the Old Marquis was seething with anger, a blade in hand, just waiting for some fool to stumble into its path.","That was why when Liu Jing had died earlier, even though he knew the killer wasn’t from the Wan Family Medicine Hall’s Nursing Home, he had gone with the flow to back down, lest he be caught in the middle and please no one.","But this time was different.","As Liu Hong thought of this, his face took on an imposing gravity. He took a deep breath and said:","\"Second Brother, you must depart for Jing State immediately. Leave Zhaoxue here alone.\"","Liu Yu was stunned. \"What? Why?\"","Liu Hong glanced at him. \"Second Brother, you know Liu Wen’s character better than I do. You should be well aware that he’s capable of a foolish act like burning the grain supply of the Three Towns.\"","\"Besides, the Old Marquis is coming in person. Do you not understand his intentions?\"","Liu Zhaoxue glanced at a hesitant Liu Hong and said softly, \"Second Uncle, this time the Old Marquis sent a formal calling card...\"","A calling card!","It dawned on Liu Yu. \"He... he’s coming to hold us accountable?\"","Liu Hong nodded. \"It can only be so. Elder Xiao wouldn’t come personally unless he had concrete evidence. Besides, why else would he send a formal calling card in advance?\"","\"When have you ever seen a Marquis act with such courtesy?\"","Hearing this, Liu Yu dazedly sank into a nearby chair, his expression shifting uncertainly. He muttered, \"Courtesy before force...\"","\"So you want me to return to Jing State to bring back reinforcements?\"","Liu Hong shot him a glare. \"I’m telling you to lie low, Second Brother, to prevent the Old Marquis from provoking you and giving him an excuse to use his troops!\"","Liu Yu’s mouth fell open as he understood. \"Then you... no, what about Wen’er? Eldest Brother will definitely ask.\"","\"You go back first. After I meet with the Old Marquis, I will send a letter to Eldest Brother to explain.\"","After speaking, Liu Hong sighed softly. \"I just hope Wen’er is alright. Otherwise...\"","’Otherwise, their eldest brother would certainly not let the matter rest.’","Liu Zhaoxue also understood this point. Her beautiful eyes glanced at Liu Hong, then shifted to Liu Yu.","\"Fine, I’ll leave the city and return to Jing State now...\"","「Not long after.」","Liu Zhaoxue returned alone to the residence on Kangning Street. She stood by the window, watching the falling rain with a deep frown.","\"Did he really fall into the Xiao Family’s hands?\"","A sinister voice replied from beside her, \"Or perhaps he’s already dead.\"","Liu Zhaoxue turned her head to look, her tone calm. \"If he’s really dead, that would only make things worse.\"","Yan Fusha stepped out of the shadows and came to her side. \"Why?\"","\"A suspicious death would make the family overthink things, and that would only implicate more people. Even I wouldn’t be able to escape involvement.\"","\"Is that so... Then should I hide for the time being?\"","Liu Zhaoxue nodded slightly. \"Let’s wait and see. Perhaps Second Brother is just hiding.\"","’But that was impossible.’","Liu Wen had been acting so secretively before he left; he was clearly plotting something.","And he had taken three hundred thousand taels of silver from the accounts.","Liu Zhaoxue thought for a moment, then changed the subject. \"How is the investigation into that other matter?\"","Yan Fusha glanced at her and countered with a smile, \"Are you sure there’s something wrong with that man, Miss Zhaoxue?\"","\"I looked into his activities since arriving in Shu State today. He’s nothing more than a reckless scholar.\"","\"Even if he has good handwriting and is valued by Guiyun Academy, there doesn’t seem to be anything special about him.\"","Liu Zhaoxue paused at these words, the scene of her meeting with Chen Yi from earlier that day inevitably surfacing in her mind.","’She couldn’t have been mistaken—Chen Yi was definitely not a simple man.’"]},{"number":260,"title":"Chapter 260 - 205: There Must Be a Master in the Xiao Family","paragraphs":["\"In any case, just keep a close eye on him for me. Report to me the moment you discover anything.\"","\"Alright, I’ll go investigate further.\"","\"But this time, Miss Zhaoxue can’t stop me from testing him.\"","\"Suit yourself...\"","...","「The next morning.」","The sky was bright.","Chen Yi got up and dressed, only learning from Xiaodie that it was already past seven.","\"It’s that late already?\"","After learning that Xiao Jinghong had left Shu State yesterday, he had gone to bed early.","He had been so busy and mentally drained over the past few days. Now that he could finally relax, a wave of exhaustion was inevitable.","Xiaodie helped him adjust his collar and said with a smile, \"Young Master, I saw you were sleeping so soundly that I didn’t have the heart to wake you.\"","Chen Yi nodded. He glanced at the overcast, rainy sky outside and asked, \"Any news in the mansion today?\"","Xiaodie knew what he was really asking. As if she had been waiting for this, she began to chirp excitedly.","\"Young Master, you’ll never guess what happened!\"","\"First thing this morning, the Old Master left the mansion with a group of men. He said he was going to the Governor’s Office to see Lord Governor Liu.\"","Chen Yi nodded slightly. ’That’s not exactly surprising,’ he thought.","Xiao Dongchen was dead, and Xiao Jinghong had swept away both the Bright Moon Building and the West City Evil Demon. Of the \"masterminds\" behind the burning of the Three Towns, the only one the Xiao Family knew about—apart from the still-unidentified Financiers—was the Liu Family of Jing State.","It wasn’t strange for the Old Master to go and have a showdown with Liu Hong now.","Then he heard Xiaodie add, \"And do you know what else? The Old Master put on that suit of Armor before he left.\"","Chen Yi froze. \"What Armor?\"","\"The Battle Armor he wore during the southern campaign against Poshisu Country, when he drove out the Barbarian Race! It’s a shame I went out too late. I didn’t get to see how magnificent the Old Master looked wearing it.\"","Heh.","Chen Yi chuckled to himself. ’The old man must have been holding that in for far too long.’","’To go confront the Liu Family with such a grand display... he’s clearly planning to intimidate them right from the start.’","’I reckon that when a Second-Grade Officer like Liu Hong sees this display, he’ll lose a good thirty percent of his nerve.’","Fortunately, the Xiao Family was in the right this time. They had Liu Wen’s body, the three hundred thousand silver coins, and the letter signed and fingerprinted by Xiao Dongchen. It should be enough to force the Liu Family to yield.","As he was thinking this, Chen Yi was about to make some small talk when two lines of large text floated before his eyes:","[Opportunity +4.]","[Assessment: Duke Dingyuan Xiao Yuan confronts the Governor of Shu State, Liu Hong, compelling an apology and a joint petition for the Holy Emperor’s judgment. To not be present, to not hear, to not witness—to let a heaven-sent Opportunity pass you by is the mark of a truly lazy man.]","Chen Yi’s eyes narrowed. \"...\"","He really had gone to bed too early last night. He’d missed a great show.","But on second thought, ’Even if I had seen this information ahead of time, it would have been difficult to accompany the Old Master to the Governor’s Office anyway.’","’Oh well. The matter’s concluded, and the outcome was good. That’s what counts.’","Although there was still a \"Financier\" to deal with, the summer grain in the Three Towns hadn’t suffered much of a loss. For the time being, the Xiao Family’s predicament had been alleviated.","With that, Chen Yi took Xiaodie to the study. He instructed her to have a carriage brought around while he gathered up his calligraphy practice sheets.","\"Also, on your way back, stop by and ask Big Sister which elders we need to prepare festival gifts for.\"","Xiaodie acknowledged the order and left.","After packing up the practice sheets, Chen Yi considered his list. ’The masters at Guiyun Academy should also get gifts... Mr. Yue Ming, Mr. Zhuo Ying, and the others.’","He then took out a brush and paper to write a list, intending to purchase everything at once when he prepared the festival gifts on Xiao Jinghong’s behalf.","But not long after...","...not only did Xiaodie return, but Xiao Wan’er also came, having heard the news. She was holding a blue-covered booklet.","Chen Yi glanced at her. Her expression was normal; she clearly wasn’t affected by the news of Xiao Dongchen’s death yesterday.","\"Big Sister, what brings you here?\"","Xiao Wan’er’s smile was as gentle as ever. \"I heard you were going to buy festival gifts, brother-in-law?\"","Chen Yi said with a smile, \"My wife gave me instructions before she left yesterday. She asked me to prepare them for her.\"","Xiao Wan’er’s smile faltered for a moment before she nodded. \"I need to prepare some as well. Let’s go together.\"","Chen Yi, of course, didn’t refuse. He picked up the stack of calligraphy sheets and followed her out of the Spring Lotus Garden.","After instructing Xiaodie and the others to watch over Xiao Wuge, Xiao Wan’er and Chen Yi boarded the carriage.","The carriage was once again driven by the martial sisters, Xie Tingyun and Shen Huatang.","Once the carriage had left the Xiao Mansion, Xiao Wan’er finally spoke. \"Brother-in-law, did you hear about what happened in the mansion yesterday?\"","Chen Yi grunted in acknowledgment. \"I did. It’s a shame.\"","Perhaps because his tone was too casual, Xiao Wan’er couldn’t help but ask, \"What exactly do you find to be a shame, brother-in-law?\"","\"A shame... a shame that Uncle Dongchen got exactly the death he deserved.\"","Xiao Wan’er froze for a second. When she realized what he meant, she shot him a reproachful look.","\"He was an elder, after all. You shouldn’t speak of him that way.\"","Chen Yi simply nodded, then changed the subject. \"Such a major incident occurred yesterday. What are your thoughts on it, Big Sister?\"","At his words, a strange expression crossed Xiao Wan’er’s face. \"I... all I can do is comfort Second Grand-uncle’s family.\"","\"Them?\"","\"Yes. Yesterday, Grandfather told them to leave Shu State. He... he also said he was going to remove Uncle Dongchen’s name from the family registry. Second Grand-uncle collapsed from illness.\"","Chen Yi’s first reaction was, ’Serves him right.’ But seeing Xiao Wan’er’s expression, he adopted a more serious tone.","\"Life and death are determined by fate. I’m sure that wherever Uncle Dongchen is now, he would understand the Old Master’s decision.\"","Xiao Wan’er nodded faintly. \"Matters of military and state are for Grandfather and Jinghong to decide. Besides, he did do those terrible things.\"","\"I just can’t help but feel a little sad. When my father was still alive, Second Uncle and Uncle Dongchen were on good terms, and so was the whole family.\"","\"I never thought...\"","Listening to her reminisce, Chen Yi could somewhat understand how she felt.","It wasn’t about right or wrong, or even about the betrayal. Purely in terms of family ties, Xiao Dongchen and the second branch still had the blood of the Xiao Family flowing through their veins.","It was inevitable that Xiao Wan’er would feel some sadness seeing them fall to such a plight.","As for Chen Yi...","He had personally engineered this outcome, so naturally, he felt nothing.","In fact, if he had known the identity of the other Financier sooner, he might have been able to play this game of chess for even higher stakes.","Just as he was about to offer a few words of comfort, Chen Yi suddenly heard a deep, hoarse voice from outside the carriage:","\"Shu State... It’s still the same as ever.\"","\"I remember the last time I was here... it was for General Jinghong’s wedding...\""]},{"number":261,"title":"Chapter 261 - 206: Sincerity Is the Ultimate Move","paragraphs":["’That voice!?’","Chen Yi didn’t waste a moment thinking. He immediately lifted the side curtain and looked outside.","Under the dim light of the sky, the rain fell in a solid sheet.","A carriage approached from ahead and to the side.","It was pulled by a southern pony, a docile breed with a slow gait.","The carriage itself was made of common, reddish-brown wood, completely unadorned. It bore no family crest, offering no clue to its origin.","Compared to the magnificent carriage of the Marquis’s Mansion that Chen Yi was in, they were worlds apart.","As the two carriages—one small and plain, the other large and luxurious—passed each other, Chen Yi’s eyes met those of a man in the other vehicle.","How to describe the man’s appearance?","He had slightly curly brown hair, rugged eyebrows, a pear-shaped face, a hooked nose, and a pair of gray eyes.","Clearly a foreigner—a man from the Poshisu Country.","But he wasn’t wearing the loud, colorful, and chaotic attire typical of the Poshisu Country. Instead, he was dressed in the short-robed style of the Wei Dynasty’s Jianghu People.","At that moment, neither man’s expression faltered. Their gazes remained steady, their faces impassive.","The only difference was that Chen Yi wore a gentle smile, as if he had merely happened to lift the curtain to admire the rainy day.","The man opposite him, however, was expressionless, his eyes filled with an apathy that suggested he was indifferent to everything.","Even upon seeing Chen Yi, he looked at him as if he were someone utterly insignificant.","Just as the carriages passed, a low voice drifted over. \"Hmph, the Xiao Family...\"","Chen Yi impassively withdrew his gaze and lowered the curtain, thinking, ’Hmph, so it’s him.’","Chen Yi was certain he wasn’t mistaken. Besides being hoarse and deep, the man’s voice had a distinct and peculiar upward lilt at the end of his words.","He had originally assumed it was the accent of the Mountain Race, or a dialect from a region far from where the Central Plains’ common tongue was spoken.","Only now did he realize it was the native accent of someone from the Poshisu Country, one they couldn’t shake even after learning the language of the Central Plains.","’A man from the Poshisu Country...’","’The bizarre Cultivation Technique that made my predecessor flee his own wedding...’","’It seems the Martial Arts practiced by the Jianghu People of the Poshisu Country are mostly of the Evil Demonic Dao.’","’There are the Medicine Men who infuse their bodies with venom to practice Poison Skills, the Human Pigs who sever their own limbs for the Bone Transformation Skill, and even practitioners who specialize in the dark arts of Black Magic.’","’A Cultivation Technique capable of controlling another’s mind wouldn’t be surprising at all.’","But what truly concerned Chen Yi, aside from the man being from the Poshisu Country, was his motive for sabotaging the Xiao Family’s search for a son-in-law.","Moreover, the disdain in the man’s voice from his memory suggested a deep familiarity with both the Xiao Family and Xiao Jinghong.","As Chen Yi considered all this, a faint smile appeared on his face. He had, at last, found some clues.","The greatest fear is the unknown.","Once a person or a problem is known, there is always a way to solve it.","It’s merely a matter of time.","The same was true for Chen Yi.","He was not short on methods for solving problems, nor was he short on patience.","’The only difference is whether I kill one person, or an entire group.’","Just then, Xiao Wan’er noticed Chen Yi was lost in thought. She trailed off from her story, lowered her head slightly, and asked softly,","\"Do you... think I’m being overly sentimental?\"","Chen Yi snapped back to reality. He turned to look at her, realizing his distraction had led her to worry, and replied with a smile,","\"If the Marquis’s Mansion had more people like you, there would probably be a lot less trouble.\"","\"People like me?\"","\"Yes. You’re reasonable, considerate of others’ feelings, respectful to your elders, kind to your family, gentle with everyone, and never biased...\"","Hearing this, Xiao Wan’er’s mouth fell open. Her earlier melancholy vanished, replaced by a faint blush on her cheeks. \"I... I’m not nearly as wonderful as you make me sound.\"","\"Everyone knows it. If not for all your hard work, just putting food on the table at the mansion would be a challenge, to say nothing of the monthly allowances.\"","\"Plus, you’re a skilled manager with a knack for finances. Every matter in the Marquis’s Mansion, big or small...\"","Actually, Chen Yi wasn’t very good at making girls happy.","Truthfully, he had no experience, nor had he ever studied the art of charming women.","He didn’t know the first thing about pick-up lines or tugging at heartstrings.","The only tool in his arsenal was sincerity.","And so, under the assault of Chen Yi’s sincere praise, the blush on Xiao Wan’er’s face deepened.","The hand hidden beneath her cloak fidgeted, rising and falling as she debated whether she should cover his mouth to make him stop.","And it wasn’t just her.","Even Xie Tingyun and Shen Huatang, driving the carriage up front, exchanged glances upon hearing his words.","’Junior Sister, the Second Young Master-in-law’s silver tongue... tsk tsk, it’s lethal.’","’Senior Sister, he’s not wrong, though. The Eldest Miss really is like that.’","’Ah, Junior Sister, sometimes the truer the words, the deeper they sink into the heart...’","Obviously, Xiao Wan’er took it to heart.","After hesitating a moment longer, she finally reached out and covered Chen Yi’s mouth, her face flushed crimson. \"Don’t... don’t say any more.\"","Chen Yi blinked, his eyes gesturing downward to show he understood and would stop.","Xiao Wan’er hastily pulled her hand back, burrowing her head so deep into her furry collar that only her flustered, darting eyes were visible.","Seeing her reaction, Chen Yi decided not to praise her any further, lest she suffocate from embarrassment.","After a brief silence, he switched to business. \"Yesterday, I had a long talk with that Boss Chen. I conveyed your and the Old Master’s intentions. As for Boss Chen...\"","Chen Yi saw her cautiously peek her head out, revealing one flushed earlobe, and couldn’t resist drawing out the suspense.","When he paused, Xiao Wan’er couldn’t help but turn to look at him.","Her gaze met his, and she saw the mischievous, teasing smile on his face.","Flustered, Xiao Wan’er subconsciously reached out and gave his waist a light pinch, asking with a pout, \"Well? What did Boss Chen say?\"","It was a girlish gesture she would never have made under normal circumstances.","She must have truly been flustered by Chen Yi’s teasing.","Chen Yi knew this as well. The anger stirred by the man from Poshisu had completely vanished, and his mood lightened considerably."]},{"number":262,"title":"Chapter 262 - 206: Sincerity Is the Ultimate Skill (Part 2)","paragraphs":["\"Boss Chen said that Hundred Herbs Hall is preparing to tour Shu State and assess the conditions in various regions so they can better coordinate with the estate later on.\"","\"He also said that both now and in the future, Hundred Herbs Hall will follow the lead of you and the Old Master. The profit-sharing ratio is negotiable and will depend on the circumstances...\"","Of course, these were just empty pleasantries Chen Yi was passing along.","Business was business. The final terms of their cooperation would have to be put in writing. A signed contract was the only way to guarantee security for both Hundred Herbs Hall and the Xiao Family.","Xiao Wan’er naturally had no objections. After taking a moment to compose herself, the blush fading from her face, she asked thoughtfully,","\"Then is there any issue with Boss Chen’s identity?\"","Chen Yi paused, choosing his words carefully. \"It’s hard to say.\"","\"However, he is a Medical Saint Hand. I imagine that should mean he’s trustworthy.\"","\"As far as I know, there aren’t many Medical Saint Hands in the entire Great Wei Dynasty. I doubt anyone would dare have him cause trouble for you and the Old Master.\"","Xiao Wan’er looked at him in surprise. \"A Medical Saint Hand? Boss Chen is so young... is his mastery of the Medical Dao really that incredible?\"","Chen Yi smiled. \"His master’s lineage is likely very formidable.\"","Xiao Wan’er nodded. Then, as if she’d had a sudden idea, a joyful expression lit up her face. She asked,","\"Then do you think Boss Chen could serve as an Instructor at the Medical Dao Academy? Or even... the Dean?\"","’No.’","’Absolutely not.’","’Chen Yi’s heart skipped a beat. He was here devising strategies and preparing to train Ma Liangcai and the others into Medical Saint Hands, but he never imagined Xiao Wan’er would try to recruit him as well.’","’If he hadn’t known that Xiao Wan’er was unaware of \"Boss Chen’s\" true identity, he would have found some way to sabotage the entire Medical Dao Academy project, no matter what.’","Xiao Wan’er seemed to sense his strange reaction and asked quizzically, \"He can’t?\"","Chen Yi’s mind raced. \"He probably can’t.\"","\"Before Boss Chen completed his training, he promised his master he would roam the land and save ten thousand lives.\"","\"So for the foreseeable future, he can’t remain in Shu State.\"","\"Really?\"","\"Of course. That night on the Painted Boat, Boss Chen was very adamant about it.\"","Upon hearing this, Xiao Wan’er couldn’t help but look surprised. She said with admiration, \"No wonder Boss Chen so rarely makes an appearance in Shu State. So he has such a grand ambition.\"","\"If only I had his level of Medical Skill.\"","Chen Yi muttered an agreement, then said comfortingly, \"Everyone has their own strengths. You don’t need to envy others.\"","\"Besides, it’s like the saying goes: give a man a fish and you feed him for a day; teach a man to fish and you feed him for a lifetime. Once the Physicians at the Medical Dao Academy complete their studies, won’t they save far more than ten thousand people?\"","Xiao Wan’er nodded, her eyes filled with anticipation, clearly imagining the future once the Medical Dao Academy was established.","Then, she pulled a blue-covered booklet from her cloak and said,","\"Brother-in-law, this is what I’ve compiled about the Medical Dao Academy over the last few days, based on what you said before. Could you take a look?\"","Chen Yi would not refuse, of course. He took the booklet and scanned through it, a sense of gratification welling up inside him.","’He had to admit...’","’The charter Xiao Wan’er had put together was incredibly detailed.’","’She had not only categorized and listed everything they had discussed previously, but had also jotted down important notes and new ideas.’","\"For the most part, it’s fine. We’ll just need to adjust some minor details based on the academy’s final structure—the dean, the instructors, the required texts, and so on.\"","\"You’re right, Brother-in-law. That’s what I was thinking, too. I just have a few questions left, and I was hoping you could help me decide on them.\"","\"For example, this part here...\"","The two of them huddled together, studying the contents of the booklet. For the most part, Chen Yi did the talking while Xiao Wan’er listened intently, committing it all to memory.","When the carriage finally stopped in front of Guiyun Academy, Chen Yi closed the booklet and said with a smile,","\"A journey of a thousand miles begins with a single step. This is more than enough for you to take that first step.\"","Xiao Wan’er nodded, her face breaking into a radiant smile, as bright and beautiful as a newly bloomed Snow Lotus.","’Exquisite.’","Chen Yi allowed himself another look before stepping out of the carriage. He gathered the twenty-odd brocade boxes containing the calligraphy pieces, ready to deliver them to Mr. Yue Ming.","Just then, Xiao Wan’er followed him out. She looked at the building with the plaque bearing the name ’Guiyun Academy’ and asked hesitantly,","\"Can I come along and have a look?\"","Chen Yi could see she was intrigued. He nodded. \"Of course.\"","He even came up with a convenient excuse. \"As it happens, it’s a bit awkward for me to carry all these boxes by myself. I’ll have to trouble you for some help.\"","\"Alright.\"","Xiao Wan’er smiled and took two of the brocade boxes. She then instructed Shen Huatang to carry a few more, leaving only Xie Tingyun behind to watch the carriage.","The three of them entered the academy together.","Xiao Wan’er looked down at the boxes in her hands and said, \"I heard Xiaodie mention before that you had them mounted, but I didn’t imagine there would be this many.\"","\"Are all of these for the exhibition hall?\"","Chen Yi grunted in affirmation and replied,","\"I don’t know how large a space Mr. Yue Ming and the others have prepared, so I wrote a few extra pieces, just to be safe.\"","\"If there are too many, you can just keep the extras for now. If there are too few... well, then there are too few. We’ll just have the dean and the others write some more.\"","Hearing the word \"keep,\" Xiao Wan’er couldn’t help but remember the poem she had \"stolen\" from Chen Yi’s study. She instinctively ducked her head, not daring to ask any more questions.","Chen Yi, of course, was oblivious to her thoughts.","He continued to lead Xiao Wan’er and Shen Huatang deeper into the academy, nodding in return to students who greeted him along the way.","The students’ reactions to Chen Yi were normal. Whether they knew him or not, they all offered a proper, formal bow.","Upon seeing Xiao Wan’er, however, their composure faltered.","Even the resident playboys—those talented scholars who prided themselves on being suave and worldly—were no exception, all of them seemingly struck dumb by her heavenly beauty."]},{"number":263,"title":"Chapter 263 - 206: Sincerity Is the Killer Move","paragraphs":["\"Is that woman with Mr. Qingzhou his wife?\"","\"...That’s Old Marquis Xiao’s eldest granddaughter, Xiao Wan’er. She’s not Mr. Qingzhou’s wife.\"","\"She’s just as the rumors say—a beauty that could topple nations. What a pity...\"","\"A pity about what, my friend?\"","\"A pity that beauty is so often ill-fated. I heard Xiao Wan’er has suffered from a serious illness since childhood, one that no medicine can cure.\"","\"How could that be? She... she...\"","\"If not for that, why would she still be unmarried at her age? Alas, it’s truly lamentable.\"","Most of the students at Guiyun Academy were from Shu State, so they were naturally familiar with the Xiao Family.","They had all heard stories about Old Marquis Xiao, Xiao Wan’er, and Xiao Jinghong.","In contrast, Chen Yi, the Xiao Family’s live-in son-in-law, was someone the Guiyun Academy students had only recently become acquainted with.","Amidst the faint murmurs of discussion, Chen Yi led Xiao Wan’er and Shen Huatang to Mr. Yue Ming’s residence, only to find it empty.","After asking a couple of passing students, he learned that Mr. Yue Ming and the others were outside the academy’s library, reportedly preparing a new study.","Chen Yi raised an eyebrow slightly, thinking to himself, ’They sure are fast.’","’It’s only been three days since I discussed the exhibition hall with Mr. Yue Ming and the others. It’s ready already?’","But on second thought, he figured they probably just repurposed an existing building, so he didn’t dwell on it.","He then changed course and headed for the library with Xiao Wan’er and Shen Huatang, all of them carrying copybooks.","Perhaps because she rarely had the chance to visit places like an academy, Xiao Wan’er found everything new and fascinating.","Looking around, she said with great interest, \"All those talented scholars are bowing to you.\"","Chen Yi smiled and nodded. \"Well, I am an Instructor at the academy now, so I’m considered their senior.\"","\"Mm, the scholarly atmosphere here is so strong. If Wuge could study here, it would surely be good for him.\"","\"Perhaps...\"","He figured if Xiao Wuge heard that, he’d be so happy he’d jump from his room straight into the pond.","In truth, Xiao Wan’er’s reaction was understandable.","Because of her health, she had rarely left the Xiao Mansion throughout her entire life.","It was only after she went to the Daoist Temple on Wumeng Mountain to use the Heaven and Earth’s Ultimate Yang Qi to alleviate her Extreme Yin Deficiency Meridian that she was able to go out.","The number of times she left the mansion each year could be counted on one hand.","And most of those outings were just to buy a few things or visit the Medicine Hall and other such places.","As for Guiyun Academy... this was Xiao Wan’er’s first time here.","It wasn’t long before the three of them found Mr. Yue Ming and the others.","Just as Chen Yi had guessed, the study—a room roughly fifty feet square—had been freshly painted. The interior was completely empty, supported only by four pillars.","The group exchanged greetings, and Mr. Yue Ming gestured around the study, asking, \"Qingzhou, take a look. What do you think of this place?\"","Chen Yi surveyed the area and nodded. \"It’ll do.\"","He didn’t have any special requirements for the exhibition hall. As long as it was spacious and well-lit, it was fine.","After all, it was a place specifically for displaying Calligraphy Dao copybooks. If it were too cramped, it would inevitably make Guiyun Academy seem petty.","\"In that case, I’ll have someone furnish this place shortly.\"","As Mr. Yue Ming spoke, his eyes kept darting toward the brocade boxes in the hands of Chen Yi and his companions.","Chen Yi understood, of course. He distributed the dozen or so brocade boxes he was holding among Mr. Yue Ming, Mr. Zhuo Ying, and the others.","\"The copybooks I promised to leave for this exhibition hall are all here.\"","A delighted expression spread across Mr. Yue Ming’s face. He immediately opened one of the brocade boxes in his hands, ignoring the present company.","Instantly, a hazy, brilliant light illuminated the study.","A line of shimmering golden characters in Wei Qing’s Style faintly emerged from the copybook.","Mr. Yue Ming’s eyes lit up as he scanned it. He exclaimed in admiration,","\"Diligence is the path up the mountain of books; hard work is the boat across the endless sea of learning...\"","\"Excellent! Excellent! The characters are well-written, and the words are wonderfully composed. This will surely encourage the students of our academy.\"","Mr. Zhuo Ying, without taking a second look, also opened the copybook in his hands and showed it to the others.","\"A sword’s sharp edge is born from grinding; a plum blossom’s fragrance comes from winter’s bitter cold.\"","\"Qingzhou’s Wei Qing’s Style is so natural and perfect. The students who come to visit the academy will surely gain something from it.\"","The other instructors present were mostly acquainted with Chen Yi, and they all had high praise for the copybooks.","But there were also two others, an old man and a young one, both dressed in long robes, who stood to the side watching quietly.","After seeing several copybooks pass by, all in Wei Qing’s Style and all at the Great Success in Calligraphy Dao Realm, the handsome young man couldn’t help but mutter,","\"What’s so special about calligraphy at this level? It’s not that much better than my grandfather’s.\"","As he spoke, he looked at the old man beside him. \"Uncle Han, if this is all there is, there was no need for me to travel so far from home to Shu State, was there?\"","Hearing this, the old man gave a wry smile and gestured for him to stop. \"Zhaoye, don’t speak nonsense. We can discuss this later.\"","However, their conversation had already drawn the attention of Mr. Yue Ming and the others.","Chen Yi and Xiao Wan’er also noticed the pair, clearly not knowing who they were.","Mr. Yue Ming recognized the two, paused for a moment, and stepped forward to make introductions. \"Qingzhou, Miss Wan’er.\"","\"These two are guests who have come a long way from Yan State. This is Han Zhangping. You can simply call him Mr. Zhangping.\"","\"He is an Instructor at Yuelu Academy and has dedicated many years to the study of Confucianism.\"","Chen Yi bowed. After the old man, Han Zhangping, returned the bow, the two considered themselves introduced.","Mr. Yue Ming then continued the introduction, \"And this is...\"","Before he could finish, the young man stepped forward on his own and bowed. \"I am the student Pei Zhaoye. Greetings, Instructors.\"","Mr. Yue Ming paused, glanced at Han Zhangping, and then turned to Chen Yi. \"The Pei Family of Yan State. I imagine you’ve heard of them, Qingzhou.\"","It was clear that the dean was not pleased with Pei Zhaoye’s behavior of interrupting at will.","Chen Yi, however, didn’t seem to mind. He thought for a moment and asked, \"Is that the ’Pei’ of Mr. Pei Qiaosong from Yuelu Academy?\"","Before Mr. Yue Ming could speak, the young Pei Zhaoye lifted his chin and said, \"The very same.\"","Everyone fell silent, though most of them didn’t pay it much mind.","They were all learned people, after all, not the type to act high and mighty just because of their age or status.","The only one who was displeased was Mr. Yue Ming. Having been interrupted twice, he was already rather annoyed.","The old man, Mr. Han Zhangping, was well aware of this. He pulled the youth behind him and made a deep bow.","\"Zhaoye is young. I hope Dean Yue Ming and the other instructors will not take offense.\"","Pei Zhaoye, however, just pursed his lips and muttered something about not having done anything wrong.","Seeing this, even the good-tempered Mr. Yue Ming started to get angry. He said bluntly,","\"Zhangping, did you two just say that Qingzhou’s calligraphy lacks originality?\"","\"In that case, why don’t you take a look at this one I’m holding? What do you think?\""]},{"number":264,"title":"Chapter 264 - 207: Qingzhou Has Passed Myriad Mountains","paragraphs":["Mr. Yue Ming’s expression was grave and earnest.","Having spoken, he directly unrolled the calligraphy scroll in his hands.","One after another, dazzling, large characters emerged.","Although it was still the Great Success Calligraphy Dao, these large characters were completely different from the Wei Qing’s Style they had seen before.","This was Cursive Script!","Each stroke was not rigidly horizontal or vertical. Instead, they were slanted and curved, varying in size.","Yet they possessed a beauty entirely different from that of Wei Qing’s Style.","An air of carefree elegance seemed to leap off the page.","\"This is... a new style?\"","As an Instructor from Yuelu Academy, Mr. Han Zhangping was a man of wide experience.","He had observed Wei Qing’s Style calligraphy that had reached Great Success or even the Perfection Realm.","But Wei Qing’s Style was strict and orderly in every stroke, possessing at most a majestic beauty. It rarely displayed the kind of free-flowing brushwork and casual grace seen in this Cursive Script.","\"Different, completely different from Wei Qing’s Style, but it is indeed the Realm of Great Success in Calligraphy Dao...\"","Han Zhangping couldn’t help but lean closer, his gaze falling upon the paper itself, ignoring the luminous glow of its Mental Realm.","\"I have long heard of Qingzhou’s new calligraphy style. Seeing it today has made this trip worthwhile.\"","He looked at Chen Yi with admiration. \"No wonder you can produce students who achieve success in the Calligraphy Dao,\" he said. \"With this pioneering new style alone, you surpass the great calligraphy masters from two hundred years of the Wei Dynasty.\"","Chen Yi smiled and bowed. \"It’s merely a clever trick. I’m not worthy of such praise.\"","Seeing this, a smile finally appeared on Mr. Yue Ming’s face, tinged with a hint of pride.","After all, Chen Yi was now an Instructor at Guiyun Academy. Furthermore, by teaching Ma Guan, a student who achieved success in the Calligraphy Dao, he had made a name for himself throughout Shu State and attracted the attention of numerous Noble Families.","As the headmaster of Guiyun Academy, it was both natural and necessary for Mr. Yue Ming to stand up for him.","\"Qingzhou has already forged his own path in the Calligraphy Dao. In time, it’s not impossible that he could become a Saint.\"","\"Mr. Yue Ming is right.\"","\"If Qingzhou’s Calligraphy Dao advances another step, your Guiyun Academy will have an incredible future...\"","Seeing that everyone, including Mr. Zhangping who had brought him to Shu State, was praising Chen Yi so lavishly, the young man to the side, Pei Zhaoye, couldn’t help but mutter:","\"What’s so great about it? It’s just a new style. My grandfather said it’s usually the unorthodox and rebellious types who think up such things...\"","This time, however, before Mr. Yue Ming could show his displeasure, Han Zhangping had already reprimanded him. \"Zhaoye!\"","\"How could a learned man like your grandfather possibly say such a thing?\"","\"But he did...\"","Seeing this, Chen Yi couldn’t help but grin.","This boy was about twelve or thirteen, even younger than the boy from the Tang Family.","He obviously wasn’t going to take those words to heart.","Even Mr. Yue Ming saw through Pei Zhaoye’s temperament. He shook his head inwardly and said, \"Zhangping, the academy is still busy today. Let’s find another time to catch up.\"","Han Zhangping naturally understood his meaning. He bowed helplessly. \"My apologies.\"","After a slight pause, he didn’t take his leave directly but instead pulled Pei Zhaoye to the side.","Mr. Yue Ming and the others exchanged a glance, then ignored the pair and went back to looking at Chen Yi’s calligraphy scroll.","As they admired it, they also began discussing details like how to display it, where to place it, and so on.","Chen Yi found it a bit boring, so he didn’t join in.","Xiao Wan’er, on the other hand, watched Mr. Yue Ming and the others with a burning gaze, seemingly interested in everything.","Chen Yi had initially thought, ’She must be captivated by my Calligraphy Dao Realm.’ But after watching for a while, Xiao Wan’er asked in a low voice:","\"Chen Yi, do you think our academy should also set up a similar exhibition hall? To display content related to the Medical Dao.\"","Before Chen Yi could answer, Xiao Wan’er continued, \"I was just thinking, if we had such an exhibition hall, it should be able to attract some Physicians.\"","\"Perhaps there would even be some truly skilled people among them, a Medical Saint Hand?\"","After hearing her out, Chen Yi secretly raised his eyebrows.","’A Medical Hall of Fame?’","’A good idea.’","Although his purpose for setting up the exhibition hall at Guiyun Academy was different, her idea could indeed attract some Physicians.","After all, in this era, most people, no matter who they were, dreamed of leaving their name in the annals of history.","Those physicians who dedicated their lives to healing the world were no exception.","With this in mind, Chen Yi looked at Xiao Wan’er and nodded with a smile. \"It’s feasible.\"","Xiao Wan’er’s face lit up with joy. \"Is it really?\"","\"Of course.\"","\"But to attract truly masterful Physicians, an exhibition hall alone isn’t enough.\"","\"We could also use methods like compiling books and erecting monuments, or making grand gestures to attract talent.\"","\"Okay, I’ll write that down later.\"","\"There’s no rush. That academy can’t be built overnight, after all. You...\"","Meeting Xiao Wan’er’s gaze, Chen Yi could see her mind was made up. He sighed inwardly, didn’t continue his thought, and said instead:","\"After the Mid-Autumn Festival, let’s pick a location first.\"","\"If I have time then, I’ll go take a look with you.\"","Hearing this, Xiao Wan’er’s eyes crinkled with a smile as she nodded. \"Okay, I’ll listen to you.\"","But as soon as the words were out, she felt they were a bit ambiguous, as if something was strange about them.","’Of course it’s strange,’ Shen Huatang thought.","’This is exactly how a wife follows her husband’s lead.’","’But the Young Mistress and her brother-in-law...’","’I really hope it’s not what I think it is, or else... we’re all doomed.’","Meanwhile, on the other side, Han Zhangping was lecturing Pei Zhaoye. \"The academy teaches you to respect your teachers and honor the Dao, and that doesn’t just apply to Yuelu Academy.\"","\"Mr. Yue Ming, the headmaster of Guiyun Academy, is a great Confucian scholar just like your grandfather. He has many disciples, and even this year’s Third Place Scholar was his student.\"","\"The Third Place Scholar?\"","Pei Zhaoye might not care much about other things, but the imperial examinations were clearly an exception. Otherwise, he wouldn’t have passed the County Examination at such a young age.","Han Zhangping nodded, his expression still stern. \"I know you’ve been clever since you were a child, but you must understand that there is always someone better out there.\""]},{"number":265,"title":"Chapter 265 - 207: Qingzhou Has Passed Ten Thousand Mountains (Part 2)","paragraphs":["\"Even with your extraordinary talent, you should focus on your studies, not on being arrogant.\"","Pei Zhaoye pursed his lips and turned his head to look at Mr. Yue Ming and the others in the distance. \"Got it,\" he said dismissively.","Whether he truly understood or was just pretending, only he knew.","Han Zhangping knew well that a personality like his wasn’t developed overnight, nor could it be corrected with just a few words.","\"Zhaoye, I brought you to Shu State this time to confirm if Chen Qingzhou’s Calligraphy Dao is truly what the rumors claim.\"","\"If it’s true, then as instructed by the headmaster, you will need to study at Guiyun Academy for a while.\"","\"Once you’ve made significant progress in the Calligraphy Dao, you can return to Yuelu Academy...\"","Before he could finish, Pei Zhaoye cut him off. \"I refuse.\"","\"His Calligraphy Dao is at the same Realm as my grandfather’s. If he’s the one teaching me, I’d rather just stay at Yuelu Academy.\"","\"You...\"","Just as Han Zhangping was about to try persuading him again, he heard several gasps of surprise from nearby.","Even Pei Zhaoye, who had just spoken, wore a look of utter astonishment, as if he had witnessed something unbelievable.","Han Zhangping turned his head, intrigued.","He saw Mr. Yue Ming and Mr. Zhuo Ying in the distance, unrolling a calligraphy scroll that was about six feet long.","Upon it were no longer the dazzling golden characters from before, but an illusory landscape.","Amidst rolling mountains, a city stood high above while a small boat sped along below, crossing treacherous peaks and ridges in the blink of an eye.","Faintly, a figure could be seen standing on the boat, a wide smile on their face.","Han Zhangping stared blankly at the scroll, his face filled with disbelief. \"This... This is...\"","If he had merely been intrigued upon seeing the Cursive Script earlier, now, witnessing the Mental Realm manifesting from the scroll, he found it impossible to maintain his composure.","His entire body trembled with excitement.","Beside him, Pei Zhaoye’s eyes were wide with shock. He was young, true. He was arrogant, true. And he certainly looked down on everyone. But that didn’t mean he was ignorant.","’Grandfather said that when a Calligraphy Dao Realm becomes like a painting, it has reached the Perfection Realm. So that scroll is...’","\"Perfect Realm Calligraphy Dao!?\"","Pei Zhaoye couldn’t believe his own eyes.","He refused to believe that the scroll was the work of the very live-in son-in-law he so despised.","But the brilliant, new style of Cursive Script on the scroll left him no room for doubt.","’How is this possible? He... he raised a new script style all the way to Perfection?’","Pei Zhaoye vividly remembered the longing on his grandfather’s aged face when he had explained how to identify the Perfection Realm of Calligraphy Dao.","’Even his grandfather hadn’t reached the Perfection Realm. So how... How could Chen Qingzhou possibly have managed it?!’","In contrast, the expressions on the faces of Mr. Yue Ming, Mr. Zhuo Ying, and the others were rather peculiar.","It was the look of someone who had just found gold in a pile of sand.","They had all thought that the twenty-odd scrolls Chen Yi had produced, all at the level of Great Success in Calligraphy Dao, would be more than enough.","Who would have thought he’d give them such a massive surprise in the end—Perfection in Calligraphy Dao!","Perfection in Cursive Script, no less!","\"A new script... the Calligraphy Dao... the Perfection Realm... Qingzhou, this... your work...\"","Seeing Mr. Yue Ming so excited he was babbling incoherently, Chen Yi smiled warmly.","\"I just got lucky. I kept writing, and somewhere along the way, I broke through.\"","Mr. Zhuo Ying was flabbergasted. \"You call that luck?\"","\"If you could advance in the Calligraphy Dao through sheer luck, our Great Wei Dynasty would have at least a dozen more Calligraphy Saints.\"","\"Zhuo Ying, the key isn’t the first part of his sentence, it’s the second part. ’I kept writing...’\"","\"I’m going to go do some writing later myself.\"","\"You? Write? Have you even reached the entry-level of the Calligraphy Dao?\"","Seeing the masters of Guiyun Academy bickering amongst themselves, Chen Yi simply assumed they were too excited to contain themselves and spoke up.","\"I believe these scrolls should be more than enough. I’ll have to trouble you with the rest, Headmaster.\"","\"Enough! More than enough! It’s no trouble, no trouble at all...\"","Each phrase came out in a different, excited pitch.","Mr. Yue Ming was grinning from ear to ear.","He had every reason to be ecstatic.","Chen Yi’s achievement of Great Success in Calligraphy Dao had already attracted many talented scholars from within Shu State.","Many more from outside Shu State had traveled great distances to seek instruction.","If word got out that Chen Yi had achieved Perfection in the Calligraphy Dao, he feared the number of prospective students would multiply several times over.","It wouldn’t just be people from Yan State and You State; he estimated that scholars would come from as far as the Capital Prefecture and the Northern State.","\"Qingzhou, next time you have a breakthrough, please give us a heads-up.\"","\"I was thankfully being extra careful just now. If I had damaged this scroll, I don’t know what I would’ve done.\"","Hearing this, Mr. Zhuo Ying chimed in, still shaken. \"Indeed. It nearly scared me to death.\"","\"Qingzhou, you know my health is poor.\"","\"Without one of these scrolls of Perfected Calligraphy Dao to call my own, I’m afraid I’ll never recover.\"","\"Hey! You old rascal, have you no shame? How can you be so shameless?\"","\"You all know my health has always been frail...\"","Only then did Xiao Wan’er finally snap out of her daze. She looked at Chen Yi and couldn’t help but ask,","\"’Qingzhou has passed ten thousand layered peaks’... is that line... about you?\"","Chen Yi froze for a second, then answered vaguely, \"Well, I suppose so.\"","’It was,’ he could only say, ’a beautiful misunderstanding.’","’But it did make a certain kind of sense when applied to him.’","Xiao Wan’er smiled and nodded. \"It’s a wonderful poem.\"","She had learned long ago from Elder Master Xiao that Chen Yi had reached Perfection in the Calligraphy Dao, so her focus just now hadn’t been on the calligraphy itself.","Instead, it was the imagery within the Mental Realm that had caught her attention.","The overall Mental Realm of the poem was magnificent and grand, conveying a sense of breaking through a great barrier to find the light.","It was hard for Xiao Wan’er not to read more into it.","She carefully recalled everything that had happened to Chen Yi recently, a flicker of joy in her heart.","’My brother-in-law... he must have finally stepped out of the shadow of marrying into the Xiao Family and regained his confidence, right?’","Of course, Chen Yi had no idea what Xiao Wan’er was thinking.","Even if he did, he could only let it remain a beautiful misunderstanding. He could never reveal his role in the burning of the summer grain in the Three Towns."]},{"number":266,"title":"Chapter 266 - 207: Qingzhou Has Passed the Myriad Mountains","paragraphs":["With nothing else to do, Chen Yi decided it was time to leave.","\"Mr. Yue Ming, you...\"","But before Chen Yi could finish, Pei Zhaoye suddenly ran over to him. \"Mr. Qingzhou,\" he said, \"your Calligraphy Dao—can you teach it to me?\"","Chen Yi frowned slightly, sizing him up without a word. He continued with his formal bow to Mr. Yue Ming.","\"Dean, I have other matters to attend to, so I must take my leave.\"","Mr. Yue Ming glanced at Pei Zhaoye, then smiled and replied, \"Of course. When you come to teach the Calligraphy Dao before the Mid-Autumn Festival, I guarantee this exhibition hall will be to your satisfaction.\"","\"As long as you are satisfied, Dean.\"","With that, Chen Yi said his goodbyes to the others and signaled for Xiao Wan’er to get ready to leave.","Seeing this, Pei Zhaoye, refusing to give up, blocked his path.","\"Mr. Qingzhou, I apologize for my previous actions. I hope you can forgive me and teach me the Calligraphy Dao.\"","Chen Yi glanced at him and shook his head. \"Offer my apologies to your grandfather.\"","Before Pei Zhaoye could say another word, Chen Yi had already led Xiao Wan’er and Shen Huatang straight out of the academy.","Pei Zhaoye stared at his back, completely baffled.","\"If he’s going to refuse me, then just refuse me. Why tell me to apologize to my grandfather?\"","Just then, Han Zhangping walked over and said in a low voice, \"Because you, Pei Zhaoye, are not worthy of his forgiveness.\"","Pei Zhaoye froze, his expression instantly turning ugly.","\"On what grounds? He’s just a live-in son-in-law of the Xiao Family, a disgrace to all scholars! How can he...\"","\"Shut your mouth!\"","Han Zhangping’s voice suddenly sharpened, making Pei Zhaoye jump.","He looked at Han Zhangping’s livid face, his mouth moving wordlessly. He didn’t dare speak again.","Han Zhangping glared at him for a moment before taking a deep breath and bowing to Mr. Yue Ming and the others. \"I apologize for today’s disturbance.\"","Mr. Yue Ming shook his head, his expression calm. \"Our hospitality was lacking. Please, see yourselves out.\"","As he watched Han Zhangping drag the reluctant Pei Zhaoye away, Mr. Yue Ming shook his head.","\"No wonder Old Pei sent him to Shu State. With a disposition like that, he’ll never amount to anything without being tempered by hardship.\"","Mr. Zhuo Ying and the others nodded but said no more.","They knew Mr. Yue Ming’s temperament.","Even if Pei Zhaoye had an impressive background and no lack of talent, he would never allow such a person to enter Guiyun Academy.","Of course, neither would Chen Yi.","While he didn’t care about Pei Zhaoye’s lack of etiquette, that didn’t mean he would accept him as a student.","’After all, forgiving Pei Zhaoye is his grandfather’s business. What does it have to do with me, Chen Qingzhou?’","「On the way back.」","As usual, Chen Yi was chatting and laughing with Xiao Wan’er.","They spent half the day going from North City to the West Market, gathering all the necessary gifts and items for the festival before finally heading home.","By then, Elder Master Xiao had already returned with his men.","Inside and outside the mansion, Armored Warriors stood in rows—a clear display of the Dingyuan Marquis’s Mansion’s might.","Chen Yi scanned the area. He saw that while Wang Lixing and the others looked serious, they also seemed relatively relaxed.","He knew then that Elder Master Xiao’s trip to the Governor’s Office must have gone well.","’It makes sense,’ he thought. Liu Wen had died outside Iron Wall Town, and there was evidence of his conspiracy with Xiao Dongchen—the letters and the three hundred thousand taels of silver.","Under these circumstances, if Elder Master Xiao couldn’t make the Liu Family back down and bow their heads, he might as well just stay home and never go out again.","The only thing Chen Yi didn’t know was what conditions the Liu Family had agreed to.","But soon enough.","When he returned to the Spring Lotus Garden, he heard some rumors from Xiao Wuge about the Old Marquis’s meeting with Liu Hong.","Overall, it was much as Chen Yi had deduced.","The summer grain tax for the Dingyuan Army’s Three Towns was waived. The Governor’s Office claimed it was in accordance with a new Imperial Court decree.","Anyone with eyes could see that was nonsense.","The Jing State Liu Family would replenish the provisions burned at Iron Wall Town at a low price.","There was also some monetary compensation.","No more, no less—five hundred thousand taels.","Adding that to the three hundred thousand taels Liu Wen had previously given, the Xiao Family likely wouldn’t be short on funds or provisions for some time.","After hearing all this, Chen Yi thought for a moment and asked, \"Do you know what conditions the Liu Family set?\"","Hearing this, the smile on Xiao Wuge’s little face vanished by half. She huffed.","\"They said Grandfather can’t reveal Liu Wen’s involvement to outsiders, and in return, they’ll keep Uncle Dongchen’s business a secret.\"","\"Is that all?\"","\"Also, I think they mentioned something about a marriage alliance.\"","Chen Yi frowned slightly. \"They still want to ask for your eldest sister’s hand in marriage?\"","Xiao Wuge shook her head. \"Not Eldest Sister.\"","\"I think they said they want to marry the Third Miss of the Liu Family’s main branch over to us. I don’t know who that is... could it be that pretty big sister we saw the other day?\"","’The Third Miss... that could only be Liu Zhaoxue.’","Chen Yi muttered to himself, ’Did the Liu Family discover what Liu Zhaoxue did, or do they have some other ulterior motive?’","After thinking it over, he concluded the latter was more likely.","If the Liu Family knew what Liu Zhaoxue had done, she would likely meet a very grisly end.","\"Did Elder Master Xiao agree?\"","\"He did. He said Xiao Ziqi should marry her.\"","\"The one from the second branch?\"","Chen Yi let out a stunned laugh. \"And Liu Hong would agree to that?\"","After this whole incident, the second branch of the Xiao Family had been explicitly exiled from Shu State.","Even though Xiao Ziqi hadn’t left due to his position at the Shu State Capital Commandery, he would find it difficult to ever set foot in the Prefecture City again.","It would be a miracle if Liu Hong agreed under these circumstances.","Xiao Wuge chuckled. \"He didn’t.\"","\"Grandfather said the Liu Family is full of vicious ambition and that they’ll stumble sooner or later.\"","\"Perhaps...\"","Chen Yi looked at the rain outside the window, certain that there must have been other conditions between Elder Master Xiao and Liu Hong.","Or rather, that the price the Liu Family paid was far greater than just this.","The other details were likely just not suitable to be revealed to the public.","’It seems Elder Master Xiao still chose a conservative approach.’","With this thought, Chen Yi made the excuse that he was tired and returned to his room to practice the Four Symbols Skill.","He didn’t know if Xiao Jinghong had gone to find Pei Guanli, but he hoped that Tiger Girl could keep her mouth shut.","Otherwise...","He’d have to think of a way to fix it.","’Should I say I happened to befriend the \"Sword Madman,\" Liu Lang?’","’I’d probably get cleaved in two by a single sword strike for my trouble...’","...","「Meanwhile.」","On Kangning Street, inside a streetside shop not far from Guiyun Academy.","Lou Yuxue scanned her surroundings, her stunningly beautiful face showing a hint of grinding teeth.","\"Cui Qingwu, you are truly infuriating!\"","All she needed was a hiding place; any old courtyard that could withstand scrutiny would have been fine.","But what did she get instead? A shop!","Lou Yuxue didn’t even have to think to know this was surely that Miss Cui’s sick sense of humor.","She was waiting to see her make a fool of herself.","\"Hmph. Does she really think I wouldn’t dare hide right under the noses of the Xiao Family and the Imprisonment Department?\"","Lou Yuxue snorted, then called two of her subordinates over to tidy up the shop, preparing to open for business as usual.","It was a shop, after all.","If the doors remained shut and they didn’t operate, it would only attract more attention.","\"My lady...\"","\"Call me Boss Lady.\"","\"Boss Lady, what kind of business are we running?\"","Lou Yuxue thought for a moment, and the thought of that fellow \"Liu Wu\" suddenly popped into her head. She subconsciously said:","\"That bastard...\"","\"Wontons? I suppose that could work...\""]},{"number":267,"title":"Chapter 267 - 208: A Light Boat, A Light Heart","paragraphs":["Chen Yi knew full well how many people were looking for him.","He could count them on his fingers.","There were Chen Yunfan, Cui Qingwu, and Fang Hongxiu, the Hundred Households from the Imprisonment Department, all of whom he had drugged unconscious.","There were the Xiao Family’s Hidden Guards he had saved, and even the Xiao Family’s old master and Xiao Jinghong were looking for him.","And then there were the Hidden Guard Lou Yuxue and her people.","Fortunately, his identity hadn’t been exposed, so for the time being, he didn’t have to worry about them targeting him.","So, he was able to spend the afternoon peacefully cultivating the Four Symbols Skill.","He was now not far from the Upper Sixth Grade and estimated he could break through in another day or two.","He should be able to do it before the Mid-Autumn Festival.","After assessing his Cultivation progress, Chen Yi summoned the glowing screen to take a look.","He skipped past the Daos of chess, calligraphy, medicine, and martial arts and their corresponding Technique Realms, his gaze falling on the final line:","[Opportunity: 488]","’488... The higher the Dao Realm, the more Opportunity points it requires.’","’Excluding my Saber Dao, which is still at Minor Success, and my Calligraphy Dao, which has already reached the Perfection Realm, the rest of my Daos are all at the Great Success Realm.’","’And to raise any one of them to Perfection requires a thousand Opportunity points.’","Chen Yi shook his head to himself. If he relied solely on Opportunity points, how long would it take to raise all his Daos to Perfection?","’The fastest way is still through an epiphany, just like what happened with my Calligraphy Dao.’","’But epiphanies require the right trigger. They’re a matter of chance, not something he can control.’","’I’ll just have to keep up my Cultivation. That’s the only way to create opportunities.’","Chen Yi looked out the window at the rain falling from the dim sky and sighed softly.","’Even though Xiao Jinghong isn’t in the Prefecture City right now, Xie Tingyun is still here in Jiaxing Garden.’","’Practicing Fist Technique, Spear Technique, or Saber Technique would cause too much of a commotion. There’s no way he could hide that from the Eldest Senior Sister of the Celestial Sect.’","’Looks like I’ll have to get Wang Ji to find another secluded residence tomorrow, one specifically for practicing Martial Arts.’","As these thoughts ran through his mind, Chen Yi raised his Saber Dao to Great Success.","The profound mysteries of the Saber Dao, as vast and powerful as a great river, instantly flooded his mind before gradually settling.","After a moment of simple comprehension, a smile touched Chen Yi’s lips.","’If I can fully master these profound mysteries before my duel with Liu Lang, I can use him to test my new skills.’","’I’m sure the look on his face will be priceless.’","Chen Yi laughed, then shook his head, pushing the mischievous thought aside.","He knew exactly where the \"Madman\" in \"Saber Madman\" came from.","’If Liu Lang found out he’d also achieved Great Success in the Saber Dao, he’d probably pester him for a duel every single day.’","Just then, the sound of footsteps came from downstairs.","Xiaodie knocked on the door and said, \"Young Master, the Eldest Miss invites you to Jiaxing Garden for dinner.\"","Chen Yi called back, \"I’ll be right there,\" changed into a light robe, and headed straight for Jiaxing Garden with Xiao Wuge and Xiaodie.","「During the meal.」","Xiao Wan’er took out the booklet she had updated that afternoon and asked for Chen Yi’s opinion.","Chen Yi flipped through it and was mostly full of praise.","\"As it stands, the charter for the Medical Dao Academy is already quite comprehensive. The remaining details can be adjusted once the physicians are in place.\"","A smile graced Xiao Wan’er’s face. After carefully putting the booklet away, she said, \"I’ll go talk to Grandfather about it later and see if he agrees.\"","\"The old master is a magnanimous man. I’m sure he won’t refuse.\"","\"I hope so. I’m just worried my preparations aren’t sufficient and that I’ll be stumped by Grandfather’s questions. Actually...\"","Chen Yi understood her implication. He thought for a moment, then shook his head. \"Eldest Sister, you compiled the charter for the Medical Dao Academy from start to finish all by yourself.\"","\"Even if the old master asks about certain details, just answer him truthfully. If his points are reasonable, add them to the charter. If they’re unreasonable...\"","He paused, then looked at Xiao Wan’er encouragingly. \"I’m sure you’ll find a way to persuade the old master.\"","Xiao Wan’er met his gaze and said hesitantly, \"I’ll give it a try.\"","Chen Yi nodded and said with a smile, \"While the academy is still in its early stages, there’s no harm in gathering opinions from many sources.\"","\"You gain clarity by listening to all sides, after all.\"","\"Besides, if we can’t find a suitable Medical Saint Hand later on, you can serve as the dean for the time being, Eldest Sister. That would be enough to get the academy up and running.\"","Xiao Wan’er, who already lacked confidence, shook her head repeatedly upon hearing this. \"No, I couldn’t...\"","She blushed and said, \"My knowledge of Medical Skill is superficial at best. How could I possibly take on the role of dean? I would just be leading the students astray.\"","Chen Yi’s tone grew more serious. \"The main reason to have a Medical Saint Hand as dean is to better attract students who are passionate about the Medical Dao.\"","\"The actual teaching will mostly be handled by the instructors.\"","\"Take Mr. Yue Ming of Guiyun Academy, for example. His scholarship is passable, but he’s not proficient in Music, Chess, Calligraphy, or Painting. And when it comes to teaching, he has no idea how to tailor his methods to his students’ aptitudes.\"","\"If he can be the dean, why can’t you, Eldest Sister?\"","Xiao Wan’er couldn’t help but let out a small laugh at hearing him speak of Mr. Yue Ming that way. As if realizing it was improper, she quickly suppressed her smile and said:","\"Mr. Yue Ming is still a learned man. Otherwise, why would all those scholars be vying to study under him?\"","\"His scholarship is mediocre at best... Never mind him. In any case, could you at least consider my proposal as a backup plan, Eldest Sister?\"","\"If we really can’t find a Medical Saint Hand to head the academy, it wouldn’t be good to leave the dean’s position vacant.\"","After some persuading, Xiao Wan’er finally gave a slight nod. \"That’s a matter for later. I’ll ask for Grandfather’s opinion first.\"","After she spoke, she seemed to remember something and turned to Chen Yi.","\"If this plan succeeds, I’m afraid I won’t be able to manage the affairs of the medicine halls as well.\"","Chen Yi raised an eyebrow slightly, understanding she was referring to the expansion of Hundred Herbs Hall.","\"The few medicine halls here in the Prefecture City, with those medicinal teas you’ve introduced, should be able to guarantee a steady income.\"","\"As for Hundred Herbs Hall’s expansion, it shouldn’t need the family’s help in the early stages. That Boss Chen should be able to handle it.\"","\"The family will only need to step in when he runs into trouble he can’t solve on his own. When that time comes, you can handle it as you see fit, Eldest Sister.\"","After a pause, Chen Yi continued, \"If you’re still worried, Eldest Sister, you could also assign someone to oversee the Hundred Herbs Hall expansion. From what I’ve seen, those few shopkeepers from before are all quite sharp-witted.\"","Xiao Wan’er thought for a moment before nodding. \"You’re very thoughtful, Brother-in-law. It’s just...\""]},{"number":268,"title":"Chapter 268 - 208: A Light Boat, A Light Heart","paragraphs":["She glanced at Chen Yi but didn’t continue, instead addressing the others, \"Let’s eat first. We can discuss this later.\"","She had wanted to suggest that Chen Yi cooperate with Hundred Herbs Hall, but on second thought, she worried he would find it too troublesome.","Besides, the Medicine Hall’s business was not insignificant, as it concerned the Xiao Family’s income and expenses. She needed to ask the Old Master before making a final decision.","Fortunately, Chen Yi didn’t know what she was thinking, or the meal would have been thoroughly spoiled for him.","After all, he was Chen Yu, and Chen Yu was him.","Making him \"cooperate\" with Chen Yu would be like his left hand fighting his right; he’d be playing two different roles all by himself.","’Just thinking about it is exhausting.’","Xie Tingyun, seeing the two fall silent, began shooting meaningful looks at Chen Yi.","’Young Master-in-law, what’s the verdict on that matter?’","Chen Yi returned a confirming glance. It went without saying that the disciples of the Celestial Sect would be a huge help to Hundred Herbs Hall’s expansion for the time being.","Xie Tingyun’s face immediately lit up with joy. After shoveling down a couple of mouthfuls of rice, she stood up, clasped her fist, and said:","\"Young Miss, this old... I have a favor to ask of you.\"","Xiao Wan’er smiled and nodded. \"Tingyun, there’s no need to be so formal. Just speak your mind.\"","Then, under Shen Huatang’s stunned gaze, Xie Tingyun announced with a perfectly straight face:","\"Now that Elder Demon Jia of the Illusory Sound Sect is dead outside Cang Lang Town, Tingyun wishes to make a trip back to the Celestial Sect.\"","\"Firstly, to deliver Mid-Autumn Festival gifts to my master and the others. Secondly, I also want to bring some people down the mountain to gain worldly experience, as they mentioned in a recent letter.\"","\"After the Mid-Autumn Festival, Tingyun will return to Shu State to await your orders.\"","After listening, Xiao Wan’er naturally had no objections and asked, \"Are the gifts you have enough? Do you need the manor to add some more?\"","\"It’s more than enough. I bought quite a lot with Miss Pei earlier. On the way back, I’ll buy some wine, rouge, and other things for Master and Mistress as I see fit.\"","Xiao Wan’er nodded and said no more.","Chen Yi watched Xie Tingyun sit back down to eat, her face beaming with joy, and couldn’t help but marvel internally. ’Speak of the devil.’","He had been planning to have Wang Ji find a suitable place to practice his martial arts, precisely because he was worried about Xie Tingyun finding out.","’This is perfect.’","With Xie Tingyun going back to swin— ahem, to visit her fellow disciples from the Celestial Sect, he could have a few days of respite.","At that moment, Shen Huatang, seeing everyone eating with their heads down, couldn’t help but nudge Xie Tingyun and ask:","\"Senior Sister, how come I don’t know anything about people from the Sect wanting to come down the mountain for experience?\"","\"Oh, just Little Six and the others. They wrote me a letter specifically, ahem... saying their worldliness is lacking and they need more training.\"","Xie Tingyun dodged the question and said dismissively, \"I’m leaving for Tian Mountain tomorrow. Junior Sister, you must protect the Young Miss well.\"","\"You don’t have to tell me that.\"","Shen Huatang retorted, but her eyes remained fixed on her senior sister.","’I have a feeling she’s cooking up another harebrained scheme.’","Recalling the secretive looks exchanged between Xie Tingyun and Chen Yi earlier, Shen Huatang grew suspicious.","’Senior Sister and the second son-in-law...’","’One is unreliable, the other is even more so. The two of them together...’","’I hope I’m just overthinking this.’","After dinner, Chen Yi returned to Spring Lotus Garden to continue his Cultivation of the Four Symbols Skill.","Xiao Wan’er, on the other hand, took the booklet containing the charter for the Medical Dao Academy to Qingjing Residence.","She explained her intentions.","The Old Master pondered for a moment, then nodded and said, \"This is indeed a matter that would benefit the country and its people.\"","Xiao Wan’er’s face lit up. \"Grandfather, you agree?\"","\"It’s rare for you to have thought things out so thoroughly. Go ahead and do it.\"","\"I will certainly do my best.\"","Hearing this, the Old Master waved his hand. A small smile appeared on his aged face as he advised:","\"Take care of your health. Don’t overwork yourself.\"","Xiao Wan’er nodded and said with a smile, \"I’ll keep that in mind.\"","\"Thanks to Doctor Ma’s medicine, my health has improved a lot recently.\"","\"The one from Jishi Medicine Hall?\"","\"That’s him.\"","\"Speaking of which, we also have Boss Chen of Hundred Herbs Hall to thank. If not for his approval, a physician with Doctor Ma’s profound skills would never have come to our Medicine Hall.\"","At this point, Xiao Wan’er remembered something.","\"I heard that Boss Chen Yu is a Medical Saint Hand.\"","\"Doctor Ma must have studied under the same school of thought as Boss Chen. No wonder his Medical Skill is so remarkable.\"","When the Old Master heard this, his expression flickered slightly. He asked, \"A Medical Saint Hand?\"","Xiao Wan’er hummed in affirmation, then asked hesitantly, \"Grandfather, are you worried there’s a problem with Boss Chen’s identity?\"","The Old Master shook his head. \"There’s no problem with his identity, but...\"","\"But he is rather like a divine dragon that shows its head but never its tail, hehe.\"","Xiao Wan’er, not suspecting a thing, smiled and nodded. \"Boss Chen does indeed rarely show his face.\"","\"Originally, I wanted to invite Boss Chen to be the acting head of the Medical Dao Academy, but my husband told me that when Boss Chen came down the mountain, he made a great vow to travel the world and save the common people.\"","\"So he spends most of his time traveling and treating the sick.\"","Hearing this, a glint appeared in the Old Master’s cloudy eyes. \"Is that so.\"","\"It seems this old man should go and meet this Boss Chen someday.\"","\"If you’re interested, Grandfather, I can go ask later if Boss Chen is still in Shu State.\"","\"There’s no hurry...\"","After a bit more small talk, Xiao Wan’er saw that it was getting late and prepared to leave.","The Old Master stood up to see her off, not forgetting to remind her to rest more. Finally, he said:","\"Our family isn’t short on silver for the time being. Once you’ve chosen a location for the academy, Grandfather will give you the silver.\"","Of the 300,000 taels of silver obtained from Xiao Dongchen, after subtracting the 50,000 taken by Xiao Jinghong, the Old Master still had 250,000 taels on hand.","He wouldn’t feel the pinch of using a portion of it to build the Medical Dao Academy.","Xiao Wan’er pressed her lips together slightly and gave a slight bow. \"Thank you for your support, Grandfather.\"","\"It’s only right.\"","\"For all these years, we’ve relied on you to manage the household. For both public and private reasons, Grandfather ought to support you.\"","\"Besides, this is a great deed that could make the Xiao Family’s name go down in history. How could I let you bear the burden alone?\"","\"So, for the Medical Dao Academy, just go for it. Make it grand, and make it great.\""]},{"number":269,"title":"Chapter 269 - 208: A Light Boat, A Light Heart","paragraphs":["A warmth spread through Xiao Wan’er’s heart. \"I will remember.\"","The old master laughed heartily, offering a few more words of encouragement to put her at ease before watching her leave.","Once the room grew quiet, the old master’s expression turned serious. After a moment of thought, he asked in a low voice, \"Could he be the one who saved you?\"","Dressed in black, Xiao Jing emerged from the inner hall. He hesitated. \"I can’t say for sure.\"","\"But his attitude toward me and the Marquis’s Mansion, as well as his identity as a Medical Saint Hand, all match the description of the man from that night.\"","\"Then investigate more thoroughly.\"","\"A Medical Saint Hand has done so much for our Xiao Family. It is only right that I invite him for a personal meeting.\"","Xiao Jing nodded. \"I’ll have my men keep a close watch on Hundred Herbs Hall. As soon as there’s any news, I will go and confirm it myself.\"","The old master said no more. Leaning on his cane, he returned to his seat in the main hall and asked,","\"What is the situation with the Liu Family?\"","\"After meeting with you, Liu Hong has remained at the Governor’s Office.\"","\"Liu Yu, who left last night, returned to the city this afternoon. Reports say he will take Liu Wen’s body back to Jing State tomorrow.\"","Xiao Jing glanced up at the old master and continued, \"Also, it seems that Liu Zhaoxue has no intention of leaving.\"","\"Oh? Her second brother is dead. As a direct descendant of the main branch, isn’t she going back to mourn?\"","\"I have not yet determined the reason.\"","\"But according to reports from my men, Liu Zhaoxue was looking for a suitable storefront today. It appears she still plans to expand Xinglin Hall in Shu State.\"","The old master grunted in acknowledgment and considered this. \"Never mind her. Keep a close watch on Liu Hong.\"","\"This time, I used Liu Wen’s death to force the Liu Family to cough up silver coins and other benefits worth several times the value of the summer grain lost at Iron Wall Town.\"","\"Furthermore, both Liu Wen and Liu Jing from their main branch died here in Shu State.\"","The old master paused, a grim light flashing in his cloudy eyes. He snorted coldly.","\"They won’t let this go so easily!\"","...","The next day, the dark clouds over Shu State had dissipated somewhat. Though the sky was still gray, it wasn’t as gloomy, and the rain had dwindled to a light drizzle.","Fresh air permeated Shu State.","Travelers no longer gathered in huddled groups, whispering about the previous day’s events. Merchants went about their business as usual.","The City Guard Army, government officials, and the Imprisonment Department, however, were busier than ever.","This was especially true in West City.","Since Xiao Jinghong and his men had taken down many from the Evil Demonic Dao, government officials who normally wouldn’t dare set foot there now patrolled the streets and alleys, rounding up the remaining criminals.","Naturally, some conflicts broke out during the process.","But with the support of the Imprisonment Officers and the City Guard Army, the remaining riffraff couldn’t cause any significant trouble.","In just half a day, dozens of people were apprehended here and there.","The watching commoners cheered, bringing prestige to the Imprisonment Department and other government offices. The scene was one of bustling excitement.","But after a day for the news to circulate, the excitement was bound to die down.","Especially once the details about the summer grain being burned in the three border towns reached the Prefecture City, everyone in Shu State, from the highest officials to the common folk, learned the full story.","First, some of the summer grain in Iron Wall Town had been burned.","The exact amount was not made public, however, leading to widespread speculation.","Some said one hundred thousand shi, others said two hundred thousand, and some even claimed a million...","This last claim about a million shi of grain being burned was quickly debunked.","The second piece of news concerned the culprits who set fire to the grain—they were all members of the Evil Demonic Dao from the Bright Moon Building.","The fact that Liu Wen, Xiao Dongchen, and others were pulling the strings from behind was not circulated at all.","Even the Financier behind Bright Moon Building was rumored to be taking orders from the Barbarian Race.","For the most part, this provided the most plausible explanation for the whole fiasco.","The final piece of news was about Xiao Jinghong—the Grand General of Shu State was now a Martial Arts Powerhouse of the Upper Three Grades.","His Sword Dao had reached the Realm of Perfection, allowing him to sweep a thousand feet with a single sword strike and effortlessly slay enemy generals.","This news, of course, thrilled those who loved a good story.","\"It seems the Barbarian Race suffered heavy losses when they were repelled five years ago.\"","\"Otherwise, they wouldn’t be resorting to such dirty tricks to cause trouble for the Dingyuan Army.\"","\"I hear the Barbarian Race is in the midst of internal turmoil. The Old Barbarian King is gravely ill, and the Eldest Prince and Third Prince are fighting for the throne. It will be difficult for them to march north anytime soon.\"","\"Under these circumstances, how would they dare to plot the burning of the summer grain in the Three Towns?\"","\"They must be worried our Great Wei army will take advantage of their internal conflict and march south.\"","\"That makes sense...\"","It was mostly scholars who paid attention to current affairs, and they could always piece together fragmented clues to deduce seemingly plausible, if not entirely accurate, conclusions.","For example, news of the Barbarian Race’s internal strife came from the horse bandits of Poshisu Country.","The story about the burning of the Three Towns was spread by the Xiao Family and the government offices.","Some of it was true and some was false, yet they spoke with such convincing detail.","It only made those who knew the truth scoff in derision.","However, as the dust settled on the incident with the burning of the Three Towns’ summer grain, a piece of news from Guiyun Academy completely shifted the public’s focus.","\"The Xiao Family’s live-in son-in-law, Chen Yi, also known as Chen Qingzhou, has achieved Perfection in the Calligraphy Dao! What’s more, it’s a new style of script he created, called—Cursive Script!\"","\"Mr. Yue Ming says the ’Cursive’ part of the name implies the fluidity of flowing clouds and running water, a sense of exquisite Pen Technique, a lively spirit, and a natural composition.\"","\"The Cursive Script written by Chen Qingzhou evokes a myriad of images, its dashing and unrestrained strokes stretching for a thousand miles.\"","\"Mr. Yue Ming also said that after the Mid-Autumn Festival, Guiyun Academy will exhibit some of Mr. Qingzhou’s work, including the very piece that achieved the Perfection Realm of Cursive Script, ’Post-rain Reflections’.\"","Some believed it, others did not.","But Shu State Prefecture City was only so large, and respected Confucian scholars like Mr. Yue Ming and Mr. Zhuo Ying were established men with families. It wasn’t hard for someone to find a connection to them and confirm the truth of the news.","\"Is... is it true?\"","\"Could it be fake?\"","\"I heard that when Mr. Qingzhou delivered the calligraphy this afternoon, there were people visiting from Yuelu Academy in Yan State.\"","\"Apparently, one of the young men there was quite scornful of Mr. Qingzhou’s Calligraphy Dao. But when he saw ’Post-rain Reflections,’ he was filled with regret and wanted to ask Mr. Qingzhou to be his master and teach him the Calligraphy Dao.\""]},{"number":270,"title":"Chapter 270 - 208: The Lightness of the Boat is the Lightness of the Heart","paragraphs":["\"Too bad it’s too late.\"","\"Don’t be fooled by Mr. Qingzhou’s youth. He has the character of a true scholar. He would never accept a student as ill-mannered as that.\"","\"Rightly so.\"","Meanwhile, the scholars on Kangning Street used their convenient proximity to not only find out the details of the exhibition but also learn the verses of \"Post-rain Reflections.\"","\"Leaving Bai Di at dawn through morning clouds, a thousand miles to Jiangling in a single day.\"","\"The monkeys’ cries on either bank are endless, as my light boat has already passed ten thousand peaks.\"","When the four lines of this peerless poem were revealed, the scholars on Kangning Street fell deathly silent.","It wasn’t so bad for the scholars who weren’t skilled in poetry.","The true poetry connoisseurs, the more they savored this work, the more they had to admit their own inferiority.","\"Mr. Qingzhou’s ’Leaving Bai Di at dawn through morning clouds’ is a masterful line beyond the reach of mere mortals. I am in complete admiration.\"","\"A line like ’Leaving Bai Di at dawn through morning clouds’—isn’t it just like soaring through the air, riding the wind?\"","\"There’s more! The phrasing ’endless’ and ’already passed’ in the final couplet is simply sublime, perfectly expressing the boat’s incredible speed.\"","\"And as for the word ’Qingzhou’...\"","Being scholars, they exchanged knowing smiles and offered an interpretation:","\"It not only means ’a light boat signifies a light heart,’ but it also reveals the master’s own name. The word ’Qingzhou’ is the masterstroke that brings it all to life.\"","Compared to his previous few poems, this time Chen Yi’s \"Post-rain Reflections\" attracted even more attention because of his Perfection Realm Calligraphy Dao.","Some who were already students of Guiyun Academy even sought out Mr. Yue Ming and the others to see the calligraphy piece with their own eyes.","For a time, very few people on Kangning Street paid any more attention to matters like the Three Towns’ summer grain or the instigation by the Barbarian Race.","This situation was obviously a welcome development for the Xiao and Liu Families.","For a few select individuals, however, it was a more complicated matter.","On Kangning Street, inside the shop extremely close to Guiyun Academy.","Lou Yuxue directed two Iron Banner Officers disguised as shop assistants to set up the shop, all while keeping an eye on the surrounding activity.","She had, of course, heard the scholars’ discussions and seen the crowds flowing in and out of Guiyun Academy’s entrance.","She felt a bit conflicted.","’What is this? A complete windfall?’","Before Hawk Ge the Third left, he had given instructions to probe the Fledgling’s Calligraphy Dao Realm.","Before Lou Yuxue even had a chance to act, the Fledgling’s mastery of the Calligraphy Dao was already common knowledge.","’The Calligraphy Dao at the Perfection Realm.’","’That Fledgling has only been in Shu State for three months, and his Calligraphy Dao has advanced again and again. It’s truly...’","’That Hawk is so damn lucky.’","Lou Yuxue roughly knew Ge the Third’s mission, which was why she was somewhat envious.","After all, the advancement in the Calligraphy Dao was due to the Fledgling’s own talent and had nothing to do with Ge the Third.","But the result and the sensation it caused would all be credited to Ge the Third.","She reckoned that not only would he not be punished, but he might even receive a reward from the Lord Golden Banner Officer.","’Fortunately, with the summer grain in Iron Wall Town being burned this time, even if the Pavilion Master is displeased, he probably won’t punish us.’","’It’s just that the outcome of the negotiations between the Xiao and Liu Families is somewhat unsatisfactory.’","Lou Yuxue knew that the mere fact that news of Liu Wen appearing in Iron Wall Town hadn’t spread was enough to show that the Xiao and Liu Families had successfully made peace.","If those two great families’ talks had collapsed,","Liu Wen, Xiao Dongchen, and even that \"Financier\" would all have been exposed by the Xiao and Liu Families.","The situation in Shu State City would then become several times more chaotic than it was now.","Thinking about these things, Lou Yuxue instructed the people in the shop to continue with their preparations and went alone deep into the inner hall to find a copy of the play \"Mandarin Duck Tower Record.\"","After a moment of thought, she took a small piece of paper and, referencing the \"Mandarin Duck Tower Record\" script, wrote a secret letter.","She not only wrote about the full story behind the burning of the Three Towns’ summer grain and the man named Liu Wu, but also included details on the Xiao and Liu Families, the current situation in Shu State, and the Fledgling’s Calligraphy Dao.","All in all, there were over a dozen pieces of information.","After finishing, Lou Yuxue confirmed there were no mistakes, tucked the slip of paper into a message tube on a falcon’s leg, and released it.","She watched the falcon fly far into the distance before turning to go downstairs.","’The Mid-Autumn Festival is approaching, and Xiao Jinghong will be returning to the Prefecture City for a temporary stay. I’m afraid it will be difficult for me to make any moves in the short term.’","’And then there’s the matter of Bright Moon Building...’","The falcon, with the white feathers on its head, obviously paid no mind to these mortal thoughts.","It took four hours to deliver Lou Yuxue’s secret letter to Guangyuan County, in the northernmost part of Shu State.","After a brief stop, it headed straight for the Capital Prefecture.","「Two days later.」","The white-headed falcon landed on the roof of the Fengyue Building, south of the Capital Prefecture’s Imperial City.","A member of the White Tiger Guard, dressed in a black robe and wearing a plain white mask, hurried over and removed the message tube from the falcon’s leg.","The message was deciphered and confirmed to be correct.","Then, a member of the White Tiger Guard in a red robe and white mask carried the letter with swift, silent steps to the deepest part of the third floor and knocked lightly twice on the wooden door.","\"Pavilion Master, a letter from Shu State.\""]},{"number":271,"title":"Chapter 271 - 209: Parting the Clouds to See the Blue Sky","paragraphs":["Thousands of miles away in Shu State, the sky was overcast, and a light rain drizzled down.","But here in the north, above the Capital Prefecture, the sky was clear for a thousand miles.","At noon, sometime after the Beginning of Autumn, the bright sun blazed down, making the two-hundred-year-old Wind and Rain Pavilion south of the Imperial City shine as if it were brand new.","Shafts of hazy light streamed through the glazed, latticed windows.","It bathed the spacious room deep on the third floor in a brilliant golden sheen.","A man wearing a white tiger pattern mask stood before a long table, holding a thick-tipped White Jade Wolf Hair Brush.","He dipped it in Hui Ink, then flourished it across the soft Smoke Water Paper, writing the three words: \"Post-rain Reflections.\"","Following that were four lines of a poem: \"At dawn, I leave Bai Di, draped in vibrant clouds; a thousand miles to Jiangling, I’ll return in a day.\"","\"The cries of monkeys on both banks are endless, yet my light boat has passed ten thousand mountains.\"","This was none other than \"Post-rain Reflections,\" written by Chen Yi.","However, Chen Yi had written it in Cursive Script, his every stroke exuding an unrestrained elegance.","But the man in the white tiger pattern mask wrote in Wei Qing’s Style.","Each stroke—every horizontal and vertical line—was rugged and bold.","Even with its smooth, flowing execution, the style didn’t match the Mental Realm evoked by the poem—one of \"crossing ten thousand mountains to find the light.\"","Thus, after he finished writing, the man in the white tiger pattern mask stared at the Mental Realm materializing above the Smoke Water Paper, silent for a long time.","Even the red-robed White Tiger Guard kneeling before him had a strange look in his eyes.","’The Pavilion Master... he’s also reached Perfect Calligraphy Dao?!’","Before he could dwell on it, the \"Pavilion Master\" he was thinking of asked, \"How did the secret report describe that ’Post-rain Reflections’?\"","He bowed his head and replied, \"Effortless and free, as if riding the wind.\"","The Pavilion Master nodded slightly, dropped the White Jade Wolf Hair Brush, and stared at the Mental Realm materializing before him—","A vast range of towering mountains, majestic and lofty, rose thousands of feet above the white clouds.","A city stood in the clouds, spanning the peaks of two mountains.","Within it were magnificent palaces, massive walls, and thousands of soldiers in Heavy Armor standing guard, along with heavy crossbows and other weapons that radiated a chilling aura.","Below the mountains, the \"boat\" could no longer be described as a \"light boat\"; it was a fleet of warships.","They were organized in formations, vast and mighty.","And he himself, dressed as a \"General\" in a white robe over Silver Armor, with a white tiger pattern mask on his face, stood at the prow.","With a raise of his hand, the warships raced along the river winding through the mountains.","They smashed through mountains and slaughtered any enemies in their path, crossing thousands of miles in an instant.","Finally, a dense forest of banners was planted in a land bathed in sunlight.","The White Robed Pavilion Master looked at the scene and chuckled inexplicably. \"My light boat has passed ten thousand mountains... Not bad.\"","The White Robed Pavilion Master offered this calm praise, then his ice-cold eyes fell upon the red-robed White Tiger Guard before him.","\"Ji Qing, what is your take on this line?\"","The red-robed White Tiger Guard, Ji Qing, thought for a moment before answering, \"This line of poetry has a feeling of ’breaking through the dark clouds to see the light again.’\"","\"This subordinate believes that the Fledgling has become much more open-minded than before.\"","The White Robed Pavilion Master said faintly, \"It seems he has seen a sliver of hope... Not bad.\"","Ji Qing’s body trembled slightly. This was the second \"not bad\" he had heard from the Pavilion Master.","As the one who had followed the \"Pavilion Master\" the longest, he understood—the Pavilion Master was truly furious.","With that thought, Ji Qing said cautiously, \"Perhaps it is because he achieved Perfect Calligraphy Dao?\"","The White Robed Pavilion Master’s tone was noncommittal. \"Perfect Calligraphy Dao would allow him to make a name for himself throughout the Nine State and Three Prefectures. It certainly has the power to ’part the clouds and see the blue sky.’\"","Then his tone shifted. \"However, I don’t believe that’s the case.\"","\"The two words ’light boat’ might be a pun on his name, but looking at everything that has happened in Shu State recently, doesn’t it also apply to the Xiao Family?\"","Ji Qing froze, raising his head slightly to glance at his master. He hesitated. \"Pavilion Master, are you saying the Fledgling knew in advance that someone was going to burn the summer grain in the Three Towns?\"","\"But according to Hawk, the Fledgling has been living in seclusion.\"","\"Aside from occasionally visiting Guiyun Academy to teach Calligraphy Dao, the few times he went out were on behalf of Xiao Wan’er to discuss the expansion of the Hundred Herbs Hall.\"","\"How could he have learned about Bright Moon Building, the Liu Family, and Gray Wolf moving against the Xiao Family?\"","\"And how could he have possibly predicted that the Xiao Family would be able to turn the crisis into an opportunity?\"","\"Unless...\"","Before he could finish, the White Robed Pavilion Master raised a hand slightly, cutting him off. \"I want the whole story, not speculation and inference.\"","\"Forgive me, Pavilion Master. This subordinate will immediately send orders to Lady Tiger and have her investigate the Fledgling thoroughly.\"","The white-robed figure glanced at him and reminded him in a cold tone, \"Ask where the Fledgling was on the night the Three Towns were attacked.\"","Ji Qing quickly bowed his head in acknowledgment.","Just as he was about to rise and leave, he heard the White Robed Pavilion Master continue his instructions:","\"Relay my orders to the General. Tell him I approve his plan. Have him start as soon as possible.\"","\"Also, as for Simurgh Phoenix, if she wants to stay in Shu State, then let her stay there.\"","\"As for the Jing State Liu Family... internal strife has already erupted. They are bringing about their own destruction. Pay them no mind.\"","Just then, two knocks came from the door. The white-robed figure paused. \"What is it?\"","\"Reporting to the Pavilion Master, a message has come from the palace. The Holy Emperor commands your immediate presence.\"","\"Prepare the sedan chair.\"","\"Yes, sir.\"","After the person outside had left, the white-robed figure looked at Ji Qing, who was still kneeling, and waved a hand.","\"Go and rewrite the secret report on Liu Wen’s death. I need to take it to the palace for my audience with the Holy Emperor.\"","\"Remember, state clearly that the Jing State Liu Family is suspected of treason. And that the Xiao Family knowingly concealed this information, harboring malicious intent.\"","Ji Qing froze upon hearing this, then pressed his forehead to the floor. \"This subordinate obeys!\"","Then, he rose, took a few steps back, and turned to leave.","After a moment of silence, the White Robed Pavilion Master glanced at the illusory image floating above the table, a thoughtful look appearing in his cold, indifferent eyes.","\"Qingzhou has grown.\"","\"A pity. A scholar can play with his brush for a lifetime, but in the end, he is still just an ant.\"","As he spoke, the White Robed Pavilion Master gently picked up the sheet of Smoke Water Paper, from which the magnificent Mental Realm had manifested."]},{"number":272,"title":"Chapter 272 - 209: Parting the Clouds to See the Blue Sky","paragraphs":["He flicked it twice.","The delicate paper instantly disintegrated into shreds, drifting out the window.","The White Robed Pavilion Master watched the paper shreds drift away and disappear, a cold glint flashing in his eyes.","Immediately, he flicked his sleeve.","His figure vanished abruptly, transforming into a phantasmal white shadow that shot into the red-walled, heavily fortified Imperial City to the north.","Faintly, a low, suppressed voice echoed in the empty, silent room:","\"Obsessed with spurning fame and fortune, how can one ever grow into a great roc that blots out the sky?\"","...","「Thousands of miles away.」","Shu State.","The rain, which had fallen for three straight days, finally stopped as the Mid-Autumn Festival approached.","Although the sky remained overcast, the sun was now visible behind the clouds.","Its furnace-like heat caused the temperature throughout the cloud-covered lands of Shu State to steadily climb.","Muggy.","It was far from pleasant.","Chen Yi, of course, felt none of it, but in front of Xiaodie and the others, he had to put on a show of being drenched in sweat.","Fortunately, he was long accustomed to such concealment.","He could fake these common physical reactions with nonchalant ease.","After lunch, he had Xiaodie prepare iced tea, then sat by the pond to fish with Xiao Wuge.","The three of them chatted idly while sipping the cool, refreshing tea.","For the most part, it was Xiaodie who did the talking, with Chen Yi occasionally chiming in with a word or two.","Xiao Wuge, on the other hand, said nothing at all, only cheering out every now and then, \"Brother-in-law, a fish is on the hook!\"","\"Brother-in-law, a big one’s coming up.\"","\"Brother-in-law, look! I’ve avenged you! This is the fish that splashed water all over you...\"","’As if I needed him to avenge me.’","Chen Yi grumbled internally, his thoughts a stream of bitter complaints typical of a fisherman who’d caught nothing.","So whenever this happened, he would just grunt an \"mhm,\" giving Xiao Wuge a noncommittal response.","Then he would pretend to ask Xiaodie, \"Has anything interesting been happening in Shu State Prefecture City lately?\"","Or, \"With the Mid-Autumn Festival approaching, which of the East and West Markets is livelier?\" and so on.","Xiaodie seemed to know a little about everything and would reply with a few sentences about some trivial matters.","\"Young Master, the most bustling place in the city recently is still Kangning Street.\"","\"Ever since your ’Post-rain Reflections’ became known, scholars have been flocking to Guiyun Academy to see it.\"","As Xiaodie spoke of this, her face broke into a wide, beaming smile.","\"I heard that Mr. Yue Ming specially hired several Guards to stand at the entrance, afraid that people might try to force their way in.\"","\"Even so, there are still many scholars with official ranks who are trying all sorts of ways to get into the academy.\"","\"It forced Mr. Yue Ming’s hand. This morning, he posted a notice saying that the exhibition hall will be open tomorrow.\"","\"However, if someone wants to view your prized calligraphy, they still need to submit a visiting card in advance. Otherwise, they can only see the piece that demonstrates Great Success in Calligraphy Dao.\"","Chen Yi just hummed, showing a lack of interest.","As he had expected, the Cursive Script calligraphy at the Perfection level of the Calligraphy Dao had indeed attracted a great number of visitors.","But what he hadn’t expected was that the number of people coming to visit the Xiao Family hadn’t decreased; on the contrary, it was trending upward.","Among them were regulars like Madam Tang of the Tang Family and Miss Wan of the Wan Family, as well as some new guests who had come after hearing the news.","Most of them wanted to pull strings and use connections, trying to see if they could become a disciple of his, Mr. Qingzhou.","On top of that, because of the incident a while back where the summer grain in Iron Wall Town was burned, many people were also coming to visit the Old Master.","The two groups of visitors combined kept the Xiao Family’s gatekeepers busy from morning till night.","The Old Master, left with no choice, first ordered that he would only see one person per day, and later simply claimed to be ill and refused all visitors.","But Xiao Wan’er wasn’t so decisive.","She was a soft-hearted person by nature, always trying to be considerate of everyone.","Therefore, she accepted most of the visiting cards handed to her, and for those she truly couldn’t turn away, she would chat and laugh with them for a bit.","From morning to night, her Jiaxing Garden was almost never empty.","Never mind Chen Yi, who wouldn’t join the hustle and bustle; even Xiao Wuge, who was supposed to be having lessons with his tutor, got two days off.","’Why bother?’","’It would be so much better to just refuse them all, like I do.’","Chen Yi had his thoughts, but he also knew that this was just Xiao Wan’er’s nature; no outsider could persuade her otherwise.","A-side, Xiaodie noticed his lack of interest and changed the subject.","\"Also, because of your ’Post-rain Reflections,’ many young scholars have recently been boasting that they’re going to overshadow you at the Mid-Autumn poetry gathering.\"","\"Overshadow me? Great! The sooner, the better. They should go ahead and crush this Young Master of yours right into the dirt.\"","Seeing Chen Yi’s nonchalant attitude, Xiaodie said seriously, \"Young Master, they won’t be able to do it.\"","\"Why not?\"","\"Because they’re simply not talented enough, of course!\"","\"...Xiaodie, who taught you how to flatter people like that?\"","\"Sister Hua and the others from the central courtyard.\"","\"Sister Hua and the others said that we servants need to have sweet mouths. That’s the only way to win the favor of the masters, madams, and young misses.\"","Chen Yi turned his head and shot her a glare. \"Stop learning such nonsense. I don’t fall for that stuff.\"","Xiaodie stuck out her tongue, replied with a smiling \"I understand,\" and then began to talk about the grand celebrations of past Mid-Autumn Festivals.","From the bustling little shows in the East Market, the grand operas in the West Market, and the competing poetry gatherings on Kangning Street, to the courtesans vying for supremacy in South City’s Yanhua Lane.","All in all, one could get a sense of the liveliness of Shu State City.","\"Young Master, where would you like to go for a stroll?\"","\"Me? Anywhere is fine.\"","’And nowhere is fine, either.’","Chen Yi would much rather stay in Spring Lotus Garden and sleep in.","But he also knew that during the Mid-Autumn Festival, there would be no shortage of pomp and ceremony in the Marquis’s Mansion.","Ancestor worship, welcoming guests, hosting banquets, and so on.","If Xiao Jinghong didn’t come back, he might actually get some peace and quiet.","But if Xiao Jinghong did return, he would have to accompany him to social engagements or go deliver festival gifts to some of the elders.","Such were the social obligations that came with marriage.","Hearing this, Xiaodie paused. She naturally didn’t dare to casually offer a suggestion. ’How could a mere Maid presume to make decisions for her master?’"]},{"number":273,"title":"Chapter 273 - 209: Dispelling the Clouds to See the Sky","paragraphs":["So she said haltingly, \"I hear that for the Mid-Autumn Festival this year, North City is going to be even more lively.\"","\"There are lantern riddles, couplet contests, and... and you can float flower lanterns on the Quchi River to make a wish...\"","Chen Yi understood what she was getting at and teased with a smile, \"Do you want to go?\"","Xiaodie nodded eagerly, then immediately shook her head vigorously, the two buns of her hair wobbling back and forth.","\"Young Master, you decide. I’ll do whatever you say.\"","\"Whatever I say? In that case, we’re not going anywhere.\"","\"Ah...\"","\"Just kidding, haha.\"","\"We’ll wait for the Mistress to return and ask her where she wants to go. Or, if she doesn’t come back, we’ll see if the Eldest Miss wants to go float lanterns.\"","The disappointment on Xiaodie’s face vanished in a flash, replaced by delight. She said she would go find Juan’er and Cui’er later to ask around.","Chen Yi, for his part, didn’t say anything more.","’Thinking about it, I’ve been here for so long, but I’ve never really had a good look around.’","’Let alone gone out just for fun.’","’Most of the time, I only leave the house on business, so my mood is never that relaxed.’","’If the opportunity is right, I wouldn’t mind going out to have some fun.’","After a bit of idle chat, Chen Yi tossed aside his empty fishing rod and prepared to return to his room to rest.","Just then, Wang Lixing walked in from outside the garden, bowed, and said, \"Second Young Master-in-law, there are people at the gate asking to see you.\"","Chen Yi paused, surprised. \"Who is it?\"","\"Assistant Governor of the Governor’s Office Chen Yunfan, and Advisor Li Huai’gu. They say they have urgent business to discuss with you.\"","\"...The two of them?\"","If it were only Li Huai’gu, Chen Yi might have believed it.","But with Chen Yunfan added to the mix, he didn’t believe for a second that those two could have any \"urgent business.\"","\"Show them in.\"","As he spoke, Chen Yi instructed Xiaodie to take Xiao Wuge back to his room for a nap while he himself started boiling water to brew tea.","「Not long after.」","Chen Yunfan and Li Huai’gu arrived together, both dressed in casual clothes.","Spotting Chen Yi’s figure from a distance, Chen Yunfan bowed with a smile on his face.","\"This humble junior, Chen Yunfan, greets Mr. Qingzhou.\"","Li Huai’gu paused, hesitating whether he should follow suit, when he heard Chen Yi, who was standing outside the pavilion, laugh and retort good-naturedly:","\"Brother, you didn’t come here just to make things awkward for me, did you?\"","Chen Yunfan winked, then straightened up and pulled the dazed Li Huai’gu forward.","\"These past couple of days, your great name has spread throughout Shu State. It puts your brother to shame.\"","\"It can’t compare to your title as the number one scholar, Brother.\"","\"Not at all, not at all. This brother of yours got his title by a fluke. Barely scraped by as number one in this year’s exams...\"","Watching the familiar way the two \"brothers\" interacted, how could Li Huai’gu not understand that Chen Yunfan had been joking earlier?","He couldn’t help but relax as well. \"If Brother Yunfan became number one by a fluke, then my own third-place title must have been improperly obtained.\"","Chen Yunfan glanced sideways at him and feigned surprise. \"Oh? So Brother Huai’gu previously thought he had genuine talent?\"","\"...I did not.\"","Seeing the honest Li Huai’gu rendered speechless by a single sentence, Chen Yi shook his head. \"My brother is always joking.\"","With that, he invited the two to sit down.","As they drank tea, he asked them the purpose of their visit.","\"Is the Governor’s Office so idle today that they let you both leave at the same time?\"","Chen Yunfan took a sip of his tea and grimaced. \"Those two old codgers are naturally not that kind.\"","\"Then you...\"","\"I snuck out.\"","Chen Yi couldn’t help but laugh. ’That really is something Chen Yunfan would do,’ he thought.","Then he looked at Li Huai’gu. \"Brother Huai’gu?\"","Li Huai’gu shook his head. \"I just got back to Shu State last night. This morning, I went to the Office to report the situation to Lord Yang and was granted leave to rest.\"","He couldn’t approve of Chen Yunfan’s cavalier attitude toward the Governor’s Office.","But since the two of them worked in the same Government Office and saw each other all the time, he couldn’t very well say much.","Chen Yi, however, was blunt. \"Brother, you should learn from Brother Huai’gu.\"","Chen Yunfan glanced at Li Huai’gu and said, \"It’s too tiring to be like him. I can’t do it.\"","\"Brother Yunfan, you...\"","\"Am I wrong? You took on a hot potato like the summer grain tax for the Three Towns. Isn’t that exhausting for both body and mind?\"","Li Huai’gu was powerless to refute it. \"Well, it is a little.\"","Then his gaze fell on Chen Yi, and he said with a hint of gratitude, \"But thanks to Brother Qingzhou’s advice, I managed to escape a disaster.\"","Chen Yunfan was taken aback. He also looked at Chen Yi and asked, \"The fact that he dawdled for over ten days without reaching Iron Wall Town—was that your idea?\"","Chen Yi was about to nod, but then it hit him. \"Over ten days and he still hadn’t reached Iron Wall Town?\"","That speed was indeed beyond his expectations.","After all, that night when he had led a band of the Evil Demonic Dao to Iron Wall Town, they had spurred their horses on and it had only taken them four hours.","For such a short distance, Li Huai’gu had actually taken more than ten days and still hadn’t arrived...","Tsk, tsk. This man was a bit too straightforward.","Facing their strange looks, Li Huai’gu gave a wry smile. \"Lord Liu sent a letter every three days.\"","\"One time he said the tax was one-tenth, the next it was two-tenths. Then he said to leave nothing behind, until the most recent letter said it was all waived.\"","\"It was honestly making my head spin, so I simply slowed my journey...\"","Hearing this, before Chen Yi could say anything, Chen Yunfan at his side was already cursing, \"He’s obviously just bullying an honest man.\"","\"That Liu Hong is so shameless! Even policies that change overnight aren’t as fast as him.\"","\"Brother Yunfan, watch your words.\"","\"What’s there to be afraid of? There are no outsiders here.\"","Chen Yunfan looked at Chen Yi. \"Right, Brother Yi?\"","Chen Yi said with a half-smile, \"Brother, if you’re so dissatisfied with the Governor’s Office, why don’t you just toss away your Official Seal?\"","\"I’ve actually had that thought...\"","After a few more jokes and laughs, Chen Yunfan couldn’t help but have some thoughts bubble up.","’I originally thought Li Huai’gu was dragging his feet because Mr. Yue Ming gave him a tip. I never expected it was Chen Yi’s idea.’","’But that was more than half a month ago.’","’Tsk, Brother Yi is still Brother Yi, after all.’","’Even without leaving his home, he could deduce from a few clues that the Liu Family would back down.’","’But apparently, he didn’t expect that all my previous reminders were a waste of breath...’"]},{"number":274,"title":"Chapter 274 - 209: Parting the Clouds to See the Blue Sky","paragraphs":["An hour passed quickly.","Though their conversation was mostly just idle chatter, the atmosphere had become even more congenial.","Seeing it was getting late, Chen Yunfan and Li Huai’gu finally stated the purpose of their visit.","Chen Yunfan placed a calling card on the table and said in all seriousness, \"The Mid-Autumn Festival is a time for family reunions.\"","\"But alas, I don’t have a single relative in all of Shu State. Only you, Brother Yi, can I call family, so...\"","Before he could finish, Chen Yi, already guessing what was coming, cut him off irritably. \"Don’t even start.\"","\"I’m just a live-in son-in-law. When do I ever get to make the decisions?\"","Chen Yunfan chuckled. \"You don’t have to make the decision. Wherever you go, I’ll go.\"","\"Oh, right. If General Jinghong is there too, Cui Qingwu can keep her company.\"","’I knew it,’ Chen Yi thought. Just as he was about to refuse, he saw Li Huai’gu also take out an invitation and say with a sheepish laugh:","\"It’s for the Guiyun Academy’s Mid-Autumn Poetry Gathering. My teacher asked me to deliver an invitation to you.\"","\"...I already turned the Headmaster down the day before yesterday.\"","\"Why would you refuse?\"","Chen Yunfan took the invitation for himself, opened it, and glanced inside. His interest was immediately piqued.","\"Brother Huai’gu, I imagine quite a few people will be attending this gathering, right?\"","Li Huai’gu nodded. \"My teacher said that some people who are visiting the academy will also be participating.\"","\"Such as Mr. Zhangping from Yuelu Academy, Mr. Zi Qian from Jinling Academy, and others.\"","But Chen Yunfan just shook his head. \"I was talking about the courtesans.\"","\"That... I wouldn’t know.\"","\"It’s a poetry gathering! Of course there will be courtesans singing and dancing.\"","\"Brother Yi, care to join?\"","Chen Yi shot him an irritated glare. \"Not interested.\"","Disappointment flashed across Chen Yunfan’s face. He smacked his lips and muttered, \"Wherever you go, I go.\"","And vice-versa.","He had made up his mind to bring Cui Qingwu along and spend the Mid-Autumn Festival with Chen Yi.","Li Huai’gu looked between the two, then said hesitantly, \"Brother Qingzhou, if you have the time, you really should go. This poetry gathering will truly be an unprecedented event.\"","Chen Yunfan froze. Forgetting his disappointment, he looked at Chen Yi and said with a serious expression, \"Go!\"","Seeing Chen Yi remained unmoved, his expression hardened. \"I might just have to pay a visit to the Old Marquis later.\"","Seeing how insistent they both were, Chen Yi could only relent. \"I’ll go to the academy tomorrow and ask Mr. Yue Ming before I decide.\"","’This ’brother’ of his was not only unlike an Imperial Top Scholar, he was hardly a respectable person at all.’","’His behavior was completely at odds with his status as a scholar and the legitimate heir of the main branch of the Jiangnan Prefecture Chen Family.’","Chen Yunfan, of course, paid no mind to Chen Yi’s thoughts. Seeing that he had relented, he said with a grin, \"When the time comes, I’ll let you witness my poetic talent.\"","\"You?\"","\"Poetic talent?\"","\"I spent ten years in arduous study of the classics. While I might not be able to just dash off a poem for the occasion, I can certainly still compose one on the spot.\"","\"...\"","After some more idle chatter, Chen Yi finally saw the two of them out.","Only after they were a good distance away did a wry smile appear on his face.","’Now, it seemed he had no choice but to go out and join the festivities for the Mid-Autumn Festival.’","’He just wondered if Xiao Jinghong would be able to make it back in time.’","...","「Wu Mountain Mutual Market.」","Xiao Jinghong returned discreetly, silently swapping places with Su Zhenyue without alerting the busy members of the Mountain Race and the Servants in the Mutual Market.","Although news of the raid on the Three Towns’ summer grain had spread throughout Shu State, here in the isolated Wu Mountain Mutual Market, no one knew a thing.","Xiao Jinghong certainly wasn’t about to be the one to spread it around.","After changing into a long white dress, she scanned the area and asked, \"Where’s Pei Guanli?\"","Su Zhenyue looked chagrined and said helplessly, \"She went back to the Mountain Race with her older brother.\"","Xiao Jinghong frowned slightly, but she didn’t blame her. She said coolly,","\"The more effort she puts into hiding, the more questionable the identity of my informant becomes.\"","\"The ’Blade Madman’ Liu Lang is indeed loyal and honorable, and he would certainly repay me for sparing his life, but there’s no way he has any connection to the Mountain Race.\"","Su Zhenyue nodded at her words, then asked hesitantly, \"Should I... go to the Mountain Race and drag her back?\"","\"It would be useless for you to go. Granny Shan won’t be persuaded. I’ll go myself.\"","\"You’re going in person? But the Mid-Autumn Festival is almost here. Aren’t you returning home?\"","Beneath her half-armor mask, Xiao Jinghong’s lips pressed into a thin line. She said,","\"This raid on the Three Towns’ summer grain has made me understand something: Grandfather doesn’t want me to stay at the residence.\"","\"But—but why? How could the Old Marquis...\"","\"’To prevent trouble before it starts, I suppose.’\"","Xiao Jinghong didn’t elaborate. Instead, she gave a quiet order, \"After I leave for the Mountain Race, I want you to write a letter to my husband for me.\"","\"Tell him to have that poetry mounted as soon as possible and hang it in my room.\"","Su Zhenyue’s mouth fell open. She hesitated. \"My lady, my handwriting is different from yours. If the Young Master sees it, I’m afraid it won’t be right.\"","\"He’ll understand.\"","As she spoke, her gaze, limpid as water, turned toward Shu State Prefecture City, and it was as if the figure of a scholar materialized before her.","「In a trance.」","The figure approached, smiling, and asked, \"Wife, when are you coming home?\"","’My husband, please forgive me.’","’Once all is settled, Jinghong will of course return...’","’To be a wife and mother?’","Startled, Xiao Jinghong snapped back to her senses. She quickly bowed her head, returned to the desk, and sat down. Picking up a notebook, she began to flip through it as she asked,","\"Tell me about the Mutual Market’s progress over the last few days.\"","Su Zhenyue watched her, hesitated for a moment, and replied, \"The continuous rain has slowed our progress somewhat...\"","’Should she tell her lady that she was holding the notebook upside down?’"]},{"number":275,"title":"Chapter 275 - 210: There’s a Wonton Shop by the Clouds","paragraphs":["Night fell.","Jiaxing Garden fell silent.","A warm, faintly fragrant wind swirled fallen flowers and leaves around, scattering them across the empty courtyard.","Red lanterns, specially hung to welcome the Mid-Autumn Festival, dangled from the eaves of the two wooden buildings.","Their reddish glow bathed the wooden buildings in a hazy light, outlining their silhouettes.","It was now close to eleven o’clock.","The croaking of frogs was loud and clear, echoing throughout the garden.","But Xiao Wan’er, in her room upstairs, seemed not to hear it at all, still bent over her desk writing.","Two oil lamps illuminated the Phoebe Wood desk.","To her left were two stacks of account books.","To her right was a Geomancy Map of Shu State Prefecture City.","Writing in fits and starts, she would occasionally flip through an account book or find a specific location on the Geomancy Map and jot it down.","Her elegant, small characters filled line after line.","Her sentences were a mix of long and short, yet they flowed coherently.","She wrote things like, ’The academy needs a quiet location; North City would be best.’ ’The Medical Dao emphasizes practical skill, so teaching and testing must go hand in hand.’ ’We can’t be extravagant with the silver coins; this must be a gradual endeavor.’ And so on.","Some were Chen Yi’s exact words of advice, while others were her own thoughts, inspired by him and combined with her own understanding.","Before long, Xiao Wan’er had filled three pages of Yunsong Paper.","Yet she felt no fatigue. On the contrary, a hint of joy graced her features.","She was completely absorbed, and enjoying every moment of it.","Her maids, Cui’er and Juan’er, exchanged a look and, with a silent understanding, tiptoed out of the room.","One went to cook white fungus soup, and the other went to heat water for the bath.","It was all out of concern for Xiao Wan’er.","By the time they had both finished their tasks, the watchman’s rattle could be heard outside Jiaxing Garden—the second watch was more than halfway through.","Cui’er, holding the white fungus soup, knocked on the door. \"Miss, you should take a break.\"","Xiao Wan’er lifted her head from the fluffy collar of her cloak, her expression still distant.","Her stunningly beautiful face held a trace of innocent charm.","Clearly, she was still pondering matters of the Medical Dao Academy.","When she saw the bowl of white fungus soup, Xiao Wan’er came back to her senses. She put down her fine-tipped wolf-hair brush and asked, \"What watch is it?\"","\"It’s almost the third watch.\"","\"Oh, is it that late already?\"","Juan’er, holding Xiao Wan’er’s nightgown, said with a smile, \"You were too focused, Miss.\"","\"If it weren’t so late, and if you didn’t have to deliver festival gifts to the masters and madams of the various houses tomorrow morning, Cui’er and I wouldn’t have dared to disturb you.\"","Hearing this, Xiao Wan’er glanced at the several filled pages of Yunsong Paper on her desk. She hesitated for a moment before carefully putting them away and nodding. \"You’re right, I should rest. I’ll continue tomorrow night.\"","These past few days, her schedule had been packed.","She had little free time from morning till night, and could only think and write a little after the guests in Jiaxing Garden had left and she was back in her room.","After all, she had already received the Old Master’s approval and had asked Chen Yi for so much advice. If she didn’t put her heart into it or ended up failing, she would feel terrible.","Cui’er couldn’t help but complain, \"Those people are unbelievable. They clearly want their young masters and ladies to become the Second Young Master-in-law’s disciples, but instead of approaching him, they keep pestering you to mediate.\"","Juan’er nodded in agreement. \"They see that you’re kind-hearted, Miss, so they all want to try and wear you down. I bet most of them are thinking that if by some chance it works out, they’ll have hit the jackpot.\"","Xiao Wan’er smiled faintly. \"It’s not that complicated. Most of them are female relatives; it would be improper for them to approach my brother-in-law directly.\"","\"But you’ve already politely refused them, and they still won’t leave.\"","\"They are guests, after all. And besides...\"","Xiao Wan’er paused, her gaze shifting toward Spring Lotus Garden as she said with a smile:","\"Besides, my brother-in-law also had visitors today—two distinguished gentlemen from the Governor’s Office. Business comes first.\"","Cui’er and Juan’er opened their mouths, wanting to say that the Second Young Master-in-law and his guest weren’t discussing any real business; they had spent the whole afternoon talking about whether there would be courtesans at the Mid-Autumn poetry gathering.","But seeing the look on Xiao Wan’er’s face, they swallowed their words.","Xiao Wan’er, however, didn’t think much of it. After she spoke, she took a few sips of the white fungus soup, feeling a little warmer. Then she bathed, changed into a pink, light silk nightgown, and lay down on her bed.","Before falling asleep, she didn’t forget to give an instruction: \"After we deliver the festival gifts tomorrow, remind me to make a trip to Spring Lotus Garden.\"","\"I have a few more questions to ask my brother-in-law.\"","Cui’er and Juan’er naturally agreed. Seeing her close her eyes, they tidied up the desk and tiptoed out of the room.","Not far from the door, Shen Huatang heard the movement. She glanced back once before resuming her post outside the wooden building.","Faintly, she could hear snippets of their muttering.","\"Clearly, the Young Master-in-law and his friend were discussing courtesans.\"","\"It wasn’t the Second Young Master-in-law, it was his companion—this year’s Imperial Top Scholar. He was the one reciting some lewd poem about ’listening to the spring rain in a small tower overnight’.\"","\"Exactly. But the Second Miss already led a raid on Spring Rain Building, so they can’t go anyway.\"","\"But that won’t stop those vixens from going to the academy’s poetry gathering...\"","Hearing this, Shen Huatang knew they were talking about Chen Yi. She couldn’t help but glance toward Spring Lotus Garden as well.","She listened intently for a moment but could only hear the faint sound of the wind, so she paid it no more mind.","’If possible, I would much rather the Second Young Master-in-law be passionate about chasing women than... ’","Chen Yi, for his part, was completely unaware of all this.","He was secretly hiding in the Purple Bamboo Forest, cultivating his Martial Arts.","Ever since Xie Tingyun returned to Tian Mountain to sweet-talk his junior martial brothers and sisters into coming down the mountain to serve as Guards for Hundred Herbs Hall, Chen Yi could finally practice his Techniques in peace.","Two days.","Two nights, to be precise.","Though it was a short time, he had already cultivated both his Mountain Shattering Fist and Hundred Flowers Palm to the peak of Mastery.","His two Body Techniques had long since reached a point where they could not be improved any further.","Only his Dragon-Falling Spear Technique and Brocade Spring Saber Technique were still lacking.","Especially the Dragon-Falling Spear Technique.","Not only had he not fully integrated the Great Success Spear Dao Profound Mysteries, but the four new spear moves that appeared after it ascended to the Celestial Tier were only at the Skilled Level. It would still be some time before he reached Mastery.","That said...","The Celestial Tier Dragon-Falling Spear Technique was indeed much stronger than the Earth Tier version.","Especially when combined with the Mental Realm of the Great Success Spear Dao, the power of the Spear Technique increased immensely."]},{"number":276,"title":"Chapter 276 - 210: There’s a Wonton Shop by the Clouds (2)","paragraphs":["The four new forms of his Spear Technique were, of course, moves specifically designed to integrate with the Heaven and Earth Spiritual Mechanism Realm. Their power was nothing short of terrifying.","Even the power of the eight Spear Technique forms he had previously practiced, like Dragon Head-Raising and Zhaoqing Mountain, had increased considerably.","However, Chen Yi had a realistic understanding of his own strength.","His Martial Arts·Body, Fist, Step, Spear, and Saber had all reached the Great Success Realm. The corresponding martial techniques were Upper Grade Earth Tier, and he had trained most of them to Mastery. However, the shortcoming in his Cultivation was far too obvious.","He had only broken through to the Upper Sixth Grade last night.","All things considered, he could at best fight Liu Lang on equal footing, and perhaps even come out slightly ahead.","If he had to fight a duel or a life-and-death battle against a Martial Artist above the Fifth Grade Realm—someone at the Fourth or Third Grade Realm—he would have to resort to a few tricks.","Like Qingfeng Drunk and Immortal Drunk.","Not exactly honorable, but they would keep him alive.","’I have to raise at least one Dao to the Perfection Realm before I’ll have a decent ability to protect myself.’","’An epiphany, I need an epiphany... Fist Dao or Spear Dao would be fine.’","’Saber Dao or Step Technique would be good too.’","As midnight approached, the epiphany Chen Yi hoped for showed no signs of arriving, so he had no choice but to end his night’s Cultivation.","After tidying up the Purple Bamboo Forest, he returned to his room, wiped himself down, changed into clean clothes, and sat cross-legged on his bed.","However, he didn’t begin his Cultivation of the Four Symbols Skill. Instead, he cleared his mind and calmly gazed out the window.","He watched the distant starlight, the dancing fallen leaves nearby, and the large golden characters that floated before his eyes—","[Daily Intelligence · Profound-rank Lower Grade: At 6:30 AM, a Hidden Guard will retrieve a secret letter from the wonton shop on Kangning Street. A minuscule Opportunity is available.]","\"Profound-rank Lower, huh.\"","Chen Yi pursed his lips. Having tasted far greater rewards, he couldn’t help but look down on a mere Profound-rank Opportunity.","But after he carefully read the full message, he couldn’t help but raise an eyebrow.","’Kangning Street... a wonton shop? How could I not know about a wonton shop on that street?’","’And it’s a drop point for a Hidden Guard to pick up a secret letter.’","Chen Yi had been in Shu State for a long time. He might not be familiar with other places, but he frequented Kangning Street and the West Market enough to remember which shops were on the street and which weren’t.","’Did the owner of the tailor shop change their business?’","After muttering to himself, Chen Yi decided not to dwell on it.","Coincidentally, he had to go to Guiyun Academy to teach the Calligraphy Dao tomorrow anyway, so it wouldn’t be any trouble to check out the wonton shop.","He then closed his eyes and began cultivating the Four Symbols Skill.","His mind gradually sank into the void.","In the depths of his meditation, a faint thought surfaced.","’It’d be great if Martial Arts·Body reached the Perfection Realm through an epiphany, too. I’m really not picky...’","...","Picky or not, Chen Yi concluded his cultivation session the next morning as he always did.","He stood up, stretched, and looked around. Smacking his lips, he said, \"My wish didn’t come true. Guess I’ll have to go with plan B.\"","And what was plan B?","To slowly accumulate Opportunity, of course. Once he saved up a thousand points, he would choose a Dao and break through to the Perfection Realm.","After washing up and getting dressed, he went downstairs to the living room.","Chen Yi glanced at the breakfast on the table and remarked in surprise, \"Are we having mooncakes already?\"","Xiaodie nodded, her eyes glued to the mooncakes, clearly craving one.","\"The kitchen made some special mooncakes. This morning, they just sent a few to each residence for a taste test. We’ll get more tomorrow evening, after the Eldest Miss leads the ladies of the estate in setting up the incense table to worship the moon.\"","\"And it’s not just mooncakes! There will also be pressed duck, red-braised duck, and osmanthus wine.\"","Chen Yi nodded and said with a smile, \"You certainly have all the details.\"","This time of year, they followed the ancient custom: men do not worship the moon, and women do not make offerings to the Kitchen God.","Therefore, the Mid-Autumn Festival moon worship was always performed by the women of the household, who would set up an incense table and pray for peace and good fortune.","As the legitimate daughter of the main branch of the family, Xiao Wan’er was the natural choice to lead the ceremony.","’The estate will probably be very lively tomorrow,’ he thought.","’For one, there will be many guests delivering festival gifts. For another, there are all the tedious formalities. I reckon we won’t be able to go out for moon-viewing until late afternoon.’","Xiaodie, however, wasn’t thinking about any of that. The only thing in her eyes was mooncakes.","Seeing this, Chen Yi gestured for Xiao Wuge and Xiaodie to sit down and eat.","He casually picked one up and took a bite, then froze.","He chewed a couple of times, then turned to Xiaodie, who was daintily nibbling her own mooncake. \"What is this filling?\" he asked.","\"It’s salt-and-pepper sesame cake filling, Young Master! Go on, eat! It’s delicious!\"","Delicious?","Chen Yi finished the mooncake in his hand, his expression stone-faced.","Even though he’d seen plenty of bizarre mooncake fillings in his past life, this was the first time he’d ever tasted one full of Sichuan peppercorn powder.","Salt-and-pepper sesame cake filling... ’Well,’ he thought, ’my mouth is certainly numb now.’","’Actually, I think I still prefer the five-nut filling.’","Remembering he had to investigate the Kangning Street wonton shop this morning, Chen Yi resolutely refused to touch a second mooncake.","After quickly downing a few mouthfuls of congee, he left Spring Lotus Garden with the festival gifts he’d prepared for Mr. Yue Ming and the others.","Glancing to the side, he saw Xiao Wan’er emerging from Jiaxing Garden with Shen Huatang and her attendants, carrying an assortment of bags, just like him.","Chen Yi gave a mock-formal bow and asked, \"Eldest Sister, off to deliver festival gifts so early?\"","Xiao Wan’er nodded. Seeing the bags in his hands and knowing he was heading to Guiyun Academy today, she said with a smile,","\"It’ll be inconvenient for you to carry those gifts all by yourself, Brother-in-law. You should have the front courtyard prepare a carriage to take you.\"","Chen Yi naturally refused. \"It’s not much. I’ll just treat it as exercise.\"","Xiao Wan’er hummed in agreement and didn’t press the matter, gesturing for him to walk with her as they talked.","She had been up since a quarter past three in the morning. In the hour and a half since, she had already finished delivering festival gifts to the residences in the rear courtyard.","After a bit of small talk, Xiao Wan’er’s expression turned a little strange. \"The second branch of the family is leaving the estate today,\" she said.","Chen Yi paused, turning to look at her. He knew she felt a bit of pity for them, and after a moment’s thought, he said,","\"The Old Master and Madam must have given this a great deal of thought before making their decision.\""]},{"number":277,"title":"Chapter 277 - 210: There’s a Wonton Shop by the Clouds","paragraphs":["\"If there were a way to let the members of the second branch stay, I’m sure the old patriarch wouldn’t disregard past feelings.\"","With Xiao Dongchen dead, it was inevitable that the second branch would be implicated.","To say nothing of how people like Xiao Wang controlled the Punishment Hall and coveted what the main branch had.","Even if the second branch were united with the main branch, certain precautions would still be necessary.","In such a situation, no family head could afford to be soft-hearted.","Let alone Duke Dingyuan, who was facing both internal and external threats to the Xiao Family.","Xiao Wan’er heard this, nodded, and said softly, \"I know Grandfather and Second Sister wouldn’t act without reason.\"","\"That’s why I didn’t go to Four Directions Hall this morning to see them off.\"","She understood all this, of course, but relationships cool once people are gone, and she couldn’t help but feel a pang of sadness.","Chen Yi understood and chuckled. \"It’s better that you didn’t. You would have avoided being seen as someone there to gloat.\"","\"How could that be?\"","\"Second Grand-uncle and Sister-in-law... they were, they were fine.\"","Seeing she was unwilling to think ill of them, Chen Yi didn’t press the matter. After a bit more small talk, he asked about the Medical Dao Academy.","Xiao Wan’er immediately suppressed her melancholy, her eyes brightening and shining with life.","\"Grandfather has already agreed! He even said he’d give me a sum of silver.\"","\"I’ve done the calculations. We don’t need too much at the start.\"","\"As long as we situate the academy within the mansion’s fiefdom, we can build it for about five thousand silver.\"","\"That’s a good idea.\"","\"Right? And then there’s...\"","Xiao Wan’er had indeed put a lot of thought into the Medical Dao Academy.","Placing the academy on the Xiao Family’s fiefdom would not only save the cost of purchasing a land deed but also allow them to get help from the people there to build it.","Compared to finding a location and workers in the Prefecture City, the expense would be less than half.","Then there was the method of integrating teaching and testing, which was mostly based on how Physicians in the Medicine Hall trained their apprentices.","It all made perfect sense.","After listening, Chen Yi couldn’t help but praise her. \"I’m already looking forward to the day that Medical Dao Academy is completed.\"","Xiao Wan’er’s pretty face flushed slightly. She lowered her head and said, \"Most of the ideas in the plan came from you.\"","\"I’m just the one who talks. You’re different. You’re the founder of the first Medical Dao Academy in Shu State, and maybe even the entire Great Wei Dynasty.\"","\"Perhaps you’ll even be the dean of that Medical Dao Academy.\"","\"Ah, stop it...\"","\"I... I can spend some silver, that’s fine, but I can’t be the dean.\"","\"Why not, Dean Xiao Wan’er?\"","As soon as he spoke, Chen Yi laughed and ran off, leaving behind a blushing Xiao Wan’er, who glared reproachfully at his retreating back, embarrassed by the word \"Dean.\"","\"Brother-in-law is just being mischievous.\"","’How... how could I possibly be the dean of the Medical Dao Academy?’","Shen Huatang, who was standing nearby, saw all this and couldn’t help but show a troubled expression.","\"My lady, actually...\"","\"What is it?\"","\"Actually, the Second Young Master-in-law is right. You as dean... would be suitable.\"","\"Huatang, how can you be just like him?\"","\"...\"","Shen Huatang had done her best.","She had practically bitten her tongue emphasizing the word \"Second,\" but Xiao Wan’er remained oblivious.","It was hard to say whether the word \"Dean\" or the name \"Chen Yi\" was occupying her thoughts at that moment.","Meanwhile, Chen Yi had no such complicated thoughts. In a good mood, he arrived at the front courtyard.","He scanned the area and noticed that besides some Armored Warriors at the gate, there were also several men in black clothes. He couldn’t help but give them a second look.","’Men from the Punishment Hall?’","Chen Yi knew that the Punishment Hall was currently being managed temporarily by Xiao Xuanshuo.","He just hadn’t expected Xiao Xuanshuo to bring men from the Punishment Hall to guard the residence alongside the Armored Guards.","’Is he planning to use the Punishment Hall as a hidden security detail?’","Chen Yi made a mental note of it, so he wouldn’t be caught by the Punishment Hall if he tried to sneak out in the future.","Then, he greeted a few Armored Warriors he was somewhat familiar with and walked straight out of the Marquis’s Mansion.","He followed Chuansi Street eastward, turned north onto South Street, and soon arrived on Kangning Street.","It was now the Hour of the Rabbit (5–7 a.m.), and the street was bustling with numerous pedestrians.","It was as if everyone had suddenly found themselves with free time.","Chen Yi squeezed through the crowd, heading toward Guiyun Academy while scanning the shops on both sides of the street, searching for that wonton shop.","He walked for a long time but couldn’t find it.","Just as he was getting puzzled, he saw a sign not far from the entrance of Guiyun Academy—\"There’s a Wonton Shop by the Clouds.\"","Chen Yi studied the shop under the sign, then glanced at its deserted entrance, a smile creeping onto his face.","’There’s a Wonton Shop by the Clouds... Interesting.’","He wondered which talented Hidden Guard had come up with a name so out of step with the business practices of the time.","’Are they aiming to lose money on this venture?’","Chen Yi had no way of knowing, so he carried the few bags of holiday gifts he had and walked into the shop.","He was just about to call for an attendant to bring him some wontons when he saw a familiar figure sitting in a corner.","It was none other than his student, Ma Guan.","After a moment’s thought, he walked over, sat down across from him, and asked with a smile, \"Heming, are the wontons any good?\"","Ma Guan was taken aback. Forgetting his food, he quickly stood up and bowed. \"This student greets Mr. Qingzhou.\"","Chen Yi waved his hand, motioning for him to sit. \"This isn’t the academy. No need for such formalities.\"","Ma Guan sat down sheepishly. Recalling the question, he hesitated before answering.","\"Overpriced and not very good.\"","\"Oh?\"","\"It’s, it’s like a total rip-off...\"","Seeing Ma Guan’s face flush red, Chen Yi was amused. He didn’t ask any more questions and called out to the shop attendant, \"A bowl of wontons, please. I’d like to see how they taste.\"","Whether it was a rip-off or not, he didn’t know.","But he was certain that the people in this shop had very distinctive appearances.","The two attendants looked burly and thick-waisted, yet they were, without a doubt, women.","Behind the counter was a plainly dressed woman with sallow skin, who had been staring at him ever since he walked in.","At first glance, Chen Yi really didn’t recognize the woman.","But upon closer inspection, his smile couldn’t help but broaden.","—The renowned White Tiger Guard Silver Banner Officer, Lady Tiger Lou Yuxue, wasn’t hiding out in Yanhua Lane, but had come to Kangning Street to open a wonton shop.","’But if she’s going to open a shop, why dress up so ugly?’","’Tsk, what is this supposed to be?’","’A clumsy imitation of Xi Shi?’","Lou Yuxue, of course, had no idea what Chen Yi was thinking. After studying him for a moment, she recognized him.","—Chen Yi, the live-in son-in-law of the Xiao Family, known within the Hidden Guard by the codename \"Fledgling,\" Chen Qingzhou.","’What’s he doing here?’","’To eat wontons?’","’I haven’t heard that he can’t get a decent meal in the Xiao Family.’","Lou Yuxue pondered this for a moment. Seizing the opportunity while one of the sturdy female attendants went to the back kitchen, she walked out from behind the counter to Chen Yi’s side and greeted them warmly.","\"Gentlemen, our shop has just opened. The wontons are free, on the house.\"","Hearing this, before Chen Yi could say anything, Ma Guan shoveled the rest of his wontons into his mouth with two quick movements of his chopsticks, forced them down his throat, and held up his bowl, stammering:","\"Proprietress, the wontons are delicious! Really good! Another bowl, please.\"","Chen Yi: \"...\"","’What was he just saying?’"]},{"number":278,"title":"Chapter 278 - 211: A Simple Gesture, No Need for Thanks","paragraphs":["Ma Guan’s principles were far too flexible.","While he certainly disliked expensive, unattractive things, he was perfectly willing to accept anything that didn’t cost much silver.","He didn’t even care if they were beautiful.","And when the word \"free\" wasn’t associated with \"charity\" and didn’t wound his fragile pride as a scholar, Lou Yuxue became like a goddess in his eyes.","Such a kind, beautiful... soul.","This was Ma Guan’s first visit to \"There’s a Wonton Shop by the Clouds,\" yet it already felt like home.","\"Proprietress, another two bowls of wontons!\"","Lou Yuxue answered with a smile and instructed a nearby waiter to bring him more.","Ma Guan shot a cautious glance at Chen Yi, a sheepish look on his face.","\"Please forgive me, Mr. Qingzhou. I was so engrossed in my studies last night that I forgot to eat or sleep, so my appetite is a bit bigger than usual this morning.\"","\"Eat up if you’re hungry. It’s no big deal.\"","Chen Yi knew, of course, that Ma Guan had little silver, so he could somewhat understand his way of thinking.","’No silver at home, no silver on his person... It’s only natural that he’d like free things.’","’Little did he know, some people and things that are free end up being the most expensive.’","Chen Yi stopped teasing Ma Guan, lest the man become so ashamed he’d want to crawl into a hole and disappear.","He turned to meet Lou Yuxue’s gaze and said with a smile, \"Proprietress, your shop just opened today, and you’re already giving away free wontons. With such a wise approach to business, you’re sure to be prosperous in the future.\"","Lou Yuxue looked into his eyes, as gentle as still water, and thought with a sigh, ’This Fledgling, having read his books, really is different.’","’Despite being so heavily suppressed by the Jiangnan Prefecture Chen Family, and then being mostly unwelcome after joining the Xiao Family in Shu State, he managed to turn his situation around step by step with his own talent, until he earned the respect of scholars throughout Shu State and even all of Great Wei’s Nine State and Three Prefectures.’","’His strength of character is truly unyielding.’","While marveling internally, Lou Yuxue said with a smile, \"To receive Mr. Qingzhou’s blessing is an honor. I just hope this little shop can help us make a modest living.\"","Upon hearing this, Chen Yi feigned ignorance. \"You know of me?\"","\"I happened to overhear your conversation just now and realized that you, sir, are the Mr. Qingzhou who has recently become famous in Shu State.\"","\"Famous is too strong a word. I merely have a minor reputation.\"","\"You’re too modest, Mr. Qingzhou. An ordinary scholar in your position would probably have let it all go to their head by now.\"","They exchanged a few more pleasantries.","Chen Yi still couldn’t figure out Lou Yuxue’s motive for striking up a conversation with him.","It was all flattery and compliments. It seemed Lou Yuxue had only come over to say hello.","It wasn’t until a while later, as two sturdy-looking women brought out more wontons, that Lou Yuxue used the opportunity to smile and head upstairs to the second floor.","Chen Yi watched her retreating figure, a thoughtful look on his face. He knew she was likely going to retrieve a secret message from the Hidden Guard.","However, when he saw the two sturdy women in the hall staring at him and Ma Guan, he gave up on the idea of following her to read the message.","’Luckily, she’s an old acquaintance. There will be plenty of opportunities to pry information about the Hidden Guard out of her in the future.’","As Chen Yi pondered this, he picked up a wonton and examined it.","The skin was thin and translucent, the filling plump and generous. It looked far more appealing than an ordinary wonton.","He then popped it into his mouth. His gaze drifted to Ma Guan. \"This is delicious.\"","The color, aroma, and flavor were all perfect. You had to admit, these wontons were expertly made.","Ma Guan was wolfing down his bowl of wontons.","When he finally had a moment’s break from chewing, he managed to say, \"If you like them, Mr. Qingzhou, shall... shall I order more?\"","Chen Yi shook his head. As he ate, he scanned the hall from the corner of his eye.","It was strange.","A quarter of an hour had passed since they’d entered the wonton shop, but the hall was still empty save for him and Ma Guan.","Business was depressingly slow.","Any other shop owner in this situation would probably be out front, hawking their wares and trying to pull in passersby for a taste.","But neither Lou Yuxue nor her waiters seemed bothered in the slightest.","Clearly, they weren’t too concerned with the shop’s profitability.","Or rather, making money was a secondary concern. They were just using this place as a temporary base of operations.","At this thought, Chen Yi’s eyes flickered. He asked meaningfully, \"Heming, did you bring your brush and ink?\"","Ma Guan paused, confused by the question, but nodded. \"I did.\"","\"Good. In a moment, I want you to do this...\"","Chen Yi gave him a few quiet instructions, then finished his wontons, stood up, and, carrying his various packages, headed for Guiyun Academy.","Ma Guan respectfully watched him go.","After finishing another two bowls of wontons, he didn’t rush off. Instead, following Chen Yi’s instructions, he took out his brush, ink, paper, and inkstone from his bag.","Then, under the astonished gazes of the waiters, he ground the ink, lifted his brush, and, with his Calligraphy Dao at the Minor Success stage, wrote a line of characters in Wei Qing’s Style:","\"The Best Wontons Under Heaven.\"","Beneath it were two lines of smaller characters: \"Jointly recommended by Chen Qingzhou and Ma Heming of Guiyun Academy.\"","The moment the characters were complete, faint golden wisps of light appeared on the paper.","This subtle radiance immediately attracted the attention of passersby outside.","This was especially true for the students of Guiyun Academy.","They were already curious about the new shop, and as they passed, their keen senses naturally picked up on the phenomenon created by Ma Guan’s Calligraphy Dao.","Even those who hadn’t planned on entering the wonton shop now found themselves walking in, driven by curiosity.","\"Brother Heming, what’s this?\"","Ma Guan picked up the sheet, blew the ink dry, and explained what Mr. Qingzhou had asked him to do.","\"The wontons are delicious and inexpensive, but their business is slow. We can’t just accept their free food for nothing in return.\"","\"So, Mr. Qingzhou asked me to leave behind a piece of my calligraphy, just as a small token of our appreciation. Just a small token.\"","The crowd understood. Their eyes were drawn to the calligraphy, and they stared at it again and again."]},{"number":279,"title":"Chapter 279 - 211: A Small Favor, Don’t Mention It","paragraphs":["Ma Guan barely needed to say another word. In twos and threes, people found seats and called out to the waiter:","\"Bring me a bowl of wontons. I want to try them.\"","\"I’ll have a bowl, too.\"","\"If even Mr. Qingzhou said they were good, this place must have a unique recipe. I have to give it a try.\"","\"Besides, we still have about an hour until class starts today. No rush...\"","A burly woman saw what was happening and quickly had the others tend to the customers while she rushed upstairs to the second floor.","KNOCK. KNOCK KNOCK.","Inside the room, Lou Yuxue was in the middle of deciphering a secret message from an opera script. Hearing the sound, she asked with some annoyance, \"What is it?\"","\"Sh-Shopkeeper, we have a situation in the shop.\"","\"What kind of situation?\"","\"A lot of customers have arrived.\"","Lou Yuxue frowned. She listened intently for a moment and, quickly grasping what had happened, couldn’t help but grumble to herself about Chen Yi’s meddling.","Just as Chen Yi had surmised, Lou Yuxue had only opened \"There’s a Wonton Shop by the Clouds\" as a temporary safe house.","Once things settled down after the \"burning of the Three Towns’ summer grain\" in Shu State, and once a new Elder from the Bright Moon Building arrived, she intended to return to her real duties.","She had absolutely no intention of running the wonton shop as a legitimate business.","Otherwise, she wouldn’t have chosen such a ridiculous name for it.","But now, thanks to Chen Yi and Ma Guan’s unnecessary stunt, the newly opened wonton shop was already attracting attention from some of the students at Guiyun Academy.","Business was visibly improving, which ran contrary to Lou Yuxue’s plans, leaving her both surprised and displeased.","After a moment’s thought, Lou Yuxue calmly instructed, \"Maintain normal operations.\"","The burly woman acknowledged the order and departed.","Lou Yuxue listened for another moment. When she heard still more customers arriving, she shook her head, feeling a headache coming on.","’That Fledgling... such a meddler.’","Afterwards, she thought no more of it and focused on deciphering the contents of the secret message.","Before long, three short lines of text appeared on the paper:","[Investigate the Fledgling’s whereabouts on the night the summer grain of the Three Towns was burned.]","[Contact the leader of the horse bandits within Poshisu Country—King Landu. Negotiate and confirm a time to meet. I intend to go in person.]","[Closely monitor the Simurgh Phoenix’s movements. Report every detail, no matter how trivial.]","Lou Yuxue’s expression changed slightly as she read the contents of the paper.","The three tasks were all different, but each one surprised her.","The first task was especially odd—to discover the Fledgling’s whereabouts on the night the summer grain of the Three Towns was burned.","From this single sentence alone, Lou Yuxue deduced the intentions of the Pavilion Master and the Golden Banner Officer.","’Are they suspecting that the Fledgling did something that night?’","’How is that possible?’","’That Fledgling has always been well-behaved and kept to himself, never even stepping out of the Xiao Family’s gates. How could he possibly have made a move that night?’","Lou Yuxue didn’t know the answer, but she was certain this task was the simplest of the three.","She only needed to go through the Hawk’s subordinate—an Iron Banner Officer hidden in the Xiao Family—to confirm the Fledgling’s whereabouts that night.","As for the remaining two tasks, contacting King Landu and investigating the Simurgh Phoenix, there were leads to follow.","The former, though a leader of horse bandits, had intricate ties to the Poshisu royal family. The Golden Banner Officer taking the initiative to meet with him must be to plot future operations.","As for the latter, the Simurgh Phoenix’s arrival in Shu State was too sudden, so it was only natural for it to displease the Pavilion Master and the Golden Banner Officer.","As Lou Yuxue considered this, she silently committed the tasks on the paper to memory, then burned the sheet until it was completely destroyed.","The missions weren’t complex, but she still had a few questions.","’First, neither the Pavilion Master nor the Golden Banner Officer gave any instructions regarding the silver coins plundered from the Jing State Liu Family and ’Liu Wu’.’","’Second, the Xiao Family was lucky to escape this time. Xiao Dongchen is dead, yet the Mutual Market was unaffected... Are there no plans to sabotage it later?’","A thought suddenly struck Lou Yuxue. ’Could it be King Landu, the leader of the Poshisu horse bandits?’","It was a definite possibility.","’It seems the General and the Pavilion Master have already devised a detailed plan for Shu State.’","’Mmm... to avoid being detected by the Xiao Family, I should wait until after the Mid-Autumn Festival to make my move.’","Having come to this conclusion, Lou Yuxue calmed her mind, tidied the room, and went downstairs.","One glance around the room and she froze.","The once-empty main hall of \"There’s a Wonton Shop by the Clouds\" was now completely full.","There were students from Guiyun Academy, refined young men and women visiting Kangning Street, and travelers just passing through.","All of them were eating wontons while looking at Ma Guan, who stood in the center holding a calligraphy scroll that read, \"Number One Wontons Under Heaven.\"","\"I’ve traveled far and wide for many years and eaten plenty of wontons, but I never thought I’d find a taste like this in Shu State.\"","\"Not bad at all.\"","\"’Number One Under Heaven’ is a stretch, but they taste good.\"","\"The calligraphy is the best part, really.\"","\"Even though it wasn’t written by Mr. Qingzhou himself, as his student, Ma Heming’s calligraphy is also a rare work of art.\"","\"Well worth the visit...\"","As Lou Yuxue listened to the jumble of conversations in the main hall, a flash of anger appeared in her eyes.","’Fledgling, you had better not have done this on purpose, or I swear I won’t let you off the hook!’","...","Chen Yi had, of course, done it on purpose.","He couldn’t stand to see Lou Yuxue struggling so hard to earn silver.","So he came up with a plan to make business at \"There’s a Wonton Shop by the Clouds\" a bit more brisk.","It was just that...","He suspected Lou Yuxue might not appreciate the gesture.","Chen Yi watched the words [Opportunity +4] float before his eyes and smiled with a touch of wicked delight.","’I’ll just consider this compensation for failing to obtain that Profound Level Opportunity.’","He then delivered the festival gifts to Mr. Yue Ming, Mr. Zhuo Ying, and the others.","After getting a brief update on the \"Exhibition Hall\" project, he went to the study hall to teach his class.","After teaching a few times, Chen Yi had naturally become much more comfortable and adept at it.","He taught methodically, starting with the entry-level basics of the Calligraphy Dao."]},{"number":280,"title":"Chapter 280 - 211: A Trivial Matter, No Thanks Needed","paragraphs":["He spent an hour explaining the nuances of the Calligraphy Dao and the corresponding Profound Mysteries of the Dao Realm.","During the second hour, he wrote two calligraphy models and had the students use them as guides to practice freely on their sand trays.","Half the day passed quickly.","Chen Yi gave Ma Guan a few instructions and left the study hall on his own, completely ignoring the students’ requests to see his Perfect Calligraphy Dao.","The exhibition hall was about to open, so he couldn’t be bothered with such an unnecessary display.","Furthermore, he had previously discussed with Mr. Yue Ming and decided that the academy would adopt a last-place elimination system. It wouldn’t be good for him to get too close to these students.","’It would make it harder for me to be ruthless when the time came to make cuts.’","However, when he arrived at Mr. Yue Ming’s residence and glanced around, his mood instantly soured, much like Lou Yuxue’s when she sees a house full of guests.","The modest courtyard was now packed to the brim with people.","There were Han Zhangping and Pei Zhaoye from Yuelu Academy, whom he had met once before. There were also some scholars of some renown in the Confucian circles of Shu State who had attended the Old Master’s birthday banquet. And then there were members of Noble Families who were clearly from out of state.","They were gathered in the courtyard in small groups, most of them looking toward the main hall, clearly waiting for Mr. Yue Ming to be free.","Seeing this, Chen Yi was about to slip away quietly when a voice called out from his side:","\"Qingzhou, is your lecture finished? Come, quickly, join me in seeing the Headmaster.\"","Chen Yi turned his head and saw it was Mr. Zhuo Ying. He made one last, desperate attempt to get out of it, saying,","\"The Mid-Autumn Festival is approaching, and I have to deliver festival gifts for my wife this afternoon. It’s not convenient for me to stay.\"","Hearing this, Mr. Zhuo Ying would take no for an answer, pulling him into the crowd.","As he walked, he gestured for the waiting guests to make way.","Only when they had entered the study in the main hall did Mr. Zhuo Ying lower his voice and say,","\"Ah, Qingzhou, I’m not trying to force you, but the situation these past few days has been rather special.\"","\"You saw all those people outside. Strictly speaking, they all came here looking for you.\"","\"Even if you don’t sympathize with the Headmaster, you have to consider the academy.\"","\"After all, those people are either famous scholars from various states or members of prestigious and influential clans. We have to let them save face.\"","’Those people just want to learn my Calligraphy Dao,’ Chen Yi thought. ’As for saving face, they should be the ones deferring to me.’","But thoughts were just thoughts.","He still obediently sat down in the study.","Sipping tea, he joined Mr. Yue Ming, Mr. Zhuo Ying, and the others in receiving the guests one by one.","For the most part, however, he said very little.","At most, he would chime in with a few pleasantries.","Things like, \"I’ve heard so much about you,\" or \"Your son has a solid foundation in the Calligraphy Dao; with time, he will surely achieve great things,\" or \"Everything is at the Headmaster’s discretion.\"","In any case, he didn’t make things difficult for Mr. Yue Ming and the others.","Once noon had passed and the guests had left one by one, Chen Yi finally put down his teacup and said bluntly,","\"It’s getting late. I should be heading back.\"","Seeing this, Mr. Yue Ming quickly waved his hands to stop him. \"No rush, no rush.\"","\"There are two matters I need to ask your opinion on.\"","\"I’m listening.\"","\"I heard from Huai’gu yesterday that you intend to participate in the poetry gathering tomorrow evening?\"","\"If I can get out of it, I’d rather not go.\"","\"Getting out of it will be difficult.\"","\"It’s not just some of the academy’s people who will be at the poetry gathering tomorrow night. Lord Liu, Lord Yang, and others from the Governor’s Office will also be attending.\"","Chen Yi raised an eyebrow. \"The Governor’s Office... Liu Hong?\"","\"...\"","Mr. Yue Ming and Mr. Zhuo Ying exchanged a glance, both clearly hearing the disdain in his tone regarding Liu Hong.","But thinking carefully about the current relationship between the Xiao Family and the Liu Family, Chen Yi’s attitude was understandable.","\"Besides the Governor’s Office, people from other Government Offices will be there, as well as some great clans and Confucian Scholars from Shu State and the Outer States.\"","\"However, we will only be observing. The success of the poetry gathering ultimately depends on the performance of you young people.\"","’So that’s it,’ Chen Yi realized. ’These two want me to do all the work again.’","\"It’s actually simple. Just display my piece, ’Post-rain Reflections,’ at the gathering. That will surely bring glory to the academy.\"","Mr. Yue Ming waved his hand. \"That won’t do, that won’t do.\"","\"Your ’Post-rain Reflections’ has already spread throughout Shu State, and many have seen your Cursive Script at the Perfection Realm. It wouldn’t be good to use it again.\"","Chen Yi thought for a moment and just said he would see how things went tomorrow night.","He didn’t refuse to go, however.","After all, he had already promised Chen Yunfan and Li Huai’gu yesterday that he would check out the poetry gathering.","Mr. Yue Ming and Mr. Zhuo Ying didn’t press him further.","They all knew Chen Yi’s temperament and that he was very firm in his own ideas. Once he made a decision, no one could persuade him otherwise.","So they only reminded him,","\"The Mid-Autumn Festival has been a grand occasion for scholars and poets since ancient times. If you feel inspired to create a masterpiece, Qingzhou, don’t hesitate to write it for us all to admire.\"","Chen Yi asked noncommittally, \"And the second matter?\"","Mr. Yue Ming paused, then said, \"The exhibition hall is set to open the day after tomorrow. After discussing it, we all hope you can be there to preside over the event.\"","Mr. Zhuo Ying chimed in, \"Your Calligraphy Dao has now reached the Perfection Realm, and in a new script style at that. Such a thing is rare even across the entire Great Wei Nine State and Three Prefectures.\"","\"There will certainly be many people coming the day after tomorrow.\"","\"If you can be there to meet them, it will only benefit your future, with no drawbacks.\"","Hearing this, Chen Yi did not agree immediately.","’Of course, I’m well aware of the benefits of something like this.’","’On a small scale, I could become a familiar face among the scholars.’","’On a larger scale, it would solidify my status as a master of the Calligraphy Dao, greatly increasing my fame.’","’More people would know of me and recognize me in the future. If anyone wanted to move against me again, they would inevitably have some reservations.’","’This is one of the few benefits that fame and fortune have brought me.’","Lost in thought, Chen Yi nodded and agreed. \"After the poetry gathering, I’ll come to the academy first thing in the morning.\"","\"But let me be clear: if my wife returns in the next two days, even if I come, I won’t be able to stay for long.\""]},{"number":281,"title":"Chapter 281 - 211: It Was Nothing, You’re Welcome","paragraphs":["Mr. Yue Ming smiled. \"Of course.\"","\"It’s scheduled for a quarter past nine in the morning, the day after tomorrow. That’s plenty of time. It shouldn’t keep you until noon.\"","They exchanged a few pleasantries.","Chen Yi rose and took his leave.","As he walked out of the academy, he instinctively glanced over at \"There’s a Wonton Shop by the Clouds.\"","When he saw the sign Ma Guan had written—\"The World’s Best Wonton Shop\"—already hanging by the entrance, along with a constant stream of customers, he couldn’t help but chuckle.","’Lady Tiger, Lou Yuxue.’","’You should just focus on running your wonton shop.’","’Heh... You’re welcome.’","A smile touched Chen Yi’s lips at the thought, and he headed straight back to the Xiao Family estate.","Right now, Hawk had fled, Gray Wolf had committed suicide, and Simurgh Phoenix was always by Chen Yunfan’s side.","Therefore, if he wanted to understand the future movements of the Hidden Guard, starting with Lady Tiger was his best option.","’It’s a good thing I spared Lou Yuxue’s life. It wouldn’t be good if the Hidden Guard truly vanished into the shadows.’","But what Chen Yi didn’t know was that after he had walked some distance, a carriage emerged from the banks of Quchi Lake nearby.","It was drawn by a common, short-legged horse, and the carriage itself was plain and unadorned.","Just then, a corner of the curtain lifted, revealing a pair of shocked and suspicious eyes staring at Chen Yi’s retreating figure.","’He... he’s not dead?!’","’I took action myself and personally confirmed the Xiao Family’s son-in-law had drowned in Quchi Lake. How can he still be alive?’","Hearing this, the young man driving the carriage glanced over curiously.","\"Master, could it be that Xiao Jinghong rescued him in time?\"","\"I heard that on that day, Xiao Jinghong personally brought Chen Yi back to the Xiao Family Punishment Hall. With her level of cultivation, it wouldn’t have been impossible for her to save him.\"","\"That’s possible, but...\"","\"Hah. The brat got lucky!\"","...","Back at the Xiao Family estate, Chen Yi’s prediction had unfortunately come true.","He would indeed have to deliver festival gifts to the various families in Xiao Jinghong’s stead that afternoon.","The reason was simple: Xiao Jinghong had confirmed that she would not be able to return home before the Mid-Autumn Festival.","After carefully reading the letter, a complicated smile appeared on Chen Yi’s face.","Although he hadn’t spent much time with Xiao Jinghong, he recognized her handwriting well enough to know she hadn’t written this letter herself.","’It seems my wife feels a little guilty. She didn’t even write the reply herself.’","Xiao Wan’er had clearly noticed as well. \"Second Sister must have been held up by other matters, so she had Zhenyue write it for her.\"","Chen Yi hummed in agreement, folding the letter. \"The summer grain in the Three Towns was burned not long ago,\" he said with a smile. \"It’s only right for her to be on guard.\"","He paused for a moment before continuing, \"I’ll go deliver the festival gifts to the various families shortly. We can’t neglect our courtesies, after all.\"","Xiao Wan’er hesitated. \"Why don’t I go with you, Brother-in-law?\"","Chen Yi considered it for a moment and didn’t refuse. He nodded. \"Thank you, Eldest Sister.\"","\"It’s no trouble. I was heading out anyway, and it’s just a short walk.\"","\"Then let’s go. The sooner we leave, the sooner we’ll be back.\"","Xiao Jinghong’s decision not to return to Shu State didn’t surprise Chen Yi.","Beyond the security of the Three Towns’ grain supply, which he had already mentioned, the Wu Mountain Mutual Market being built with the Mountain Race was also a top priority that could not be neglected.","Furthermore, with the Old Master’s scheme, having Xiao Jinghong command the Three Towns’ military from afar would also better protect the Xiao Family.","But as Chen Yi pieced this all together, he couldn’t help but sigh inwardly.","He had originally thought that by dealing with Xiao Dongchen and forcing the second branch of the Xiao Family into exile, things would become easier for the Old Master and Xiao Jinghong.","Now, it seemed they still had a long way to go.","「Throughout the afternoon.」","Chen Yi and Xiao Wan’er hurried around Shu State City, delivering gifts.","Most of the gifts were for key officials in Shu State’s various Government Offices, as well as for some of the Noble Families with centuries-old lineages.","The gifts were modest; it was the thought that counted.","To his wry amusement, however, though they had set out with half a cart of festival gifts, they returned with the cart just as full as before.","The members of those families and the officials from the Government Offices had been anything but reserved with their reciprocal gifts.","If Chen Yi and Xiao Wan’er hadn’t turned down many of them, the carriage would have been piled even higher with assorted items.","As evening approached, they finally finished delivering the gifts and started for home.","「On the way back.」","Seeing that Chen Yi had grown somewhat quiet, Xiao Wan’er asked hesitantly, \"Tomorrow is the Mid-Autumn Festival. What are your plans, Brother-in-law?\"","Chen Yi glanced at her, then turned his gaze out the window. \"If there’s nothing pressing at the estate, I plan to take Xiaodie to the poetry gathering at the academy tomorrow.\"","\"The poetry gathering... C-can I come along too?\""]},{"number":282,"title":"Chapter 282 - 212: Why Would a Man Go to a Painted Boat and Not Call for a Lady?","paragraphs":["Faced with Xiao Wan’er’s hopeful gaze, Chen Yi naturally couldn’t bring himself to refuse.","Besides, the poetry gathering at Guiyun Academy was already expecting the young ladies of Shu State’s Noble Families. One more in Xiao Wan’er wouldn’t make a difference.","\"If you can come, Big Sis, Guiyun Academy is sure to shine all the brighter tomorrow night.\"","Xiao Wan’er’s face lit up, realizing she could attend the poetry gathering too.","But after the initial joy, a touch of hesitation crept in.","\"But I... it’s my first time attending a poetry gathering like this... Do I need to prepare anything?\"","Chen Yi knew she was feeling insecure and teased her with a smile, \"All you need to do is show up in your finest attire, Big Sis.\"","\"Even if you just sit there and do nothing, no one else could possibly outshine you.\"","Xiao Wan’er blushed. \"You’re exaggerating.\"","\"How am I?\"","\"Tomorrow will be your first time attending a poetry gathering. If Mr. Yue Ming and the others find out, they’ll be overjoyed. Why would they possibly give you a hard time?\"","\"Really?\"","\"Of course.\"","Half-convinced, Xiao Wan’er asked, \"Then tell me, what usually happens at these poetry gatherings?\"","Chen Yi chuckled, at a loss for words, then began to describe the general schedule for the Mid-Autumn poetry gathering.","Fortunately, Li Huai’gu, Mr. Yue Ming, and the others had given him a rough outline; otherwise, he wouldn’t have been able to provide much detail either.","\"...It’s mostly paying homage to the moon, admiring the moon, and reciting or composing poetry and couplets.\"","\"There will be many people there tomorrow, including quite a few ladies. If you have a good piece of writing, Big Sis, you can certainly present it for Mr. Yue Ming and the others to critique.\"","Xiao Wan’er subconsciously shrank back, her expression less that of a high-born young lady and more like the cute and pretty girl next door.","\"I’m not skilled in poetry. I’d rather not make a fool of myself.\"","\"It’s fine if you don’t write anything. My older brother is bringing Cui Qingwu tomorrow, and Brother Huai’gu’s wife will also be there. If you get bored, you can always keep them company.\"","\"They don’t compose poetry either?\"","\"They probably won’t, hmm... At least, I know Brother Huai’gu’s wife doesn’t compose poetry.\"","\"Cui Qingwu is from the Qinghe Cui Family, so she might know a thing or two.\"","\"Miss Cui? She’s here in Shu State?\"","\"You didn’t know, Big Sis? She’s been in Shu State for some time now, though she’s been staying with my older brother.\"","\"Come to think of it, the two of them are also engaged.\"","\"Is that so...\"","Thinking back, Chen Yi realized he had never actually told Xiao Wan’er about Cui Qingwu’s arrival in Shu State.","Part of the reason was Cui Qingwu’s identity as Simurgh Phoenix of the Hidden Guard, and part was that she had been very quiet since arriving in Shu State.","It was strange, though. To this day, Chen Yi didn’t quite understand why Cui Qingwu had joined the Hidden Guard, nor did he know her reasons for coming to Shu State alone.","It was as if she had come solely for Chen Yunfan.","’Is this a case of following her man wherever he goes?’","But he had once heard Chen Yunfan express his dissatisfaction with that engagement.","\"If you have any concerns, Big Sis, you can bring Wuge, Huatang, and the others along tomorrow night. It’ll just be for a bit of fun, anyway.\"","Xiao Wan’er’s expression relaxed upon hearing this. She nodded and said, \"Alright.\"","\"It will also be Wuge’s first time at a poetry gathering. I’ll have to keep an eye on him.\"","But as soon as she said it, she caught Chen Yi’s mischievous gaze. A faint blush crept onto her stunning face, and she trailed off, unable to continue.","Growing up, her poor health had rarely allowed her to attend any lively events outside the Xiao Mansion.","Poetry gatherings, Lantern Festival fairs, the Mid-Autumn Festival, the Spring Festival—she had missed them all, year after year.","If her health hadn’t improved, if she didn’t feel that bone-deep chill as much as before, she would have likely chosen to remain in Jiaxing Garden this time as well.","But as Xiao Wan’er’s thoughts drifted, she couldn’t help but recall Chen Yi’s teasing, and a sense of playful indignation welled up inside her.","’This man is such a tease.’","’He knows full well I have so little experience with the outside world, yet he still teases me like this.’","Chen Yi more or less guessed what was on Xiao Wan’er’s mind and decided not to tease her any further. He lifted the carriage curtain and glanced outside.","It was nearly dusk, and the sky had grown much dimmer.","The streets, however, were bustling with activity.","Pedestrians thronged the sides of the road, pouring into the various shops in groups.","Buying lanterns, new clothes, mooncakes... Most were making preparations for the Mid-Autumn Festival tomorrow night.","In contrast, the various government offices on duty in Shu State City weren’t nearly as relaxed.","Soldiers of the City Guard Army were stationed on every major street and alley.","Numerous Imprisonment Officers from the Imprisonment Department were also patrolling the area, on guard against any potential incidents.","The number of government officials deployed on South Street, where the various Government Offices were located, was several times higher than anywhere else.","After watching for a moment, just as Chen Yi was about to close the curtain, his eyes suddenly caught sight of a familiar figure—","It was none other than Liu Zhaoxue, the eldest legitimate daughter of the main branch of the Liu Family, dressed in red and with a beauty that rivaled even Xiao Wan’er’s and Xiao Jinghong’s.","She was currently standing on South Street, not far from the Dingyuan Marquis’s Mansion, sizing up a street-facing storefront.","The shop was festooned with lanterns and streamers, and the lanterns outside all bore the word \"Xinglin.\"","Beneath the central eaves hung a plaque, veiled by a red cloth.","’Xinglin Hall?’","The two words surfaced in Chen Yi’s mind, and his gaze immediately fell upon Liu Zhaoxue.","’Liu Wen is dead, yet Liu Zhaoxue hasn’t returned to the Jing State Liu Family to mourn. How can she have the heart to stay in Shu State and run Xinglin Hall?’","Chen Yi found the situation rather strange.","’It seems Liu Zhaoxue is determined to make something of herself here in Shu State.’","Then again, upon further reflection, Chen Yi realized her choice was likely born of a certain helplessness.","He had previously heard that the Jing State Liu Family intended to marry her to Xiao Xuanshuo.","Perhaps it was this that had driven her to defy convention and remain in Shu State.","Beside him, Xiao Wan’er had also spotted Liu Zhaoxue, and the smile on her face gradually faded. She was clearly recalling some unpleasant past events.","Even though she knew Liu Wen was dead and had been connected to the burning of the Three Towns’ summer grain, she still remembered everything that had happened that day in Fengchun Building."]},{"number":283,"title":"Chapter 283 - 212: Why Would a Man Go to a Painted Boat and Not Call for a Maiden? (Part 2)","paragraphs":["How could someone as intelligent as Xiao Wan’er not have figured out Liu Zhaoxue’s intentions for having Liu Wen tag along at the banquet?","Now, seeing Liu Zhaoxue again, her feelings were complicated.","It wasn’t resentment, so much as the vexation that comes with being deceived.","That was especially true since Liu Wen had not only been insolent toward her that day, but had also dragged Chen Yi into it.","Xiao Wan’er felt that since she had been the one to invite Chen Yi to Fengchun Building, she was not only upset but also felt rather guilty about what had happened.","Just then, Chen Yi closed the carriage curtain. Noticing Xiao Wan’er’s gaze, he smiled and said, \"I’m surprised Liu Zhaoxue is still in Shu State.\"","Xiao Wan’er pressed her lips together and turned her head. \"I heard about it from Sister Wan a couple of days ago.\"","\"The Jing State Liu Family intends to open Xinglin Hall branches all over Shu State. They’ve specifically ordered Liu Zhaoxue to stay here and oversee things for the time being.\"","Chen Yi’s interest was piqued. \"Temporarily?\"","Xiao Wan’er hummed in agreement. \"I heard Liu Hong himself gave those instructions in front of some people at the Governor’s Office.\"","\"Perhaps someone else from the Jing State Liu Family will come to replace Liu Zhaoxue and take over the expansion of Xinglin Hall in the future.\"","Chen Yi frowned to himself.","If he remembered correctly, the agreement reached when the old master met with Liu Hong had explicitly stated that the Jing State Liu Family was not to send any more people to Shu State.","Liu Zhaoxue staying in Shu State was already her exploiting a loophole in the agreement.","If more of the Liu family were to come, wouldn’t that be a blatant slap in the old master’s face?","With this in mind, Chen Yi asked pointedly, \"This time, Xinglin Hall won’t just be targeting our few Medicine Halls, but every medicine hall and apothecary in Shu State.\"","\"Do you know how the people at Wan Family Medicine Hall intend to respond?\"","Xiao Wan’er shook her head. \"I don’t know.\"","\"Between the expansion of Hundred Herbs Hall and matters with the Medical Dao Academy, I haven’t been paying much attention to the Medicine Hall side of things lately.\"","After a pause, she looked at Chen Yi and said, \"After the Mid-Autumn Festival, perhaps you could go and ask?\"","\"Me?\"","\"Yes. Just to get a better sense of Xinglin Hall’s plans, so we can prepare a response in advance.\"","Chen Yi considered this for a moment, then nodded. \"Alright.\"","’Xinglin Hall’s expansion into Shu State will probably follow their old playbook.’","’They’ll win through their Physicians’ exquisite Medical Skill, their inherited formulas, and a supply of low-cost medicinal herbs from their backers.’","’As long as Xinglin Hall doesn’t encroach on Hundred Herbs Hall’s business, there’s nothing to worry about.’","Seeing him agree, a smile touched Xiao Wan’er’s lips as she said:","\"After the Mid-Autumn Festival, I’d like to make a trip to the fiefdom. If you’re free, you should come with me.\"","\"To choose a site?\"","\"Yes. The first step is always the hardest. The Medical Dao Academy has to start somewhere...\"","「Meanwhile.」","Liu Zhaoxue glanced at the sky, then ordered her subordinates to make the necessary preparations.","\"Uncle Lin, we’re opening after the Mid-Autumn Festival. Make sure our Physicians are well-rested.\"","\"And as for Elder Chang, please pay him extra attention. Since the other Medical Saint Hands aren’t coming, he is the public face of Xinglin Hall in Shu State.\"","\"Yes, Third Miss.\"","Liu Zhaoxue nodded and turned to the next person. \"Uncle Fu, finalize the contracts with the herb merchants as soon as possible. Any delay could cause problems.\"","The older man, Shopkeeper Fu, had a troubled expression as he said:","\"There’s been a complication.\"","\"What kind of complication?\"","\"The merchants are out of the cheapest herbs our Xinglin Hall requires. They say their entire stock was sold to Hundred Herbs Hall in the West Market.\"","\"Furthermore, Hundred Herbs Hall has also bought up their entire supply of several quality herbs used as medicinal guides.\"","Liu Zhaoxue frowned. \"Not a single stalk?\"","Uncle Fu shook his head. \"None at all.\"","\"It’s my fault. I was so focused on stocking the expensive herbs that I neglected the others.\"","\"However, I’ve already written back to Jing State. The major merchants there still have plenty of inventory. It can be shipped to Shu State within half a month at most.\"","\"I can’t wait that long,\" Liu Zhaoxue said, her tone sharp with displeasure.","\"Arrange a meeting with those merchants for me tomorrow morning to negotiate a new contract. Tell them that whatever price Hundred Herbs Hall offered, Xinglin Hall will triple it.\"","’They’re just common, low-priced herbs, after all. She refused to believe those merchants would turn down good money.’","But Uncle Fu quickly tried to dissuade her. \"Third Miss, you mustn’t! You absolutely mustn’t do that.\"","\"Oh? And why not?\"","\"According to the merchants, Hundred Herbs Hall just signed a new contract with them for a massive quantity of herbs—enough to last them until the end of next year.\"","Liu Zhaoxue’s brows knitted together. \"How much?\"","Uncle Fu said hesitantly, \"An estimated two hundred thousand taels of silver.\"","\"They also added a specific penalty clause for breach of contract. Even if Xinglin Hall truly offered triple the price, the merchants wouldn’t agree.\"","Liu Zhaoxue fell silent after hearing his report.","Triple two hundred thousand taels is six hundred thousand, which was nearly all the silver she had on hand.","’She really had overestimated her own resources with that earlier boast.’","\"I recall that Hundred Herbs Hall sells various types of tea beverages, correct?\"","Uncle Fu nodded. \"You’re correct, Third Miss. Hundred Herbs Hall doesn’t focus on treatments by Physicians.\"","\"They only sell low-cost herbs and five types of potent medicinal teas.\"","\"It’s said that since they opened, they’ve earned a handsome sum of silver from those teas alone.\"","Liu Zhaoxue nodded slightly. Her gaze shifted toward the West Market as she said pensively:","\"Go buy some of their teas and bring them back. Have our Physicians study them and see if they can reverse-engineer the recipes.\"","Uncle Fu froze for a second. \"But...\"","\"Just do as I say.\"","\"Yes. This old servant will go at once.\"","After he left, Liu Zhaoxue took a deep breath to compose herself, then boarded her carriage to return to her residence.","After listening to Uncle Fu, one thing had become clear to her—","if she wanted to expand Xinglin Hall throughout Shu State, she wouldn’t just be competing with rivals like the Xiao Family Medicine Hall. Hundred Herbs Hall was now a hurdle she could not avoid."]},{"number":284,"title":"Chapter 284 - 212: Why Would a Man Go to a Painted Boat and Not Call for a Girl?","paragraphs":["’If I don’t prepare now, I’ll surely be at a disadvantage later.’","Just as Liu Zhaoxue was mulling this over, she suddenly heard a familiar, sinister laugh from ahead.","\"Have you run into some trouble, Miss Zhaoxue?\"","Liu Zhaoxue snapped out of her thoughts. She frowned at the driver in front of her. \"Elder Yan? What are you doing here?\"","The man was none other than Yan Fusha of the Five Poison Sect.","\"Don’t worry, Miss Zhaoxue. Your driver has only fallen asleep. He’s not in any danger.\"","\"Now, why don’t you tell me what trouble you’re in? The sooner we resolve it, the better for us both.\"","A flicker of annoyance crossed Liu Zhaoxue’s eyes, but her tone was calm. \"You needn’t trouble yourself with the management of the Medicine Hall, Elder Yan.\"","\"You’re mistaken, Miss Zhaoxue. The Five Poison Sect is counting on Xinglin Hall’s successful expansion before we can begin our plans.\"","\"Don’t forget, you and I are in the same boat now.\"","But before Liu Zhaoxue could respond, Yan Fusha’s tone shifted.","\"However, I have faith in your abilities, Miss Zhaoxue. I’m certain Xinglin Hall will flourish in Shu State.\"","Liu Zhaoxue explained reluctantly, \"Now that my second brother is dead, my family has grown suspicious of me. It’s not a good time to stir up more trouble.\"","Yan Fusha chuckled. \"Ah, if you put it that way, Miss Zhaoxue, then I understand.\"","\"Since you don’t want me to get involved, I’ll wait. I’m in no hurry.\"","\"As it happens, I’ve discovered some interesting things about that Mr. Qingzhou over the past couple of days. I was just about to test the waters and see what he’s really made of.\"","Liu Zhaoxue’s heart skipped a beat. \"Chen Yi?\"","\"What did you find out about him?\"","\"On the night the Three Towns’ summer grain was burned, he wasn’t at the Xiao Family estate. He was on a Painted Boat at Quchi.\"","\"But I made inquiries at the Painted Boats. He didn’t hire any female companions for the evening, not even the Cultured Courtesans.\"","At this, Yan Fusha asked, \"Tell me, don’t you find it suspicious for a grown man to go to a Painted Boat and not summon a few ladies for company?\"","Liu Zhaoxue paused, then replied with a touch of displeasure, \"Forgive me, Elder Yan, but I know nothing of such dalliances.\"","Yan Fusha smiled. \"If you hadn’t repeatedly reminded me that there’s more to Mr. Qingzhou than meets the eye, Miss Zhaoxue, I wouldn’t have become so suspicious.\"","\"How do you plan to test him?\"","\"I’ll capture him and interrogate him. Then we’ll know.\"","Liu Zhaoxue pursed her lips. Knowing he had already made up his mind, she didn’t try to dissuade him any further.","\"Just be sure not to reveal your identity.\"","\"Don’t worry, Miss Zhaoxue. I may be a crude man, but I know his status is special. I won’t let him jeopardize our grand plan.\"","\"Besides, he’s just a scholar who knows nothing of Martial Arts. Once he’s in my grasp, he’ll be powerless to make any waves.\"","\"Let’s hope so...\"","...","「Xiao Family, Spring Lotus Garden.」","Xiao Wuge was overjoyed to learn that he would be attending the Guiyun Academy’s poetry gathering the next evening.","After dinner, he continued to pester Chen Yi with all sorts of questions.","Unlike Xiao Wan’er, Xiao Wuge showed no signs of nervousness. On the contrary, he was eager to go.","\"Brother-in-law, do you think I could compose a poem, too?\"","\"Brother-in-law, if my poem receives thunderous applause, will Big Sis be happy enough to let me take a few days off?\"","\"Brother-in-law...\"","Chen Yi cut him off with a sigh. \"Tomorrow, you are to do nothing. Just stick with your sister.\"","’Trying to be a child prodigy like Fang Zhongyong, of all things.’","Xiao Wuge’s little face fell. \"Can I stick with you, Brother-in-law?\"","\"No. Your sister is a little worried. Staying with her will help put her at ease.\"","\"What’s Big Sis worried about?\"","\"She’s probably just a bit apprehensive, since it’s her first time attending a poetry gathering.\"","Xiao Wuge paused for a moment, then broke into a grin. \"So even Big Sis gets scared sometimes.\"","Chen Yi patted his head. \"You’d better not say that in front of her. You’re asking for a beating.\"","Xiao Wuge nodded eagerly, chuckling. \"Then I’ll be sure to take good care of Big Sis tomorrow.\"","\"Off to bed with you. We have a lot to do around the estate in the morning.\"","\"Okay...\"","After Xiao Wuge went back to his room to sleep, Chen Yi changed into light sleepwear, sat cross-legged on his bed, and began his Cultivation of the Four Symbols Skill.","He cultivated until the hour of the Rat—","[Daily Intelligence · Profound-rank Top Grade: At the Hour of the Dog (7-9 PM) on the Mid-Autumn Festival, attend the Guiyun Academy poetry gathering. A small Opportunity can be obtained.]","Chen Yi awoke from his Cultivation. He glanced at the two lines of large, golden text and pursed his lips slightly before getting out of bed. Picking up his Five-section Spear, he headed to the Purple Bamboo Forest to practice his Technique.","In another four hours, Xiao Wan’er would be leading the women of the household in worshiping the moon and honoring their ancestors.","He still had plenty of time.","But just as he arrived at the Purple Bamboo Forest, he sensed a slight disturbance nearby and frowned.","\"Who’s there?\"","As if expecting to be discovered, a woman’s voice cried out, \"Take this!\"","A crisp JINGLE JINGLE followed.","Chen Yi got a clear look at the newcomer. After a brief moment of surprise, he smashed his fist down.","The fierce, domineering pressure, as heavy as a mountain, instantly flattened the newcomer to the ground.","Immediately, a cry for mercy rang out:","\"Brother-in-law, ow, ow, ow...\""]},{"number":285,"title":"Chapter 285 - 213: Emperor’s Heart Skill","paragraphs":["The newcomer was no stranger.","It was Pei Guanli, the very person Chen Yi had entrusted to go to the Wu Mountain Mutual Market and inform Xiao Jinghong that the Three Towns’ summer grain supply had been attacked.","He had thought the Tiger Girl wouldn’t be back until after the Mid-Autumn Festival, so he never expected her to come running back now.","It was quite a surprise.","Just then, Pei Guanli lifted her little head and looked at him pitifully. \"Brother-in-law, it hurts...\"","Chen Yi snapped back to his senses, retracted his Fist Intent, and asked with a smile, \"When did you get back?\"","\"You didn’t knock out all the mansion guards to sneak in this time, did you?\"","Pei Guanli felt the pressure on her body vanish and immediately scrambled to her feet.","\"No, no! Brother-in-law, I was extra careful coming in this time.\"","Chen Yi looked at Pei Guanli, dressed only in Night Clothes and carrying a bundle, her feet still bare below her knees. He nodded.","\"That’s good.\"","\"Otherwise, if you had alerted the Armored Warriors and the people from the Punishment Hall, you definitely wouldn’t have escaped a flogging this time.\"","The Marquis’s Mansion’s Punishment Hall was now controlled by Xiao Xuanshuo, and he was nothing like the Second Branch when they were in charge.","In a way, his second uncle from the First Branch was even more unreasonable than that old codger Xiao Wang.","Brushing the dirt and leaves off herself, Pei Guanli grinned. \"If they dared to touch me, I guarantee they’d regret it.\"","\"I brought back a lot of treasures this time.\"","Chen Yi walked over and plucked a leaf from the ends of her hair. \"What kind of treasures?\"","Pei Guanli patted the bundle hanging from her waist and replied, \"Gu Insects and Poison.\"","\"Ah Ma said that Shu State isn’t very peaceful lately, so she told me to bring extra for self-defense.\"","Chen Yi’s heart stirred. He recalled the Five Poison Sect’s arrival in Shu State and realized he’d apparently forgotten to pass this news on to the Mountain Race.","He wasn’t sure if Granny Shan’s comment about Shu State being \"not peaceful\" was referring to the Five Poison Sect or the Xiao Family’s affairs.","Chen Yi temporarily pushed his doubts aside and asked, \"Then you didn’t run into my wife on your way back, did you?\"","\"Sister Jinghong? No, no.\"","Pei Guanli lifted her head proudly, a sly smile spreading across her round face.","\"While Sister Jinghong was away rescuing the Three Towns, I quickly slipped back to my clan.\"","\"Then, when I figured enough time had passed, I secretly snuck out of the clan again.\"","\"After I got to the Prefecture City and heard Sister Jinghong wasn’t around, I came to find you, Brother-in-law.\"","Chen Yi tapped her smooth forehead. \"Aren’t you the clever one.\"","Pei Guanli rubbed her forehead, a slightly embarrassed look on her face. \"Brother-in-law, actually... there was a small mishap this time.\"","\"At the time, I...\"","Pei Guanli recounted, in full detail, the events of her trip to the Mutual Market to see Xiao Jinghong.","\"Brother-in-law, do you think Sister Jinghong will suspect you?\"","Chen Yi thought for a moment, then shook his head. \"Not for now.\"","\"But she’s probably even more certain now that the letter you delivered came from a questionable source.\"","With Xiao Jinghong’s intelligence, the moment she realized Pei Guanli was deliberately avoiding her, she was bound to figure a few things out.","A dejected look appeared on Pei Guanli’s face. She said in a low voice, \"I’m sorry, Brother-in-law. I-I screwed things up.\"","Chen Yi patted her head, comforting her with a smile. \"It’s not your fault. I was the one who didn’t think it through.\"","In such an urgent situation, it was already a feat that he’d managed to find Pei Guanli and have her successfully notify Xiao Jinghong.","How could he have worried about all the other details?","Fortunately, Pei Guanli had handled it well this time and hadn’t come face-to-face with Xiao Jinghong, which gave him some time to salvage the situation.","Pei Guanli looked up at him. \"Really?\"","Chen Yi nodded. \"If my wife had caught you this time, that would have been the worst-case scenario.\"","He didn’t believe for a second that the Tiger Girl could withstand an interrogation from Xiao Jinghong.","It would be a miracle if she didn’t spill the beans on the spot.","Pei Guanli giggled. \"Actually, it was all thanks to Ah Ma for reminding me.\"","\"Granny Shan? She knows about this?\"","\"Yup. Ah Ma is super sharp.\"","\"When she saw me return to the clan with my brother, she guessed I’d gotten into trouble outside, so...\"","Pei Guanli paused, sticking her tongue out slightly. \"But I promise, I absolutely did not mention you to Ah Ma, Brother-in-law.\"","Chen Yi shook his head. ’It doesn’t matter whether she mentioned me or not.’","’People like Granny Shan are the same as Xiao Jinghong. Once they grow suspicious, no ordinary method can cover it up.’","\"You’ve been traveling for so long, you must be tired. Go get some rest first.\"","\"It just so happens there’s a poetry gathering at the academy tomorrow night. I’ll take you along for fun.\"","\"A poetry gathering? Awesome, awesome! I want to go!\"","\"Brother-in-law, let me tell you, I was about to die of boredom back in the clan.\"","\"Ah Ma insisted on teaching me how to concoct Poisons and raise new Gu Insects...\"","Before long, Pei Guanli was resting in Xiao Jinghong’s wooden building.","Perhaps because she had been traveling for days on end, it wasn’t long before she fell into a deep sleep.","Chen Yi straightened up a bit. He then recalled the letter from Xiao Jinghong today, where she’d asked him to write out some calligraphy, have it mounted, and hang it in her room. A smile couldn’t help but touch his lips.","’Magpie Bridge Immortal, Thoughts of a Summer Night, Two Thoughts on a Summer Night, and Thoughts of Summer...’","’With so many poems, I wonder if they’ll be enough to make my wife go easy on me after she finds out the truth.’","’Probably not,’ he figured.","Xiao Jinghong was magnanimous, but it depended on the matter at hand.","Putting himself in her shoes, if he were the one being kept in the dark like this, he’d be upset too.","A simple beating would be getting off light.","He’d deserve to be strung up and beaten at least three times.","An image of Xiao Jinghong stringing him up in the Punishment Hall and whipping him flashed inexplicably through Chen Yi’s mind, and he couldn’t help but shiver.","’Forget it. I should first think of a way to keep this hidden for now.’","’At the very least, I have to drag it out until after this whole mess has blown over and my wife is in a good mood.’","’Then again, I might get an even worse beating then...’","As these thoughts ran through his mind, Chen Yi saw that it was getting late. He gave up on the idea of practicing his Techniques and had no choice but to return to his room to continue his Cultivation of the Four Symbols Skill."]},{"number":286,"title":"Chapter 286 - 213: Emperor’s Heart Skill (2)","paragraphs":["...","In the hours before dawn, the sky was still dark.","The moon was bright in the night sky, and the stars were few.","Even though it was the night before the Mid-Autumn Festival, the moon could still be considered full.","The brilliant moonlight spilled down, blanketing all of Shu State in a silvery sheen.","It was a dim, hazy, yet uniquely beautiful sight.","At this moment, within the residences along the streets and alleys of the Prefecture City, a faint clamor began to rise.","Amidst the rising and falling sounds, one could faintly hear the voices of women worshipping the moon and praying for blessings.","\"We pray for favorable weather...\"","\"We pray for our families’ health and safety...\"","The aroma of mooncakes and wine also drifted on the wind, enough to make some of the younger maids’ mouths water.","Xiaodie was one of them.","Although she wasn’t qualified to join Xiao Wan’er in the moon worship, she had to wake up early to help arrange the offering altar, table, and chairs.","After two hours of bustling about, the stomach she had filled last night was empty again.","So now, as Xiaodie stood by the central courtyard’s covered walkway, the scent of the offerings made her stomach go GRUMBLE GRUMBLE.","Even Cui’er and Juan’er, who were standing beside her, heard it clearly and began to tease her in low, laughing voices:","\"Xiaodie, didn’t the Second Young Master-in-law give you dinner last night?\"","\"Hasn’t it been that long since you ate? Hungry again already?\"","Xiaodie blushed and offered a word of defense for Chen Yi, but she didn’t deny the fact that she was hungry.","’But I really am hungry!’","Shen Huatang heard them and glanced back, saying softly,","\"Just hang on a little longer. Once the Young Lady finishes the moon worship, we can get something to eat.\"","Xiaodie blinked and asked, \"Sister Huatang, are you hungry too?\"","Shen Huatang opened her mouth, then decided to take back her words of comfort.","’As a practitioner of Martial Arts, once you’ve trained your body to its peak, enduring hunger is the most basic of skills.’","’Never mind a few hours without food and water; she could last for days and nights without eating or drinking.’","Seeing that she had fallen silent, Xiaodie sheepishly ducked her head and hid behind Cui’er and Juan’er.","She wasn’t a complete fool; she finally realized that Shen Huatang didn’t get hungry as easily as she did.","Fortunately, the moon and ancestor worship ceremony concluded just as dawn approached at the hour of the Rabbit.","When the altar was being cleared, Xiao Wan’er distributed the mooncakes, melons, and fruits to the various household courtyards, letting everyone share in the good fortune.","Xiaodie received a whole armful.","She got five or six mooncakes, two bags of pastries, half a pressed duck, and some wine and tea.","She couldn’t carry it all, so she had to thread a rope through everything, wrap it around her hand, and cradle the bundle in her arms, returning to the Spring Lotus Garden out of breath.","Only after placing everything on the table did Xiaodie let out a long breath and wipe the sweat from her forehead.","’Time to go wake the Young Master and the Master.’","But as Xiaodie said this, her eyes were glued to the mooncakes, pastries, and other treats.","She swallowed hard and finally made a decision.","After carefully looking left and right to make sure no one was around, she casually grabbed a mooncake and stuffed it into her mouth.","\"So good... mph...\"","Just then, a voice came from behind her.","\"Sister Xiaodie!\"","Xiaodie jumped in fright, hastily covering her mouth and turning to respond with a muffled, \"Mph!\"","When she saw who it was, her eyes flew wide. \"Mph-mph-mph?\"","Pei Guanli noticed something was amiss. Her eyes twinkled as she grinned mischievously. \"Aha, Sister Xiaodie, you’re sneaking food! I’m going to tell Brother-in-law.\"","\"Mph-mph, mph-mph...\"","Xiaodie shook her head again and again, her hand clamped over her mouth as she chewed and chewed with all her might.","Unfortunately, this was the problem with five-nut mooncakes: the filling was dense and easy to choke on.","She chewed several times, but the food in her mouth didn’t seem to get any smaller. She was choking, and her face turned bright red.","Seeing this, Pei Guanli forgot about teasing her and quickly poured her a cup of water.","\"Eat slowly, slow down... I was just teasing you.\"","After finally managing to swallow, Xiaodie patted her chest and caught her breath.","She was a mess of fright, choking, and astonishment.","\"Wh-when did you get back?\"","\"Last night.\"","Seeing that she had recovered, Pei Guanli sat down at the table, picked up a pastry for herself, and popped it into her mouth, speaking as she ate,","\"We can talk in a bit. I need to get something in my stomach first.\"","\"You have no idea how careful I’ve been these past few days, terrified of being seen.\"","Xiaodie looked at her in confusion. \"Careful? Is someone after you?\"","\"Of course—\"","Pei Guanli caught herself and quickly said, \"No.\"","She then explained, \"I was just worried I wouldn’t make it back in time to celebrate the Mid-Autumn Festival with you all, so I rushed here without stopping to eat.\"","Xiaodie gave her a skeptical look. Just as she was about to say more, Chen Yi’s voice came from upstairs. She quickly called out a reply and ran up.","Pei Guanli breathed a sigh of relief, muttering something about ’thank goodness for Brother-in-law’.","Not long after, Chen Yi and Xiao Wuge came downstairs, neatly dressed.","Because of the poetry gathering tonight, both were dressed in magnificent attire.","They wore matching black robes with crossed lapels and Jade Belts.","The difference was that Xiao Wuge’s collar was embroidered with gold thread, and a Jade Pendant engraved with the character for \"Xiao\" hung from his waist.","Pei Guanli looked from one to the other, then gave a thumbs-up with her greasy hand. \"Brother-in-law, you look handsome.\"","Xiao Wuge cleared his throat and asked, \"Sister Guanli, what about me?\"","\"You... are a little less handsome than Brother-in-law.\"","Pei Guanli expected Xiao Wuge to be upset.","But to her surprise, Xiao Wuge listened and said cheerfully, \"Then I’m not bad either.\"","Chen Yi patted him on the shoulder and said with a laugh, \"Don’t spend too much time learning from your Sister Guanli, or you’ll turn into a fool.\"","Pei Guanli immediately puffed out her cheeks. \"Brother-in-law, I’m not a fool!\"","\"Alright, let me rephrase.\"","\"Wuge, don’t learn from your Sister Guanli, or you’ll become less intelligent.\"","\"I am not... un-in-telligent! You stink, Brother-in-law!\"","Leisurely days were always leisurely and pleasant.","It might have been a redundant statement, but it was a perfect reflection of Chen Yi’s current mood.","With the Jing State Liu Family in retreat and the Hidden Guard lying low, he finally had a rare moment of free time to relax.","So he spent the entire morning holed up in the Spring Lotus Garden, not going anywhere.","After breakfast, he went to the study to rewrite those four poems for Xiao Jinghong."]},{"number":287,"title":"Chapter 287 - 213: Emperor’s Heart Skill","paragraphs":["His Calligraphy Dao, having reached the Perfection Realm, made the four poems all the more dazzling.","As he unrolled them one by one, four distinct tableaus unfolded.","From time to time, a woman in red would appear in the illusory scenes.","It was none other than his wife, Xiao Jinghong.","Pei Guanli, Xiao Wuge, and the others watched with envy, clamoring for him to write them into a poem as well.","Chen Yi refused them all, and after finishing, he called it a day.","After instructing Xiaodie to have that mounter, Boss Dai, visit again after the Mid-Autumn Festival, he grabbed his homemade fishing rod and went straight to the pond.","Today was the Mid-Autumn Festival, a time for family reunion and joy.","As a live-in son-in-law, he was supposed to stay in his place and keep a low profile.","But just as Chen Yi finished putting bait on his hook, he heard Xiaodie’s frantic voice from outside.","\"Young Master, Young Master, something terrible has happened!\"","Chen Yi glanced back at her. Seeing her anxious expression, he furrowed his brow slightly and asked, \"What has you so flustered?\"","Xiaodie was so out of breath from running that she could barely speak. After a moment of patting her chest to catch her breath, she managed to say, haltingly:","\"The... The Capital Prefecture... an imperial edict has arrived! It says... to punish... the Old... Old Master... a-a six-month suspension of his salary.\"","Hearing this, Chen Yi’s brow smoothed out.","’The Hidden Guard must have reported the burning of the summer grain at Iron Wall Town and the conflict between the Xiao and Liu Families back to the Capital Prefecture.’","’It’s only natural that the Holy Emperor would be furious upon learning the truth.’","\"The edict only mentioned the salary suspension. Was there anything else?\"","Xiaodie nodded. \"Yes, they’re also requisitioning ten percent of the summer grain from the Three Towns. The Capital Commandery has been ordered to transport it to the Capital Prefecture.\"","Summer grain, ten percent.","Chen Yi thought for a moment and understanding dawned on him.","Ten percent wasn’t too much or too little; it fell right within the normal range for grain tax collection in a Border Town.","’But this punishment doesn’t feel like a punishment.’","’It’s more like a rap on the knuckles, a warning, and an act of balancing the scales.’","This time, in their conflict with the Liu Family, the Xiao Family had gained three hundred thousand silver coins. This not only compensated for the losses at Iron Wall Town but even left them with a surplus.","In contrast, the Jing State Liu Family had lost Liu Wen, forfeited three hundred thousand silver, and been forced to withdraw from Shu State.","On the surface, the Xiao Family had won a resounding victory.","But after this punishment from the Holy Emperor...","The ten-percent grain tax, amounting to two hundred thousand shi of grain, was worth roughly one hundred eighty thousand silver at current market prices.","Add to that the grain burned at Iron Wall Town...","The three hundred thousand silver coins the Xiao Family had gained were now pretty much gone.","’In other words, in the conflict between the Xiao and Liu Families, aside from forcing the Jing State Liu Family to promise to withdraw from Shu State, the Xiao Family had gained almost no other benefits.’","Which meant...","’After all my hard work, did I just end up balancing the Xiao Family’s books for them?’","At this thought, Chen Yi’s expression darkened.","’Damn it.’","If he didn’t still have the two hundred ninety thousand silver he’d \"liberated\" from Lou Yuxue, all his efforts would have been for nothing.","Seeing his expression, Xiaodie, who was standing to the side, couldn’t help but grow nervous as well.","\"Young Master, d-do you think something will... will happen to the family?\"","\"Just now, when I was coming back, so many people... so many people looked like the sky was falling.\"","Chen Yi snapped out of it and said irritably, \"What’s there to worry about?\"","\"Whether it’s the salary or the grain tax, it just means spending a bit more silver. Nothing bad will happen.\"","After hearing this, Xiaodie’s expression eased considerably. She patted her chest in lingering fear. \"Thank goodness, thank goodness. I knew it would be alright.\"","Chen Yi thought for a moment and asked, \"Besides that, the edict didn’t say anything else, did it?\"","\"Oh, right, there was more.\"","\"The Holy Emperor also bestowed a suit of armor upon the Old Master, saying something about it being the Mid-Autumn Festival and the rites and customs stipulating whatnot.\"","’Armor...’","Chen Yi recalled that the Old Master had been wearing a suit of armor when he went to see Liu Hong.","Now the Holy Emperor was bestowing another suit of armor. The implication was obvious.","The Holy Emperor was simply telling the Old Master—I know everything you have done in Shu State!","’Impressive. It really is impressive to be the Emperor.’","With just a few words, the fruits of Chen Yi’s half-month of painstaking planning were mostly wiped out.","And he’d given the Old Master a rap on the knuckles in the process.","\"Also, the Holy Emperor bestowed something on the Second Miss... a sword of some kind. He said it was a divine weapon, and that a great sword belongs to a hero.\"","After hearing Xiaodie’s report, Chen Yi curled his lip. \"Give a beating then hand out a sweet date. Classic Emperor’s Heart Skill.\"","’No doubt about it.’","’It’s definitely because Xiao Jinghong revealed her strength when she killed Black Tooth, attracting the attention of the one in the Imperial City.’","’\"A great sword belongs to a hero\" is just empty rhetoric.’","’If Xiao Jinghong’s Cultivation wasn’t so high, Shu State would be in even more chaos than it is now.’","’At that point, no matter how many great swords were sent, it would be like making a wedding dress for someone else to wear.’","Just then, Xiao Wan’er arrived at Spring Lotus Garden with Shen Huatang and others in tow.","\"Brother-in-law.\"","Chen Yi rose at her voice. Seeing that Xiao Wan’er’s expression was also tense and solemn, he guessed she only had a partial understanding of the Xiao Family’s current situation.","With that thought, Chen Yi performed a slight bow and greeted her with a smile.","\"The poetry gathering is still a ways off. What brings you here at this hour, Eldest Sister?\"","Xiao Wan’er shook her head and said worriedly, \"Just now, the Holy Emperor issued a decree to punish Grandfather. I... I don’t quite understand...\"","Chen Yi didn’t immediately try to comfort her. Instead, his gaze fell on the Sword Box in Shen Huatang’s hands behind her. He raised an eyebrow and asked, \"Is that the great sword bestowed by the Holy Emperor?\"","Xiao Wan’er was taken aback. She glanced behind her, then nodded hesitantly. \"The Holy Emperor bestowed it upon Second Sister.\"","\"Let me see.\"","Without waiting for an answer, Chen Yi took the Sword Box from Shen Huatang, removed the Long Sword from within, and examined it.","\"Not bad. It is indeed a divine weapon.\"","Most weapons of this era were forged by famous smiths in the Jianghu. While it was a cliché to describe them as sharp enough to cut a falling hair, it was no exaggeration.","However, with the existence of Martial Arts, the effectiveness of a divine weapon depended on who wielded it.","Take the one in Chen Yi’s hands, for example—it was three chi and three cun long, weighed thirty jin, and was three fingers wide at the blade, making it a bit wider and thicker than a typical Long Sword."]},{"number":288,"title":"Chapter 288 - 213: Emperor’s Heart Skill (4)","paragraphs":["But in Chen Yi’s hands, it would at most be used like a long blade.","Seeing him cradling the sword and studying it, Xiao Wan’er knew he had already heard about the Holy Emperor’s edict. Her expression grew somber as she spoke:","\"Grandfather said that after this, the family’s finances will be a bit tight. I’m afraid the matter of the Medical Dao Academy... will have to be postponed for a while.\"","Chen Yi paused, then looked at her with a smile. \"I don’t think we need to postpone it.\"","\"Huh?\"","\"The revenue from the tea drinks sold at the Medicine Halls should be arriving soon. Judging by last month’s figures, it should be at least ten to twenty thousand taels of silver.\"","\"Even after deducting all the expenses, the household should still have a considerable amount of silver left. That would be just enough to build the Medical Dao Academy, wouldn’t it?\"","Xiao Wan’er opened her mouth to speak. \"But... but, Grandfather...\"","Chen Yi put away the Long Sword and waved his hand. \"What the Old Master needs isn’t just ten or twenty thousand taels of silver. He isn’t counting on the family.\"","\"He, like the Old Mistress, has his mind set on the Mutual Market.\"","It was like someone who owed a mountain of debt to a bank.","When the news first broke, his friends and family might have thought about helping him chip in.","But once they learned he owed an astronomical sum, they didn’t even bother trying to pool their money.","It was no use.","The Xiao Family treasury, which Xiao Wan’er controlled, was in a similar situation.","Even if she emptied out all the silver, it wouldn’t be enough to fill the massive deficit of the Dingyuan Army.","That being the case, it was better to use the silver elsewhere.","Hearing this, Xiao Wan’er didn’t know whether to feel happy or worried.","’Come to think of it, what Chen Yi said did make sense.’","But she still had reservations about actually spending the money to build the Medical Dao Academy.","She was worried the household would run short on money later, and also that the academy would be a waste of funds.","Chen Yi could guess what she was thinking, so he continued to reassure her, \"Money is something you earn, not something you save.\"","\"The Medical Dao Academy will certainly have some initial costs, but once it’s established and gains momentum, the benefits will be even greater.\"","Xiao Wan’er’s eyes were fixed on him, her expression clearly showing she wanted him to elaborate.","\"Think about it. The people who come to study the Medical Dao and its skills will have to pay some tuition, right?\"","\"And if we have a Medical Saint Hand in residence, it would be reasonable to charge double the fee, wouldn’t it?\"","\"That’s one source of income right there.\"","\"Second, we could have the academy research new formulas. We could then partner with other Medicine Halls, or have the Xiao Family Medicine Hall manage them exclusively.\"","\"And another thing...\"","Chen Yi was really going to great lengths to dispel Xiao Wan’er’s worries and convince her to part with the money.","Most people in this era were like that.","They lacked the concept that \"money is earned, not saved,\" and they also lacked the methods to do so.","If Chen Yi were the Old Master and in control of the Xiao Family, he could think of a thousand ways to make the Xiao Family a large sum of money in a short amount of time.","Hundred Herbs Hall was a prime example.","Fortunately, Xiao Wan’er trusted him. After his repeated attempts at persuasion, she reluctantly nodded. \"I’ll listen to you.\"","Chen Yi’s mouth was dry from all the talking. He signaled for Xiaodie to brew some tea and led Xiao Wan’er to a pavilion to rest.","\"How is the Old Master’s mood? I hope his health hasn’t been affected.\"","Xiao Wan’er gently shook her head. \"Grandfather is fine.\"","\"He said he’d expected it. The blame for the loss of the summer grain at Iron Wall Town lies with the Dingyuan Army, so it’s only right that he receive some punishment.\"","\"He just didn’t expect the Holy Emperor’s penalty to be so severe.\"","Chen Yi grunted in agreement. \"It’s certainly not a small amount. Counting what was burned, they’ve lost twenty percent of their provisions in total.\"","\"If Governor Liu learns of this, he’ll probably laugh out loud.\"","Xiao Wan’er froze at his words, then gave him a strange look. \"There’s something you don’t know, Brother-in-law.\"","\"Hm?\"","\"The Holy Emperor issued an edict punishing Governor Liu today as well.\"","\"I heard that the imperial scribe, Eunuch Feng, announced the edict in front of everyone at the Governor’s Office. The wording was severe—it all but accused the Liu Family of plotting a rebellion.\"","On hearing this, Chen Yi couldn’t help but laugh.","Well then.","’Looks like the current Holy Emperor doesn’t miss a thing.’","’He obviously knew the Xiao and Liu Families had been negotiating in private, so he decided to expose it all and punish both sides equally.’","’Not only did he confiscate the Xiao Family’s gains, but he also ruined the Liu Family’s attempt to cover up the fact that Liu Wen burned the summer grain in the Three Towns.’","’Now, the Xiao and Liu Families had both lost their fig leaves. The whole world could see them for the joke they were.’","’Fortunately, the Xiao Family was the victim. At worst, their defenses were lax.’","’With Xiao Jinghong’s recent victory establishing his might, people wouldn’t dare to laugh too loudly.’","’The Jing State Liu Family, on the other hand, was in a different boat.’","’Plotting to burn a Border Town’s grain supply is tantamount to treason.’","’That the Liu Family wasn’t sentenced to the extermination of their nine relations was already a sign of the Holy Emperor’s mercy.’","’In these circumstances, the Liu Family was likely to face no small amount of trouble in the future.’","’Just the people looking to kick them while they’re down would be more than the Liu Family could handle.’","A smile crept onto Chen Yi’s face as he considered all this.","\"It all comes down to comparison.\"","\"Compared to the Liu Family, the Old Master and the Old Mistress are extremely fortunate to have only lost some silver. At least their reputation is intact.\"","Xiao Wan’er understood the difference, of course. She nodded. \"Grandfather said the same.\"","Relieved of her worries about the Medical Dao Academy, her expression brightened considerably. She relaxed and said:","\"The poetry gathering is approaching. Perhaps we should start preparing?\"","\"Prepare what?\"","\"Poetry, or something from the arts of Music, Chess, Calligraphy, and Painting. I was thinking of bringing something to the academy to share and discuss with everyone.\"","\"I don’t think that’s necessary... Eldest Sister, you can play the Zither?\"","Meeting his eager gaze, Xiao Wan’er hesitated before nodding. \"I studied it for a while, but...\"","\"...it’s been a long time since I’ve played.\"","Chen Yi’s interest was instantly piqued. \"How about you show off your skills before the poetry gathering, Eldest Sister?\"","\"As it happens, I’ve come across a few good compositions...\""]},{"number":289,"title":"Chapter 289 - 214: One Side Green, One Side Red","paragraphs":["「An hour later.」","Melodious zither music drifted from the Spring Lotus Garden.","It was like a school of fish swimming through a stream, like a bird gliding through a mountain valley, like a fine steed galloping freely across a boundless prairie.","Such was the ethereal, joyful melody of \"Carefree Travel.\"","Even though it was Xiao Wan’er’s first time playing the piece, and her performance was far from perfect, it still stirred the flowers, birds, fish, and insects of the Spring Lotus Garden into a lively dance.","As the sunlight shone down, flowers and blades of grass could be seen faintly fluttering in the air.","But scenery was just scenery.","Compared to Xiao Wan’er, who sat gracefully in the pavilion playing her Zither, it all paled in comparison.","Even classic idioms used to praise legendary beauties could not begin to describe her.","Her dark hair danced, her brows like distant mountains.","Her nose was delicate, her lips like jade, her cheeks as pure as driven snow.","In her red dress, her slender waist gave her a pliant, graceful figure, like a peony in full bloom.","Chen Yi stood to one side of the pavilion, watching Xiao Wan’er with a smile. The words of Li Taibai’s \"Qingping Tune\" surfaced in his mind.","Clouds yearn to be her dress, flowers to be her face;A spring breeze brushes the balustrade, rich with glistening dew.If not seen atop the Jade Mountain of the gods,Then she must be from the Jasper Terrace, met beneath the moon.","Though there was no spring breeze at this moment, and Xiao Wan’er was not the voluptuous Lady Yang, she truly looked like a goddess who had descended to the mortal world.","Graceful, noble, and extraordinarily beautiful.","Before long, the piece came to an end.","Xiao Wan’er raised her eyes slightly. Just as she was about to speak, her gaze met Chen Yi’s, and she subconsciously lowered her head again.","\"Chen Yi, your ’Carefree Travel’ is quite different from the usual gentle and lyrical pieces. Its melody is more cheerful, and there’s a certain heroic quality to it.\"","\"It’s just... I only just received the Zither Score, so my phrasing is poor, and I’m not yet skilled with the movements, pauses, or the coda. I couldn’t express the piece’s true essence.\"","Chen Yi saw her shy expression, chuckled, and offered his praise.","\"Your skill with the Zither is unparalleled, Sister Wan’er. I couldn’t detect any hint of rustiness, despite how long it’s been since you’ve played.\"","\"There were still some mistakes. For example, at the end of the first section, the melody should have been deeper and more resonant.\"","\"The Middle Stage of the second section, ’Birds Flying South,’ needs to be majestic and passionate...\"","Xiao Wan’er truly seemed to feel that she had made far too many mistakes in her performance.","She spoke in such detail not only to explain her errors to Chen Yi but also to impress them upon herself so she would not repeat them.","Chen Yi, however, wasn’t thinking that deeply about it.","He was silently memorizing the Finger Technique and other details he had just observed in Xiao Wan’er’s playing, trying to identify the different movements, pauses, and flourishes to understand their distinctions.","In short, he was learning her techniques on the sly.","Be it the Medical Dao, the Zither Dao, or the Martial Arts, he always had to try his own hand at something before he could truly learn its techniques and skills.","In comparison, the Zither Dao was more complicated for him.","It was especially difficult to correlate the terminology on the Zither Score—things like sections and breathing—with the actual strings. That made it harder than hard.","However, after watching Xiao Wan’er’s complete performance, Chen Yi now had the full melody of \"Carefree Travel\" in his mind.","With a little time to practice, achieving Initial Insight in \"Carefree Travel\" would not be difficult.","Chen Yi was about to offer more praise when he noticed Xiao Wan’er, Xiao Wuge, and Pei Guanli all looking at him. He asked in confusion, \"What is it?\"","Pei Guanli giggled. \"Brother-in-law, you were spacing out.\"","Xiao Wuge added, \"Brother-in-law, Sister Wan’er just suggested you give it a try, too.\"","Chen Yi’s mouth fell open. He pointed to himself. \"Me?\"","Xiao Wan’er nodded and said with a smile, \"I’ve long heard of your Mastery in Music, Chess, Calligraphy, and Painting. Why not play a piece for us as well?\"","Chen Yi tried to protest. \"Sometimes, you can’t believe rumors. The truth is, my Zither skills... are nonexistent.\"","Perhaps someone might have believed that when he first arrived in Shu State.","But now, not only did Xiao Wan’er disbelieve him, even Shen Huatang, who usually gave him the cold shoulder, was unconvinced.","Without another word, Pei Guanli pushed him down in front of the Zither. \"Come on, Brother-in-law, just let us have a listen,\" she said with a gleeful laugh.","\"Play that ’Carefree Something-or-other’ piece, the one Sister Wan’er just played. It’s a perfect chance to see how you two compare.\"","Chen Yi looked at their faces, their eyes filled with both encouragement and expectation, and could only nod in resignation.","’It can’t be helped.’","’They’re the ones who insisted.’","’So they can’t blame me for the awful show.’","Chen Yi pouted to himself, then took a deep breath. He let his hands fall naturally, his long fingers settling on the Zither strings.","The next moment—TWANG.","The smile on Xiao Wan’er’s face, who had been beaming moments before, faded slightly at the first note.","THWACK.","The second sound was the string smacking directly against the Zither’s soundboard, crisp and unpleasant.","Shen Huatang quickly circulated her True Essence to dull her hearing.","THUD.","After the third note, it wasn’t just Xiao Wan’er who was bewildered.","Pei Guanli and Xiao Wuge, who had held such inexplicable confidence in Chen Yi, now wore looks of utter astonishment.","The group exchanged glances, none of them understanding what was wrong.","Chen Yi, by contrast, remained perfectly calm. In his fine robes and Jade Belt, his movements were fluid and unconstrained.","Since the cat was out of the bag, he decided to just let loose and play.","He didn’t care whether he was playing accurately or if it sounded good.","He simply copied the motions he remembered from Xiao Wan’er’s performance, his ten fingers flying back and forth, left and right.","A series of THUD-THUD-THWACKS and THUD-THUD-THWACKS rang out.","None of it could be described as melodious, majestic, or carefree.","If Xiao Wan’er’s earlier performance could be called \"pleasing to the ear,\" then Chen Yi’s could only be described as \"thunderous slaughter.\"","Pei Guanli stood there, completely stunned, her expression blank.","Xiao Wuge covered his ears, staring at Chen Yi’s hands, hesitating over whether he should go up and stop him.","Xiao Wan’er, however, gradually began to smile. Her gaze toward Chen Yi seemed to say, ’So there is something you’re not good at after all.’","For some time now, no matter what question she had—be it about running the Medicine Hall, the Medical Dao Academy, Poetry, calligraphy, or chess—as long as she asked, Chen Yi could always offer some insight."]},{"number":290,"title":"Chapter 290 - 214: One Side Green, One Side Red","paragraphs":["What’s more, Chen Yi was often right, and his words were frequently profound and thought-provoking.","It reached the point where Xiao Wan’er subconsciously believed Chen Yi was capable of anything. At times, she even felt dull and ignorant in comparison.","Yet now, after hearing the piece Chen Yi played, she found herself breathing an inexplicable sigh of relief.","’Perhaps it was because she realized that no one in the world was truly perfect.’","A quarter of an hour later, the song ended.","Two lines of large, golden characters appeared:","[Successfully learned Zither Score: Carefree Travel. Level: Initial Insight]","[Zither Dao: Uninitiated 0/1 (Points assignable)]","Chen Yi glanced at the text, then stood up, feeling as if he could have played for longer. He looked at Xiao Wan’er and the others, smiled, nodded, and said, \"My apologies for that poor performance.\"","Shen Huatang was the first to break. She rolled her eyes, turned her head away, and muttered something to the effect of, \"He really did give a poor performance.\"","Pei Guanli, however, just burst out laughing. \"Brother-in-law, I never thought your zither skills would be this bad! You’re so much worse than Sister Wan’er.\"","Xiao Wuge didn’t laugh. He just looked at Chen Yi with suspicion, asking hesitantly,","\"Brother-in-law, the rumors back in Jiangnan Prefecture were that you had achieved Mastery in Music, Chess, Calligraphy, and Painting.\"","Chen Yi spread his hands and said with a smile, \"It’s true.\"","\"When it comes to the zither, I’ve mastered nine out of ten aspects—I’m just clueless about the tenth. It’s a shame you all wouldn’t believe me.\"","His reflection shone in Xiao Wan’er’s bright eyes. Suppressing a laugh, she said, \"It’s not that we didn’t believe you, Brother-in-law.\"","\"It’s just that your Calligraphy Dao and Chess Dao are truly without peer, so we subconsciously assumed the rumors were true.\"","Chen Yi smiled and shook his head. \"The rumors aren’t entirely accurate.\"","\"It’s just like the rumors back in Jiangnan Prefecture that my wife was eight feet tall with an eight-foot waist. It’s all just gossip getting twisted.\"","\"Say what?\"","\"They said Sister Jinghong was eight feet tall with an eight-foot waist?\"","Pei Guanli said indignantly, \"Those people in Jiangnan Prefecture are such liars.\"","Chen Yi pretended not to hear her.","He was now a live-in son-in-law of the Dingyuan Marquis’s Mansion. As the saying goes, \"marry a chicken, follow the chicken,\" so he could now consider himself a man of Shu State.","As it was nearing noon, the group began to set up for lunch in the Spring Lotus Garden.","There were mooncakes, pressed duck, roast chicken—a lavish spread of all kinds of delicacies.","Xiao Wan’er’s mood naturally lifted, and she stopped worrying about the Medical Dao Academy and the Holy Emperor’s decree punishing the old master.","Xiao Wuge was still young. Though he knew something bad had happened at the mansion, his simple view was that as long as his family was still around, everything was alright.","Shen Huatang, along with Xiaodie and the others, had set up a small table and were eating their lunch under a tree to one side.","Pei Guanli was her usual carefree self. In between eating and drinking, she made sure to ask about the poetry gathering that evening.","\"Brother-in-law, when are we heading to the academy?\"","Chen Yi finished a duck leg, wiped his mouth, and replied, \"Let’s wait until this evening and see what the mansion has arranged.\"","Xiao Wan’er paused, a little surprised. She looked at him and asked, \"Won’t that be a bit late?\"","\"It’s no problem.\"","\"These poetry gatherings have so many formalities—moon-worshipping, moon-gazing, listening to music, not to mention reciting poetry and composing couplets. If we go too early, we’ll just be spectators.\"","Chen Yi was in no hurry at all.","With so many instructors and students at the academy, his presence would hardly be missed.","Even with a large number of guests, the prestige of people like Mr. Yue Ming was more than enough to command the scene.","Xiao Wan’er said hesitantly, \"We should still go a bit earlier.\"","\"Because of the imperial decree today, I’m afraid Grandfather and the others are in no mood to enjoy the evening banquet.\"","Before she came to the Spring Lotus Garden, the old master had asked her to summon the accountants from both the mansion and the Medicine Hall.","He said they needed to calculate exactly how long the summer grain from the Three Towns would last, as well as the specific cost of purchasing more provisions.","To that end, Xiao Shen and others from the third branch of the Xiao Family had already gathered at the Qingjing Residence.","Chen Yi thought for a moment and no longer objected. \"In that case, it wouldn’t hurt to head to the academy a bit earlier and take a look.\"","Xiao Wan’er hummed in agreement, her face breaking into a smile. \"If we’re too early, we can just take a stroll by Quchi.\"","Pei Guanli threw her hands up in agreement. \"Yes! We can go look at the decorative lanterns and guess riddles.\"","\"Back when I was with my clan, my older brothers and sisters were always telling me how lively the Mid-Autumn Festival is in the city.\"","Chen Yi glanced at her and couldn’t resist teasing, \"Are you any good at them?\"","\"Why wouldn’t I be?\"","\"Alright, I’ll give you one. One part is red and fears water, the other part is small and fears spiders. What am I?\"","Pei Guanli’s smile froze. After a moment of thought, she stared at him blankly. \"Brother-in-law, what kind of word is that?\"","Xiao Wan’er covered her mouth and laughed. \"It’s a ’firefly’.\"","\"The red part is fire, which fears water, and a fly is small and fears spiders. Put them together and you get ’firefly’.\"","\"Ah? That one doesn’t count, it doesn’t count!\"","Seeing the indignant Tiger Girl, Chen Yi posed another riddle.","\"It has a head but no tail, and horns but no mouth. It wags its head and horns, and its body is all water. Guess the object.\"","Before Pei Guanli could answer, Xiao Wuge’s eyes lit up. \"I know! I know this one!\"","\"Brother-in-law, it’s a fish, right?\"","Chen Yi nodded with a smile. \"That’s right.\"","Pei Guanli, unwilling to admit defeat, forgot all about eating. She pouted, tugged on his sleeve, and begged him for another riddle.","\"Alright, one more.\"","\"It’s called sugar, but it isn’t sweet. It’s called salt, but it isn’t salty. In winter, it fills the...\"","Amid the boisterous chatter of Chen Yi, Pei Guanli, and Xiao Wuge, Xiao Wan’er remained silent.","She just sat quietly to one side, watching and listening, occasionally taking a small bite of mooncake as her mind filled with memories of the past.","Though Xiao Wan’er had been in poor health since birth, her days in the mansion had been quite happy.","Back then, her father, Xiao Fengchun, had returned from Jinling to succeed to the title of Duke Dingyuan.","For a long time after, Xiao Fengchun was mostly away on duty, much like Xiao Jinghong was now.","Only during the holidays would Xiao Fengchun return to the mansion for a family reunion.","She remembered the Mid-Autumn Festival ten years ago, also held right here in the Spring Lotus Garden."]},{"number":291,"title":"Chapter 291 - 214: One Side Green, One Side Red","paragraphs":["When Xiao Fengchun returned home, he brought special gifts for her and her younger sister: two Ivory Longswords seized from the Barbarian Race.","Although they were merely decorative, Xiao Wan’er was still overjoyed.","It was the first time she had ever received a gift in the shape of a weapon.","She still remembered her father’s exact words of comfort: \"It doesn’t matter that you can’t practice Martial Arts. It’s the heart that counts.\"","Xiao Wan’er hadn’t understood back then, but she understood now—her father wanted her to be strong.","To remain calm in the face of trouble, to be righteous and unyielding.","In that regard, she admitted she fell short of her younger sister.","After all, Xiao Jinghong had left Shu State at a very young age to follow her master, practice Martial Arts, and travel the world.","But as for where exactly she went or what she did, Xiao Wan’er knew very little.","She only knew that her younger sister was incredibly talented in Martial Arts and possessed a high level of cultivation.","As she thought of this, a melancholic expression inevitably clouded Xiao Wan’er’s face.","Now, her parents had fallen on the battlefield. Her younger sister had been forced into the army and was constantly away on duty, unable to even return home for the Mid-Autumn Festival.","Catching her altered expression from the corner of his eye, Chen Yi guessed it had to do with her family. He simply smiled and said:","\"Big Sister, why don’t you try one?\"","Snapping back to the present, Xiao Wan’er met Chen Yi’s gaze, and a faint smile finally touched her lips.","\"Alright.\"","\"When young, it has four legs. When grown, it has two. When old...\"","As Xiao Wan’er listened to the riddle, she thought to herself:","’I ask for nothing else. I only hope my younger sister is safe.’","...","「Southwest of Shu State, Wumeng Mountain.」","The Mountain Race people who lived here were also subjects of Great Wei, but their Mid-Autumn Festival customs differed greatly from those in the various states of the Central Plains.","In addition to worshipping the moon and honoring their ancestors, the Mid-Autumn Festival was also the best time of year for the young men and women of the Mountain Race to get engaged.","Bonfires would be lit and dances would begin.","Through song and dance, a man and a woman might just become family.","Early in the morning, men and women were scattered throughout the Mountain Race’s village, making their own preparations.","They had to wear their finest clothes.","They had to prepare creative gifts.","They also needed to practice their mountain folk songs and love songs.","So, from time to time, a song or two would echo through the mountains, drawing a few teasing remarks from those who knew the singer.","\"Brother Da Di, those lyrics are all wrong! The girl of your dreams won’t be impressed.\"","\"Get lost! Your singing is what’s terrible...\"","Meanwhile, the young women of the Mountain Race were also busy getting ready.","They adorned themselves with family heirlooms—jewelry of gold, silver, and priceless gems that had been stored away for special occasions.","The glittering array, combined with their lovely faces, created a unique and captivating beauty.","Xiao Jinghong arrived just after lunch, when the bustle in the village had died down considerably.","Not that she would have paid any mind to the noise, even if there had been any.","After surveying her surroundings, Xiao Jinghong proceeded as usual to the aged bamboo house in the center of the village. Standing outside, she bowed and cupped her fist.","\"Junior Jinghong, requesting an audience with Granny Shan.\"","She did not use her official title, instead presenting herself as a junior of the Jianghu out of respect for Granny Shan’s Martial Arts Cultivation.","Just then, a raspy, elderly voice came from within the bamboo house. \"Jinghong, you’ve arrived? Come in.\"","The door opened.","Xiao Jinghong acknowledged with a \"Yes.\" As she straightened up, she caught sight of a man in a short blue tunic hurrying over, likely having heard of her arrival. She gave him a brief nod of greeting before entering the bamboo house.","The door closed behind her.","The man outside stared at where her figure had vanished, sighing with a sorrowful expression.","\"The children of the Wei Family... in the end, they are different from us of the Mountain Race.\"","\"Forget it...\"","He departed with a forlorn air.","His footsteps faded into the distance.","Xiao Jinghong had heard all of this, of course, but her expression remained completely untroubled. She calmly sat down across from Granny Shan.","She removed her half-armor mask, setting it aside. The movement revealed a world-toppling beauty, unadorned by any powder or paint. She looked at Granny Shan and spoke:","\"This junior came in a hurry and did not prepare a festival gift. I hope Granny will forgive the oversight.\"","Granny Shan was gaunt and frail. Seated at the table, she was a full head shorter than the perfectly postured Xiao Jinghong.","She wore a black hemp robe, and a necklace woven from tortoise shells and wolf fangs hung on her chest. A gentle smile graced her deeply wrinkled face.","\"Jinghong, you have done our Mountain Race a great service. There is no need for such pleasantries.\"","\"Besides, you are burdened with military duties and must also oversee the Wu Mountain Mutual Market. For you to find the time to visit an old woman like me... it already makes me very happy.\"","Though she spoke her words slowly, her voice was still resonant and full of vigor.","Not at all like that of a typical old woman.","Of course, Xiao Jinghong never considered her an ordinary old woman to begin with.","After a few more pleasantries, she asked, though she already knew the answer, \"Has Guanli already left the tribe?\"","Granny Shan nodded with a smile. \"That girl can never sit still. She was only here a few days before she was clamoring to go to the city.\"","\"She has a good heart, though. She even remembered to bring some things back with her.\"","Seeing that her expression was normal, Xiao Jinghong said gravely, \"Granny, you must have heard about what happened a few days ago, so I won’t beat around the bush.\"","\"Did Guanli happen to mention anything to you about that letter?\"","Granny Shan seemed to have anticipated the question. \"I’ve heard a little,\" she replied.","\"That girl can’t hide what’s on her mind. She’s been restless ever since she returned. I imagine she’s worried you’ll reprimand her.\"","Xiao Jinghong shook her head slightly. \"This junior only wishes to know the truth of the matter. I won’t make things difficult for her.\"","Granny Shan clearly believed her, chuckling as she said, \"I don’t know many of the specifics myself.\"","\"But I do know that girl Guanli has matured a great deal since going down the mountain this time. She’s not as mischievous as she used to be.\"","\"She must have met someone out there who earned her respect.\"","’Respect?’","The image of a frail, scholarly man subconsciously surfaced in Xiao Jinghong’s mind.","’Husband?’","Before she could dwell on it, Granny Shan continued, \"However, that girl probably doesn’t know much about the letter either.\""]},{"number":292,"title":"Chapter 292 - 214: Green on One Side, Red on the Other","paragraphs":["\"The ’Sword Madman’ Liu Lang didn’t use your name when he found her.\"","Xiao Jinghong’s eyes flickered. \"Then how did he come to know Guanli?\"","Granny Shan smiled, the wrinkles on her face crisscrossing into deep ravines. She then took a letter from her sleeve and placed it on the table.","\"Liu Lang rose to fame in the harsh Northern Desert and had some contact with that rascal son of mine.\"","\"This time, not only did he have Guanli bring you a letter, but he also brought me news of them.\"","Xiao Jinghong knew she was referring to Pei Guanli’s father. She took the letter and glanced over it, a flicker of emotion crossing her face.","The Five Poison Sect has returned to the Jianghu. I’ve heard some members have already headed to Shu State. Please be careful, Mother.","Immortal Bai, not seen for thirty years, has left Wind and Rain Tower. Many seniors in the Jianghu are stirring at the news.","Furthermore, I am currently on the steppes. At Hero Kang’s request, I am investigating the movements of the various tribes. Once matters here are concluded, I will set out for the south.","Xiao Jinghong read it twice before setting the letter down. She frowned slightly and said,","\"You dealt the Five Poison Sect a devastating blow, Granny. How can they possibly be returning to the Jianghu?\"","Granny Shan retrieved the letter and said with a chuckle,","\"Although I killed their Sect Leader and a few Protectors and Elders, the Five Poison Sect still has many remnants outside of Shu State.\"","\"I thought I’d never hear of them again in my lifetime. I never expected to have to face them again in my old age.\"","\"A snake that isn’t killed will eventually become a menace.\"","Xiao Jinghong nodded. \"I won’t let them run rampant in Shu State, either.\"","Hearing this, Granny Shan said approvingly, \"I know you’re a good girl.\"","\"But the Five Poison Sect are no ordinary Evil Demons. Their methods are too vile. If your Xiao Family makes an enemy of them, I fear you will suffer losses as well.\"","Xiao Jinghong fell silent.","’She knew her family’s situation all too well.’","The Xiao Family’s reputation was all that remained; their actual strength was a far cry from what it once was.","Aside from her, the manor had few Martial Arts Powerhouses whose Cultivation had even reached the Middle Three Grades.","Dealing with Evil Demons like the Five Poison Sect, who excelled at stealth, assassination, and Poisoning, was truly beyond their capabilities.","At this thought, Xiao Jinghong said softly, \"If the right opportunity presents itself, I will act.\"","Granny Shan understood her predicament and changed the subject.","\"If you can protect the Wu Mountain Mutual Market, you’ll be doing my Mountain Race a great service.\"","\"Rest assured, Granny. The Mutual Market is just as important to my Xiao Family. I will do everything in my power.\"","\"That’s good...\"","After a moment of silence, Granny Shan gazed out the window, her ancient face filled with wistful emotion as she spoke.","\"The Jianghu isn’t what it used to be.\"","\"Decades ago, Immortal Bai reigned supreme, your master the Sword Master roamed the world with his sword, and figures like the Sword Ghost and the Spear God were mostly heroic and righteous folk.\"","\"It’s nothing like today. In this vast Jianghu, you can barely find any decent rising stars.\"","After a pause, Granny Shan looked at Xiao Jinghong and smiled. \"Of course, you’re one of them.\"","Xiao Jinghong shook her head gently. \"I am still a far cry from my master and his generation.\"","\"Besides, I’m so entangled in worldly affairs, I have neither the means nor the opportunity to get involved in the matters of the Jianghu.\"","Granny Shan sighed. \"Be that as it may, you are still the Sword Master’s disciple.\"","\"Before, when your connection to him wasn’t obvious, it didn’t matter. The old grudges of the Jianghu’s older generation wouldn’t be laid at your feet.\"","\"But now that you’ve made your move, people have recognized the Sword Master’s signature arts. I’m afraid it will be difficult for you to remain detached from now on.\"","Xiao Jinghong was well aware of this, yet a smile touched her lips.","\"My master is wandering the world. As his disciple, I can’t very well let people go and disturb him.\"","Granny Shan laughed at her words. \"It’s good that you feel that way.\"","\"Fortunately, you’re strong enough—far stronger than my own grandson and granddaughter.\"","\"If Ah Da and Guanli had even a tenth of your ability, I could die without regrets.\"","Xiao Jinghong simply smiled and didn’t respond.","However, after this conversation, her suspicions about Pei Guanli and the letter had greatly diminished.","After all, she could doubt Pei Guanli, and she could doubt Liu Lang, but she couldn’t possibly doubt an elder like Granny Shan.","Granny Shan had even shown her a family letter from the north; she couldn’t have done all that just to provide cover for Pei Guanli.","\"I wonder what business Immortal Bai has, coming out of seclusion this time.\"","\"Him? I reckon his mouth has been idle for too long, so he’s come out of the mountains to tell people’s fortunes.\"","At that, Xiao Jinghong couldn’t help but laugh.","\"This is bound to stir up some trouble in the Jianghu again.\"","Granny Shan nodded in agreement. \"That old coot brings disaster wherever he goes.\"","\"As long as he doesn’t come to Shu State, I’ll be spared the trouble of giving him a piece of my mind.\"","Xiao Jinghong paused, surprised. \"You’ve crossed paths with Immortal Bai before, Granny?\"","\"That’s a story from long ago...\""]},{"number":293,"title":"Chapter 293 - 215: An Unreasonable Request","paragraphs":["\"That Gongye Bai fellow was a bit better when he was young. At worst, he’d just use those fists of his to bully people.\"","\"Now that he’s older and his Martial Arts Cultivation has deepened, he’s become an insolent old fool.\"","\"He wants a hand in everything, stirring up the entire Jianghu until it’s in chaos.\"","Granny Shan seemed to be recalling some old grudges. Her tone grew heavier and her voice rose.","\"The way I see it, the name he chose for his Wind and Rain Tower is perfect—it exists solely to stir up wind and rain in the Jianghu...\"","Listening to Granny Shan’s endless tirade against Immortal Bai, a rare smile touched Xiao Jinghong’s lips.","That Immortal Bai was indeed an anomaly in the Jianghu.","His cultivation was clearly profound, and he was generally considered a righteous man, yet his actions always had a hint of perversity.","It was hard to say if he was born a jinx or if he could truly determine a person’s fate with just his words.","In any case, those for whom he had read a fortune never ended up well.","In fact, Granny Shan wasn’t the only one wary of Immortal Bai.","Even Xiao Jinghong’s master—the Sword Master, Li Wudang—had privately grumbled about him.","Without any actual profanity, of course.","\"Jinghong, most of the old-timers in the Jianghu will give your master some face.\"","\"But there is one person—Immortal Bai of the Wind and Rain Tower—whom you must be wary of. If you meet him, run as far as you can.\"","\"That old coot is like a Dog Skin Ointment; once he sticks to you, nothing good will come of it.\"","Recalling her master’s words, Xiao Jinghong could understand Granny Shan’s feelings as she berated Immortal Bai.","But after listening for a moment, she couldn’t help but feel a flicker of doubt. ’It seems Granny Shan really did have some kind of history with Immortal Bai when she was young.’","’Her words, both spoken and unspoken, gave off a sense of exasperated disappointment in him.’","Just then, Granny Shan noticed the look in Xiao Jinghong’s eyes, realized she had misspoken, and paused before saying:","\"Girl, in short, just try to avoid getting involved with Immortal Bai in the future.\"","Xiao Jinghong smiled. \"This junior will remember your advice.\"","Granny Shan adjusted the small pendant bottle hanging on her chest, shifted twice to get comfortable, and continued:","\"For Immortal Bai to leave his mountain, something must be drawing him out. That man... AHEM. As for what it is, I’ll need to see where he shows his face.\"","\"He’s being watched by all those idlers who love a good spectacle, so hiding his tracks will likely be difficult.\"","Xiao Jinghong nodded. \"The letter from just now also mentioned that some other seniors have emerged.\"","After listening to Granny Shan ramble on for so long, she certainly didn’t believe that Immortal Bai was simply restless at the Wind and Rain Tower.","Just like her master, the Sword Master, grand masters of that caliber were like divine dragons—showing the head but hiding the tail.","Their thoughts and motivations couldn’t be judged by ordinary standards.","\"Girl, let them chase who they will. We’ll focus on our own business.\"","After this word of advice, Granny Shan changed the subject. \"A few days ago, I heard from Ah Da that the progress on the Wu Mountain Mutual Market has been slowed by the rain?\"","Xiao Jinghong hummed in affirmation. \"Before I came to see you, I had already ordered them to speed up the work. I’m aiming to have it completed within two months.\"","Granny Shan nodded slightly, her old face breaking into a smile. \"You are so steady in your work. I can rest easy.\"","\"Unlike my Mountain Race, who are all just a bunch of mud-legs. They can’t read a single character and only know how to charge ahead recklessly.\"","\"In the future, if Ah Da and the others go to the Mutual Market, please look after them if any issues arise.\"","Xiao Jinghong agreed, not feeling that it was beneath her status to do so.","Granny Shan then asked about the follow-up arrangements for the Mutual Market, mostly concerning which merchants would be coming and going, and what could be bought and sold.","In reality, according to the agreement between the Xiao Family and the Mountain Race, the market was only intended to bring convenience to the various tribes living on Wumeng Mountain.","Though it was called a \"Mutual Market,\" the term \"bazaar\" would have been more accurate.","After all, whether it was the Xiao Family, the Dingyuan Army, or the people of the Mountain Race, they were all subjects of the Great Wei Dynasty.","The reason for establishing such a market, from the Xiao Family’s perspective, was to earn some silver to supplement the funds and provisions for the Dingyuan Army.","For the Mountain Race, it would make their lives more convenient, so they no longer had to travel hundreds of miles of mountain roads just to buy salt or fine grains as they had in the past.","They chatted idly for a bit.","As evening approached, Granny Shan invited Xiao Jinghong to stay the night.","\"Girl, today is the Mid-Autumn Festival. Since you’re not going back to the Prefecture City, you can stay here and keep an old woman company.\"","Xiao Jinghong thought for a moment and didn’t refuse. \"Then I shall impose on you tonight, Granny. I will return to the Mutual Market tomorrow morning.\"","Granny Shan chuckled. \"Don’t be a stranger.\"","\"This Wu Mountain Mutual Market is beneficial to us both, but I know your Xiao Family is under a lot of pressure.\"","\"If the one in the Capital Prefecture doesn’t give his approval, the Capital Commandery here in Shu State will also have complaints.\"","Xiao Jinghong said in a level tone, \"As long as the two Commanders don’t show themselves, you have no need to worry, Granny.\"","\"I’m not worried about the Mountain Race. I’m afraid it will only worsen the Xiao Family’s situation.\"","\"You arrived in time to avert the disaster in the Three Towns this time, but there’s no guarantee something similar won’t happen at the Wu Mountain Mutual Market next time.\"","As soon as she finished speaking, a grim, cold smile appeared on Granny Shan’s aged face.","\"If you can’t handle it in the future, you just tell me. I’d like to see who in this land of Shu State dares to get out of line.\"","Xiao Jinghong smiled and nodded, lifting her mask to her face. \"This junior will remember.\"","Then she bowed, turned, and left the bamboo house.","Watching Xiao Jinghong walk away, Granny Shan couldn’t help but sigh.","\"That poor girl.\"","\"If Xiao Fengchun hadn’t died so young, why would she have to shoulder the entire, immense weight of the Xiao Family alone?\"","Xiao Jinghong faintly heard Granny Shan’s words, but her steps didn’t falter as she continued forward.","From a very young age, she knew her life was destined to be tumultuous, that she could never be a carefree wanderer like her master, Li Wudang.","Even if Xiao Fengchun hadn’t died, as a member of the Xiao family, she would naturally have to do her part for them."]},{"number":294,"title":"Chapter 294 - 215: An Unreasonable Request (Part 2)","paragraphs":["But now, she had merely increased that power from ten percent to its full capacity.","As she mulled this over, Xiao Jinghong arrived at the familiar bamboo house, her gaze falling upon the horizon.","The dim, yellow light of the fiery sunset clouds shone through the cracks in the bamboo window, casting itself upon her and faintly revealing her somewhat slender, beautiful silhouette.","Delicate and fragile, yet as upright and straight as a Long Sword.","Xiao Jinghong’s eyes swept over the clouds as she silently took out several letters from home from within her robes.","She pinched a letter between her fingers, fanning them open like a fan and holding them before her face so the last rays of the setting sun struck the back of the pages.","The black ink seemed to be dyed with a layer of gold, shimmering brilliantly.","’My husband, please forgive me. Jinghong has broken her promise this time.’","Xiao Jinghong had promised Chen Yi she would return home before the Mid-Autumn Festival.","But now, with this sudden turn of events, she had no choice but to remain where she was.","’If love between two hearts can last, why must they be together day and night...?’","’One can only hope.’","...","「Shu State Prefecture City.」","It was just past the middle of the Hour of Shen, yet though the sky was still bright, the streets were already packed with people.","In the East and West Markets, the shops along the streets had opened their doors early.","This was especially true for the taverns and restaurants, where people came and went in an endless stream.","In addition to the patrons, temporary stages had been set up inside.","There were opera singers, ballad singers, and dancers—they had everything one could ask for.","At the very least, they had to invite some famous actors, courtesans, or, failing that, the top performers from Yanhua Lane.","It was partly to liven up the atmosphere, and partly because they were unwilling to be outdone by their rivals.","Out on the streets, wooden carts were parked in the middle of the stone-paved roads, propped up back-to-back to form stalls.","Most of these stalls displayed various prizes, each corresponding to a slip of paper covered in small writing.","This was all done under the festive name of \"lantern riddle guessing.\"","Men and women, young and old, walked among them, their faces all wreathed in smiles as they chatted and squeezed their way through the crowds.","The most excited of all were the children, who had come out early carrying their lanterns, just waiting for night to fall so they could light them.","All in all, it was a scene of bustling prosperity.","However, the most prosperous and lively place in Shu State City today was still Kangning Street in the North City.","Every year, the places where talented scholars and beautiful ladies gathered would always attract a crowd of curious onlookers.","They came to see which tavern had hired the most courtesans, whose songs were the best, and which patrons were the most generous.","For the poetry gatherings held on Painted Boats, in taverns, or in pavilions, the rivalry was even more intense.","News of which gathering produced a masterpiece, or which scholar gave a dazzling performance, would be spread by word of mouth.","To put it simply, the young ladies competed in beauty, while the scholars socialized through literature.","And so, as the place in Shu State City where the most scholars and young ladies would gather tonight, Guiyun Academy already had people waiting outside long in advance.","Carriages arrived one after another, and the sight of a familiar face or two stepping out would stir up a buzz of discussion.","\"Prefect Liu is here so early?\"","\"Early? If he didn’t come early, would he make the lords from the Governor’s Office and the Inspectorate Office wait for him?\"","Upon hearing this, some of the better-informed people in the crowd cautiously changed the subject.","\"I heard that Governor Liu Hong was punished by the Holy Emperor today. I wonder if he’ll still show up tonight as planned.\"","\"Hard to say.\"","\"Lord Liu was dragged down by a younger member of his clan. It’s truly an undeserved disaster for him.\"","\"Exactly. Who would have thought that Liu Wen would dare to conspire with the Evil Demonic Dao to burn the summer grain of the Three Towns?\"","\"The fact that his entire clan wasn’t exterminated is already a sign of the Holy Emperor’s mercy...\"","As they spoke, a few more carriages arrived. Even from a distance, they looked grand and magnificent with their ornate canopies.","\"Whose carriage is that?\"","Among the crowd was a well-connected and knowledgeable man who recognized the emblem on the carriage and said with a low laugh:","\"The Assistant Governor of the Governor’s Office, Chen Yunfan.\"","\"He’s also this year’s top scorer, the Imperial Top Scholar.\"","Others glanced over and recognized the clan emblem of the Jiangnan Prefecture Chen Family, which inevitably led to a few disdainful or mocking remarks.","\"Since the founding of the Great Wei, every Imperial Top Scholar has been like the God of Literature descended to earth. Not only were their essays brilliant, but they were also humble and steady in character.\"","\"But this one, ever since he came to Shu State, doesn’t seem to know the meaning of the word ’steady’.\"","\"I heard he’s not only a regular at Yanhua Lane, but he also caused quite a few embarrassing incidents when he was collecting the summer grain outside the city.\"","\"He did plenty of things like rigging the scales and swapping the measuring buckets, which made a lot of common folk complain bitterly.\"","\"Huh? But I heard he didn’t order that, and some people were investigated and punished afterward.\"","\"Wasn’t that because Lord Xiao Dongchen is sharp enough to see every detail? After he found the culprits, he just gave the credit to him, right?\"","\"Officials really do protect their own...\"","Chen Yunfan faintly overheard the surrounding chatter. He pursed his lips but said nothing.","He had indeed made a fool of himself before. A moment’s carelessness had allowed someone to play tricks right under his nose.","Although it didn’t really affect him, many people knew about it. The story was passed around, making his already terrible reputation even worse.","Some people even lumped him together with Chen Yi, who had just arrived in Shu State, jokingly calling them the \"Twin Stars of the Chen Family.\"","They even came up with a saying: \"First came the runaway groom who repented and saw the light, then came the Imperial Top Scholar who tested the law himself.\"","In short, they had nothing good to say.","Cui Qingwu had also heard some of the talk and offered a comforting smile.","\"Brother Yunfan, you don’t need to take it to heart. Once they see what you’re capable of, they’ll naturally shut their mouths.\"","\"Just like your brother, Chen Yi. Hasn’t his reputation improved now? He’s even respected.\"","Chen Yunfan waved his hand dismissively. \"It’s just idle gossip. I’ve heard more than my share over the years.\"","\"Let them talk if they want to. As long as they’re not stupid enough to say it to my face.\"","With that, Chen Yunfan lifted the curtain to look outside and muttered,","\"Looks like Brother Yi isn’t here yet...\"","Hearing this, Cui Qingwu glanced at him and chuckled softly. \"Your brother can indeed afford to arrive a little later these days.\"","\"That’s true. Come on, let’s go inside first and see which ladies have... erm, which scholars have arrived.\""]},{"number":295,"title":"Chapter 295 - 215: An Unreasonable Request","paragraphs":["Cui Qingwu pretended not to hear and followed him out of the carriage, walking into Guiyun Academy.","Behind him, Huan’er and Chun Ying followed.","The four of them—masters and servants—plus the driver, Ning Yu, could be considered quite a low-key entourage.","In contrast, the belatedly arriving Chen Yi and his companions seemed like a much larger and more imposing retinue.","Besides him, Xiao Wan’er, and Xiao Wuge, their entourage included Xiaodie, Shen Huatang, Pei Guanli, and four Armored Guards from the Marquis’s Mansion.","Two carriages bearing the banner of the Dingyuan Marquis’s Mansion were parked outside the academy. It was hard not to attract attention.","\"Someone from the Xiao Family is here. Besides Mr. Qingzhou, I didn’t expect the Young Master and the young miss to come as well.\"","\"Miss Xiao Wan’er is truly as beautiful as the rumors say. Her looks could topple nations.\"","Hearing the surrounding chatter, an uncomfortable Xiao Wan’er pulled at her cloak and softly urged, \"Let’s go inside.\"","Chen Yi smiled and nodded, entering the academy under the protection of Wang Lixing and the other guards.","Once inside, they saw a wide stone path lined with two rows of lanterns. On either side stood several students the academy had asked to help.","The one leading them was none other than Ma Guan—Ma Heming.","Seeing Chen Yi and his group approach, he hurried forward, bowed, and said, \"Mr. Qingzhou, if you please, come with me first.\"","\"The headmaster instructed me to bring you to him as soon as I saw you.\"","Chen Yi paused for a moment, then glanced at Xiao Wan’er. Seeing that she didn’t object, he suggested, \"Let’s go together.\"","Xiao Wan’er murmured her assent and followed behind him, pulling Xiao Wuge along.","As they walked, most of her initial curiosity and excitement had already faded.","Especially after seeing the crowds outside the academy and the decor within, she felt a slight sense of alienation.","In contrast, Pei Guanli, who had been here once before for a poetry gathering, felt no such unease.","She was even excitedly recounting some of the things she had seen during her last visit.","But a single mention from Xiaodie about a lost calligraphy copybook was enough to make her small, round face fall.","\"Last time was just an accident... It’s all my brother-in-law’s older brother’s fault. If only he had just let me poison him properly...\"","As she was speaking, Chen Yi, who was walking ahead, paused. His eyes held a trace of surprise as he looked at the few people walking toward them.","It was none other than Liu Zhaoxue of the Jing State Liu Family, along with several guards and maids.","Xiao Wan’er, at his side, had the same reaction.","She looked at the approaching group and hesitantly offered a greeting, \"Sister Zhaoxue.\"","Liu Zhaoxue’s gaze swept over the two of them. A faint smile appeared on her face. \"Zhaoxue greets Sister Wan’er and Mr. Qingzhou.\"","After a pause, she bowed deeply and continued,","\"I had intended to visit your home in a few days to offer my apologies. Since we’ve met today, the opportunity seems fitting.\"","\"On behalf of my second brother, I ask for your forgiveness.\"","\"I don’t dare ask for forgiveness, I only hope this will not affect the relationship between you and me, Sister.\"","Liu Zhaoxue didn’t mention the Xiao and Liu Families at all, speaking only of her relationship with Xiao Wan’er. It was a way of avoiding the heart of the matter.","Xiao Wan’er looked at her and considered for a moment. The hesitation on her face vanished as she shook her head and sighed. \"I am sorry, Sister Zhaoxue.\"","Liu Zhaoxue was taken aback, clearly not expecting the ever-magnanimous Xiao Wan’er to refuse her so directly.","It left her unable to continue with the speech she had prepared.","At that moment, Chen Yi stepped forward. Ignoring Liu Zhaoxue, he addressed Xiao Wan’er and the others. \"Let’s go.\"","\"Mr. Yue Ming has invited us. It must be urgent.\"","Xiao Wan’er nodded and silently followed him into the building.","None of them were inclined to deal with the people from the Liu Family.","Only Pei Guanli muttered \"Shameless\" as she passed by Liu Zhaoxue.","Once they were in the distance,","The door closed.","Liu Zhaoxue took a deep breath, her expression returning to a calm state, and turned to leave.","A burly guard beside her gathered his qi into a thread and spoke in a low voice using ventriloquism:","\"That girl from the Mountain Race... she must be Granny Shan’s granddaughter, correct?\"","Liu Zhaoxue nodded subconsciously. When she realized what she’d done, she turned back to look at the speaker and was met with a pair of blood-red eyes brimming with killing intent.","\"Yan Fusha, you...\"","\"Miss Zhaoxue, I have an impudent request.\"","\"Heh heh... would it be possible for me to ’test’ that little girl as well?\"","Liu Zhaoxue: \"...\""]},{"number":296,"title":"Chapter 296 - 216: No Turning Back","paragraphs":["Liu Zhaoxue knew full well that cooperating with the Five Poison Sect was like asking a tiger for its skin.","However, her current circumstances no longer allowed her to wait for another opportunity.","Unless she was willing to be like her aunt, Liu Xiangning, and accept her father’s arrangements.","—To be married into one of the other Noble Families, or even into the Royal Family.","But Liu Zhaoxue was unwilling.","So, before she was betrothed, she could only let her ambitions run wild.","She would either succeed—overcoming all obstacles to become the master of the Jing State Liu Family.","Or she would die trying...","’So what if I die? It’s better than being used as a marriage tool, bearing the title of Jing State’s greatest beauty.’","Liu Zhaoxue had long been prepared for this.","It was just that her plans had only just begun to unfold, and with the situation in Shu State unclear, she had to be extra cautious.","Especially considering that since the Jing State Liu Family had arrived in Shu State, they had lost two young masters from the main branch in succession—proof enough of the Xiao Family’s power in the region.","Never mind Liu Jing, an unimportant son of a concubine whose ability, temperament, and methods were all severely lacking.","But Liu Wen was different.","Not only was he the second son of the Liu Family’s main branch, but his mother also came from a great family in Jing State. He wanted for neither money, resources, nor manpower.","He even possessed some cunning, and his talent in the Martial Arts was not to be underestimated.","Liu Wen’s unexpected death in Shu State made Liu Zhaoxue feel for the first time that events were spiraling out of her control.","To that end, she set three rules for herself.","Do not rush ahead recklessly for quick merits, avoid direct conflict with the Xiao Family, and guard against the Five Poison Sect sabotaging her efforts.","Liu Jing had rushed in recklessly right after arriving, ordering the Bright Moon Building to plunder the Xiao Family’s medicinal supplies. He got what he deserved.","Liu Wen had died outside Iron Wall Town because he directly clashed with the Xiao Family, and he even implicated her Third Uncle, Liu Hong, who was then punished by the Holy Emperor.","Mulling over these things, Liu Zhaoxue offered a low-voiced reminder, \"Try not to create unnecessary complications. Caution is paramount.\"","Yan Fusha grinned, his disguised, rugged face revealing a hint of ferocity. \"Don’t worry,\" he said. \"Our great work is not yet complete. I won’t do anything foolish.\"","\"I mean clean up after yourself. Don’t let this get back to me.\"","After speaking, Liu Zhaoxue turned and left with her personal attendants.","Yan Fusha watched her walk away, a dark look flashing in his eyes. He immediately gestured toward a corner.","\"Follow her. Keep a close eye on her.\"","After two men dressed as common scholars in long robes acknowledged the order and departed, Yan Fusha pushed his way into the crowd as if no one else was there.","Originally, he had only planned to test the waters and probe that live-in son-in-law of the Xiao Family.","But after seeing that girl from the Mountain Race, he changed his mind.","’Granny Shan,’ he thought, ’this blood feud of several decades will begin with your granddaughter.’","Elsewhere, Liu Zhaoxue, who was well aware of the feud between the Five Poison Sect and the Mountain Race, naturally guessed Yan Fusha’s intentions.","Even if she wanted to stop him, she was powerless to do so.","After all, for now, she still had to rely on those practitioners of the Evil Demonic Dao from the Five Poison Sect to get things done.","Just as Liu Zhaoxue was lost in thought, she suddenly heard someone call out, \"Zhaoxue.\"","She looked toward the voice, the unusual expression on her face vanishing instantly. She bowed respectfully. \"Third Uncle.\"","The newcomer was none other than the Left Governor of Shu State, Liu Hong.","Although he was currently in plain blue clothes, his sturdy frame filled them out, giving him a natural air of authority.","After a glance to either side, Liu Hong beckoned to Liu Zhaoxue and said with a smile:","\"The poetry gathering hasn’t started yet. Let’s go take a look at that exhibition hall first.\"","A flash of surprise appeared in Liu Zhaoxue’s eyes. Without stopping to ask if they were even allowed into the exhibition hall, she simply agreed and followed by his side.","Two strong and capable Guards followed close behind.","A few other personal attendants protected them from the sides, subtly obscuring the figures of Liu Hong and Liu Zhaoxue.","「Before long.」","The group arrived at the exhibition hall, which was adjacent to the academy’s library.","An elegant, middle-aged man in a pale blue robe was already waiting at the entrance.","Seeing Liu Hong’s figure, the man came forward from a distance, cupped his hands in salute, and said, \"Lord Liu.\"","Liu Hong raised a hand and said with a smile, \"Mr. Lingchuan, there’s no need for such formalities. I’m just going in for a quick look.\"","Hearing his words, Liu Zhaoxue looked at the man before them. With a start, she realized who he was.","Mr. Lingchuan, Zhu Lingchuan, a member of the prominent Zhu Family of Shu State.","Although this Mr. Lingchuan was not widely known, his elder brother, Zhu Hao, was the Deputy Commander of the Shu State Capital Commandery, in charge of overseeing the state’s salt and iron industries, among other duties.","With this in mind, she gave a slight bow. \"Zhaoxue pays her respects to Mr. Lingchuan.\"","Mr. Lingchuan nodded at her, then stepped aside and gestured, saying:","\"There are many people coming and going for the poetry gathering today. To avoid anyone disturbing Lord Liu’s enjoyment, I will not accompany you inside.\"","Seeing his serious expression, Liu Hong didn’t press the issue and simply beckoned for Liu Zhaoxue alone to follow him.","After the two of them entered, Mr. Lingchuan casually closed the main doors and stood outside, motionless, with his hands tucked into his sleeves.","The other Guards instinctively took up positions to guard the key access points.","Inside the exhibition hall, the doors and windows were shut tight. With no lamps lit, the room was quite dim.","As a practitioner of the Martial Arts, Liu Zhaoxue was unaffected.","Liu Hong, however, frowned slightly and motioned for her to light an oil lamp.","Liu Zhaoxue did as he asked, using a flint to light an oil lamp. She held it and stood beside him, surveying the spacious hall.","The decor was rather simple. Arranged around the four walls were several dozen trays holding calligraphy scrolls, all of which were covered by red cloth.","A faint light, like the glowing strokes of written characters, could be seen glimmering through the red cloths.","Liu Hong’s gaze swept the room. Ignoring the other scrolls, he walked directly to the one that was placed opposite the entrance.","He swept the cloth aside with one hand.","A Mental Realm instantly emerged—","great golden characters ascended into the air, mountains rolled and fell, a city stood atop a lofty peak, and a lone skiff drifted leisurely into the distance.","Liu Hong looked up at the lines of poetry and the unfolding scenes, his expression tranquil.","Liu Zhaoxue, however, was not nearly as calm.","Although she had heard many rumors about this piece, *Post-rain Reflections*, over the past two days, none of it could compare to the awe of seeing it with her own eyes."]},{"number":297,"title":"Chapter 297 - 216: No Turning Back (Part 2)","paragraphs":["Especially the signatures at the end: Chen Yi, Chen Qingzhou.","Every stroke flowed as smoothly as clouds and water, dazzling to behold.","Seeing the complete work only deepened Liu Zhaoxue’s inexplicable apprehension and suspicion toward Chen Yi.","Just then, Liu Hong asked without turning his head, \"Zhaoxue, what do you think of this calligraphy?\"","Liu Zhaoxue came to her senses and said after a moment’s thought, \"It’s good. Extremely good.\"","Describing a new style of calligraphy at the Perfection Realm with a simple ’good’ felt rather inadequate.","But since Liu Zhaoxue didn’t understand her third uncle’s reason for asking, she gave a guarded reply.","Liu Hong chuckled softly. \"Good calligraphy. It is indeed a fine piece.\"","\"This new script is in harmony with the world itself. The characters are full and powerful, yet contained. It’s clear the artist has studied their craft deeply.\"","\"And its Mental Realm is so ethereal...\"","Liu Hong turned his head to look at Liu Zhaoxue, a cryptic smile playing on his lips. \"Faced with such a magnificent, surging Mental Realm, what did you think of?\"","A chill went down Liu Zhaoxue’s spine. She feigned contemplation before answering, \"Riding the wind and breaking the waves... advancing ever forward?\"","Liu Hong’s reaction was noncommittal. He turned back to stare at the calligraphy piece, saying nothing more.","Liu Zhaoxue watched him out of the corner of her eye, a sudden sense of foreboding washing over her.","She felt like prey being targeted by a powerful predator.","The air grew heavy, suffocating...","A fine sheen of sweat broke out on her smooth forehead, and the hand holding the oil lamp began to tremble.","The lamplight wavered.","Liu Hong’s voice was calm when he spoke. \"A Calligraphy Dao Realm is tied to one’s disposition and nothing else.\"","\"A domineering person writes in a domineering style, a free spirit in a free style, and a person of rigid principles in a rigid style. It’s as simple as that.\"","\"This Chen Qingzhou’s Calligraphy Dao is seamless and natural, yet it’s not hard to see his disposition.\"","\"The primary trait of his disposition is ’spontaneity.’ The strokes vary in size according to his whim, showing he dislikes being bound by convention.\"","\"Then there’s the poem... ’Riding the wind and breaking the waves’ is certainly in there.\"","\"But what I see is a rainbow after the storm, the calm that comes after weathering the tempest.\"","Liu Hong paused and asked, \"Doesn’t this feel like a reflection of what happened to the Xiao Family the other day?\"","Liu Zhaoxue started. \"Third Uncle, are you referring to the attack on the granaries in the Three Towns?\"","Liu Hong turned to face her, his tone icy. \"I’m referring to you, Liu Wen, Liu Jing, and the main branch of the family!\"","The color drained from Liu Zhaoxue’s face. \"I...\"","Liu Hong raised a hand to cut her off. \"I know perfectly well what you’re up to.\"","\"You’re just unwilling to be manipulated by the family, to be used as your father’s pawn.\"","\"I understand that you want to break free, but you shouldn’t have plotted against Wen’er.\"","\"Third Uncle, why would you suspect me of such a thing?\"","\"The Fengchun Building.\"","Hearing those three words, Liu Zhaoxue’s heart sank. ’He knows.’","Liu Hong continued, \"That day at the Fengchun Building, you invited Xiao Wan’er, then feigned carelessness as you let the news slip to your second brother, all to orchestrate what would appear to be a reasonable ’accident.’\"","\"If not for that, I doubt Wen’er would have taken such a desperate gamble and run off to the outskirts of Iron Wall Town.\"","Liu Zhaoxue rushed to deny it. \"That wasn’t my intention! I just wanted to help Second Brother achieve his heart’s desire.\"","Liu Hong remained unmoved. He began to cover the calligraphy with a red cloth as he spoke.","\"I don’t want to know what your intentions were. I came to you today to tell you one thing, and one thing only.\"","\"If you don’t want to end up like Wen’er, then get out of Shu State. Go back to Jing State.\"","\"Third Uncle...\"","\"Don’t call me that. I can’t afford to be your ’Third Uncle’.\"","\"Person after person from the main branch of the Liu Family has come to Shu State. I know better than anyone what you’re all after.\"","At this, a sneer touched Liu Hong’s lips. \"But search your heart and ask yourself: does your father—my dear older brother—truly have the capability?\"","\"Look at what he’s done. He raises his children to be ambitious and treacherous. He taught his sister only how to manipulate her husband with pillow talk. And he himself does nothing but cower in Jing State.\"","\"Tell me, do you think he’s content to sit back and watch the clouds roll by, or does he actually want to sit at the board and play the game?\"","At this, Liu Zhaoxue fell silent.","She finally understood the reason behind her third uncle’s words.","Ultimately, it was because she, Liu Wen, and the others had meddled too much in Shu State’s affairs, causing their third uncle to be punished by the Holy Emperor.","\"I have learned my lesson.\"","Liu Hong shot her a look, then turned to leave. \"You’d do well to remember that.\"","\"I don’t want to have to clean up the bodies of anyone else from the main branch!\"","Liu Zhaoxue watched him until he was gone, then silently performed a bow.","She had thought her actions were completely covert, never expecting her third uncle to see right through her.","But upon reflection, she found she could accept it.","After all, her third uncle, Liu Hong, might be the Chief Steward of the Liu Family’s third house, but in practice, his was little more than a collateral branch cut off from the family’s center of power in Jing State.","Otherwise, her father wouldn’t have sent people to Shu State time and time again.","Aside from his designs on the Xiao Family, her father also had plans for Liu Hong and his third house.","It just seemed that now, her father’s schemes were about to fall through yet again.","Thinking of this, Liu Zhaoxue took one last look at the red cloth covering *Post-rain Reflections*, then extinguished her oil lamp and left the hall.","’Her third uncle was right about everything.’","’But once the bow is drawn, the arrow cannot be recalled.’","’How could she possibly give up now?’","......","Running into Liu Zhaoxue was unexpected, but not entirely surprising.","She was from the Jing State Liu Family and the niece of Liu Hong, the Left Governor in the Shu State Governor’s Office. It was entirely plausible that she would have an invitation to Guiyun Academy.","Thus, Chen Yi didn’t give it much thought and simply led Xiao Wan’er and the others to Mr. Yue Ming’s courtyard.","After a brief chat, he figured out why Mr. Yue Ming had summoned him, and he couldn’t help but feel exasperated.","\"Dean, it’s just a few more people today. You don’t need to be so worried, do you?\"","Mr. Yue Ming looked abashed and laughed wryly. \"I’m not normally like this, of course, but... but things are different now.\"","\"This poetry competition will have guests not only from the prominent Noble Families of Shu State, but also from academies in all the other states.\"","\"It would be one thing if a student from Shu State won the title of Poetry Champion.\""]},{"number":298,"title":"Chapter 298 - 216: The Arrow Has Left the Bow","paragraphs":["\"But if we let one of those outsiders win, wouldn’t it needlessly tarnish the reputation of our Guiyun Academy?\"","Chen Yi shook his head and said helplessly, \"Headmaster, it’s only a poetry gathering. Whoever wins the title of Poetry Champion deserves it. It’s a testament to their skill.\"","\"Besides, I’m not from Shu State myself. I’m from Jiangnan Prefecture.\"","\"If I were to win the title of Poetry Champion, I doubt many would be convinced, would they?\"","\"That... is also true.\"","Mr. Yue Ming was, of course, well aware of this.","However, he had waited so long for an opportunity to bring glory to Guiyun Academy that he wanted everything to be perfect.","But seeing that Chen Yi wasn’t committing one way or the other, Mr. Yue Ming had no choice but to drop the matter.","He then picked up a letter from his desk and handed it to Chen Yi. \"Mr. Ju Yi from Jinling Academy just sent over a few letters.\"","\"One of them is specifically for you.\"","Chen Yi stepped forward and took it. Just as he was about to open it, Mr. Yue Ming continued,","\"The poetry gathering is about to start. You can read the letter when you get back; it won’t be too late.\"","Chen Yi subconsciously squeezed the envelope. It felt like there was something else inside besides the letter. He tucked it safely inside his collar.","He didn’t know much about Mr. Ju Yi, his teacher in name only, so he couldn’t guess why the man would send a letter at this particular moment.","Fortunately, it would only be for half a day. He could afford to wait.","They did not linger long.","The group left the residence together. In the fading twilight, they followed a stone path illuminated by lanterns toward the site of the poetry gathering.","By this time, most of the guests had arrived for the poetry gathering, packing the specially prepared study hall to the brim.","The most prominent seats were naturally occupied by Liu Hong, Yang Ye, and other high-ranking officials of Shu State. Beside them sat several highly respected great scholars.","These included Mr. Yue Ming, Mr. Zhuo Ying, Mr. Lingchuan, and Mr. Zhangping of Yuelu Academy, among others.","Compared to them, even Liu Si, the Prefect of Shu State, could only take a seat off to the side.","To say nothing of Chen Yunfan, Li Huai’gu, and their peers.","Chen Yi scanned the room. Instead of taking a seat of honor with Mr. Yue Ming, he led Xiao Wan’er and the others to sit beside Chen Yunfan.","Shen Huatang, meanwhile, took Xiaodie to another side of the study hall to wait with a group of maids and servants.","After exchanging a few pleasantries and greetings, Chen Yunfan leaned in closer. \"Why did you bring that Tiger Girl along? She’s not going to poison anyone again today, is she?\"","The memory of being knocked out by Pei Guanli’s sedative at the last academy poetry gathering was apparently so profound that he still had lingering fears.","This was especially true after he learned of Pei Guanli’s true identity, which made him all the more wary of her.","Chen Yi couldn’t help but laugh. \"Brother, are you still worried about that?\"","He knew just how deep Chen Yunfan’s Martial Arts Cultivation ran; he didn’t believe for a second that his friend was truly afraid of Pei Guanli.","\"How could I not be?\"","\"That girl dared to use poison at the Old Marquis’s own birthday banquet! She’s completely lawless...\"","Catching Pei Guanli’s gaze out of the corner of his eye, Chen Yunfan immediately sat up straight and cleared his throat.","\"The academy invited quite a few courtesans today, Brother Yi. Don’t miss the beautiful sights and songs.\"","Chen Yi paused, then, noticing the looks from Xiao Wan’er and the others, replied, \"You’re joking, Brother.\"","\"How am I joking? I...\"","Before Chen Yunfan could finish, Cui Qingwu gave him a quiet tug. With an apologetic glance at those around them, he pulled Chen Yunfan aside to whisper about other matters.","Xiao Wan’er looked at Chen Yi’s feigned innocence, smiled sweetly, and said,","\"I hear that several of the courtesans who sent you invitations before are also in attendance today. You really should watch and listen closely.\"","’That’s ancient history,’ Chen Yi muttered to himself.","Grumbling internally, he took in the scene around him—Chen Yunfan and Cui Qingwu were whispering affectionately, Li Huai’gu and Lady Yun were lost in their own world, and Xiao Wuge and Pei Guanli...","...those two were looking everywhere, their eyes wide, clearly finding everything new and exciting.","After a moment’s thought, Chen Yi figured he might as well make a pair with Xiao Wan’er.","\"Are you feeling comfortable, Wan’er?\"","Xiao Wan’er subconsciously pulled her large cloak tighter, half her face disappearing into the fluffy white fur trim. \"It’s alright,\" she murmured softly.","She was, in truth, a little uncomfortable.","She had only ever heard about poetry gatherings, never attended one herself.","Now that she was here, she was discovering that this sort of occasion didn’t suit her at all.","There were too many strangers, and it required so much polite conversation.","She also had to be mindful of her posture and status, all while enduring the occasional whispered criticisms and impolite stares.","It was all making her feel out of place.","If Chen Yi and the others weren’t sitting by her side, she probably would have already found an excuse to leave.","Chen Yi noticed her discomfort. He offered a few comforting words with a smile, then started telling her amusing stories to distract her.","But while Chen Yi’s group chatted quietly, other parts of the hall were much more boisterous.","The students of Guiyun Academy were gathered together, the members of the Noble Families had formed their own small cliques, and the guests from other state capitals did the same.","The groups kept to themselves, but as they laughed and chatted, their topics of conversation began to overlap.","\"There’s been a lot of trouble in Shu State lately. It’s truly become a laughingstock for the whole world.\"","\"Indeed. Who would have thought the culprit behind the attacks on the Three Towns wasn’t from the Barbarian Race or Poshisu Country, but was...\"","A long-faced young scholar jutted his chin toward Liu Hong on the high platform. \"...that one.\"","Ma Guan, sitting in the middle of the group, cut in. \"Brother Yuan Lin, quiet down, lest the masters overhear you.\"","\"If he can do such things, why can’t we talk about them?\"","\"Speaking ill of others behind their backs is not the act of a gentleman.\"","\"If you’re so inclined, Brother Yuan Lin, why don’t you go up on that stage and hold forth in front of Lord Liu himself?\"","The long-faced scholar pointed at Ma Guan. \"You...\"","He was bold enough to say such things in private, but if he were to actually stand before Liu Hong, the Lord Governor of Shu State, he’d probably be too scared to utter a single word.","Someone nearby tried to smooth things over. \"The masters are all watching.\"","\"Alright, let’s talk about something else...\"","Meanwhile, at another table, Pei Zhaoye of Yuelu Academy was in the middle of a heated debate.","\"Who cares if he takes me as a student?\"","\"There are countless people in this world who have reached Perfection in the Calligraphy Dao, even some in the Saint Realm. If I don’t study under Chen Qingzhou, there are plenty of other famous masters.\"","A similarly-aged scholar in blue robes asked with a smirk, \"Then why did you try to become his disciple right then and there?\"","\"Who said I did?\"","\"Weren’t you? The masters from Guiyun Academy can all attest to it.\"","\"I also heard Mr. Qingzhou said he ’couldn’t teach you.’ HAHA! Is that true?\"","\"Outrageous!\"","Pei Zhaoye’s face flushed red with anger. Stiffening his neck, he retorted, \"Today is the Mid-Autumn Poetry Gathering! We’re here to befriend one another through poetry, not the Calligraphy Dao.\"","The scholar in blue robes said, \"Oh? So you’re saying, Brother Pei, that you plan to compete with Mr. Qingzhou in the art of poetry?\"","\"If he wants to compete, then we’ll compete!\"","His voice was rather loud, making it difficult for Chen Yi to ignore.","However, he was in the middle of a quiet conversation with Xiao Wan’er and couldn’t be bothered with the chatter around him.","「Not long after.」","The poetry gathering began as scheduled.","Courtesans took the stage, performing songs and dances. With the endless courses of the banquet, the atmosphere could certainly be described as \"elegant.\"","After three rounds of drinks, Mr. Yue Ming gave a short speech, then conferred with the other masters and announced the topic:","\"The theme is the bright moon, in celebration of the Mid-Autumn Festival.\"","It was a fitting theme for the occasion, and many of the scholars who had come prepared looked visibly pleased.","Even Chen Yunfan looked eager to give it a try.","\"Brother Yi, I’ll go first later. Don’t you jump ahead of me.\"","Chen Yi smiled and nodded. It wouldn’t have mattered to him if he didn’t write at all, let alone who went first.","However, as he glanced around their table, a flicker of confusion crossed his face. \"Where did Pei Guanli go?\"","Xiao Wuge, his eyes glued to the performers on stage, answered distractedly, \"Sister Guanli said she was going to the latrine.\"","Xiao Wan’er tapped him lightly on the arm. \"Mind your manners,\" she chided. \"Don’t use such crude language.\"","Upon hearing this, Chen Yi thought for a moment, then stood up. \"Wait here, I’m going to go check on her.\"","He was still a little worried. It wouldn’t do to have that Tiger Girl try her poisoning tricks here.","\"Hurry back, Brother Yi. It’ll be your turn after I’m done writing.\"","\"Got it...\""]},{"number":299,"title":"Chapter 299 - 217: The Good Show Begins","paragraphs":["Chen Yi rose and left. Under normal circumstances, his departure might not have drawn any notice.","But here, at the Guiyun Academy’s poetry gathering, many had come to Shu State specifically for the Calligraphy Dao of Chen Yi—the renowned Mr. Qingzhou.","Thus, the moment he left, quite a few people noticed his movements, even in the crowded, spacious courtyard.","This was especially true for Mr. Yue Ming, Mr. Zhuo Ying, and the others on the high platform.","The poetry topic had just been announced, yet Chen Yi, on whom they had pinned such high hopes, wasn’t thinking about composing poetry to showcase his Calligraphy Dao. Instead, he walked out with a carefree expression, looking as if he were just out for a stroll.","The two old men looked rather embarrassed.","Mr. Zhuo Ying leaned in closer. \"Dean, Qingzhou must have simply gone to relieve himself. When nature calls... It’s normal, perfectly normal.\"","Mr. Yue Ming nodded slightly. \"Let’s hope so.\"","Having spent some time with him, he had a decent understanding of Chen Yi and knew that an occasion like today’s wouldn’t necessarily stir his poetic muse.","Fortunately, while he hoped for a successful outcome, he wasn’t obsessed, so he wouldn’t be overly demanding of Chen Yi.","Just then, Liu Si, the Prefect of Shu State, who had also noticed Chen Yi’s departure, glanced at the expressions around him. He leaned forward to look toward the head of the platform, cupped his hands, and said:","\"Mr. Yue Ming, I have long heard that Qingzhou’s Calligraphy Dao has reached Perfection, but I have never had the opportunity to witness it.\"","\"Today is the Mid-Autumn Festival. Why haven’t you arranged for him to compose a poem? It would be a fine opportunity to showcase his Calligraphy Dao and let us all feast our eyes.\"","Mr. Yue Ming glanced at him and said in a level voice, \"Qingzhou is an Instructor at my academy, not some songstress performing for an audience.\"","\"He will compose poetry if he wishes and practice his calligraphy if he wishes. Even I, the dean of this academy, will not force him.\"","Mr. Zhuo Ying added with a smile, \"The Dean is right.\"","Then he turned to Liu Si and said with a smile, \"Prefect Liu, an academy isn’t like your Government Office. We don’t stand on ceremony about superiors and subordinates here.\"","Liu Si’s old face flushed red. \"You two gentlemen are correct. I stand corrected.\"","Having said his piece, he sullenly drew back.","Although he was the Prefect of Shu State, in charge of all affairs great and small in the Prefecture City, there wasn’t a single person present whom he could afford to offend.","Those without official posts were learned, renowned, and from powerful families. As for those who did hold posts, every one of them was higher in rank and wielded more authority than he.","Especially Liu Hong and Yang Ye, who were seated beside Mr. Yue Ming—both were Second-Grade Officers.","If today’s poetry gathering were not a private occasion, a good number of the people present would likely be behaving far more cautiously.","At this moment, Liu Hong looked around as if he had only just taken notice and asked with a smile:","\"Brother Ming, where might Chen Qingzhou be sitting?\"","\"Whether he composes poetry or practices his calligraphy is secondary. I should at least be allowed to see the man and put a face to the name.\"","Mr. Yue Ming paused, turning his head to meet Liu Hong’s gaze.","He could ignore others or put them off with a vague excuse, but with Liu Hong, he had to be more cautious.","\"Qingzhou has just stepped away. Later, after I’ve spoken with him, I will bring him over.\"","Liu Hong looked at him with a faint, unreadable smile. \"Spoken with him?\"","\"What? Is his Calligraphy Dao truly so great as to warrant such high regard from you?\"","Mr. Yue Ming’s expression returned to calm as he admitted it directly. \"You’re right, Brother Gong Mo.\"","\"Qingzhou’s Calligraphy Dao has reached Perfection, and in a new script style, no less. His decision to join Guiyun Academy is a great blessing for our institution.\"","As he spoke, he gestured toward Mr. Zhangping and the others on the opposite side. \"If it were Yuelu Academy or Yingtian Academy, I believe they would treasure a talent like Qingzhou just as highly as I do.\"","As soon as he finished, Mr. Zhangping nodded with a smile. \"Dean Yue Ming left one thing out.\"","\"What’s most precious is this—Qingzhou can teach others how to attain the Calligraphy Dao.\"","Fang Sifeng, the representative from Yingtian Academy, was a middle-aged Confucian Scholar with a slightly arrogant air about him.","Even when facing the dignitaries on the high platform, he kept his chin held high.","Hearing Han Zhangping’s words, he grinned and said, \"Mr. Zhangping, whether or not that Chen Qingzhou can actually teach someone to master the Calligraphy Dao is, I’m afraid, still up for debate.\"","The expressions of Mr. Yue Ming, Mr. Zhuo Ying, and the others changed subtly.","Mr. Zhuo Ying immediately looked at him, displeased. \"Si Feng, both the Dean and I have personally witnessed Qingzhou’s ability to guide others to success in the Calligraphy Dao.\"","\"Furthermore, the Dean and I were able to achieve Minor Success in our own Calligraphy Dao thanks to Qingzhou’s adept guidance.\"","\"By saying that, are you calling me a liar? Are you calling the Dean of our Guiyun Academy a liar?\"","Si Feng’s face fell. He forced a smile and said, \"My apologies, Mr. Zhuo Ying. I was merely stating a possibility.\"","\"After all, until now, this claim that Chen Qingzhou can teach the Calligraphy Dao is merely the word of Guiyun Academy.\"","Before Zhuo Ying could speak, Mr. Yue Ming raised his hand slightly, looked at Fang Sifeng, and asked in a serious tone:","\"Then what is it you propose?\"","\"Since Dean Yue Ming asks, I will be so bold as to make a suggestion. Why not have Chen Qingzhou teach a lesson for us all?\"","At his words, even Han Zhangping, who had previously spoken in support of Mr. Yue Ming, fell silent.","Someone among the representatives from the other academies even spoke up, \"Mr. Sifeng’s proposal is an excellent one.\"","\"This way, we’ll also have something to report when we return to our own academies.\"","Hearing this, Mr. Yue Ming, Mr. Zhuo Ying, and the others exchanged a glance, immediately guessing the intentions of these people.","A moment of silence passed.","Yang Ye, dressed in simple gray clothes and sitting next to Liu Hong, coughed upon seeing everyone fall silent and then muttered:","\"Today is the Mid-Autumn Festival, a poetry gathering. How has it turned into an inquisition where all the great Confucian Scholars put Guiyun Academy on trial?\"","At his words, everyone looked toward him.","Seeing that it was Yang Ye, the Right Governor of Shu State, Fang Sifeng’s expression changed slightly. He cupped his hands and said with a laugh, \"Lord Yang, please don’t take offense. I had no intention of spoiling the mood.\"","Yang Ye gave him a noncommittal look. \"So it was intentional?\"","\"Er... Lord Yang is right. Tonight is for the Mid-Autumn poetry gathering. We should go back to appreciating the moon and the poetry.\""]},{"number":300,"title":"Chapter 300 - 217: The Good Show Begins","paragraphs":["Seeing Fang Sifeng’s defeat, the others from the academy said no more.","Mr. Yue Ming and Mr. Zhuo Ying also breathed a sigh of relief. They nodded at Yang Ye, then called someone over to ask if anyone had completed their poems.","Liu Hong watched the scene with a smile, as if his earlier mention of Chen Yi’s name had been nothing more than a casual remark.","Yang Ye leaned back in his chair, looking perfectly composed. As his gaze swept over Liu Hong’s face, a flicker of suspicion inexplicably crossed his mind.","’Why would this old fox have his sights set on Chen Yi?’","...","The hour grew late.","In the night sky, a full moon bathed in silver light outshone the twinkling stars.","Within the two great courtyards of Guiyun Academy, the poetry gathering was in full swing.","In one courtyard, filled with gifted scholars and beautiful ladies, bursts of laughter would occasionally erupt, interspersed with exclamations of \"A fine poem!\" and the like.","Most likely, someone had presented a poem, drawing cheers from the onlookers.","In the other courtyard, Shen Huatang, Xiaodie, Wang Lixing, and the others were just as boisterous.","Theirs, however, was a boisterousness born of feasting and drinking.","Xiaodie, however, wasn’t enjoying her food. She kept getting up to peer toward the other courtyard, her pretty face filled with anticipation.","Noticing her expression, Shen Huatang circulated her True Essence to listen in on the surroundings while murmuring in a low voice,","\"Don’t bother looking. Too many scholars showed up today; this won’t be over any time soon.\"","\"Even if the Second Young Master-in-law does compose a poem, he’ll save it for the end. Just relax, have something to eat, and wait.\"","Xiaodie blushed. \"Sister Huatang, I... I’m just worried the Young Master-in-law will be struck by a fit of poetic genius and put everyone else to shame.\"","\"Isn’t that a good thing? Besting the entire field would prove the Second Young Master-in-law’s literary talents are extraordinary.\"","After speaking, Shen Huatang secretly pursed her lips. ’It’s not all good, though,’ she thought.","’At least, not for the Eldest Miss.’","\"It is good, but I’m afraid they’ll get angry from the humiliation and bully the Young Master-in-law.\"","\"How could they? With Mr. Yue Ming and all those officials from the Government Office watching, who would dare to start anything here?\"","\"They would...\"","Xiaodie still remembered the scholars who had denounced Chen Yi, both to his face and behind his back, during Li Huai’gu’s wedding.","\"They were so aggressive, baring their fangs and brandishing their claws. It was terrifying to watch. Even just scaring the Young Master-in-law counts as bullying.\"","Shen Huatang was speechless.","She really couldn’t figure out what was going on in the little maid’s head.","Just then, a voice called out, \"Ah, so this is where you are.\"","Xiaodie froze for a moment, then looked up in delight. \"Young Master-in-law, what are you doing here?\"","The newcomer was none other than Chen Yi.","He had left the courtyard of the poetry gathering fifteen minutes ago. After wandering about and searching, he still hadn’t found Pei Guanli.","He’d guessed that Tiger Girl had gotten bored and run off to the courtyard where the guards and servants were gathered.","But even after arriving and scanning the area, Chen Yi still couldn’t see any sign of Pei Guanli, and he couldn’t help but frown.","Xiaodie didn’t notice his strange mood. She sidled up to him, her face alight with excitement.","\"Young Master-in-law, have you already finished your poem?\"","Chen Yi snapped out of his thoughts. His gaze swept over the small group as he shook his head, his expression normal. \"I just stepped out for a bit. I haven’t started writing yet.\"","Xiaodie wasn’t disappointed. \"The Young Master-in-law is a great poet and a fine calligrapher. As long as you put your mind to it, it’ll be no problem at all.\"","Chen Yi chuckled, flicking her lightly on the forehead. \"I have all these great talents, do I? How come I’m the last to know?\"","\"But it’s true...\"","Off to the side, Shen Huatang and Wang Lixing watched the master and servant banter, neither of them noticing anything amiss.","Shen Huatang merely took advantage of a lull in the conversation to ask about Xiao Wan’er’s situation.","Chen Yi replied with a smile, \"Big Sister has people looking after her over there. She seems to be doing alright.\"","\"But I’ve been out for some time now. I should be getting back.\"","Even though Xiaodie wanted to talk with him longer, she could only say hesitantly, \"Take care, Young Master-in-law.\"","Chen Yi nodded to the group, told them to enjoy the food and drink, and then turned to walk toward the other courtyard.","The two courtyards were a moderate distance apart. The path between them led through a brightly lit corridor and around a rockery to a small, stone-paved trail.","The path was flanked by lush flowers and plants, and he could faintly hear the whispers of a few couples meeting secretly in the shadows.","Chen Yi walked on without disturbing their rendezvous, his mind preoccupied with Pei Guanli’s whereabouts as he headed back toward the poetry gathering.","’That girl may be a tiger, but she knows her limits.’","’Especially when she’s with me. If something came up, Pei Guanli would have told me. She wouldn’t just vanish without a word.’","At this thought, Chen Yi’s eyes turned cold.","’Did something happen?’","’Who could it be?’","’Pei Guanli is from the Mountain Race and Granny Shan’s granddaughter. It’s unlikely that people from the Government Office or the Noble Families would bother her, let alone attack her.’","’That much was clear from the Xiao Family’s reaction—or lack thereof—when they learned Tiger Girl had used poison to take down a whole group of guards.’","’Excluding the Noble Families and the Government Office, that only left one other group.’","’Jianghu People.’","’Or, to be more specific—the Evil Demonic Dao!’","’The Five Poison Sect!’","Chen Yi’s heart sank.","He’d once heard Liu Lang speak of the grudge between the Five Poison Sect and the Mountain Race; to call it a blood feud would be no exaggeration.","With the Five Poison Sect now in Shu State, he had already been planning to send word to the Mountain Race.","He’d simply been too busy dealing with Liu Wen and Xiao Dongchen these past few days to get around to it.","As for why the Five Poison Sect was here, Chen Yi had a guess.","They could only have been brought by Liu Zhaoxue.","’If so, perhaps they’re acting on a whim?’","As these thoughts raced through his mind, Chen Yi’s expression turned grim, and he quickened his pace toward the courtyard of the poetry gathering.","As he walked, he checked for the tools he carried on his person.","’The Five-section Spear is here. Qingfeng Drunk and Immortal Drunk, too. What else do I have that can defend against the poisons of the Five Poison Sect?’","Just as Chen Yi was about to pass through a mahogany corridor and enter the courtyard where the poetry gathering was being held, he abruptly stopped in his tracks."]}]);
